	quest.0017FFFAD7CD2EFE.quest_subtitle: "Harder, Better, Faster, Stronger"
	quest.0017FFFAD7CD2EFE.title: "More EV Circuits!"
	quest.0021051273D48936.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Autoclave&r - despite being optional - is a machine you'll definitively want to grab."
		""
		"This unlocks unique Batteries that are &6far superior&r to their standard counterparts."
	]
	quest.0021051273D48936.quest_subtitle: "The Road To Power Storage"
	quest.0021051273D48936.title: "HV Autoclave"
	quest.004CEA979BC74728.title: "Upgrade orb"
	quest.007FF6F71BEF7E3C.quest_subtitle: "Before you head out to find your first Meteorite make sure to have an Iron Pickaxe or better. Meteorites are made out of a very hard material called Sky Stone which requires it. Make sure you mine to the center of the meteorite to collect the Certus Quartz Crystals, Certus Quartz Blocks and your Inscriber Presses!"
	quest.007FF6F71BEF7E3C.title: "Your First Meteorite"
	quest.0089AA3A92C02334.quest_desc: [
		"Granite Dust centrifuges into Redrock Dust and the familiar Silicon Dioxide Dust."
		""
		"Silicon Dioxide is generally just great to have, and Redrock centrifuges into Calcite (that's renewable Calcium) and Flint."
	]
	quest.0089AA3A92C02334.quest_subtitle: "Redrock, Silicon Dioxide..."
	quest.008ABF78E56209F7.quest_desc: [
		"New to this updated pack is a &dGuides + More&r section. The information inside is available to view at any time, but whenever it becomes relevant, you will be &6directed towards it&r for some light reading."
		""
		"The information found inside may interest you if you would like &amore of an insight&r into some of &bGTCEu's mechanics&r - and in some cases, is absolutely indispensable."
		""
		"Quests that unlock a tutorial node will have an &6orange-ish descriptor&r at the bottom of the quest description."
		""
		"Get reading!"
	]
	quest.008ABF78E56209F7.quest_subtitle: "Tips and tricks to help you prosper"
	quest.008ABF78E56209F7.title: "Tutorialised"
	quest.00961AB544612C82.quest_desc: ["\"Ну такие вкусные дырочки\" - DOOMvenik"]
	quest.00961AB544612C82.title: "Рогалики"
	quest.00B5B5675D80D904.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.00BB2F25D925C48B.quest_desc: ["Коварная свеча - один из немногих сохранившихся артефактов святилища душ. Представляет собой свечу, призывающую замученные души на бой с вами."]
	quest.00BB2F25D925C48B.title: "Потухшие свечи"
	quest.00C14E3B8009DF7F.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest will be completed with &eeither&r an &3LuV Energy Hatch&r&r... or an &3LuV Dynamo Hatch&r for your Multiblock Generators."
		""
		"Starting at &dLuV&r, you'll start upgrading more multiblocks, which means more energy hatches! Both the &9EBF&r and the &9Assembly Line&r will need power upgrades."
		""
		"Don't forget that &d4 Amp&r variants exist!"
	]
	quest.00C14E3B8009DF7F.title: "Upgrading your Assembly Line"
	quest.00CB8D60E7831A57.title: "Find &6Catacombs"
	quest.00E1A728E6F6D6A0.quest_desc: [
		"&aBenzene&r is a &9Gas Fuel&r. To skip some frustration, let's check out the two best ways to obtain it."
		""
		"The first option is typically &dWood based&r. Put Logs in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r for &9Wood Tar&r. The Charcoal you obtain can then be processed in &3Extractors&r for even more &9Wood Tar&r, which you &3distill&r for &aBenzene&r."
		""
		"Your second option is &dHeavy Oil based&r. Put Heavy Oil in a &3Distillery&r for &9Heavy Fuel&r, which you &aseverely steam-crack&r and &3distill&r again for &aBenzene&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For information on how to process Oil, check the Light Fuel and Naphtha Quests."
		""
		"In general, it is better to prioritize placing down more machines (&dparallelisation&r) over overclocking the recipes. That way, you end up losing less energy processing the resources."
		""
		"&aBenzene&r is burned in a &3Gas Turbine&r. This power source starts weaker than its &eDiesel&r cousin, but gets a big boost when refined to &6Nitrobenzene&r in &6HV&r. Ultimately, your power source is your choice."
	]
	quest.00E1A728E6F6D6A0.quest_subtitle: "In the end, it's always Benzene"
	quest.00E1A728E6F6D6A0.title: "The Church of Benzene"
	quest.00E2BAEDB8199E4E.quest_desc: [
		"&aGasoline&r is an extremely powerful Combustion Fuel. It's over &63 times&r as energy dense as &dDiesel&r!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r This Combustion Fuel exists solely as a &echallenge&r for you to overcome if you desire to take on it."
		""
		"It's completely &doptional&r, so we'll let you figure out how to obtain it, without any further tips."
	]
	quest.00E2BAEDB8199E4E.title: "Gasoline"
	quest.00F4547B33E7054E.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.00F4547B33E7054E.quest_subtitle: "&6Burns the attacker"
	quest.012BF60FBD5D41AC.quest_desc: [
		"All good ore processing lines start with a crush, and in your case, you'll want to macerate either your &5Raw Ore&r, or your Ore blocks (if you're using &dSilk Touch&r!)"
		""
		"When you can make the large multiblock Miners, your ore yield is almost &aquadrupled&r further, and you won't need to macerate for the first step - the &bLarge Miner&r will output its ores as if they had been macerated."
	]
	quest.012BF60FBD5D41AC.quest_subtitle: "Well. You've gotta start somewhere!"
	quest.012BF60FBD5D41AC.title: "The First Maceration"
	quest.013E936F2BE8E1BE.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.013E936F2BE8E1BE.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.0148232307C5D524.quest_desc: ["Из этих в какой-то степени странных материалов можно создать много интересных вещей."]
	quest.0148232307C5D524.title: "Материалы Caverns and Chasms"
	quest.017019EB38F7A18C.quest_desc: [
		"Doping is the process of intentionally introducing impurities into semiconductors to alter their properties."
		""
		"&7Silicon&r can be doped with small amounts of &ePhosphorus&r to make a better &eSilicon Boule&r."
		""
		"Phosphorus-doped Silicon Boules typically yield &68 times&r more wafers than their non-doped counterparts. However, they are not strictly needed until &5EV&r, where they'll be used in more complex wafers."
		""
		"&9Note&r: All processing of Phosphorus Boules and Wafers will require a &dCleanroom&r."
	]
	quest.017019EB38F7A18C.quest_subtitle: "That's dope, bro!"
	quest.017019EB38F7A18C.title: "Phosphorus Boules"
	quest.0179D5430F3433C3.quest_desc: ["В нашем мире с давних времён существует могущественная раса, которая стоит на вершине иерархии во всём мире - драконы. Они делятся на три типа: &6огненные&r, &bледяные&r и &dгрозовые&r. Их зубы могут прокусить металл, их когти могут срубить деревья."]
	quest.0199DBC46D7BC2B9.quest_desc: [
		"&3Advanced HPCA Components&r are improved versions of their regular counterparts, and allow for increasing the computation you can produce from an HPCA."
		""
		"The &3HPCA Advanced Computation Component&r produces &a4x&r the computation for only &a2x&r the Cooling!"
	]
	quest.0199DBC46D7BC2B9.quest_subtitle: "Time for some computational advancement!"
	quest.0199DBC46D7BC2B9.title: "Advanced HPCA Components"
	quest.01AB252C72B565FE.quest_desc: [
		"&9IV&r Components - fortunately for you - aren't a massive step up in terms of complexity."
		""
		"However, the amount of &dTungsten&r required in crafting these is huge."
		""
		"&aEmitters&r and &aSensors&r are in their own league, as they require &dNether Stars&r and &dIridium&r, both of which have their own dedicated Quests."
	]
	quest.01AB252C72B565FE.quest_subtitle: "...and if you disagree, you'll see the light soon enough"
	quest.01AB252C72B565FE.title: "There is no limit to \"Fun\""
	quest.01B2B0B4C6110AC2.quest_desc: ["Люкструктозавр - древний монстр, живущий в вулканах первобытных пещер."]
	quest.01B2B0B4C6110AC2.title: "Большое вымирание"
	quest.01B6247D19E974DB.quest_desc: ["Аский фастфуд."]
	quest.01B6247D19E974DB.title: "Адские закуски"
	quest.01BBE636EBB71416.quest_subtitle: "One of the Quarry's drills."
	quest.01BBE636EBB71416.title: "&3Stainless Steel Drill"
	quest.0226F89EEC57C5EC.quest_subtitle: "Found upon his throne in &eSavanna &rbiomes"
	quest.023FF9633765A0EB.quest_desc: [
		"Build the structure displayed with Fusion Glass in &aEMI&r."
		""
		"To save on Fusion Casings, fit Input + Output Hatches wherever you can (as displayed in the structure)."
		""
		"The &aFusion Reactor Mk3&r is even more expensive than the Mk2! The key difference is that it has a higher &6Energy To Start&r than the Mk2, allowing you to run new recipes."
		""
		"It can also overclock lower voltage recipes, such as those in the Mk1 or Mk2 reactor. See the Mk1's quest for how these mechanics work."
	]
	quest.023FF9633765A0EB.quest_subtitle: "The most expensive form of Fusion"
	quest.023FF9633765A0EB.title: "Fusion Reactor III"
	quest.02408EBF371C3B0A.quest_desc: ["The Hand Crank allows you to manually rotate mechanisms. Useful for initial charging or controlling simple devices."]
	quest.02408EBF371C3B0A.title: "Hand Crank"
	quest.024F55CAFFBC4BE7.quest_desc: ["The Shortblade can be used in off handed attacks and in crafting to cut materials."]
	quest.026682BD379CF002.quest_desc: ["Your first metal hammer! Time to get to some true smithing!"]
	quest.026682BD379CF002.title: "Iron Hammer: Tier III"
	quest.0269FCDE2628904A.quest_desc: [
		"Your classic Nether Quartz vein."
		""
		"Silicon isn't too difficult to come by, but Quartzite isn't a bad source."
	]
	quest.0269FCDE2628904A.quest_subtitle: "Source of Nether Quartz, Silicon"
	quest.0269FCDE2628904A.title: "Quartz"
	quest.029CF0D9E5097F87.quest_desc: [
		"Just like &bMV&r, you'll need to make higher-tier components."
		""
		"The painful &dFlawless Gems&r have been replaced with slightly-more-painful &dEyes of Ender&r. Also notice that the &aMotors&r require &d2x Silver Cables&r."
		""
		"&aHulls&r and &aMachines&r use &dGold Cables&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&lTips to make life less painful:&r"
		""
		"- Consider using &dElectrotine decomposition&r and &dOre Processing&r for &eElectrum&r."
		"- Consider using the &3Chemical Bath&r with &dMercury&r for &eGold&r from a wide variety of ores."
	]
	quest.029CF0D9E5097F87.quest_subtitle: "Wouldn't you agree? Fun!"
	quest.029CF0D9E5097F87.title: "We call this \"fun\""
	quest.02A9377B124D01AC.quest_desc: ["Доспех полководцев Легиона Затмения. Ходят слухи, что этот доспех ковался в самой Бездне и до сих пор черпает из неё силу, увеличивая запас здоровья владельца. Обеспечивает отличной защитой в бою."]
	quest.030E299F75640977.quest_desc: [
		"Your first Nether expedition should be for &eSulfur&r - which is found in this vein! Be careful, as this vein usually spawns from y-levels of 10 to 30. Bring Fire Resistance potions!"
		""
		"Sphalerite is extremely valuable, as its ore processing gives Gallium. It also smelts directly into Zinc."
	]
	quest.030E299F75640977.quest_subtitle: "Source of Sulfur, Iron, Zinc"
	quest.030E299F75640977.title: "Sulfur"
	quest.03349E265BC1D30D.quest_desc: ["В глубинах пещер вы можете найти хижину, где находится стол спелеолога и особый путеводитель по моду."]
	quest.03349E265BC1D30D.title: "Путешествие в подземелья"
	quest.033814C6CFAF56E6.quest_desc: [
		"Чтобы прогрессировать, вам нужно создать Fluix Crystal. У вас есть два варианта:"
		""
		"- Используйте компас, чтобы найти метеорит, где вы могли бы найти какой-нибудь кристалл Флюикса."
		""
		"- Бросьте заряженный кристалл Цертус-кварца, Нижний кварц и пыль Редстоуна в бассейн с водой и подождите."
	]
	quest.0338C9219DC2F819.quest_desc: [
		"The next board material."
		""
		"It's as easy as using some &aEpoxy&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r."
		""
		"&8Anyone in favor of this getting reworked?"
	]
	quest.0338C9219DC2F819.quest_subtitle: "The biggest upgrade you've ever seen"
	quest.0338C9219DC2F819.title: "Fiber-Reinforced Epoxy"
	quest.033C72478F243B7F.quest_desc: ["Provides a larger amount of Quanta than skulls, but can be difficult to acquire."]
	quest.0353FDDEA821D925.quest_subtitle: "Found in the &9Sunken City&r, at the seas. Locate with an &9Eye of Abyss"
	quest.0353FDDEA821D925.title: "Defeat the &dLeviathan"
	quest.035CF39E6CC98B77.quest_desc: [
		"Heavy Fuel can be obtained from many sources, but your best bet is distilling it from &eHeavy Oil&r. "
		""
		"You could just burn it in a combustion generator now for &9Power&r, but there's something even greater... check the Quest to the left."
	]
	quest.035CF39E6CC98B77.quest_subtitle: "Things are getting really Heavy around here..."
	quest.035CF39E6CC98B77.title: "Heavy Fuel"
	quest.036292964BDE4944.quest_desc: ["This will be very useful for Oil Processing."]
	quest.036292964BDE4944.quest_subtitle: "Will turn various fluids into their lighter parts. So this is how we get distilled water?"
	quest.03896D148D7B4E3B.quest_desc: [
		"It can produce 100s of times more EU/t than diesel. It comes in several sizes from small to large."
		""
		"How it works under the hood can be a bit overwhelming, nevertheless, you don't need to understand the details to be able to design a powerful reactor. We recommend that you experiment with various designs in creative mode until you find one that suits you."
		""
		"Note that the Nuclear Reactor cannot explode, emit radiation, or otherwise damage the map. The only thing that it can damage is the items you put in it if the temperature gets too high (more on this later). You should feel free to experiment, and enjoy your new life as a nuclear scientist!"
		""
		"The main component is the Nuclear Casing which is made with Nuclear Alloy : a mix of cadmium, beryllium and blastproof alloy."
		""
		"The upper part of the structure accepts Nuclear Item or Fluid Hatches (or simple casings). Those are the inputs and outputs of the reactor."
		""
		"Each hatch has one input (either item or fluid) and two outputs. The input slots will form a grid, displayed in the reactor GUI (accessible by right-clicking on the controller)."
		""
		"Each hatch has a temperature and stores heat which can be dissipated in several ways. The heat will naturally move to an adjacent hatch or to the outside if the hatch is on the edge (the heat is then lost). The speed of this process is equal to the hatches content's heat transfer coefficient (shown in REI) times the temperature difference. The heat can also be extracted in a fluid hatch by producing steam. A temperature above an item's maximum temperature will destroy it."
		""
		"The core nuclear reactor elements are neutrons. Those are produced by the nuclear fuel. There are two type of neutrons, fast and thermal : the fast carry energy while the thermal do not. Neutrons move in a straight line until they encounter an element or exit the reactor (for fast neutrons, their energy is then lost). The flow of neutrons is shown in the reactor GUI."
		""
		"When a neutron encounters a non-empty hatch, two things can happen : the neutron is absorbed or scattered. A scattered neutron will randomly change direction. If the scattered neutron is fast, it has a chance of slowing down, becoming a thermal one. This transfers the energy from the neutron to the hatch in the form of heat. An absorbed neutron stops its course and also transfers its energy if it was a fast neutron."
		""
		"The number of absorbed neutrons in a single hatch can be seen in the GUI. The probability for each processes is shown in REI. Those will strongly depend on the hatch's content and the neutron type (fast or thermal). Nuclear fuels absorb thermal neutrons far better."
		""
		"When a neutron, either fast or thermal, is absorbed in nuclear fuel, more neutrons are generated. Those are always fast neutrons and have random direction. Their generation is accompanied by the direct release of energy in the form of additional heat in the hatch."
		""
		"Above a certain threshold, the number of generated neutrons will decrease with the temperature until reaching zero. This process wastes some energy, but guarantees the stability of the reactor. The number of generated neutrons (and effective efficiency), the direct energy and the temperature threshold are in REI."
		""
		"Each nuclear component has maximum number of absorptions. When reached, the item is either destroyed or transformed into a depleted version. This is particularly useful for nuclear fuel because some part of the U238 is transformed into Plutonium in the depleted version, meaning some of it can be transformed back into fuel."
		""
		"The same thing happens for fluids: a bit of fluid is transformed after each neutron absorption. This can be used to mass produce useful isotopes like deuterium and tritium. In both cases, the outcome is shown in REI."
	]
	quest.03896D148D7B4E3B.quest_subtitle: "A large multiblock whose purpose is to generate massive amounts of energy by consuming nuclear fuel."
	quest.038B71E71E3C8213.title: "Defeat a &6Valkyrie"
	quest.038F3D779491310A.title: "Shifting Blade"
	quest.039F4C3E503F2102.quest_desc: ["Trim pieces will allow you to extend your network around corners or other configurations without sacrificing a true storage drawer. It is helpful when setting up a controller based system."]
	quest.03A7A2C805212F63.quest_desc: ["В местных заброшенных лагерях, вы можете найти кожу, из которой можно создать комплект первобытной брони."]
	quest.03D44ED78095418F.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &4брони&r, а также &4лук&r из теневого шёлка и других ресурсов &4забвенных пустот&r."]
	quest.03DA8E6659757DE9.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &dсамку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &dбестиарии&r."]
	quest.03DA8E6659757DE9.quest_subtitle: "&dАметистовое"
	quest.03DBF1961AE21C76.quest_desc: [
		"&dSteam Machines&r accept any Steam that is pumped from nearby Boilers into their internal storage tank. They will run recipes from EMI up to 32 EU/t (&7LV&r-tier)."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on Steam in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.03DBF1961AE21C76.quest_subtitle: "Surprisingly Steamy"
	quest.03DBF1961AE21C76.title: "Steam Machine Behaviour"
	quest.03FBBA4A693011A8.quest_desc: [
		"An excellent Iron-Copper hybrid vein."
		""
		"Chalcopyrite will play an integral role in the late game, when you're looking to get your hands on some Platinum Group Sludge."
	]
	quest.03FBBA4A693011A8.quest_subtitle: "Source of Copper, Iron"
	quest.03FBBA4A693011A8.title: "Pyrite"
	quest.03FFC76D89BE5D29.quest_desc: ["The Sickle head will allow you to break plant blocks in a wide area."]
	quest.0425179329ED1B72.quest_desc: [
		"The &aHPIC&r unlocks &3IV Energy Hatches&r and &3Dynamos&r... You know the drill!"
		""
		"Making an &3IV Chemical Reactor&r is &doptional&r. You can craft this with a &3Large Chemical Reactor&r if you wish."
		""
		"If you wish to automate your LCR with patterns, circle back to the P2P Tunnel Quest for more information."
	]
	quest.0425179329ED1B72.title: "High Power Integrated Circuit"
	quest.042EE2F5E9F5CFBF.quest_subtitle: "Uraninite is used to create Reactors that also use uraninite to generate electricity. You need 36 blocks to create a functioning Reactor, the higher tier, the more power generated from Uraninite."
	quest.0436F7B60BDEB091.quest_desc: [
		"Here's a &6nifty&r list of some resources that you'll need in bulk for early-game. Collect more than we're asking for in this quest - you'll end up running out before you know it, and it's always a good habit to gather more than you need in &aGregTech&r."
		""
		"We'd actually advise that you &etackle this quest first&r, so that you can claim its &breward&r. That way, you can do a little bit of main (read: &ointeresting&r) progression &4&lBEFORE&r you're forced to go mining."
		""
		"Eight furnaces might seem &cexcessive&r if you're new to &aGregTech,&r but trust us... you can never have too many."
	]
	quest.0436F7B60BDEB091.quest_subtitle: "Gather some resources!"
	quest.0436F7B60BDEB091.title: "What do I need to progress?"
	quest.04679F17164E7CD3.quest_desc: ["Доспех полководцев Легиона Затмения. Ходят слухи, что этот доспех ковался в самой Бездне и до сих пор черпает из неё силу, увеличивая запас здоровья владельца. Обеспечивает отличной защитой в бою."]
	quest.046AD33371C52EED.quest_desc: ["В &dКраю&r можно найти &dдревнюю крепость пустоты&r. В ней обитает могущественный страж, что охраняет эту крепость тысячалетиями."]
	quest.046B4A0B2639B16A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Multiply the energy density by 2&r and you have &aHigh Octane Gasoline&r."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Automating this requires a lot of &3Distillation Towers&r! A huge portion of your base would be dedicated to producing this constantly without anything bottlenecking."
		""
		"If you have a base successfully running on &aHOG&r, feel free to brag and share some screenshots on our &8Discord&r."
	]
	quest.046B4A0B2639B16A.quest_subtitle: "Fetch me my Draconium!"
	quest.046B4A0B2639B16A.title: "High Octane Gasoline"
	quest.047D06C32B1284A8.quest_desc: ["&dSnow Queen&r is the Lord of Ice and Cold of the twilight forest. She is considered one of the strongest bosses of the twilight forest."]
	quest.047D06C32B1284A8.title: "Snow Queen"
	quest.04B2BCD5B4E56C49.quest_desc: ["Доспех Героя, сразившего Тёмного Лорда в жестокой битве. После этого силы тьмы отступили обратно в Бездну и больше не предпринимали попыток нападения. Этот доспех впитал в себя сущность того героя и наделяет владельца силой и регенерацией."]
	quest.04B4FB69D88D1C76.quest_subtitle: "One of the Quarry's drills."
	quest.04B4FB69D88D1C76.title: "&8Steel Drill"
	quest.04BB5D285A9B1D43.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.04D9F6587EF8D9B7.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Potion Jar&r stores up to 100 potions. You can remove them by using an empty bottle or a potion flask on the jar."
		""
		"Wixies will use these jars during Potion Autocrafting."
	]
	quest.04D9F6587EF8D9B7.quest_subtitle: "Storing Potions"
	quest.04DD3F761C210822.title: "Crude Blast Furnace"
	quest.04E9D2F484702965.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Power Substation&r is a multiblock power storage system. Fill it with &a2-18 layers&r of assorted &9Capacitor Blocks&r to increase its storage. Each layer must be full of capacitors, and you can use Empty Capacitors to fill unused spaces."
		""
		"&9Capacitors&r also hold significantly more energy than the batteries used to make them. In the &3Power Substation&r, &9Capacitors&r can be mixed, so they do not all have to be the same tier."
		""
		"At &1IV&r, you can make &5EV&r and/or &1IV&r Capacitors."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Energy can be inputted with regular Energy Hatches, and output with regular Dynamo Hatches."
		""
		"You can also use &9Substation Hatches&r to transmit many more amps. These hatches only work in Substations, and do not work in regular multiblocks."
	]
	quest.04E9D2F484702965.quest_subtitle: "Centralised power, at last"
	quest.04E9D2F484702965.title: "Power Substation"
	quest.04F6E968CEEC3D49.quest_desc: [
		"&aCetane-Boosted Diesel&r is &650% more energy dense&r than regular &aDiesel&r, and only requires 1 part &dTetranitromethane (TNM)&r for every 50 parts &aDiesel&r. What a steal, right?"
		""
		"The catch comes in the complexity of making &dTNM&r. In order to concoct it, you must react &aNitric Acid&r with either &dEthenone&r or &aMethyl Acetate&r, both of which have quite an involved process themselves!"
	]
	quest.04F6E968CEEC3D49.quest_subtitle: "This is to go further beyond"
	quest.04F6E968CEEC3D49.title: "Cetane-boosted Diesel"
	quest.04FAF93691F0BD9C.quest_subtitle: "Nah, it doesn't explode and do external damage, but it only works inside machinery, sorry to burst your bubble."
	quest.04FAF93691F0BD9C.title: "TACTICAL NUKE! INCOMING!!"
	quest.05003665368F5A57.quest_desc: [
		"Faster Ore Processing only at the cost of this &3Macerator&r! A must have."
		""
		"Also used to craft the &3Large Maceration Tower&r."
		""
		"And now, it's finally time for mass ore processing automation."
		""
		"The next Quest will kick things off!"
	]
	quest.05003665368F5A57.quest_subtitle: "No more being Ore-poor!"
	quest.05003665368F5A57.title: "Shredding your Ores with greater speed"
	quest.0533ACC607B33EE4.quest_desc: ["Тёмный лорд - порождение Бездны. Именно он вёл в бой Легион Затмения, пытаясь принести мир в жертву Бездне. Его доспех - прямое воплощение ужаса и боли всех, кто пал от его рук. Увеличивает урон носителя, заставляя проливать всё больше крови во имя тьмы."]
	quest.054C53F2662824ED.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.05774552286C1F73.quest_desc: ["Эти облучённые радиацией вещи выпадают с жутких монстров токсичных пещер."]
	quest.05774552286C1F73.title: "Радиоактивные технологии"
	quest.057CB349E1D67E10.quest_desc: ["Half-size 1x2 storage drawers will store 8 stacks of an item per drawer (16 stacks overall)."]
	quest.057CB349E1D67E10.title: "Half Storage Drawer: Two Item"
	quest.0599031E366DFD14.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &aчешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.0599031E366DFD14.quest_subtitle: "&aЗелёный комплект"
	quest.0599031E366DFD14.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.05ADBAE5B6F38956.quest_desc: [
		"It's quite the investment to own a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r, but it is &oby far&r the most prominent &6source of Oil&r."
		""
		"It pumps fluids from underneath Bedrock itself. Note that the fluids aren't actually there, instead being simulated."
		""
		"Fluid veins are stored within &cchunk-sized regions&r. Each vein has a different fluid, but they are mostly types of Oil."
		""
		"You can't carry out prospecting for fluid veins &oyet&r - this will come at &6HV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each vein generates with a different base yield. This is typically between &d150L&r to &d300L per second&r."
		""
		"When drained, fluid veins will slowly deplete. This will cause the fluid yield to decrease over time until it reaches its depletion yield. At that point, you should move the Rig to a different vein."
		""
		"A &3Basic Fluid Drilling Rig&r will last for 100,000 operations (with 1 second per operation) until depletion. This is enough for &6well over 10,000&r buckets of Oil. Higher tier Rigs will massively increase the yield, while also decreasing the depletion rate."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lWhat you can find in the &2Overworld&r&l:&r"
		""
		"&9Oil:&r richer in &aLight Fuel&r, the most appreciated variant."
		"&9Light Oil:&r richer in &aRefinery Gas&r, usable for power."
		"&9Heavy Oil:&r richer in &aHeavy Fuel&r, which has uses that are more niche."
		"&9Raw Oil:&r richer in &aNaphtha&r, the best source of the early-game oil products."
		"&9Natural Gas:&r grants &aRefinery Gas&r with no distillation required."
		"&l&9Salt Water:&r grants &aSodium&r and &aChlorine&r, useful later."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lWhat you can find in the &cNether&r&l:&r"
		""
		"&9Natural Gas:&r grants &aRefinery Gas&r but with higher yield than the Overworld vein."
		"&9Lava:&r hopefully, you know what this is."
		""
		"When starting out, you may have to tap randomly until you find something you like. Remember that whatever you pump could also be used to refuel your Fluid Rig."
	]
	quest.05ADBAE5B6F38956.quest_subtitle: "Fluid Drilling Rigs in CEu!"
	quest.05ADBAE5B6F38956.title: "Fluid Drilling Rigs"
	quest.05D97F244E928ACE.quest_desc: ["Reveals even more enchanting clues."]
	quest.0611E32BAF6B62D2.quest_desc: ["A very high level hammer made of the metal of an ancient society pushed into the nether."]
	quest.0611E32BAF6B62D2.title: "Netherite Hammer: Tier VI"
	quest.063AE635AD0E0B31.quest_desc: ["The Adze is a shovel/axe combo that gives the advantages of both tools at a decreased speed due to its weight."]
	quest.06422AB7B816826E.quest_desc: ["When a Butt is added to a tool as a head it will increase the swing speed of the tool due to the decreased weight."]
	quest.069FD86133D7D582.quest_desc: [
		"&aRTM Alloy Coils&r raise the Heat Capacity to a scorching &d4,500K&r."
		""
		"These will be required in &9IV&r, but as always, you should get them earlier for the &6Coil bonuses&r."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o These coils used to be Tungstensteel Coils. This however made most of the EV tier very easy to skip over and postpone to IV, so they were changed to the new RTM Alloy. GTNH was the first to make this change, and used TPV Alloy instead, made from Titanium, Platinum, and Vanadium."
		""
		"&o&7Which coil do you prefer?"
	]
	quest.069FD86133D7D582.quest_subtitle: "What happened to my Tungstensteel!?"
	quest.069FD86133D7D582.title: "RTM Alloy Coils"
	quest.06AE5AE758D86117.quest_desc: ["Око, находящееся под защитой разбойников."]
	quest.06B4AAC7DD796182.quest_desc: [
		"&aUranium&r has very few uses in &2GTCEu&r right now, as we're &4yet to&r implement our &3Nuclear Reactor&r (it's planned!)."
		""
		"Make &dUranium Hexafluoride&r from &aUraninite&r. This will allow you to seperate the isotopes between U-238 and U-235."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Fluorine&r is fully recycled in the reaction, but you will need around maybe 40 buckets to bootstrap."
		""
		"&9Hydrogen&r is consumed, so you will need quite a lot of it. Either electrolyze a lot of water using several &3LV Electrolyzers&r for the best energy efficiency, or recycle any unused &dhydrocarbons&r such as Methane."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r You can make this setup compact by having one single &3Centrifuge&r and using a &6Fluid Regulator&r set to &dSupply Exact 1,000&r."
	]
	quest.06B4AAC7DD796182.quest_subtitle: "Let's hope this quest doesn't put you on a list"
	quest.06B4AAC7DD796182.title: "Uranium Refinement"
	quest.06ECAECBEAA0A9F8.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.06F6E4262BDCB21D.quest_desc: ["Доспех Героя, сразившего Тёмного Лорда в жестокой битве. После этого силы тьмы отступили обратно в Бездну и больше не предпринимали попыток нападения. Этот доспех впитал в себя сущность того героя и наделяет владельца силой и регенерацией."]
	quest.06FCFD49B9DC5C59.quest_desc: [
		""
		"- Any animals you slay using a Knife are guaranteed to drop secondary items, such as Leather and Feathers;"
		""
		"- Grassy plants (grass, wheat, rice etc) cut with a Knife will occasionally yield Straw, a firm and useful fiber;"
		""
		"- They act as a modest melee weapon: swings faster than a sword for lesser damage;"
		""
		"- Later on, they are also useful for cutting and portioning ingredients when preparing meals."
	]
	quest.06FCFD49B9DC5C59.quest_subtitle: "Knives are scavenging tools: they allow you to obtain a few more resources from both fauna and flora."
	quest.06FCFD49B9DC5C59.title: "Any Knife"
	quest.07137122925727C8.quest_desc: ["Double Headed tools make up the large majority of tools in the game. The surrounding quests will describe the individual tool heads that define tools."]
	quest.07137122925727C8.quest_subtitle: "Place a vanilla tool such as a pickaxe, an axe or a hoe in a workbench and upgrade it"
	quest.07159FCD9744DD98.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Active Transformer&r has a second use - &6Laser Power&r. Lasers are like superconductors, but behave slightly differently. They share the energy input across all connected active transformers, allowing widespread power distribution. You can use &3Active Transformers&r to convert regular EU to and from Lasers."
		""
		"Like optical cables, they can only be connected to &eone input and output&r. But, these ones also only can move in &estraight lines&r. To turn them, an &3Active Transformer&r with a Laser Source Hatch (output) and Target Hatch (input) is needed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This is yet again another TecTech feature, but there's a bit more to it this time. TecTech's lasers were tiered by voltage and carried thousands of amps instead. CEu doesn't faff around with any of that tiering. You only need one type of laser here!"
	]
	quest.07159FCD9744DD98.quest_subtitle: "Time for some lasers!"
	quest.07159FCD9744DD98.title: "Laser Power Transmission"
	quest.071DA7912CF9E83A.quest_desc: ["Одолейте &dпустотного червя&r и заполучите древние артефакты, что были в нём запечатаны."]
	quest.0735DAEAD7C90AD7.quest_desc: ["Ох уж эти чайники..."]
	quest.0735DAEAD7C90AD7.title: "Варка чая"
	quest.073B8A584CDFD3AA.title: "Flamberge Blade"
	quest.07415D6305C3B1D2.quest_desc: ["The Steam Compressor unlocks some tantalising new recipes that will help you to progress towards Steel."]
	quest.07415D6305C3B1D2.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Compressor compresses..."
	quest.07415D6305C3B1D2.title: "Steam Compressor"
	quest.0764CCDD7FEBC4DA.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &cморской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.0764CCDD7FEBC4DA.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасная"
	quest.0764CCDD7FEBC4DA.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.0774EC59CD3DD7A5.quest_desc: [
		"Get any kind of &3Pump&r, place it above an Oil spout and... give it some power."
		""
		"Do &cnot&r pump above an Ocean, as the pump will attempt to pull water, resulting in getting the pump stuck. Sorry!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each Oil deposit can have between &63,000&r and &69,200&r buckets of Oil, which is a LOT! Refining the Oil&r onsite into either &aLight Fuel&r or &aDiesel&r (or both) is perfectly viable. The next few Quests will explain each type's pros and cons."
		""
		"Store any obtained Oil in &3Drums&r, but you would do yourself a favour to use a &3Super Tank&r as soon as you can make them."
		""
		"&cWarning: &rDo not forget to &dchunkload&r with FTB Utilities (open the map in the top left corner, claim the chunks with left-click, and enable force loading with shift-left-click)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&lNote:&r&l The Oil path is one path towards &9&lEthylene&r&l. The other paths involve getting natural with some Ethanol.&r"
		""
		"For now, Oil is &doptional&r. It becomes mandatory much later when you get to &5EV&r."
		""
		"Oil can also be refined in the form of &aLight Fuel&r, &aDiesel&r or even &aGasoline&r, which are excellent power options."
		""
		"If you chose this path, you should use it for both Power and Ethylene."
		""
		"Oil spouts are a &6great starting point&r - they will tide you over until you unlock Fluid Drilling Rigs."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Oil geysers were originally from Buildcraft. If you played a GregTech 5 modpack &cwithout&f Buildcraft, you needed to use the Fluid Rig and tap randomly to try and get lucky, or wait until &6HV&f, where prospecting for fluids was available."
	]
	quest.0774EC59CD3DD7A5.quest_subtitle: "Ever mined into an Oil deposit?"
	quest.0774EC59CD3DD7A5.title: "US Simulator"
	quest.07876A2F43E796CF.quest_desc: [
		"Создайте костюм &eхимзащиты&r."
		"\"Мы делаем сборку, Джесси\" - Стеф Уайт"
	]
	quest.078CD1E42CDE69D3.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.078CD1E42CDE69D3.title: "Combat gear"
	quest.07906458E1A15683.quest_desc: [
		"This Large Miner is nearly identical to the regular one, except it has a wider range and uses more drilling fluid."
		""
		"It's an optional upgrade - one you might not even need!"
	]
	quest.07906458E1A15683.title: "Multiblock Miner II"
	quest.079442C113D54856.quest_desc: [
		"You may notice that some fluids say they are \"&aAcidic&r\", with &9Sulfuric Acid&r being one of them."
		""
		"This means that many fluid pipes will not be able to transport them safely!"
		""
		"At &bMV&r, the cheapest pipes for acid transportation are probably &aGold&r, with the more expensive &aVanadium Steel&r or &aChrome&r pipes taking second and third place."
		""
		"&aStainless Steel&r or &aPolytetrafluoroethylene&r (try saying that fast) will be valid options once you are in &6HV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You have three options for acid storage at around this point: &dGlass Vials&r, &dGold Drums&r, or &dSuper Tanks&r. Glass Vials are like &9Fluid Cells&r, and are made to store acids. Gold Drums are self-explanatory. Super Tanks will be unlocked after &9Polyethylene&r, and can store any fluid without restriction."
		""
		"&cWARNING:&r Acids in the wrong pipes will cause &cvoiding&r, &cpipe burning&r, and high chance of &cdeath&r! Be careful!"
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The acid transportation and storage mechanics originate from GregTech 6."
	]
	quest.079442C113D54856.quest_subtitle: "...if you don't read this quest."
	quest.079442C113D54856.title: "It will Melt Your Flesh"
	quest.07BD12EA5928548B.quest_desc: ["Тыква, выросшая в аду на песке душ."]
	quest.07BD12EA5928548B.title: "Тыква печали"
	quest.07D6B144C3BAA21B.quest_desc: ["Откройте новую информацию о драконьей стали и кузне в бестиарии, а затем постройте кузню с помощью которой, вы будете ковать &cдраконью сталь&r."]
	quest.07D6B144C3BAA21B.quest_subtitle: "&cСоздание драконьей стали"
	quest.07D6B144C3BAA21B.title: "Драконья кузня"
	quest.07E257D6CEA58227.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &bморской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.07E257D6CEA58227.quest_subtitle: "&bСиняя"
	quest.07E257D6CEA58227.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.07E7678095258EDB.quest_desc: [
		"The Lathe is an important machine to help shape metals. Thanks to it, you can turn &6one Ingot into one Rod and 2 small piles of Dust&r, and &6one Bolt into one screw&r. That's twice the material efficiency on those recipes as opposed to crafting by hand. "
		""
		"However the &bMV&r &3Extruder&r has the ability to turn &6one Ingot&r directly into &6two Rods&r alongside its many other functions."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r &oThe GT6 Lathe acts like GTm's lathe, but Bolts lathe into one Screw and 1/72 of a pile of Dust. Disgusting!"
	]
	quest.07E7678095258EDB.quest_subtitle: "The Lathe lathes!"
	quest.07E7678095258EDB.title: "Basic Lathe"
	quest.07F97720F1C7F480.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.082AB255886E73C2.quest_desc: [
		"The first Circuit of the &4Wetware&r line."
		""
		"&6Congrats&r!"
	]
	quest.082AB255886E73C2.quest_subtitle: "Eek, it's alive!"
	quest.082AB255886E73C2.title: "Best LuV Circuits!"
	quest.0833472E1FCFA868.quest_desc: ["The Coke Oven processes coal into coal coke, which burns longer and is needed for steel smelting. Creosote is a byproduct."]
	quest.0833472E1FCFA868.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.0880DEC1118DCC89.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &7самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &7бестиарии&r."]
	quest.0880DEC1118DCC89.quest_subtitle: "&7Серое"
	quest.088FCB5267CB7A89.quest_desc: ["This belt will give random positive potion effects for a short duration. These will vary in strength. "]
	quest.08D4C071292F7B94.quest_desc: ["Adds a significant amount of Eterna, but no other stats. Good for mixing with other bookshelves to reach max Eterna quickly."]
	quest.08F5B42A93472C9D.quest_desc: ["Первые блюда из хоглина."]
	quest.08F5B42A93472C9D.title: "Внутренности хоглина"
	quest.08FC281493BD7368.quest_desc: ["Can be made into a unique sword that cuts through stone."]
	quest.0906EC11E1795CC1.quest_subtitle: "A part designed to share energy between two ME Networks without sharing anything else, also used to craft Fluix ME Glass Cable."
	quest.0906EC11E1795CC1.title: "Sharing Power Between Networks"
	quest.092202DA102742E4.quest_desc: [
		"- Repairing an item will require materials (and appropriate tools) for one of its modules"
		""
		"- Repairing will cycle over all of the item's modules"
		""
		"- Repairing magically unstable modules will cost experience"
		""
		"- Each repair fully restores the durability of the item"
	]
	quest.092202DA102742E4.quest_subtitle: "Modular items can be repaired in a workbench."
	quest.092202DA102742E4.title: "Repairing"
	quest.09405EEC7A1BB001.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.094988E300E44D4F.quest_desc: [
		"RU - Зажги обсидиановый портал"
		""
		"EN - Light the Obsidian Portal"
	]
	quest.0960C894446A786C.quest_desc: [
		"New in the &a1.4 update&r, Dual Hatches will greatly help with automation with Multiblocks."
		""
		"They can contain both &6Fluids and Items simultaneously&r, meaning you can simply connect a &bPattern Provider&r and be off to the races. No more faffing around with P2P or Buffers!"
	]
	quest.0960C894446A786C.quest_subtitle: "Compact and Useful"
	quest.0960C894446A786C.title: "Two Hatches for the Price of One"
	quest.0988B5FB795FF7DA.quest_desc: [
		"The next Board for the &1Quantum&r Circuit line."
		""
		"&9Tips:&r For efficient and fast board production, you should use two &3Large Chemical Reactors&r, both supplied with &6HV&r power or higher (make them both share the same &3Energy Hatch&r):"
		""
		"&9-&r One &3LCR&r should be dedicated to &aIron III Chloride&r. The &dHydrogen&r is loopable, so reproduce &dHydrochloric Acid&r locally - that way, you'd only need to passively input &aIron Dusts&r and &aChlorine&r."
		""
		"&9-&r One &3LCR&r should be making both the &acoated Boards&r and the &aempty Circuit Boards&r to make future &ecrafting requests&r with AE2 extremely easy. Keeping an Input Hatch full of Sulfuric Acid shouldn't be a problem, either."
	]
	quest.0988B5FB795FF7DA.title: "Extreme Circuit Boards"
	quest.09D05DD705B6F75B.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of metal will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from villagers who work metal."
	]
	quest.09EB7C423E9FB87E.quest_desc: ["Mix gasoline and aluminium to make napalm---"]
	quest.09F16718BC2A2AFD.quest_subtitle: "Find a scroll in the world or purchase it from villager"
	quest.0A0931D04AE50D4B.quest_subtitle: "The Vacuum Freezer is what it sounds like, it cools down or freezes solids and liquids in order to make them usable."
	quest.0A0931D04AE50D4B.title: "I hope it's safe to put ice cream in here."
	quest.0A1165C6D1F62C2B.quest_desc: [
		"&3Molecular Assemblers&r can be used to automate Crafting Table recipes, which means you can automate just about anything now."
		""
		"To maximise the number of recipes a single Molecular Assembler can do, make a 3D matrix of Molecular Assemblers and ME Pattern Providers - where each component is surrounded on 6 sides by the other."
		""
		"Using higher-tier materials in crafting will yield more Molecular Assemblers."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cWarning:&r Try to avoid using GT tools in AE2 autocrafting! It causes AE2 to freak out... you may or may not destroy the TPS, or even worse, end up having thousands of tools being crafted as soon as one of them breaks."
		""
		"If you're stubborn enough to &oreally&r want to use GT tools in AE2 autocrafting, prioritise encoding recipes that use tools with high durability, but &4do not&r setup autocrafting for the tools themselves. Instead, use the alternate &3Assembling Machine&r recipes."
	]
	quest.0A1165C6D1F62C2B.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting at last!"
	quest.0A1165C6D1F62C2B.title: "Autocrafting"
	quest.0A1ABE9CF7740AAA.quest_desc: ["The Ring of Discount provides a small bonus to max mana and mana regen. It also reduces the total cost to cast a spell."]
	quest.0A486A5299753835.quest_desc: ["The first ME system will be from the Create mod. You can use it for auto-crafting or simply to store resources. Later, you will get an advanced ME system from AE2.  "]
	quest.0A486A5299753835.title: "First ME System"
	quest.0A64F8E4E9674C59.quest_desc: ["Батона больше нет с нами."]
	quest.0A64F8E4E9674C59.title: "Простая выпечка"
	quest.0A884622985A7417.quest_desc: [
		"The Advanced Quantum Chestplate combines protection, a personal battery and an &6ultimate Jetpack&r into a single powerful piece of gear."
		""
		"Note that this stores &oa lot&r of energy. You may want to invest in an &3LuV Turbo Charger&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This armor piece is inspired by the IndustrialCraft  Addon Gravisuite, which added the Gravitation Suit, analogous to this chestplate."
	]
	quest.0A884622985A7417.quest_subtitle: "I'll be seeing you in the skies!"
	quest.0A884622985A7417.title: "Best Flight!"
	quest.0AC80D084DE48B42.title: "Crucible Blade"
	quest.0ACC0092A8F722C6.title: "Wire"
	quest.0AFADD21454D968E.quest_desc: [
		"This Nether Limonite vein variant isn't to be slept on."
		""
		"Thanks to the &adoubled yield&r of Nether ores, this is an excellent source of Iron and Gold."
	]
	quest.0AFADD21454D968E.quest_subtitle: "Source of Iron, Gold"
	quest.0AFADD21454D968E.title: "Limonite"
	quest.0B07F044C4AD8C6A.quest_subtitle: "Used in the creation of Engineering Processors in an Inscriber."
	quest.0B25A282F677744B.quest_desc: [
		"Tungsten in Swedish translates directly as \"Heavy Stone\", which is pretty funny. You may know of this element as Wolfram too, hence its formula being W."
		""
		"&aTungsten&r will be the main &1IV&r Cable material, but will also show its face elsewhere!"
	]
	quest.0B25A282F677744B.quest_subtitle: "Wolfram Alpha"
	quest.0B25A282F677744B.title: "Tungsten"
	quest.0B27217B40C19911.quest_subtitle: "Connects the WAT to the network."
	quest.0B48D7E64E78E9A4.quest_desc: ["Although the explosion isn't that big.... it does start a fire...."]
	quest.0B48D7E64E78E9A4.quest_subtitle: "Kaboom?"
	quest.0B4A3C28EDB2F73D.title: "Piglin Ruin"
	quest.0B4BA438FE7F3640.quest_desc: [
		"A source of Bauxite for your first ever Titanium."
		""
		"Kyanite and Mica decompose into some desirable products if you electrolyze them, but there are definitely better options, so you shouldn't hunt them down if you want their byproducts."
		""
		"&8(This vein probably irks your average GTNH player...)&r"
	]
	quest.0B4BA438FE7F3640.quest_subtitle: "Source of Aluminium, Fluorine, Titanium"
	quest.0B4BA438FE7F3640.title: "Mica"
	quest.0B537911C795E4B6.quest_desc: ["Предметы, которые облегчат ваше пребывание в пещерах."]
	quest.0B537911C795E4B6.title: "Пещерные механизмы"
	quest.0BAB52BE15CE157F.quest_desc: [
		"Steam machines need steam to function, and that's exactly what the boiler provides. It will slowly use fuel to heat up. When it's hot enough, it will start to produce steam. Don't forget to feed it with water or your fuel will burn for nothing."
		""
		"You can also smelt water buckets into steam buckets. Make your first Bronze Compressor before the boiler to save a lot on the plates!"
		""
		"It probably looks expensive to you right now, but don't forget that you can triple ores with the Forge Hammer. Also, as soon as you will have your first two machines, it will become more than twice less expensive!"
		""
		"The boiler will automatically produce and send steam to adjacent machines, up to 8 millibuckets per tick."
		""
		"Bronze machines can only process recipes up to 2 EU/t, meaning that the recipe will use 2 Energy Units per Tick. As 1 millibucket of steam = 1 EU, a boiler at max temperature can power 4 machines simultaneously!"
	]
	quest.0BAB52BE15CE157F.quest_subtitle: "Oh, That's Hot! Remember that the boiler is an advanced machinery that is able to power several machines at once and saves fuel efficiently. Don't forget to give it water or else the fuel wastes burning to ashes."
	quest.0BAB52BE15CE157F.title: "Full Steam Ahead!"
	quest.0BADFBA6F96E457E.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Network Switch&r allows multiple HPCAs to be used in conjunction with each other! This allows you to provide far more computation to your &aResearch Station&r."
		""
		"HPCAs can be connected to &3Network Switches&r with transmission and reception hatches, and then the Network Switch can output to a &aResearch Station&r with another transmission hatch."
		""
		"HPCAs cannot connect to &3Network Switches&r by default, and each connected HPCA requires an &3HPCA Bridge Component&r to enable this functionality."
	]
	quest.0BADFBA6F96E457E.quest_subtitle: "With our powers combined..."
	quest.0BADFBA6F96E457E.title: "Network Switch"
	quest.0BB8D556305EB307.title: "Visit &6Ether River"
	quest.0C09F89291D29EF8.quest_desc: [
		"Similarly to the Steam Multiblocks - hopefully, you made these! - you're going to need some &3Buses&r if you want to move items in and out."
		""
		"For fluids, you'll instead need &3Hatches&r. Higher tiers of &3Hatches/Buses&r have more slots."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r You can Sneak + Right Click a placed &3Hatch&r or &3Bus&r while holding a &2Screwdriver&r (and an empty offhand) to swap its I/O Direction"
	]
	quest.0C09F89291D29EF8.title: "Multiblock I/O"
	quest.0C301014EC4D17B8.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have Steel, you can make a Hang Glider. This might be a good item to grab before you hit up the &cNether&r."
		""
		"If you don't have enough Leather yet, make a &9Butchering Knife&r and employ its inherent Looting III to hunt some cows."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Hang Glider originally came from a mod known as OpenBlocks. As its utility was too great to be left on earlier versions, it was ported all the way up to modern versions."
	]
	quest.0C301014EC4D17B8.quest_subtitle: "No, it's Steve with a glider!"
	quest.0C301014EC4D17B8.title: "Is it a Phantom? Is it an Elytra?"
	quest.0C62F224BC07DCF0.quest_desc: ["Когда-то драконов в мире было намного больше, но рыцари-драконоборцы очень сильно сократили их популяцию. Теперь найти настоящего древнего дракона - большая редкость. Эта тяжёлая древняя броня,, принадлежавшая когда-то одному из сильнейших драконоборцев, впитала в себя силу поверженных драконов. Обеспечивает огромную защиту против драконов."]
	quest.0C62F224BC07DCF0.title: "Поножи драконоборца"
	quest.0C690272ED4FB1C3.quest_desc: [
		"The ore generation in &2GregTech&r is very different to vanilla or normal modded Minecraft. All ores generate in &6huge veins&r, which can contain &dhundreds&o&r of ore blocks."
		""
		"GTCEu now features the functionality of &dVisual Prospecting&r natively, which will mark discovered veins on your map. &9Right Click&r an ore block in the vein, or a surface rock to add it to the map. You can toggle the ore vein view in the lower left corner of the fullscreen map."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The full extent of ore generation is explained in the Tips and Tricks tab, but here is what you need to know:"
		""
		"&9-&r Ore veins generate in a &4Grid&r. Every vein is &9spaced by (approximately) 3 chunks&r from one to another in a cardinal direction."
		""
		"&9-&r It's a good practice to make &dWaypoints&r (default &4N&r) for every vein you've found and and to label their type. You may want to come back to the vein several times."
	]
	quest.0C690272ED4FB1C3.quest_subtitle: "More like SNORE generation!"
	quest.0C690272ED4FB1C3.title: "Ore Generation"
	quest.0CC86A5100E1E60B.quest_desc: ["Already has energy when crafted, place next to a polarizer (make sure facing correct way, might have to place around to find it) to start being able to make magnetic ingots."]
	quest.0CFAF0FAF993C3DF.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &bчешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.0CFAF0FAF993C3DF.quest_subtitle: "&bСиний комплект"
	quest.0CFAF0FAF993C3DF.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.0CFE26AD23EA5001.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &dдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.0CFE26AD23EA5001.title: "Инструменты из драконостали"
	quest.0D040E301EEAE02D.quest_desc: ["Вы начинаете свой путь пекаря."]
	quest.0D040E301EEAE02D.title: "Начинающий пекарь"
	quest.0D10B5E838DF9196.quest_subtitle: "It's a regular coal's twin sibling, nothing different from each other, but handy at least."
	quest.0D10B5E838DF9196.title: "Coal's Twin"
	quest.0D212038C0A45E0B.title: "Cartridge"
	quest.0D330FAD6C993DBC.quest_desc: [
		"This is the next upgrade to your Spellbook!"
		""
		"This will increase your overall mana and mana regen, as well as unlocking the ability to create and use Tier 2 Glyphs."
	]
	quest.0D3B74E82F1CFE8A.quest_desc: [
		"&aHighly Advanced SoC&rs will make crafting &4wetware circuits&r much easier."
		""
		"The drawback is that the recipe requires UV power, but that's no problem to you, right?"
	]
	quest.0D3B74E82F1CFE8A.quest_subtitle: "Can we get much higher?"
	quest.0D3B74E82F1CFE8A.title: "Highly Advanced SoCs"
	quest.0D678122867D6889.quest_subtitle: "Elytra which allows you to boost without rockets."
	quest.0D678122867D6889.title: "Craft the &6Soul Elytra"
	quest.0D69186F8138A0C9.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of gemstones will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from mason villagers."
	]
	quest.0D7C978F9CDF771B.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLuV Lapotronic Orb&r is even better than the &1IV&r one! Of course, such power comes at a steep cost..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In older versions of GT, such as GTNH in the past or in GCYL, these orbs were ludicrously expensive! They required 8 orbs of the previous tier! Thankfully, those days are long past."
	]
	quest.0D7C978F9CDF771B.quest_subtitle: "Even more power!"
	quest.0D7C978F9CDF771B.title: "Ludicrous Batteries"
	quest.0D8988AF02D890EA.title: "Find ancient battleground"
	quest.0D9DFC48E3D2F434.quest_subtitle: "Energy Dischargers drain energy away from charged machinery and store it in an internal storage pocket and can redirect the power into another piece of machinery using cables."
	quest.0DAD0A6360448B39.quest_desc: [
		"A fancy tool to help with base building. The gadget has different modes that you can view by holding the relevant hotkey - it defaults to &eG&r."
		""
		"Be sure to check out the &3Destruction Gadget&r and the &3Copy Paste Gadget&r."
		""
		"You &6should&r be able to charge this in the charger slot of any &bGregTech machine&r, but unfortunately, this is currently &cbugged&r. Have a look at the &dTurbo Charger&r quest in the top-right of this page if you want to charge this."
	]
	quest.0DAD0A6360448B39.quest_subtitle: "A familiar face in the land of Greg"
	quest.0DBA2118C58A9676.quest_desc: ["The Mechanical Press is used to create sheets from ingots and compact items in basins. It requires rotational power to operate."]
	quest.0DBA2118C58A9676.title: "Mechanical Press"
	quest.0DBC148D92A9F69F.quest_desc: [
		"Well... gotten any Aluminium Ingots yet?"
		""
		"Each Electric Age has Circuits corresponding to its tier. The Good Electronic Circuit is the &dfirst MV Circuit&r you can make out of the three tiers of &bMV&r Circuitry."
		""
		"Always be on the lookout for a cheaper way to make your circuits - new sets of recipes become available each time you make a new tier of &2Circuit Assembler&r. Conveniently, this tier of Circuit unlocks one now! Its recipes are far, far cheaper than hand-crafting Circuits."
		""
		"&6Having this and Aluminium will grant access to MV Machines.&r"
	]
	quest.0DBC148D92A9F69F.quest_subtitle: "Does that mean we're at MV yet?"
	quest.0DBC148D92A9F69F.title: "First MV Circuit!"
	quest.0DC999F79A685194.quest_desc: [
		"&aTrinium&r is a very important material for progression. You'll need it to make a &9Fusion Reactor&r, but it stays relevant all throughout &cZPM&r. We &7(well, this particular questbook writer!)&r can never have enough of this stuff."
		""
		"It also requires an &dLuV&r EBF to smelt! Perhaps dedicate a setup solely for cooking this, unless you're confident that your infrastructure can deal with it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In Stargate, Trinium was strong enough to block a point-blank C4 explosion. It's considered to be a hundred times stronger than steel, at only one-hundreth the weight."
	]
	quest.0DC999F79A685194.quest_subtitle: "Another Stargate material!"
	quest.0DC999F79A685194.title: "Trinium"
	quest.0DD703B94D202B68.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.0DD703B94D202B68.quest_subtitle: "The Bronze Pump is good at inserting water into your machinery that requires water, especially boilers. Make sure they're near a water source in order for this to work automatically!"
	quest.0DD703B94D202B68.title: "Pump Your Pistons!"
	quest.0DE5C3FBC9A6A690.quest_desc: [
		"As is common for every tier, the &3Circuit Assembler&r is an essential part of progression, always opening up a new Tier of circuits."
		""
		"At this point you should be placing an &3Extractor&r next to your Circuit Assembler. Send off dozens of stacks of &aSoldering Alloy&r Ingots, and you won't have to worry about refilling again."
	]
	quest.0DE5C3FBC9A6A690.quest_subtitle: "Yippee, yahoo"
	quest.0DE5C3FBC9A6A690.title: "Advanced Circuit Assembler"
	quest.0E2AD156E5EF263A.quest_desc: ["Used to inscribe spells on with the Scribe's Table."]
	quest.0E349CAEF1D249B6.title: "Defeat the &6Slider"
	quest.0E36BE756DB549DE.quest_desc: ["The speed controller allows you to precisely set the rotation speed of the output shaft. Useful when your mechanisms require a specific speed to operate."]
	quest.0E36BE756DB549DE.title: "Rotation Speed Controller"
	quest.0E4B5D2FC378DC92.quest_desc: ["Броня рыцарей Легиона Затмения. Когда-то в мире произошла большая война, в которой этот легион сражался за приход вечной ночи. Является довольно лёгким, тем самым не сковывая движений владельца."]
	quest.0E4B5D2FC378DC92.title: "Шлем солдата Затмения"
	quest.0E65A2873121FE90.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &6мирмекса&r."]
	quest.0E72017800A9766C.quest_desc: [
		"Getting into Applied Energistics at this point is possible, but also a little bit involved..."
		""
		"You will need to make quite a few &7LV&r machines, and the &7LV-tier&r recipes for some AE2 items are comparatively expensive without access to more advanced technology."
		""
		"In &7LV&r, you're able to craft:"
		""
		"&6-&r Energy Acceptor"
		""
		"&6-&r ME Terminal"
		""
		"&6-&r 1k ME Storage component"
		""
		"&6-&r ME Chest"
		""
		"&bChannels are disabled&r in this modpack, so feel free to put a few ME Chests with 1k Cells side-by-side to increase your storage capacity! You can use an ME Terminal to access all their contents at the same time."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r This pack includes &5Fluix Crystals&r, but they are generated as a GT material, rather than the default AE2 Fluix Crystals. To get them, put &dFluix Dust&r in the &aAutoclave&r, which is made from &7Certus Quartz Dust&r, &eNether Quartz Dust&o&r and &cRedstone&r in a &aMixer&r. No need to charge the Certus Quartz. It gets... charged in the Mixer... or something like that."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Feel free to use AE2's in-game guide! Alternatively, you could consider:"
		""
		"The official &dApplied Energistics 2&r website: &9https://appliedenergistics.org/guides&r"
		""
		"An &binstructionary video&r made by &aPansmith&r, which covers Applied Energistics 2 on &6Minecraft 1.12.2&r. The fundamentals are still near-identical, however."
		"&9https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u0ouTWgdcXk&r"
	]
	quest.0E72017800A9766C.quest_subtitle: "Time to ditch those chests"
	quest.0E72017800A9766C.title: "The Digital Age? Already!?"
	quest.0E85DC247D5F6CDC.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &bморской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.0E85DC247D5F6CDC.quest_subtitle: "&bБирюзовая"
	quest.0E85DC247D5F6CDC.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.0E9DAD44DD160B4E.quest_desc: ["Растения, уже подготовленные для варки напитков."]
	quest.0E9DAD44DD160B4E.title: "Сушёные растения"
	quest.0EA88FDF0A8CF786.quest_desc: ["The fifth, and final, level of storage upgrade will increase the storage of a drawer block by 32 times."]
	quest.0EAC071414AEC07E.quest_desc: [
		"You can now &3centrifuge&r &aResin&r, which will still give Raw Rubber - but this time alongside &aGlue&r (and the less useful Plantball)."
		""
		"Give yourself a headstart and get on producing Glue. You can use it to make &6cheaper Resistors&r, as well as &6cheaper Circuit Boards&r in the &3Assembling Machine&r (and it is especially useful &oin the near future&r)."
		""
		"&eNote:&r Submit a fluid by having it stored in a &lbucket&r in your inventory. Sorry - it's an FTB Quests quirk."
	]
	quest.0EAC071414AEC07E.quest_subtitle: "Extractor? I hardly knew 'er!"
	quest.0EAC071414AEC07E.title: "Glued"
	quest.0EAF2C5B5EB755C5.quest_desc: [
		"If you're familiar with GregTech, you may be aware of its &cmany nerfs&r to vanilla recipes. &bGTCEu&r doesn't go easy on you - take a look at the crafting recipes for &eBuckets&r or &ePaper&r. However, we'll ease off the insanity in earlygame, and 1 Log will give you 4 Planks. &aRejoice!&r"
		""
		"&o&8\"My adventure starts with some tree punching!? Huh, I thought GregTech was supposed to shake things up a bit...\"&r"
	]
	quest.0EAF2C5B5EB755C5.quest_subtitle: "Begin your playthrough as before"
	quest.0EAF2C5B5EB755C5.title: "The Beginning of it All"
	quest.0ED5CB1120D1BD6E.title: "First spell"
	quest.0EDB1E145CB2D26F.quest_subtitle: "There doesn't seem to be anyone here yet. At least you can use these cool doors."
	quest.0EDB1E145CB2D26F.title: "Make your way to the &f&lFinal Castle."
	quest.0EDC1CB91ADAC3DB.quest_subtitle: "Used alongside an Inscriber and Inscriber Logic Plate to create a Printed Logic Circuit."
	quest.0EFEE489906256AA.quest_desc: ["The Advanced Electrolyzer allows you to decompose &6far more&r Dusts. This will make getting materials such as &aAluminium&r&o a lot&r easier!"]
	quest.0EFEE489906256AA.quest_subtitle: "We made it to MV, and, well..."
	quest.0EFEE489906256AA.title: "Advanced Electrolyser"
	quest.0F192D1F44B9B599.quest_desc: [
		"Getting &aIndium&r requires a lot of &dSulfuric Acid&r, and two different ores: Galena and Sphalerite."
		""
		"&dSulfuric Acid&r can be produced in large scale in the &3Large Chemical Reactor&r, or obtained as a waste from the &9Platinum Group Sludge&r process."
		""
		"In &dLuV&r, the mandatory &9Naquadah chain&r will grant &aIndium&r too, which means this setup will have a limited life."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This is another small chain inherited from GregTech 5. However, this used to yield one tiny Dust instead, which was... interesting."
	]
	quest.0F192D1F44B9B599.quest_subtitle: "Superconductor Supreme"
	quest.0F192D1F44B9B599.title: "Indium"
	quest.0F2A7F519B3C67FB.quest_desc: [
		"Transporting EU is done via direct connection, using &aWires&r or &aCables&r."
		""
		"Wires are the inferior option as they will &celectrocute&r you and &close more energy&r as the electricity travels through the wire, so you want to use insulated Cables. Keep in mind that you can't combine cables into thicker variants, so make sure you insulate the right thickness to avoid any headaches."
		""
		"&cCable loss&r means you will have to stick your Machines close to your Generators, but that will only be a problem in earlygame. If you peek through the quest book, you will eventually be able to obtain &6Superconductors&r, sidestepping this issue!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Keep in mind that GregTech cables suffer from \"cable loss\". Every block of cable that an EU packet travels will decrease its stored EU."
		""
		"For instance, transferring &7LV&r current along 6 cables each with a loss of 5 EU/t will result in the packets arriving at their destination with a meagre 2 EU/t (32 - [6*5]). For this reason, you will want to keep your cables short until you can start to consider better alternatives."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Superconductors&r are special Wires available for each Voltage tier. They don't have any Cable counterpart, but that isn't necessary, as they have absolutely &6zero cable loss&r! They also don't damage you when you touch them. "
		""
		"They are the best choice for wiring at any tier, if not a little expensive in comparison to the other wires."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"GT6-style Cables are &denabled&r. It means that placing Cables will only connect them to the block they were placed against. To open more connections, use your &5Wire Cutter&r on the grid."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2GTCEu&r Cables now have &6native RF support&r! You can plug any RF appliance into an EU source and it will automatically convert. The ratio is &a4 : 1&r (RF : EU). Not that you can produce RF in this pack - but it's a thought if you wanted to make your own!"
	]
	quest.0F539EC8D2361791.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Large Gas Turbine&r may not impress you in &5EV&r, but it can scale to &9better production&r than the base 4096 EU/t, and boasts &9higher efficiency&r than those pesky singleblock generators."
		""
		"Each Large Turbine will require a &aTurbine Rotor&r and a &3Rotor Holder&r. More on the Turbine mechanics in the &lnext&r Quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r This Quest &eonly&r requires the Controller, but obviously you still need all the multiblock parts to construct the Turbine."
		""
		"Turbines &cvoid&r energy if they're unable to output. If you plan on using this with HV power, use a Rotor with close to 100% Power stat."
	]
	quest.0F539EC8D2361791.quest_subtitle: "Gassed Up"
	quest.0F539EC8D2361791.title: "Large Gas Turbine"
	quest.0F7BAC3F5F3CDBDB.quest_desc: ["The first level of storage upgrade will increase the storage of a drawer block by 2 times."]
	quest.0F7CE2BA2A295A4D.quest_desc: [
		"This includes Tungsten, Blastproof Alloy, Beryllium - these materials are very important for nuclear fission - and Diamonds at last!"
		""
		"Hopefully you have learned to check every REI recipe by now, so you should easily find that Blastproof Mixed Ingots and Tungsten Nuggets can be made with a Compressor... until you have your first Implosion Compressor of course!"
	]
	quest.0F7CE2BA2A295A4D.quest_subtitle: "An Implosion Compressor is an interesting machinery that contains explosions inside it. Using Industrial TNT, it is able to compress the most resistant materials."
	quest.0F8F0F7880235BA2.title: "Find &6Soul blacksmith"
	quest.0FCE2D85C99256FB.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.0FEFCC67CC56A958.quest_desc: [
		"Throwing Knife: A schematic that allows you to make small swords that have the ability to be thrown."
		""
		"Howling Blade: A schematic of a sword fuller that when swung creates a gust that can deflect arrows."
		""
		"Sturdy Guard: A schematic that unlocks a long forgotten guard that allows you to block attacks or arrows with proper timing."
	]
	quest.0FEFCC67CC56A958.quest_subtitle: "Can be found in dungeons."
	quest.0FEFCC67CC56A958.title: "Schematics"
	quest.100082345FA03A9B.title: "Defeat a &6Sentry"
	quest.1011551290D3D7EA.quest_desc: [
		"If you're looking for a change of scene, the &5Void Dimension&r is a perfectly empty area for you to build your factory."
		""
		"It wouldn't be unwise to procure some manner of &aflight&r before venturing here - maybe look around and see if this pack has &6any options&r."
	]
	quest.1011551290D3D7EA.quest_subtitle: "Goodbye, cruel Overworld"
	quest.1011551290D3D7EA.title: "Void Dimension Portal"
	quest.10230B3BB466CD28.quest_desc: [
		"Caverns and Chasms добавляет много интересных и полезных вещей, связанных с пещерами."
		"От новых вёдер до мощной брони."
	]
	quest.10230B3BB466CD28.title: "Caverns and Chasms"
	quest.1030A9F4AAC685ED.quest_desc: [
		"&aLiquid Air&r is a great way to get large amounts of &aNitrogen&r and &aOxygen&r at the cost of using more energy than &3LV Centrifuges&r."
		""
		"However, this will also give you both &6Helium&r and &6Argon&r - which are great to boost smelting in the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r."
		""
		"&cNote:&r You will need at least &3HV Input and Output Hatches&r to be able to run this recipe."
	]
	quest.1030A9F4AAC685ED.title: "True Distillation: Air"
	quest.1050ADF1C264EC38.quest_desc: ["&6Древние записи&r, записанные могучими охотниками на драконов были утеряны и разбросаны по всему миру. Ваша задача находить эти записи и востановить &6знания минувших эпох&r."]
	quest.1050ADF1C264EC38.quest_subtitle: "Записи прошлых веков..."
	quest.1050ADF1C264EC38.title: "Древние записи"
	quest.1069BF4C1771A4F6.quest_desc: ["Gemstones deserve to be sifted. In &2earlier stages&r of the game, this is slow and has poor yields, but when overclocked, sifting quickly becomes a great way to &dmaximise&r your gemstone yield."]
	quest.1069BF4C1771A4F6.quest_subtitle: "Great Grey Wolf Sif-ting"
	quest.1069BF4C1771A4F6.title: "Sifting"
	quest.1081BFCAB3F07FFF.title: "Large steam boiler"
	quest.10987A49F647279E.quest_desc: [
		"At the cost of 4x the drilling Power, the &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r gains &616x the output&r in Fluid."
		""
		"The depletion of veins is also halved. This means you will get a total of &632x&r as much Oil (or whatever fluid) from a bedrock fluid vein until depletion!"
		""
		"Even when depleted, you can still use this and be firmly power positive."
		""
		"One single &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r should be enough to supply Power for a base up to &dLuV&r... and possibly beyond!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"As a &9reminder&r, since this last appeared in &bMV&r:"
		""
		"&9-&r &aLight Oil&r can be used for &dLPG&r and &dMethane&r to run in &3Large Gas Turbines&r."
		"&9-&r &aOil&r can be used for &dDiesel&r and &dCetane-Boosted Diesel&r to run in &3Large Combustion Engines&r."
		"&9-&r &aHeavy Oil&r can be used for &dNitrobenzene&r to run in &3Large Gas Turbines&r."
	]
	quest.10987A49F647279E.quest_subtitle: "\"Extreme\" is an apt descriptor"
	quest.10987A49F647279E.title: "Extreme Fluid Drilling"
	quest.10B753CFD971CB80.quest_subtitle: "Ender Cells are energy transferring machinery that is wireless and will transfer power through another Ender Cell using the same channel number. Each Ender Cell must contain an Energy Cell in order to function and store power."
	quest.10DBEF685353A185.quest_desc: ["An infused version of the Hellshelf. To infuse, place the shelf in the enchanting table while you meet the required levels and enchanting stats (seen by clicking the infused hellshelf here, or in JEI). "]
	quest.10ECB471A77F5136.quest_desc: [
		"Arguably the second best &7LV&r machine to craft, but we're down if you want to argue otherwise."
		""
		"This unlocks the ability to convert one &6Ingot into one Plate&r, which is a better ratio than the Forge Hammer."
	]
	quest.10ECB471A77F5136.quest_subtitle: "The Bender bends!"
	quest.10ECB471A77F5136.title: "Basic Bender"
	quest.10F09A92D0107DBF.quest_desc: ["Те самые острые крылышки."]
	quest.10F09A92D0107DBF.title: "Острые крылышки"
	quest.10FB27DD3C7BEC2F.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to be less fancy, just call it plastic."
		""
		"For the polymerization process, add &aOxygen&r, which gives better returns than Air, then solidify like you would with Rubber."
		""
		"&aPolyethylene (PE)&r is the key to unlocking &6many new things&r. It's commonly used as &dSheets&r, or in &dFluid&r form."
		""
		"In addition, some recipes are now more efficient! Check out diodes and machine hulls (both &8LV&r and &bMV&r)."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The OreDict and fluid name for Polyethylene in 1.12.2 GTCEu was &bplastic&f, for cross-mod compatibility."
	]
	quest.10FB27DD3C7BEC2F.quest_subtitle: "Baby's first polymer!"
	quest.10FB27DD3C7BEC2F.title: "Polyethylene"
	quest.10FD7C65FC83ADD6.quest_desc: [
		"Yet another &bForge Hammer&r step, but you'll be making &dSand&r renewably. With renewable Sand comes renewable Glass (remember to try using an &9Arc Furnace&r for that sweet &adoubled&r yield!)."
		""
		"Quartz Sand Dust centrifuges into a chanced output of &3Certus Quartz&r Dust."
	]
	quest.10FD7C65FC83ADD6.quest_subtitle: "Two vast and trunkless legs of stone..."
	quest.111649D7E16D869F.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Caster's Wand&r only accepts a single spell, and is inscribed using the Scribe's Table."
		""
		"Wand spells always start with Projectile > Accelerate, and MUST be inscribed with a spell that does not have another method (like touch, self, etc)."
		""
		"This allows you to cast spells beyond the 10 spell cap. If you want to use Break, just inscribe the wand with Break by itself."
	]
	quest.112189FE1A12537A.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"&3Item Collectors&r will pick up items - similar to any kind of &aVacuum Chest&r you may be familiar with from &dother mods&r."
		""
		"Higher tiers of &3Collector&r will increase the &ecollection radius&r over multiple chunks. This can be useful if your farm relies on in-world drops, such as &bSugar Cane&r, or... &7uh, bizarrely,&r &8chicken eggs.&r"
		""
		"&eAny&r Item Collector will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.112189FE1A12537A.quest_subtitle: "Oops, dropped my Pickaxe."
	quest.112189FE1A12537A.title: "Gotta Catch 'Em All"
	quest.1137D2BA7E03D685.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Implosion Compressor&r turns the Dust form of Gems into their Gem form."
		""
		"It's required to get &aEnder Pearls&r."
		""
		"In descending order of efficiency, &4ITNT&r, &cTNT&r, &6Dynamite&r, or &ePowerbarrels&r can be used for the Implosion."
	]
	quest.1137D2BA7E03D685.quest_subtitle: "Controlled GregTech Explosion"
	quest.1137D2BA7E03D685.title: "Implosion Compressor"
	quest.113F3D2E48F62CBB.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3World Accelerator&r... well, accelerates the world. Placing it down and powering it will cause it to tick-accelerate any Tile Entities around it. Using a Screwdriver, you can also toggle it to tick-accelerate random blocks in its area, such as farmland. "
		""
		"Keep in mind that GregTech machines are blacklisted from tick acceleration - this is for the better, as tick-accelerating a GregTech machine can lead to it consuming many Amps at once and nuking your power system."
	]
	quest.113F3D2E48F62CBB.quest_subtitle: "I Have Become Chronos"
	quest.113F3D2E48F62CBB.title: "At The Speed Of Light"
	quest.1141A722D356C088.quest_desc: ["После победы над огненым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &7драконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.1141A722D356C088.quest_subtitle: "Серая"
	quest.115C4226F6473F0C.quest_desc: [
		"Use both of your new machines to turn a material into a Fluid, and solidify it back to a Rotor! This combination makes Rotors far easier to craft - &6four Ingots per Rotor&r, as well."
		""
		"You can also do the same for &6Gears&r and &6Small Gears&r, which will then be superseded when you make a &3MV Extruder&r."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Some metals, like Steel, require higher voltages than &7LV&r for Fluid Extraction, so make sure to keep an eye on the recipe tier in EMI."
	]
	quest.115C4226F6473F0C.quest_subtitle: "Time to end the misery of hand crafting rotors!"
	quest.115C4226F6473F0C.title: "C-C-Combo!"
	quest.116C490ADB7B6AD3.quest_desc: ["Используя железо и &dкровь дракона&r, создайте драконью сталь. А затем изготовьте из неё броню и инструменты."]
	quest.116C490ADB7B6AD3.quest_subtitle: "&dГрозовая драконья сталь"
	quest.11779738F2B152AB.quest_desc: ["Броня рыцарей Легиона Затмения. Когда-то в мире произошла большая война, в которой этот легион сражался за приход вечной ночи. Является довольно лёгким, тем самым не сковывая движений владельца."]
	quest.11779738F2B152AB.title: "Поножи солдата Затмения"
	quest.117926D919A97E73.quest_desc: ["This hatch acts like an infinite water source for multiblocks! It can make some setups much more convenient, and also has effectively infinite throughput, so it doesn't have the limitations of the &9Infinite Water Source Cover&r not being fast enough."]
	quest.117926D919A97E73.quest_subtitle: "Water, water, everywhere!"
	quest.117926D919A97E73.title: "Reservoir Hatch"
	quest.117A4E87379D144F.quest_desc: ["\"DOOMvenik ещё ни разу не проиграл.\""]
	quest.117A4E87379D144F.title: "Печенька"
	quest.117FBB18DEE6F08B.quest_desc: [
		"&aEpoxy&r is the foundation for all future Circuit Boards in the game. Get ready to make a lot of this stuff."
		""
		"&9&lNote:&r This questline is quite complicated, so tackle everything else before trying to make Epoxy. You'll need all the help you can get!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are several ways to obtain the ingredients for &aEpoxy&r."
		""
		"We'll ignore recipes related to Glycerol, as they're never worth it unless modpack devs tweak things around. &mHint hint, if you're making your own pack!&r"
		""
		"Try and use &3Large Chemical Reactors&r to shortcut recipes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&dChlorine&r is only partially recycled, so you'll need a constant supply. Feeding it manually should be sufficient at first."
		""
		"Recipes involving &dSodium Hydroxide&r could be looped by electrolyzing the &9Salt Water&r co-product."
		""
		"Doing this will probably require you to make some Quadruple Pipes, Pump Covers, Fluid Filters... or route everything using AE2."
		""
		"In general, closed loop setups are nice to prevent overproduction or overconsumption, but go for whatever's more fun for you."
	]
	quest.117FBB18DEE6F08B.quest_subtitle: "Prime circuit board material"
	quest.117FBB18DEE6F08B.title: "Epoxy"
	quest.11933C553C2A43A2.quest_desc: [
		"&6-&r Чтобы растить ручного дракона, вам понадобятся такие вещи как: посох управления драконом&r, горн дракона&r, флейта дракона&r и пища для дракона&r."
		""
		"&6-&r Для дракона, вы также сможете создать броню. А когда его рост дойдёт до третьей стадии, вы сможете на нём летать, а также создавать драконью сталь."
	]
	quest.11989C3388C969DF.quest_desc: [
		"If you're a builder, &bweep no more&r - this custom multiblock, freshly made with the powers of &dKubeJS&r, is made for you."
		""
		"By providing the multiblock with a near-negligible amount of &6Construction Foam&r, you'll gain access to increased yields of many different &bbuilding blocks&r to spice up your base."
		""
		"Don't go too crazy!"
		""
		"&8(Crazy? I was crazy once!)&r"
	]
	quest.11989C3388C969DF.quest_subtitle: "If you build it, they will come"
	quest.11989C3388C969DF.title: "Building Resources"
	quest.11993B6B46751D32.quest_desc: ["Доспех очень богатых жителей северных регионов. Выполнен на манер доспехов викингов. Обеспечивает хорошую защиту, но не замедляет владельца."]
	quest.11993B6B46751D32.title: "Нагрудник Золотого рога"
	quest.11D226CF2A5A318C.quest_subtitle: "Place a chtonic extractor on a bedrock and hit the top with a hammer"
	quest.11D3B21A177B0E14.quest_desc: [
		"&dLuV&r Components are significantly more difficult to produce than their predecessors. They require an &9Assembly Line&r, many different forms of materials, and lots of fluids too!"
		""
		"You will notice that &9Samarium&r is required for &aLuV+ Motors&r. Samarium by itself isn't very difficult to obtain, but smelting it is slightly more involved. It requires &9Liquid Helium&r in the Freezer. If you made &9IV Superconductors&r, you've likely seen this already."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In the original GregTech 5, these components were unobtainable! You'd be free from GT if you were at this point! How times change."
	]
	quest.11D3B21A177B0E14.quest_subtitle: "Fun levels - critical"
	quest.11D3B21A177B0E14.title: "Pure Joy"
	quest.11D5BE8E6709CF73.title: "Toolboxes"
	quest.11FD440CD0A9DA5C.quest_desc: ["Create an armour made of incredibly durable and beautiful naga scales. This armour will be very useful in the first stages of the game!"]
	quest.11FD440CD0A9DA5C.title: "Naga's armour"
	quest.12344C141B7E1FEB.quest_desc: ["More chaotic, higher potential."]
	quest.124B32A0583A636A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Chemical Bath&r is used to &ddye Lenses&r using &aChemical Dye&r. This will let you engrave more types of Wafers!"
		""
		"This is also required for &aEyes of Ender&r."
	]
	quest.124B32A0583A636A.quest_subtitle: "Please don't bathe with electronics..."
	quest.124B32A0583A636A.title: "High Voltage Bathing"
	quest.1283B4D7B5D82193.quest_desc: [
		"In this &blightweight&r modpack, we've included enough QoL to &o(hopefully)&r fit your needs, and the pack is &aperfectly playable&r as is."
		""
		"&dStorage Drawers&r and &dApplied Energistics 2&r make an appearance to help with &estorage&r and &6logistics&r. Their recipes have been modified to fit progression, but you hopefully won't need to play 50 hours to make your first &5Molecular Assembler&r. There are also a few other mods that you may wish to pursue for some &ahelpful QoL&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"But maybe you require... &osomething more&r?"
		""
		"If you're playing solo, feel free to &aadd mods&r to your instance. Some more &bQoL&r could be nice... more &3Tech&r could sate your cravings... maybe even some &5magic mods&r, as long as you don't add &eProjectE&r. Promise?"
		""
		"On the 1.12.2 version of &aGregtech: CEu&r, there were multiple &aGregTech&r addons that may be ported to 1.20.1 in future. Rest assured that this pack will do its &dbest&r to support them if they make it to this version!"
	]
	quest.1283B4D7B5D82193.quest_subtitle: "Omw to install DecoCraft"
	quest.1283B4D7B5D82193.title: "More mods?"
	quest.128677882E7DA170.quest_desc: ["Обьедените древние артефакты, чтобы заполучить могущественную реликвию - &dРезак Пространства&r. Он может копать само пространство!"]
	quest.1286F9F4255B9A38.quest_desc: [
		"Tunnels are 1 input to N outputs. This means you can output to as many points as you want, but only input at a single point per tunnel."
		""
		"Networks can support any number of tunnels, of any different types, and they all function independently."
		""
		"ME Tunnels can be used to carry channels from one location to another, and can carry up to 32 channels, same as a Fluix ME Dense Covered Cable, while only requiring a single channel per point, making tunnels a very powerful tool to expand me networks, especially over a distance."
		""
		"The channel required by a P2P-Tunnel cannot be carried through another P2P-Tunnel."
		""
		"To configure a ME P2P Tunnel you must first attune the tunnel to carry what you want it to, then you need to configure the outputs to their input."
		""
		"You configure the connections by using the Memory Card; First Shift+Right Click the input to save it on your memory card, then simply right-click the different outputs to store the input onto the outputs."
	]
	quest.1286F9F4255B9A38.quest_subtitle: "A versatile configurable system to move items / redstone / power / and fluids from one location to another though an existing ME Network without storage."
	quest.128F63D7FF97635A.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.12B4423F055BFBF5.quest_desc: [
		"&aLaminated Glass&r is the shiny new tier of Glass for &9IV&r and above. It's made in the &3Forming Press&r using a polymer you won't be familiar with: &dPolyvinyl Butyral&r."
		""
		"None of the steps should be particularly difficult if you already have the &3Distillation Tower&r for Cracked Fuels, and you have also automated Epoxy."
		""
		"If you don't already have both set up, you know what to do!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r &dPolyvinyl Acetate&r (required for the Glass) can also be used for &aGlue&r!"
	]
	quest.12B4423F055BFBF5.quest_subtitle: "Another Polymer Rises From The Darkness"
	quest.12B4423F055BFBF5.title: "Laminated Glass"
	quest.12C40FEBB4BD40CE.quest_desc: ["Древняя технология, позволяющая бесконечно плавать под водой."]
	quest.12CA2605B7A13566.quest_desc: ["После победы над грозовым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &1драконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.12CA2605B7A13566.quest_subtitle: "&1Электрическая"
	quest.12CAEA99C1F2148D.quest_subtitle: "Used in the creation of all Processors."
	quest.12D605F59A3176A2.quest_subtitle: "Find ancient ruins deep down in cold or mountainous biomes"
	quest.12DF2E5269BE87D5.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3Block Breaker&r... well, we'll &dleave it to you&r to figure out what this one does. There are likely some &anifty farms&r you can create with clever usage of this machine - especially with the &6many vanilla mechanics&r introduced between 1.12.2 and 1.20.1!"
		""
		"Higher tiers of &3Block Breaker&r come with an additional speed bonus."
		""
		"&eAny&r Block Breaker will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.12DF2E5269BE87D5.quest_subtitle: "I've had it with these blocks!"
	quest.12DF2E5269BE87D5.title: "Break the Targets!"
	quest.12FEE0A47E4658D5.quest_desc: ["A requirement for &dLuV&r+ cables."]
	quest.12FEE0A47E4658D5.quest_subtitle: "Cables need better coating now"
	quest.12FEE0A47E4658D5.title: "Polyphenylene Sulfide"
	quest.13354F24F80F65FB.quest_desc: [
		"Were you aware that &aGregTech&r comes with its own set of tools? If not, you may also be pleasantly surprised to hear that they &6&lsurpass&r their vanilla equivalents."
		""
		"Let's use the GregTech Axe as an example. If you use one to mine a log in a tree, it'll fell the &2entire tree&r for you. Timber!"
		""
		"Constant \"lumberjacking\" will eat through your Axe's &9durability&r in seconds, so you may want to make your Axe out of a &estronger material&r such as &bDiamond&r. Just be careful you don't make a vanilla Diamond Axe."
		""
		"As a reward, take these &2Spruce saplings&r and use them to make some big trees. You'll need to do a lot of smelting in the near future, and planks will tide you over as an &deffective&r fuel source!"
	]
	quest.13354F24F80F65FB.quest_subtitle: "Who needs Veinminer?"
	quest.13354F24F80F65FB.title: "Lumbering On"
	quest.1366981BD8CD98E1.quest_desc: [
		"&aRotors&r have a &9Power&r, &dEfficiency&r and &4Durability&r that are based on tool stats."
		""
		"&9Power&r is a multiplier applied to the production of the &3Turbine&r. This stacks multiplicatively with the &3Rotor Holder&r."
		""
		"&dEfficiency&r reduces its fuel consumption. This again stacks multiplicatively with the &3Rotor Holder&r."
		""
		"&4Durability&r is the lifetime of the &aRotor&r in seconds, when the &3Turbine&r&r is active."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&3Rotor Holders&r above the tier of the &3Large Turbine&r will multiplicatively &6double&r the production for every tier, whilst additively increasing the efficiency by 10% every tier."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lSome pros of Large Turbines:"
		""
		"&9-&r Turbines can scale &9Power&r production far, far higher than their base output, thanks to tiered &3Rotor Holders&r."
		""
		"&9-&r The &aRotor&r can give a huge boost to &dFuel efficiency&r and &9Power&r production."
		""
		"&9-&r You get a lot of satisfaction for setting them up properly (yay!)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l...and some cons of Large Turbines:"
		""
		"&9-&r Turbines work off &eInertia&r, which requires them to continuously run to achieve maximum Power."
		""
		"&9-&r Any excess Energy produced will be &cvoided&r. You will &lneed&r to use large Energy Buffers and an &3Advanced Energy Detector&r if you wish to stay efficient."
		""
		"&9-&r They require a &aRotor&r, which will lose durability over time and eventually &cbreak&r."
		""
		"&9-&r A little bit of Math is required to get the expected results."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A Turbine's &9Power&r output affects both the fuel consumption and the EU/t generation. It is calculated with the following formula:"
		""
		"&eproduction = baseEUt x rotorPower x 2^(rotorHolderTier - turbineTier)&r"
		""
		"The &dEfficiency&r reduces fuel consumption, but does not alter the EU/t generation. It is calculated with the following formula:"
		""
		"&eefficiency = rotorEfficiency x (1 + 0.1 x (rotorHolderTier - turbineTier))&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let's simulate a Large Steam Turbine, with an Ultimet Rotor and an &5EV&r Rotor Holder:"
		""
		"Production = 1024 x 1.60 x 2 = 3276 EU/t"
		""
		"Efficiency = 1.30 x 1.10 = 143%"
		""
		"(Therefore, steam consumption would be 4582 L/t - this is above a Titanium Boiler, or a Tungstensteel Boiler with ~70% throttle)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next, we'll analyse the Gas Turbine, with a Chrome Rotor and an &5EV&r Rotor Holder:"
		""
		"Production = 4096 x 1.70 x 1 = 5325 EU/t"
		""
		"Efficiency = 1.55 x 1.00 = 155%"
		""
		"(The same fuel consumption would produce 3435 EU/t using 6.7 Turbo Gas Turbines!)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Finally, how about we check out the Plasma Turbine, with a HSS-S Rotor and a &cZPM&r Rotor Holder:"
		""
		"Production = 16834 x 2.50 x 4 = 168340 EU/t"
		""
		"Efficiency = 1.80 x 1.20 = 216%"
		""
		"(This is more than a ZPM Amp!)"
	]
	quest.1373526C3FFC6CAA.quest_desc: ["Hope you have some raw iron you didn't smelt yet."]
	quest.1373526C3FFC6CAA.title: "Crushed Raw Iron"
	quest.13887C73B47C0467.quest_desc: ["The Mechanical Arm can move items between inventories within its range. It can be programmed for complex movement paths."]
	quest.13887C73B47C0467.title: "Mechanical Arm"
	quest.13901DA3D4F5C5A6.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPrimitive Water Pump&r is an easy way to automatically generate water for your boilers. It doesn't physically pump water from the world, instead generating it &einternally&r. Therefore, you don't need access to a &3body of water&r to make use of it. However, the humidity of the biome does apply a negligible bonus to its water production."
		""
		"It's a multiblock, so &5consult EMI&r for the structure. Multiblocks can be previewed in-world if you sneak right-click the \"&a&ocontroller&r\" block with an empty hand (in this case, the controller block is the &bPrimitive Water Pump&r itself)."
		""
		"&6Small tip for you:&r no need to worry about your base's biome for now, as your boilers will need very little water to keep up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &cOutput Hatch&r is where water will be generated. You can make it face up or down to auto-output water into your pipes, which can go &ethrough&r the Treated Wood Frames - just place the pipe before you encase it in the frames. "
		""
		"Later you can use a &8ULV&r or &7LV&r Output Hatch to further boost the Pump's output."
		""
		"&2Reminder:&r Use a Wrench to rotate GregTech blocks (sneak right-click)."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This Multiblock was ported from GT IMPACT, a classic 1.7.10 GregTech modpack."
	]
	quest.13901DA3D4F5C5A6.quest_subtitle: "There's no such thing as \"free\" water"
	quest.13901DA3D4F5C5A6.title: "Primitive Water Pump"
	quest.13A976D0D612BC84.quest_desc: [
		"This is a guide on how to automatically route &lall&r your Hot Ingots to your Chemical Bath, while keeping everything automated in tip-top shape."
		""
		"The cheap way would be to use filters, and manually add Hot Ingots one by one... which is so boring! Let's try the fun option."
		""
		"Install an &aItem Tag Filter&r Cover on the side of your &3Chemical Bath&r, open it and set it to whitelist \"&e&lhot_ingots&r\"."
		""
		"From here, you can route with &9any logistics system&r of your choice."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Connect the output of your &3EBF(s)&r to the input of your &3Chemical Bath&r and the output dump (Chest or Crate)."
		"You can also have a &dRestrictive Pipe&r in front of the output dump to ensure the Chemical Bath will be prioritized."
		""
		"&l&9Note:&r If you wish to know more tags for more automation setups, they will display if you press Shift when hovering over an item. For instance, an item tagged with &e&o#forge:plates/copper&r would be filtered as &e&lplates/copper&r."
		""
		"&9Other Note:&r The Item Tag Filter partially supports &dregex&r. Hover over the info icon for more information."
	]
	quest.13A976D0D612BC84.quest_subtitle: "Stop burning your darn hands!"
	quest.13A976D0D612BC84.title: "250IQ"
	quest.13B5E4EF97D6308F.quest_subtitle: "Dielectric Paste is an ingredient used to glue and craft electric parts used in the machinery, you should prepare a lot if you plan on upgrading."
	quest.13B5E4EF97D6308F.title: "Electric Glue"
	quest.13D8F6001BE3FC5C.quest_desc: ["The ultimate enchantment storage and combination solution."]
	quest.13E9DF7E980CFC5B.quest_desc: [
		"Be sure to &aproperly&r read &lthis&r quest - it has some &dimportant information&r that will remain relevant all throughout your playthrough."
		""
		"Informative quests such as this will appear in the chapter they are unlocked. You can also consult the &b\"Guides + More\"&r quest tab if you feel like you're forgetting something."
		""
		"The quest structure is intended to guide you through all the major milestones in &aGregTech&r progression. Every single quest should be &2beneficial&r to look at in some way - if something is 100% optional, we'll mention it, so don't worry about missing anything crucial."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are no drawbacks to playing this modpack in &dPeaceful&r - in fact, we highly urge you to do so, as there is little benefit from hostile mobs. Feel free to also to use &o/keepInventory&r, &o/sethome&r, and abuse minimap teleport as you see fit."
		""
		"Although we won't force these settings onto you, we &4don't&r intend for this modpack to provide a punishing &eSurvival&r experience, but more so help you learn the ins and outs of &aGregTech CEu&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Lastly, it's good to be &lsavvy&r with &eEMI.&r &aGregTech&r items will frequently have several recipes, so you should never assume the first recipe &eEMI&r displays is the most efficient. \"Professional\" &eEMI&r usage involves the &bidentification of patterns&r in autogenerated recipes (example: all the Iron related items &6macerate&r into Iron Dust)."
		""
		"When complex recipes arise - and we won't sugarcoat, &aGTCEu&r can be intimidating - we'll make sure to direct you towards the more &5efficient routes&r. However, we urge you to experiment on your own. It's no fun to follow the quest book by rote, right?"
	]
	quest.13E9DF7E980CFC5B.quest_subtitle: "Read this, and read it again!"
	quest.13E9DF7E980CFC5B.title: "Important Information"
	quest.13F072CD438F5D2A.quest_desc: ["Зачем?..."]
	quest.13F072CD438F5D2A.title: "Сборщик духовок"
	quest.13FE27F2483D112C.quest_desc: ["При &eудачном&r изучении этой таблички вы узнаете информацию о первобытных пещерах, изолированных от внешнего мира с древних времён."]
	quest.13FE27F2483D112C.quest_subtitle: "Первобытные пещеры"
	quest.140E91C53C30C096.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &dLuV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"The pattern stays the same: the rightmost circuit comes in &dlarger quantities&r and is overall &aeasier&r to produce."
		""
		"Make sure to set up &3wetware board production&r as soon as possible! These take a &6very long time&r to make."
		""
		"It's &dLuV&r, not &4LUV&r."
	]
	quest.140E91C53C30C096.title: "&dLuV&r Circuits"
	quest.141E4F79A9F63800.quest_desc: ["The basic material for most entry-level Create mechanisms."]
	quest.141E4F79A9F63800.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.1436DB89E21264F3.quest_desc: [
		"Not many items are made in the &3Extractor&r during the &6Steam Age&r, but it's used to make &9Rubber&r, which you'll need after Steel."
		""
		"You can also process Dirt in the Extractor for &aBones&r, which makes getting &aBone Meal&r a lot easier for Peaceful players."
	]
	quest.1436DB89E21264F3.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Extractor extracts..."
	quest.1436DB89E21264F3.title: "Steam Extractor"
	quest.143B1AE1F3CF53EF.quest_desc: [
		"Seasoned sci-fi fans might recognise &2Naquadah&r from the series &dStargate&r! You'll find this becomes an essential material from &dLuV&r onwards."
		""
		"Naquadah can be processed in &dLuV&r for Titanium, Trinium, Barium, Gallium, Indium, Phosphorus, Enriched Naquadah, and Naquadria. Versatile!"
		""
		"Moving the spotlight to the other ore, &cPlutonium&r is used to start the Radon loop, required in &9IV&r."
	]
	quest.143B1AE1F3CF53EF.quest_subtitle: "Source of... a lot."
	quest.143B1AE1F3CF53EF.title: "Naquadah"
	quest.14587AE142D84E12.quest_desc: ["The most consistent source of Lead and Silver."]
	quest.14587AE142D84E12.quest_subtitle: "Source of Lead, Silver"
	quest.14587AE142D84E12.title: "Galena"
	quest.145B60BAC740910A.quest_subtitle: "Used in the creation of Logic Processors in an Inscriber."
	quest.145F71A817C5996E.quest_desc: ["Good news for any mainframe haters out there - &dLuV&r Circuits that aren't mainframes!"]
	quest.145F71A817C5996E.quest_subtitle: "Spread the LuV"
	quest.145F71A817C5996E.title: "More LuV Circuits"
	quest.1478BE654172DB0E.quest_desc: ["The Potion Bag allows you to cary a large amount of potions but of limited variety."]
	quest.1492F3C3FB608067.quest_desc: ["The Booster is a sort of jetpack that uses gunpowder as fuel. Can be activated by crouch jumping, jumping in air, or while flying an elytra."]
	quest.14AAC7075B000B15.quest_subtitle: "A block designed to do one thing, store Storage Cells. This block holds 10 storage cells so you can tightly pack your storage into a very small space."
	quest.14D277A164202FF8.quest_desc: [
		"The first &1IV&r circuit. Congratulations on making it this far!"
		""
		"This will be used when you get to &5EV&r."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The original texture for the Mainframes was taken from an image of an IBM zEnterprise mainframe."
	]
	quest.14D277A164202FF8.quest_subtitle: "Whoah, what a unique... texture"
	quest.14D277A164202FF8.title: "Mainframes - first IV Circuits!"
	quest.14DB8A515CA50932.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Enchanter's Sword&r allows you to attach a Touch Spell to the sword. "
		""
		"All spells on the Sword gain 1 additional Amplify augment to the last effect on the spell."
		""
		"To apply a spell to the sword, use a Scribe's Table. Create the spell without using a form."
	]
	quest.15069CA263BFE7ED.title: "Rending scissors Blade"
	quest.151648179684B088.quest_desc: [
		"Runic Chalk is used to draw permanent Runes on that ground. These runes will cast spells on entities that walk over them."
		""
		"To attach a spell to a rune, inscribe a &eSpell Parchment&r using a Scribe's Table."
		""
		"Note: The Rune will need Source to operate."
	]
	quest.151648179684B088.quest_subtitle: "Placeable Spells"
	quest.15177A2EE609689D.title: "Netherite Armor"
	quest.15358C492A96474A.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of fibre will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from fletcher villagers."
	]
	quest.15645E46CC0E6764.quest_desc: [
		"You now have access to two &3new Maintenance Hatches&r. Both hatches &6do not require Maintenance&r when first placed in a Multiblock. We're going to ask for both here."
		""
		"The &3Automatic Maintenance Hatch&r is pretty simple - it eliminates the need for Maintenance, &6forever&r."
		""
		"The &3Configurable Maintenance Hatch&r is more interesting. You can configure it to cut off &a10% duration&r on recipes, at the cost of making Maintenance happen three times as fast. That's &d16 real hours&r of activity."
		""
		"&9Reminder:&r You can put Tape in the maintenance Hatch to automatically fix problems."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Automatic Maintenance Hatch texture and mechanic comes from TecTech, an addon mod originally made for GregTech: New Horizons. "
		""
		"&oYou'll see more from TecTech if you stick with us all the way to the late game."
	]
	quest.15645E46CC0E6764.quest_subtitle: "Huge News for Maintenance Haters"
	quest.15645E46CC0E6764.title: "Advanced Maintenance"
	quest.156ECC53DB98ED6A.title: "Cane"
	quest.158EA0D37DBD148B.quest_desc: ["Обьедените разные ресурсы, чтобы получить &4теневой шёлк&r и использовать его в создании снаряжения."]
	quest.15923B47D23CCF34.quest_desc: [
		"You DO have access to some beefy &bfluid storage&r right now, but you'll need to make a &eMultiblock&r to access it!"
		""
		"The &3Wooden Multiblock Tank&r&r holds &a250,000 mB&r, but you won't be able to use it to store &chot Fluids&r such as Lava, or &cGases&r such as Steam or Oxygen."
		""
		"The &3Bronze Multiblock Tank&r holds &a500,000 mB&r, lifiting the maximum fluid tempreture and can now store &cGases&r. "
		""
		"The &3Steel Multiblock Tank&r holds &a1,000,000 mB&r, and lifts all the aforementioned fluid restrictions."
		""
		"Get &eany&r of the Tanks to complete this quest. The Steel version is &dway too expensive&r right now - so you should probably make the Wooden  or Bronze one instead."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Fluid transfer can either be facilitated through the Controller block, or through up to &atwo Valves&r."
		""
		"Valves can &9auto-output&r by placing them on the &dbottom layer&r and making them &dface down&r (as always, use a &5Wrench&r to adjust their facing)."
		""
		"Unlike &3Drums&r, these Tanks aren't portable... but you probably guessed that already."
		""
		"This Quest generously rewards an extra &6Coke Oven&r. Make the most of GTCEu's &bwallsharing&r mechanic, and place it next to an existing Coke Oven to save on casings."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Just like Drums, these multiblocks are ported from GregTech 6."
	]
	quest.15923B47D23CCF34.quest_subtitle: "So long, and Tanks for all the fish!"
	quest.15923B47D23CCF34.title: "Multiblock Tanks"
	quest.15928F50AE80A5CF.quest_desc: [
		"The Gas Collector collects Air that can then be centrifuged into &aOxygen&r and &aNitrogen&r."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5 players remember when they had to use a Compressor with IC2 cells to get Compressed Air... here, cell chemistry is no more."
	]
	quest.15928F50AE80A5CF.quest_subtitle: "Time to sell some Air"
	quest.15928F50AE80A5CF.title: "Basic Gas Collector"
	quest.159670F55DD10CD9.quest_desc: ["The Drawer Controller Slave will allow you to extend your storage system when connected to a storage controller. This is more performance friendly than having multiple controllers."]
	quest.159C31FE32578AD2.quest_desc: ["This is the basis for creating the other functional components of the processor CPU."]
	quest.159C31FE32578AD2.quest_subtitle: "This particular block does not provide any additional functionality to the processor, but can be used as a \"filler\" block"
	quest.15A88EE622C1F407.quest_subtitle: "Energizing Rods are a type of machinery that energizes items contained in an energizing orb and transforms them."
	quest.15AEB8885DE3D188.quest_desc: [
		"The first step in making better gear will be by upgrading your hammer to Stone (Tier II)."
		""
		"To upgrade a hammer you will need another hammer to do so, hence the reward from the previous quest."
	]
	quest.15CE1D3E19871988.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.15EC934CE8F4DC86.quest_desc: ["&8ULV&r Circuits are used in some AE2 recipes, such as the &aAnnihilation Core&r and &aFormation Core&r."]
	quest.15EC934CE8F4DC86.quest_subtitle: "Good on you for making these!"
	quest.15EC934CE8F4DC86.title: "Best ULV Circuits!"
	quest.1646BF9194100E57.quest_desc: [
		"Prepare &a128 Cupronickel&r, &a32 Bronze&r and &a16 Tin Alloy&r to craft the Heating Coils required for your first Electric Blast Furnace."
		""
		"This is still less than half (!) of the cost of the whole EBF in raw materials. You will also need about a stack each of Invar and Steel, so get mining."
		""
		"The Cupronickel Coils will allow the EBF to perform recipes up to &d1,800K&r (ignoring Voltage bonuses). That's pretty hot if you ask us."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on Coils in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.1646BF9194100E57.quest_subtitle: "Baby's first heating coil"
	quest.1646BF9194100E57.title: "Cupronickel Coils"
	quest.1647E0C649E2131C.quest_desc: [
		"There are two really important factors to know when building Multiblocks."
		""
		"Check EMI, and remember to keep things versatile."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rule number one - check EMI!"
		""
		"This one was probably obvious, but EMI is so much more than just a cute picture of how the Multiblock looks when built! Use your mouse to &drotate&r the preview, and &9hover over the blocks used&r to view any extra information."
		""
		"The EMI page also contains an ingredient list of required blocks. You can also &dright-click&r a block in the preview to get a display of all blocks that work in that specific position."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rule number two - multiblocks are versatile!"
		""
		"There is no \"definite\" way to form the Multiblock. Most of the time, you have complete freedom over the &9tier of Buses/Hatches&r used - and you also have the ability to&d choose where you want your inputs/outputs&r."
		""
		"Taking the EBF as an example, any tier of Energy/Bus/Hatch can be used, and they can be placed anywhere in place of a casing. Fluid Hatches are also optional, though you probably want them if you need to handle recipes involving fluid."
	]
	quest.1647E0C649E2131C.quest_subtitle: "Multiblock University"
	quest.164DF16E07F16AEE.quest_desc: ["После победы над ледяным драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &bдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.164DF16E07F16AEE.quest_subtitle: "Белая"
	quest.16A1EF8B80A96633.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Sapphire Lens, engrave a Silicon Wafer into an ULPIC Wafer."
		""
		"This can be processed in a Cutter for ULPIC Chips, which are important for some multiblock components!"
	]
	quest.16A1EF8B80A96633.quest_subtitle: "Pickin' up Chips"
	quest.16A1EF8B80A96633.title: "ULPIC Chips"
	quest.16A6AE5C770DB83A.quest_desc: [
		"Any Steel you encounter in day-to-day life is most likely &7Stainless Steel&r. It is extremely resilient against corrosion.&r"
		""
		"Stainless Steel is the material for &6HV&r components, like Aluminium for &bMV&r and Steel for &7LV&r. It is also used in high quantities for the &3Distillation Tower&r."
		""
		"It requires &cChromium&r, obtained mainly from &cRuby&r, and &2Manganese&r, obtained from &2Pyrolusite&r and others in its vein."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Smelting Stainless Steel requires &dHV Power&r, which you likely do not have at this point. Scaling Power Production is crucial."
		""
		"If you &9haven't already&r, it would be a good idea to get a second EBF going. They can share blocks, so that means your second EBF only requires &a10 Cupronickel Coils&r instead of 16."
		""
		"Have one EBF run off &bMV&r for Aluminium and any other recipes requiring &bMV&r Power, and one running off &6HV&r with &32 MV Energy Hatches&r."
	]
	quest.16A6AE5C770DB83A.quest_subtitle: "HV is in your grasp"
	quest.16A6AE5C770DB83A.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.16A8F491189EB1D1.quest_desc: ["Центральный остров &dКрая&r куда ведёт портал в крепости, охраняется &dЭндер-Драконом&r. Могущественным созданием, обладающее огромной силой пустоты."]
	quest.16B735F9C391D260.quest_desc: ["The &3HV Assembling Machine&r is the next step in progression, but also unlocks a handful of useful utilities - snoop around this quest for more."]
	quest.16B735F9C391D260.title: "HV Assembling Machine"
	quest.16C56E551AC17784.quest_desc: ["Выглядят аппетитно."]
	quest.16C56E551AC17784.title: "Кексы"
	quest.16E3465CF94E2BDD.quest_desc: [
		"If you've killed a Blaze before, you may have noticed it dropped &eSulfur Dust&r instead of a &cBlaze Rod&r."
		""
		"In order to get &6Blaze Powder&r, you must instead combine &7Carbon Dust&r and &eSulfur Dust&r in a &3HV Chemical Reactor&r."
	]
	quest.16E3465CF94E2BDD.quest_subtitle: "Took a while to get some of this, right?"
	quest.16E3465CF94E2BDD.title: "Blaze Powder"
	quest.16E7CAC7BC8BFD8E.quest_desc: [
		"Yeah, we admit it... this Multiblock is entirely &doptional&r. Many playtesters kept using their &6HV&r singleblock miners and didn't run into any issues with regards to throughput."
		""
		"However, the &3Large Miner&r will further boost your returns when collecting ores from veins. Ores are mined as if they were &amacerated&r, but they yield &6three times&r as many &dCrushed ores&r."
		""
		"You'll need to automate &aDrilling Fluid&r before you run this. You might also want to use a &3Quantum Tunnel&r from AE2 and &3GTEU P2P Tunnels&r to transfer items and provide power."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o There were some interesting side effects when we ported this over from Gregicality, as the multiblock actually originated from GregTech 5."
		""
		"&oIts current implementation isn't perfect, as you don't really get much of a benefit by upgrading this miner to the advanced versions. We were considering a rebalance of energy consumption and yield per tier."
	]
	quest.16E7CAC7BC8BFD8E.title: "Multiblock Miner"
	quest.16F2592C15C1D037.quest_desc: ["The Steam Engine converts steam energy into powerful rotation. Install it on a boiler to get a huge amount of power for your factory."]
	quest.16F2592C15C1D037.title: "Steam Engine"
	quest.1722389078675E47.quest_desc: ["Будьте осторожны."]
	quest.1722389078675E47.title: "Пороховой бамбук"
	quest.1722813F617DF39B.quest_desc: [
		"The &aPattern P2P Tunnel&r is an upgraded version of &9Item/Fluid P2P Tunnels&r."
		""
		"The input side is placed on an Pattern Provider containing patterns. It can have multiple outputs, which should connect to inventories."
		""
		"When multiple crafts of a single pattern are requested, the P2P Tunnel will evenly distribute the crafts between all of the connected outputs."
		""
		"The Pattern P2P Tunnel also respects &eBlocking Mode&r, which is set in the interface containing the patterns."
	]
	quest.1722813F617DF39B.quest_subtitle: "Pattern 2 Pattern"
	quest.1722813F617DF39B.title: "Pattern P2P Tunnels"
	quest.1729A82B2351DE53.quest_desc: [
		"When any growable plant is placed on Rich Soil, its growth will be randomly boosted, similar to the usage of Bone Meal."
		"Rich Soil can be tilled into Rich Farmland through the use of hoes. Rich Farmland is immune to mob trampling and won't unravel to Melons or Pumpkins, but requires hydration in order to boost crops."
		""
		"Mushrooms planted on Rich Soil under sufficient darkness will eventually form a Mushroom Colony. Such colonies will grow from 2 to 5 mushroom caps over time, dropping them when harvested."
	]
	quest.173C1FA72301B5E7.quest_desc: [
		"&cWarning&r: &9Plasmas&r are &cextremely hot&r, with temperatures exceeding &d30k Kelvin&r! "
		""
		"However, this &6&ldoesn't&r mean that a special type of pipe is required to transport plasma. Plasmas are treated slightly differently, and bend the rules a bit."
		""
		"Fluid pipes that can handle plasmas, such as &aTungsten&r, &aNaquadah&r, or &aDuranium&r can hold any plasma &6regardless of temperature&r. This means they &lwon't&r melt under the heat of the plasma!"
		""
		"WARNING:&r Plasmas in incompatible pipes will cause &cvoiding&r, &cpipe burning&r, and &ldisproportionately high&r rates of &cdeath&r. Be careful!"
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This mechanic originates from GT6, just like the acids!"
	]
	quest.173C1FA72301B5E7.quest_subtitle: "The stars are calling..."
	quest.173C1FA72301B5E7.title: "Fluid of the Stars"
	quest.17742B177BFBE35C.quest_desc: ["The min redstone upgrade will output a redstone signal equivalent to the lowest filled drawer level."]
	quest.1776FA1F3255731E.quest_desc: [
		"&7High-Speed Steels&r (HSS) are resistant Steel alloys typically used in rails."
		""
		"If you previously made &dUltimet&r for whatever reason, you've already acquired &aMolybdenum&r. Otherwise, it can be found in a Nether vein."
		""
		"We hope you have a lot of &9Tungstensteel&r, because you're gonna need more! It's used for the creation of &aHSS&r alloys - in this case, &aHSS-G&r."
	]
	quest.1776FA1F3255731E.quest_subtitle: "This time, we're going at HIGH speed!"
	quest.1776FA1F3255731E.title: "HSS-G"
	quest.177ADFFD33DDA624.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations! You've reached the end of the circuit progression."
		""
		"The only &4UHV&r circuit is the &6Wetware Mainframe&r, which is used for crafting some endgame stuff."
	]
	quest.177ADFFD33DDA624.title: "&4UHV&r Circuits"
	quest.178285129CEA9F9F.quest_desc: [
		"It's shiny! That's about it!"
		""
		"Yeah, you wish you could make jewelry out of it."
	]
	quest.178285129CEA9F9F.quest_subtitle: "Source of Necklaces"
	quest.178285129CEA9F9F.title: "Garnet"
	quest.1783D89CE81C8E2E.quest_desc: [
		"Technically, real-life HSS-E doesn't contain Manganese, but some other HSS alloys do have Manganese, so... close enough?"
		""
		"&aHSS-E&r has some niche uses in progression."
		""
		"This alloy has great durability and damage property for tools. It has the best Power multiplier (until Neutronium!) as a &dRotor&r for &3Large Turbines&r, though it's slightly less efficient than &aHSS-S&r."
	]
	quest.1783D89CE81C8E2E.quest_subtitle: "Turbine Upgrade, perhaps?"
	quest.1783D89CE81C8E2E.title: "HSS-E"
	quest.1783F3551BE3CC14.quest_desc: [
		"The Wooden Hammer will be your first tool on your smithing journey."
		""
		"Check the advancements tabs to gather greater info on the mod outside of these quests."
	]
	quest.1783F3551BE3CC14.title: "Wooden Hammer: Tier I"
	quest.178EB2CDC8095709.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.17A2B441AAF85148.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.17A2B441AAF85148.quest_subtitle: "&6Auto-melting"
	quest.17A7564E50233D43.quest_desc: ["A strait bow is a standard bow giving average draw time and damage."]
	quest.17A9AB06CBA7AD85.quest_desc: ["The skin of the innocent..... oh boy that sounds bad....."]
	quest.17D7D34F519F7E5F.quest_desc: [
		"To create the final tier of your Spellbook, you'll need to have killed the &6Wilden Chimera&r."
		""
		"This is a Ritual that you'll need to complete using a &9Ritual Brazier&r."
	]
	quest.1815A439BA9879B7.title: "Visit &6Warm Shore"
	quest.18192764B477D2D7.quest_desc: ["Только для настоящих колдунов."]
	quest.18724D965654056F.quest_subtitle: "By itself, it's not useful, but after using it on a Zombie or a Husk, it will upgrade into the Player Aerial Pearl."
	quest.18794889FA8D5405.quest_desc: ["Засунув личинку багрового комара в &dкапсид&r, можно получить &dтаинственного червя&r. Если бросить его в пустоты это призовёт древнюю сущность, именуемую &dПустотный Червём&r..."]
	quest.1883DF46FCE478C7.quest_desc: ["Andesite Casing is the foundation for many Create mechanisms. Apply an Andesite Alloy to any type of stripped log."]
	quest.1883DF46FCE478C7.title: "Andesite Casing"
	quest.188A8C3DD38C2762.quest_desc: [
		"The Large Turbines are the most complex Multiblock Generators that you'll find in GTCEu in the present day."
		""
		"Let's delve into Turbines!"
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on Turbine Mechanics in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.188A8C3DD38C2762.quest_subtitle: "My mechanics are... complex"
	quest.188A8C3DD38C2762.title: "Large Turbine Mechanics"
	quest.188C019760FC849D.quest_desc: ["Используя железо и &cкровь дракона&r, создайте драконью сталь. А затем изготовьте из неё броню и инструменты."]
	quest.188C019760FC849D.quest_subtitle: "&cОгненая драконья сталь"
	quest.189612F2C7C60E81.quest_desc: [
		"&lWhy process ore?"
		""
		"The main purpose of GregTech Ore Processing is to provide &abyproducts&r on top of the initial outcome. At Steam Age, none of the byproducts are obtainable, but this will become relevant soon."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lHow should I start?"
		""
		"The steps available in the Steam Age go as follows:"
		""
		"One Ore (block) &9->&r Two Crushed Ores (Macerator)"
		""
		"One Crushed Ore &9->&r One Impure Dust (Hammer)"
		""
		"One Impure Dust &9->&r One Dust (In world crafting)"
		""
		"One Dust &9->&r One Ingot (Furnace, you should know this one)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A pickaxe or mining hammer enchanted with Hammering, or a GregTech Hammer directly, gives Crushed Ores from breaking Ore blocks, but only at a 1:1 ratio."
		""
		"Silk Touch is essential to obtain an ore block - this pack includes a recipe for the book."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The rule bends for ores giving more than two dusts (such as &cRedstone&r), and for dusts that cannot be smelted (&cRedstone&r... again!)."
		""
		"However, you can still smelt the ore directly to get &9half the amount&r you would from the full processing."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&dEMI does not indicate Impure Dust to Clean Dust conversion&r, so keep that in mind that you can &athrow them into filled cauldrons&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Take this reward for listening to us waffle on WITHOUT nodding off!"
	]
	quest.189612F2C7C60E81.title: "Beginner Ore Processing"
	quest.189F84D6C76CDC8B.quest_desc: [
		"It's time to be blunt - Steam as a power option isn't gonna cut the mustard anymore. If you're going to stick with Steam until the bitter end, we wish you luck... so read on."
		""
		"The &3Large Steam Turbine&r acts as a multiblock Steam Turbine for &6HV&r power. It's quite an expensive multiblock to build just for a measly 1024 EU/t, but it also boasts the powerful ability to scale to &9higher power production and higher efficiency&r."
		""
		"&8(We're trying our best to sell it here, okay?!)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Turbine outputs &dDistilled Water&r if given an &3Output Hatch&r, which you could loop back to your &3Large Boilers&r. We don't entirely endorse this, as your Boilers could end up exploding if this system fails."
		""
		"Each Large Turbine will require a &aTurbine Rotor&r and a &3Rotor Holder&r. You can find out more about the Turbine mechanics in the &lnext&r Quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r This Quest &eonly&r requires the Controller, but you'll still need all the multiblock parts to construct the Turbine."
		""
		"Turbines &cvoid&r energy if they're unable to output. If you plan on using this with &6HV&r power, use a Rotor close to a 100% Power stat."
	]
	quest.189F84D6C76CDC8B.quest_subtitle: "If you're still running off Steam... boy, do we have a solution for you!"
	quest.189F84D6C76CDC8B.title: "Large Steam Turbine"
	quest.18A2FBE2D4133FA2.quest_desc: [
		"Arcane Pedestals are needed for the Ritual Brazier and crafting items with an Enchanting Apparatus."
		""
		"Go ahead and make yourself 8 of them!"
	]
	quest.18A2FBE2D4133FA2.quest_subtitle: "Fancy Tables"
	quest.18A2FBE2D4133FA2.title: "Arcane Pedestals"
	quest.18C8BCD674682F5A.quest_desc: ["Квест для парочек."]
	quest.18C8BCD674682F5A.title: "Романтический ужин"
	quest.18F8DADD01FEC9C2.quest_desc: [
		"The Cooking Pot is a workstation where you can both prepare and store a large amount of meals. When placed above any suitable heat source (campfire, open flames, lava, a stove etc.), it will start bubbling, indicating it's ready to cook."
		""
		"You can put up to six ingredients inside a pot. If they match, the pot will start cooking them up into a meal. Most meals need a container to be served on, such as Bowls; the result slot will tell you which one to use. Simply add the container on the corresponding slot, or right-click the pot with it, to take a serving!"
		""
		"Meals tend to be quite large, so they don't stack up as high in your inventory. If you're not going to eat them all right away, you can just mine the whole pot and take it with you! Cooking Pots can hold 64 servings of any meal with a container, regardless of their maximum stack limit."
	]
	quest.18FB6AA280646F14.quest_subtitle: "Delve deep underground"
	quest.191D54A7CE72C36B.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.191D54A7CE72C36B.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.192EE909C57F390A.quest_subtitle: "Rare chance of spawning after breaking an &6Ancient Vase&r."
	quest.192EE909C57F390A.title: "Defeat a &3Stalker"
	quest.1931FC6DEAC29646.quest_desc: [
		"With the creation of this machine, many recipes that once required you to use a hammer can instead be made here!"
		""
		"It can process &bCobblestone into Gravel&r, and &dGravel into Sand&r - and it's zippy at that to boot."
		""
		"Last but not least, it makes &aPlates&r at a better ratio: &6three Ingots for two Plates&r. A worthwhile investment!"
		""
		"You know what? &aBonus&r! We'll give you the &8Anvil&r back if you craft the Forge Hammer. This is a gentle reminder that you can repair GregTech tools in an Anvil."
	]
	quest.1931FC6DEAC29646.quest_subtitle: "The Forge Hammer hammers..."
	quest.1931FC6DEAC29646.title: "Steam Forge Hammer"
	quest.1937057C27596942.quest_desc: [
		"Basalt Dust centrifuges into Olivine, a material which can be used to substitute Emerald in a small handful of recipes - for example, when making Engraved Crystal Chips."
		""
		"You also get a pittance of Dark Ash."
	]
	quest.1937057C27596942.quest_subtitle: "Olivine, Dark Ashes..."
	quest.19430A891A62692E.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони их хитина &cпустынного червя&r."]
	quest.19430A891A62692E.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасная"
	quest.19430A891A62692E.title: "Хитиновая броня"
	quest.1950E4C67EC16413.quest_desc: ["Although bosses are not the main objective in this modpack, they will be rewarded in the future and simply help you relax and engage in other activities."]
	quest.1950E4C67EC16413.title: "Bosses"
	quest.195E5BFDE4C5A0DE.quest_desc: [
		"Better &aSMDs&r? SMDs that'll unlock far cheaper &7- &8and faster &7-&r Circuit recipes? We're sold!"
		""
		"These'll require Alloys that you haven't made yet, most of which will be commonly used in &dLuV&r and onwards. Get on it!"
		""
		"Whilst you don't need these right now, &aAdvanced SMDs&r will become a hard requirement for the &dCrystal&r Circuit line. Note that using these in your current circuits will &2halve&r the recipe duration."
	]
	quest.195E5BFDE4C5A0DE.title: "Advanced SMDs"
	quest.1965F1DD63E622EC.quest_desc: ["Use the ingots of &6ignitium&r to create a powerful piece of equipment. It will definitely not let you down in battle...."]
	quest.196FC518F744B983.quest_desc: [
		"Making the best &6HV&r Circuits will allow for easier &6HV&r Machines for your on-demand automation. Convenient!"
		""
		"Starting from here, all circuit lines will be consistent with each other until the end of the game."
		""
		"Each tier until &cZPM&r will show its own challenges when acquiring new and better Circuits."
	]
	quest.196FC518F744B983.quest_subtitle: "The Pinnacle... the Zenith"
	quest.196FC518F744B983.title: "Best HV Circuits!"
	quest.1976F9B2220BBEDE.quest_desc: [
		"This Maintenance Hatch is an upgrade to the Automatic Maintenance Hatch."
		""
		"It allows your Multiblock to run regular &aCleanroom recipes&r when not contained inside one - but not Sterilized recipes."
	]
	quest.1976F9B2220BBEDE.title: "Cleaning Maintenance Hatch"
	quest.1993478A82341354.title: "Chestplate"
	quest.199361B5FEC959EA.quest_desc: [
		"From now on, all Circuits should be made in a &3Circuit Assembler&r. Use it now to enjoy &6far cheaper LV and MV circuits&r."
		""
		"Each time you upgrade to a new tier of &3Circuit Assembler&r, you will be able to craft more &dadvanced themes&r of circuit. These will use &ccomplex&r and &m&7sometimes&r unfamiliar ingredients, but will be more efficient to craft overall."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Circuit Assembler has made appearances in and out of GregTech versions. GT5 did not have it, and it was reimplemented in GT5 Unofficial. GTCE decided not to port it, and the tug-of-war continues with its inclusion in GTCEu."
	]
	quest.199361B5FEC959EA.quest_subtitle: "Hopefully, your first MV Circuit expense"
	quest.19ABDAE8C8A23466.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.19ABDAE8C8A23466.quest_subtitle: "&6Burns the attacker"
	quest.19CD0FC343158355.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.19D02325579F2AA8.quest_desc: [
		"The Volcanic Sourcelink generates Source by consuming burnable items. Archwood logs will generate bonus Source."
		""
		"As it burns items, it will convert nearby stone into lava."
		""
		"This also generates Lava Lilys."
	]
	quest.19E5E31614FE485E.quest_desc: [
		"Electric machines work exactly the same as steam machines, except that they require electricity instead of steam and they progressively overclock recipes up to 32 EU/t."
		""
		"You can use REI to view the recipes for the electric version of the machines you are already familiar with."
		""
		"We strongly suggest that you automate Machine Hull, Analog Circuits, Motors, Pistons, Robot Arms and Conveyor Belts using Assemblers as soon as possible, that will make crafting electric machines basically free!"
	]
	quest.19E5E31614FE485E.quest_subtitle: "You have done well to make it this far. Now that we have moved on from steam, we are now doing even more complicated machinery using electricity, but the results are rewarding."
	quest.19E5E31614FE485E.title: "&6I want a Nokia phone now!"
	quest.19E7D8B9CD473791.title: "Jewelcrafting Guide"
	quest.19FBAF9A70549BF5.quest_desc: [
		"This unit holds 10 storage cells, so you can pack your storage tightly in a very small space."
		""
		"Displays their contents and storage cell status on the front of the drive."
		""
		"Red - Indicates that the storage cell is full."
		""
		"Orange - Indicates that the storage cell cannot hold more types, but it can hold more items."
		""
		"Green - Indicates that the cell can hold more types or elements."
		""
		"Black - Indicates that there is no channel or the power is down."
		""
		"It is important to note that without the ME network, this block does nothing. It is only useful in conjunction with the element input and output method, and it requires 2 AE / t power and additional power for each memory cell stored within it."
	]
	quest.19FBAF9A70549BF5.quest_subtitle: "A block designed to perform a single task - storing memory cells."
	quest.1A118FBA223B14F9.quest_subtitle: "Found in the &6Ancient Factories&r, in the Overworld Caves. Locate with an &6Eye of Mech"
	quest.1A118FBA223B14F9.title: "Defeat the &4Harbringer"
	quest.1A1749750B6EF51A.quest_desc: ["The redstone upgrade will ouptut a redstone signal equivalent to the level that the storage is full."]
	quest.1A29EFBCEA017F99.quest_desc: [
		"The Brewery can be used to make &aLubricant&r from &aRedstone&r and &aCreosote&r/&aOil&r. Lubricant has some niche uses, namely being used in the &3Cutter&r to significantly reduce the duration of its recipes."
		""
		"The Brewery is a very, very slow machine, but it requires almost no power to run its recipes. Building &2many Breweries&r will help you obtain enough Biomass on your quest for plastic. Oh, and you can use it to brew &dPotions&r too!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r The Brewery \"unlocks\" the Biomass path towards &9Ethylene&r. The same can be done in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r. The other path involves Oil.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You could make your own Brewery if you want to build up a company and start selling Booze... in GregTech 6.&r"
	]
	quest.1A29EFBCEA017F99.quest_subtitle: "*hic*... *hic*"
	quest.1A29EFBCEA017F99.title: "Local Brewery selling Booze"
	quest.1A29FC5A73FDE328.quest_subtitle: "Solar Panels generate energy during the day time, the higher tier, the more power generated during the day."
	quest.1A32AA035EEDCF24.quest_desc: ["Why it does bleeding...? I don't know. But is it funny? Yeah."]
	quest.1A4AD56965407DC5.quest_desc: [
		"Silicone Rubber has its uses in Cable insulation, Conveyor recipes, and more."
		""
		"You may want to shelve this quest for now, as tackling Silicone Rubber can be a pretty severe &dChlorine&r sink."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Rubber will eventually be usurped by either &aSilicone Rubber&r or &aStyrene-Butadienne Rubber&r for &1IV&r Cables."
		""
		"Both these rubbers will be required once you make it to &dLuV&r."
	]
	quest.1A4AD56965407DC5.quest_subtitle: "An alternate rubber"
	quest.1A4AD56965407DC5.title: "Silicone Rubber"
	quest.1A6A383B4EF26B20.title: "Drill Head"
	quest.1A6D6EA172DB63A1.quest_desc: ["В нашем мире с давних времён существует могущественная раса, которая стоит на вершине иерархии во всём мире - драконы. Они делятся на три типа: &6огненные&r, &bледяные&r и &dгрозовые&r. Их зубы могут прокусить металл, их когти могут срубить деревья."]
	quest.1A77CA35F054F988.quest_desc: [
		"You could waste &o&eprecious years of your life&r in EMI looking for the most optimal Oxygen recipe, given the many ways to obtain it. Various minerals will produce it when electrolyzed."
		""
		"If only the quest book had more information!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The best way to get &bOxygen&r is by electrolyzing &bSilicon Dioxide&r. Silicon Dioxide is obtained from various sources, most notably Glass Dust. We would &chighly&r recommend setting up an automated, passive line of machines for Oxygen via this method! At first, the machines will consume tons of power, but once the machine buffers are filled up, the machines will rarely turn on. "
		""
		"To figure out how to get renewable Glass for this purpose, check out the relevant quest in the &eRenewables \\& You&r section."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Another method is &acentrifuging Air&r after making a &dGas Collector&r, which you might not be able to make just yet. This recipe also gives &aNitrogen&r, which is handy as it can speed up certain &3Electric Blast Furnace&r recipes&r."
		""
		"Technically, you could source it by &aelectrolyzing Water&r. In reality, electrolysis of water is more suitable for &aHydrogen production&r due to the higher energy cost."
		""
		"Try your best not to &cvoid&r Oxygen! This applies to most fluids and chemicals in GregTech, and is a good habit to pick up. The less Oxygen you void, the less energy and time you spend on generating more."
		""
		"&eNote:&r Submit a fluid by having it stored in a &lbucket&r in your inventory. Sorry - it's an FTB Quests quirk."
	]
	quest.1A77CA35F054F988.quest_subtitle: "Ackshually, it's Dioxygen..."
	quest.1A77CA35F054F988.title: "Breath of Fresh Oxygen"
	quest.1A8F438DB8508276.title: "Visit &6Frosted prison"
	quest.1AA0237C138D0D5B.quest_desc: ["The Crafting Table is your first workshop. With it, you'll create your first tools and mechanisms."]
	quest.1AA0237C138D0D5B.title: "Crafting Table"
	quest.1AA42229A8F7CD48.title: "The Electric Era"
	quest.1AA60A55FA9B6080.quest_desc: ["A Map will help you navigate the vast expanses of this world. Don't forget to mark important locations!"]
	quest.1AA60A55FA9B6080.title: "Map"
	quest.1AB3414273A18FD1.quest_desc: [
		"В токсичных пещерах, вы сможете встретить &aуран&r, который излучает сильную радиацию."
		"\"Уолтер, убери свой уран подальше, Уолтер\""
	]
	quest.1AB3414273A18FD1.title: "Радиоактивные материалы"
	quest.1AD003487B4EC2EF.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Active Transformer&r is a multiblock used to transform energy on a much larger scale. For example, you can convert &6HV&r to &7LV&r power directly by using the apropriate energy hatches."
		""
		"It also has a second function, detailed in the above quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This is yet another feature from TecTech, which also required these cables to be painted. They do look fantastic if you paint them, but it's optional in CEu."
	]
	quest.1AD003487B4EC2EF.quest_subtitle: "More than a large transformer"
	quest.1AD003487B4EC2EF.title: "Active Transformer"
	quest.1AD309112ADD8D8D.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Large Combustion Engine&r is a multiblock that can burn &dCombustion Fuels&r for even... more... power generation!"
		""
		"By default, this puppy outputs 2048 EU/t, which is equivalent to 4 &3Turbo Combustion Generators&r."
		""
		"This might not convince you, but unlike the singleblock generators, you can actually &6boost this&r by providing &aOxygen&r. This will &cdouble&r the fuel consumption, but &atriple&r the power generation. This'll output 6144 EU/t with &6150% Fuel efficiency&r."
		""
		"You'll also need to supply a small amount of &aLubricant&r to the LCE during operation - nothing too crazy."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &3LCE&r is also void-free, unlike Large Turbines. Any energy that cannot be output will momentarily pause the multiblock."
		""
		"To harness the cataclysmic power of the 6144 EU/t output, you'll need a &34A EV Dynamo Hatch&r or an &3IV Dynamo Hatch&r."
	]
	quest.1AD309112ADD8D8D.title: "Large Combustion"
	quest.1ADB6E725663B3AB.quest_desc: ["The Claw head will allow you to pry open items in Tetra dungeons as well as break wooden items quickly."]
	quest.1AF0866A8C2CFCA8.quest_desc: ["В магнитных пещерах, вы встретите два типа кристалла: &cалый неодим&r и &9лазурный неодим&r. Из котрых можно создать разные предметы."]
	quest.1B0A4271FCBD581F.quest_desc: ["Now that were getting into Electric Muiltiblock Structures you will start using Energy Hatches. You can upgrades the Hatches to other tiers as you wish."]
	quest.1B0A4271FCBD581F.quest_subtitle: "This machine part will be needed in order for more advanced electric machinery to function so remember to make some of these."
	quest.1B0A4271FCBD581F.title: "Where's the Plug?"
	quest.1B26C03FD0CDAAEA.quest_subtitle: "Now that you have some Certus Quartz Crystals it's time to charge them. Toss one into the Charger you made earlier and get to cranking!"
	quest.1B45DB5C85B68182.quest_desc: [
		"Your only source of Diamond!"
		""
		"Diamond has &6five times more durability&r than Iron for tools. The catch is that you'll need Diamond Plates for some tools, which is gated behind the Cutting Machine."
		""
		"Diamond and Graphite both electrolyze into a ton of Carbon. Hint, hint..?"
		""
		"&cNote:&r Avoid macerating Diamonds in the early game. Recovering gem dusts into the actual gem cannot be done for a while - and even then, the process is slow and time-consuming..."
	]
	quest.1B45DB5C85B68182.quest_subtitle: "Source of Diamond, Carbon"
	quest.1B45DB5C85B68182.title: "Graphite"
	quest.1B520580219AFAE9.quest_desc: [
		"Rocket Fuel mostly exists for compatibility with other mods. You'll love it if you're making your own pack."
		""
		"As an actual fuel for GTCEu generators? Terrible!"
		""
		"In this modpack, &aRocket Fuel&r is required to obtain &dNether Stars&r."
		""
		"Automating it may be a big hit to your resources, but you can safely batch craft using an overclocked &3Large Chemical Reactor&r."
	]
	quest.1B520580219AFAE9.quest_subtitle: "Honey, where are my Microverse Projectors?"
	quest.1B520580219AFAE9.title: "Rocket Fuel"
	quest.1B82FEF57E241253.quest_desc: ["A small piece of iron needed to create Andesite Alloy."]
	quest.1B82FEF57E241253.title: "Iron Nugget"
	quest.1B98D4F59823C52D.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1B9E6F09E7AB8C87.quest_desc: ["Acts as a blaze burner and yes, you can use it to make a steam engine, but be warned that you do need to pump the carbon dioxide out (through an exhaust or smokestack.)"]
	quest.1BABE9CD979E7E47.quest_desc: ["Пирожков с капустой в сборке нет."]
	quest.1BABE9CD979E7E47.title: "Пироги"
	quest.1BB40CCF17D00719.quest_desc: [
		"If you're &lstill&r running off the &3Large Bronze Boiler&r, you may &o(read: may not)&r want to upgrade to the &3Large Steel Boiler&r."
		""
		"It's slightly more efficient than the &3LBB&r, and produces &d900 EU/t worth of Steam&r..."
		""
		"We'd politely recommend that you try other power options at this point."
		""
		"Anyway, here's a checkmark to skip the quest."
	]
	quest.1BB40CCF17D00719.quest_subtitle: "Steam isn't the only answer, but we won't stop you"
	quest.1BB40CCF17D00719.title: "One Hundred Million Pressure Cookers"
	quest.1BD22FC74CD3DB9A.quest_desc: [
		"The Holosphere is given to the player with the first hammer that is created (though it also can be crafted again later if lost). The left menu (CRFT) is currently the only one available."
		""
		"In the holosphere you will be able to check all the materials and their statistics as components. It is very useful in planning out your next tool upgrade."
	]
	quest.1BD22FC74CD3DB9A.title: "Holosphere"
	quest.1BE0349B8F3890D3.quest_desc: [
		"Here's a list of the components you will need in &bMV&r. To alleviate the pain, be sure to autocraft or &dbulk-craft&r these parts, especially &aMotors&r."
		""
		"Familiar with the &aEmitter&r? This tier's Emitter requires a &dFlawless Emerald&r in its recipe, which'll be only attainable with the &3Sifting Machine&r for now."
		""
		"Conveyors, Pumps and Robot Arms are objective upgrades to &7LV&r versions if you use them as covers."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on Overclocking in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.1BE0349B8F3890D3.quest_subtitle: "Hated crafting these in the previous tier?"
	quest.1BE0349B8F3890D3.title: "MV Components"
	quest.1BE779AF4487E3EB.quest_desc: [
		"This Large Miner is nearly identical to the regular one, except it has a wider range and uses more drilling fluid."
		""
		"It's an optional sidegrade - one you might not even want."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o There may be a rebalance for these in the future. See the Multiblock Miner quest for details."
	]
	quest.1BE779AF4487E3EB.title: "Ludicrous Ore Drilling"
	quest.1BF02D43986ABB03.title: "Conveyor"
	quest.1BF70751B4ED7E7E.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.1BFD0A51D3AE51E6.quest_desc: ["Used to make concrete liquid or mixture"]
	quest.1C036BCB2C488CFF.quest_desc: [
		"&aPatterns&r are used for AE2 autocrafting. Using &aPolyvinyl Chloride&r increases the yield by &64 times&r, and higher-tier plastics have even greater yields."
		""
		"Don't get too excited, though - to really get into the automation side of AE2, you'll need to get some &dSilicon Ingots&r first."
		""
		"A sub-note for autocrafting... whilst it's possible to perform chemical chains on-demand with AE2, doing so can build some bad habits that'll come back around to bite you in higher tiers. We urge you to passive things wherever you can."
	]
	quest.1C036BCB2C488CFF.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting at last!"
	quest.1C036BCB2C488CFF.title: "Patterns"
	quest.1C1976238A2FBEE0.quest_desc: ["On this line you can see the Steam, or &8&8ULV&r, equivalents."]
	quest.1C1976238A2FBEE0.title: "&8ULV&r Circuits"
	quest.1C232674CD04024D.quest_subtitle: "&6The Undergarden&r portal is built the same way as a Nether Portal, but instead of Obsidian you use Stone bricks and activate with catalyst."
	quest.1C232674CD04024D.title: "Visit &6Undergarden"
	quest.1C4597EAA70A7111.title: "Очень странные блюда"
	quest.1C50A758A1DE25CB.quest_desc: [
		"The &bMacerator&r frees you from the painful process of &egrinding stuff into dust&r with a &3Mortar&r, but at the steep cost of time. Processing a single piece of Iron Ore in this machine will take &ctwenty seconds&r - twice the time it takes to smelt an ingot in a furnace!"
		""
		"The Macerator also marks the advent of &eOre Processing&r, but that's a scary topic that we'll dip our toes into in the next quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The macerator will output only the first item shown in recipes from EMI. The other slots are locked until you make a &6HV&r Macerator. How unfortunate..."
		""
		"Our (&oimportant!&r) advice: it's actually better to keep directly smelting for now! The efficiency loss is made up with faster mining. Use the Macerator to make things like &aClay Dust&r instead!"
	]
	quest.1C50A758A1DE25CB.quest_subtitle: "The Macerator macerates..."
	quest.1C50A758A1DE25CB.title: "Steam Macerator"
	quest.1C55AE6AD5BDE304.quest_desc: [
		"&3Kanthal Heating Coils&r are the next major step in progression. They increase the temperature of your &3Blast Furnace&r to &d2,700K&r, allowing you to process new materials. They may also &eaccelerate&r less hot recipes - check the quest to the top-left for details."
		""
		"You will need a staggering &a128 Ingots&r for a full set of Coils, which will easily take over an hour. We advise that you move on to other projects while your &3EBF&r is hard at work - that or build another one!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"An &3MV Chemical Bath&r is required to cool &cHot Ingots&r down. They're &chot&r when held, as the name implies. &o&7Maybe you should save your hands and automate this...&r"
		""
		"With the construction of a &3Kanthal EBF&r, you're now able to make &dSilicon Ingots&r, opening up the vast majority of AE2!"
	]
	quest.1C55AE6AD5BDE304.quest_subtitle: "Is it getting hot in here?"
	quest.1C55AE6AD5BDE304.title: "Kanthal Coils"
	quest.1C767009F505A813.quest_desc: [
		"Covers are placed by right-clicking with Cover in hand on a face of a machine, and removed with a &5Crowbar&r (or by mining the machine, but that's way slower)."
		""
		"Pretty much any GregTech \"machine\" will accept Covers, even if they wouldn't provide any functionality."
		""
		"Opening a Cover is done by sneak-right-clicking it with an &5empty hand&r. You can also right-click with a &5Screwdriver&r, or sneak-right-click on another face using the grid."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For Covers that transfer Items/Fluids, you will have a button to enable/disable other forms of transfer through the cover:"
		""
		"&9- &rDisabled: only the cover will be allowed to transfer on this machine side."
		""
		"&9-&r Allow Filtered (only relevant with a filter!): other transfer will be enabled only if it matches the filter"
		""
		"&9-&r Allow Unfiltered: any other transfer is allowed on this machine side."
		""
		"Placing a cover of a lower voltage tier on a machine is &9safe&r."
	]
	quest.1C767009F505A813.quest_subtitle: "Extra utility without taking up blockspace!"
	quest.1C767009F505A813.title: "Cover Behaviour"
	quest.1C8D3981C9926FB7.quest_desc: ["&6Посох управления&r, нужен для того, чтобы контролировать движения дракона. Вы можете приказать ему летать, охранять вас, следовать за вами, сидеть и т.д."]
	quest.1C997C65D07E6C07.title: "Circuit Processing"
	quest.1CB9A26C3296858E.quest_desc: [
		"One could define a Subnetwork &7(or \"Subnet\" for short)&r as any network that isn't part of your main network."
		""
		"The simplest way to create a Subnet is by attaching an &bME Interface&r to a &aStorage Bus&r. This means that the Storage Bus will treat the Interface as an inventory to be read from - i.e., it'll be able to see &5all of the items&r in the network connected to the Interface."
		""
		"As your main network will &4not&r be transferred through the Storage Bus, you'll need to give your subnet power from the main network with &6Quartz Fibre&r. Ensure that you don't accidentally connect the two networks with regular cabling."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Question is - how does this &abenefit you&r as a player? The logistics powers made available with subnetworking are immense, so we'll cover a few examples &9in light detail&r. The rest is left as an exercise to the reader!"
		""
		"- A subnet for your ore processing system, which &bautomatically handles&r all the intermediate byproducts without them constantly entering and exiting your main network!"
		"- Really, it's useful to subnet &dlarger processing chains&r such as &ePlatinum processing&r. This way, you can ensure that byproducts can be appropriately recycled, and reduce overhead."
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Subnets can be infinitely nested, but as always in &bmodded Minecraft&r, this should be performed in moderation (or even better, avoided), as many levels of nesting can cause &4performance issues&r when calculating the network."
		""
		"Oh... and if you've re-enabled Channels in this pack, subnetworks only consume a single channel from your main network. What a bargain!"
	]
	quest.1CB9A26C3296858E.quest_subtitle: "Socially Distanced Network"
	quest.1CB9A26C3296858E.title: "Subnets 101"
	quest.1CBA5477CB7C45E7.quest_desc: ["Nichrome will require your &aElectric Blast Furnace&r to be at least &6EV&r, with &bKanthal&r coils to boot."]
	quest.1CBA5477CB7C45E7.quest_subtitle: "Operation Nichrome Dome"
	quest.1CBA5477CB7C45E7.title: "Nichrome"
	quest.1D11C0E1CE2924CD.quest_desc: ["Это око охраняет древнее существо глубоко под водой."]
	quest.1D16EDF6BC8A0BE3.quest_subtitle: "Found in &fsnowy&r biomes"
	quest.1D1F4BD3405603B0.title: "Netherite-gold armor"
	quest.1D3EDFD37AFCCB25.quest_desc: [
		"Geodes are gained as a random chance from mining Deepslate."
		""
		"To break open these geodes place them in a workbench where they can be opened with a hammer."
		"From them you can gain random resources and even rare prisitine versions of gems."
	]
	quest.1D6CC3C7F6BE4055.quest_desc: [
		"The &3High Performance Computation Array&r, also known as the &3HPCA&r, is the multiblock used to create &9Computation&r, measured in CWU/t (Compute-Work Units per tick)."
		""
		"The HPCA is a modular multiblock with many unique components you've likely not seen before. There are &a9 slots available&r for different components, and there are some example layouts in the EMI previews, so reviewing these may help if you feel confused."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are two main types of components:"
		""
		"- &9Computation Components&r: These generate CWU/t and require EU/t and cooling."
		"- &9Cooling Components&r: These provide a certain amount of cooling, and require EU/t."
		""
		"Currently Available Components:"
		""
		"- &9Empty&r: Fills a slot but otherwise does nothing."
		"-&9 Heat Sink&r: Requires no power but provides 1 cooling."
		"- &9Active Cooler&r: Requires power, PCB Coolant, but provides 2 cooling."
		"- &9Computation&r: Creates 4 CWU/t, but requires a lot of power and cooling."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The HPCA draws some power to idle. Its power and cooling requirements will sit between the idle upkeep power and a maximum value depending on how much computation is being used."
		""
		"If the HPCA is not given enough cooling, Computation components can be &4damaged&r if it is allowed to run above &c100C&r (the idle temperature is &a20C&r). Only computation components can be damaged - all other blocks will be unharmed!"
		""
		"The HPCA can only have 1 &3Computation Data Transmission Hatch&r. You can connect it to the Reception Hatch of the &9Research Station&r with Optical Fiber Cable to transmit the computation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Basic CWU/t Requirements for ZPM Tier:"
		""
		"- &a4 CWU/t&r for &cZPM&r Sensors, Emitters, and Field Generators"
		"- &a8 CWU/t&r for &cZPM&r Enegy Hatches"
		"- &a16 CWU/t&r for &3UV&r Circuits and beyond."
		""
		"Don't feel forced to go for 16 CWU/t immediately. There's lots to do in between these milestones."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This mechanic is loosely inspired by TecTech's Quantum Computer, which is similar but has some much more annoying mechanics like the Uncertainty Resolver."
	]
	quest.1D6CC3C7F6BE4055.quest_subtitle: "That's no Quantum Computer..."
	quest.1D6CC3C7F6BE4055.title: "HPCA"
	quest.1D717E742E50A6BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eMicro&r Circuits are where the &3Cleanroom&r becomes a requirement to progress."
		""
		"Don't get caught out by the &aMainframe&r - it requires a &3HV Circuit Assembler&r."
	]
	quest.1D717E742E50A6BD.quest_subtitle: "Micro Miners"
	quest.1D717E742E50A6BD.title: "Craftable in &bMV&r and &6HV&r"
	quest.1D71BA7DA68CF606.quest_desc: ["This is just your standard sword blade with no extra frills."]
	quest.1D7E172F0C8B1DEC.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.1D8170A19E54C5B9.quest_desc: [
		"With &5EV Circuits&r, you can compress your Coprocessors into &3Dense&r variants to get more value-for-money. "
		""
		"The crafting ratio is in your favour, so you'll likely have more &eparallel autocrafting power&r than you'd need to finish the pack."
	]
	quest.1D8170A19E54C5B9.quest_subtitle: "Who are you calling Dense?"
	quest.1D8170A19E54C5B9.title: "Dense Coprocessors"
	quest.1D86B2E553503E53.quest_desc: ["The Dominion Wand is used for controlling the creatures you might encounter in the world! Each being responds differently to the wand, so make sure to read up in the Worn Notebook!"]
	quest.1D86B2E553503E53.title: "Summoning Help!"
	quest.1D90D810E787E7E0.quest_desc: ["Can be hammered into bedrock to gain resources or added to a pickaxe to make a unique mining tool to break multiple blocks at a time."]
	quest.1DA54DA70E12F499.quest_desc: [
		"&5You:&r &oThat's it, I'm uninstalling! This pack is stupid! We're barely in &7LV&r&o, but you're asking me to make you a &6HV&r&o machine!?&r"
		""
		"Yes! This is indeed not completable yet, which is also why this quest appears in the &6HV&r Chapter."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Remember how disappointing it was that you couldn't get byproducts with your Macerator? Well... that disappointment won't be going away until you reach &6HV&r."
		""
		"&6The Macerator will unlock its second and third slot at HV&r. Trust us - this is great news for your Ore Processing. In fact, one byproduct is completely locked behind this (after the Thermal Centrifuge step)."
		""
		"&cNote:&r Unlike GTCE, the &bMV&r Macerator in GTCEu &4doesn't&r have a second slot."
		""
		"&5Writer:&r &oCome back to me when you are stronger, young Cricket.&r"
	]
	quest.1DA54DA70E12F499.quest_subtitle: "What? Why?!"
	quest.1DA54DA70E12F499.title: "Universal Macerator"
	quest.1DDC3D44E5F69504.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1E27C654E2F6FFF2.quest_desc: [
		"As an ore, Coal is hardly worth large-scale processing, because there are too many additional steps. required to turn it into usable fuel. It's still good to have some in your back pocket."
		""
		"Just run it through a Furnace."
	]
	quest.1E27C654E2F6FFF2.quest_subtitle: "Source of pollution"
	quest.1E27C654E2F6FFF2.title: "Coal"
	quest.1E435A4C1547934D.quest_desc: ["However, it does not support buses, so you must first upgrade from a dense cable to a smaller cable (such as Fluix ME Glass Cable or Fluix ME Smart Cable) before using buses or panels. Shows the load similarly to Fluix ME Smart Cable, with each highlighted line representing the four channels in use."]
	quest.1E435A4C1547934D.quest_subtitle: "Higher capacity cable, can transmit 32 channels as opposed to standard cable which can only transmit 8."
	quest.1E5EFC5880605DD4.quest_desc: [
		"First off, be sure to check the &9tooltip&r - there's a lot of information in there!"
		""
		"Don't forget the &3Maintenance Hatch&r. If the structure refuses to form, rotate or replace the Controller, it can be a bit finicky. Don't worry - it doesn't have to be cube-shaped."
		""
		"The Controller always has to be in the center. The rest of the top layer has to be &dFilter Casings&r."
		""
		"All edges have to be &dPlascrete&r, and the sides can be &dCleanroom Glass&r."
		""
		"Placing &3Generators&r or &3Mufflers&r inside is &cnot allowed&r. They're too dirty, so the Cleanroom will unform."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Upon assembly, the Cleanroom starts &4contaminated&r. While contamined, contained machines will not be able to operate."
		""
		"The Cleanroom will drain 30 EU/t and slowly increase the cleanliness until its cleanliness is at 100%."
		""
		"Once &9Clean&r, recipes can run. At that point it will only draw 4EU/t. Keep it powered at all times or it will get dirty again!"
		""
		"The bigger the Cleanroom, the longer it takes to become Clean."
		""
		"&9Note&r: When the time comes, Multiblocks must also be put into Cleanrooms in order to run cleanroom recipes!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Need to transfer EU? Try using &3Hulls&r or &3Diodes&r."
		""
		"Item and Fluid transfer can be done using &3Passthrough Hatches&r."
		""
		"&3Machine Hulls&r can also \"double\" as &6ME Cables&r to extend your ME Network inside your Cleanroom."
		""
		"If you used any &dDoor(s)&r in the structure, they can remain open. Not very realistic, but convenient!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&eConfigs:&r If you dislike the Cleanroom mechanics, it can be toggled off in the config file with &5\"B:enableCleanroom\"&r. Multiblocks can be made to ignore cleanroom requirements with &5\"B:cleanMultiblocks\"&r. We encourage you to try it out before deciding."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In the real world, a Cleanroom is a well-isolated room which maintains a very low concentration of dust and airborne particles. They're normally used for scientific research, and in real-life semiconductor manufacturing. Clean rooms are specifically designed to keep out as many airborne particulates as can be. "
		""
		"Clean rooms are also sometimes used with the purpose of preventing materials from escaping! This is often the primary aim in fields such as pharmaceutics, nuclear work, and hazardous biology."
		""
		"The more you know!"
	]
	quest.1E5EFC5880605DD4.title: "All About the Cleanroom"
	quest.1E63D8214168C09E.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.1E7BF65DB32B8B3E.quest_desc: ["&aRandom Access Memory&r is required for more advanced Electronic Components."]
	quest.1E7BF65DB32B8B3E.quest_subtitle: "Random Access Memories"
	quest.1E7BF65DB32B8B3E.title: "Download more RAM"
	quest.1E87BCA90B5A45AA.quest_desc: ["Time to head to the nether to get some fine heat treated Blackstone that is surprisingly stronger than basic metals."]
	quest.1E97CA32D74269B8.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &cдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.1E97CA32D74269B8.title: "Инструменты из драконостали"
	quest.1E9BE8D3F8A602DC.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest explains the core mechanic of the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r, whilst the quest below will explore the mechanics of the Multiblock Parts that you'll also need. Be sure to refer to them."
		""
		"Anyway, the &3EBF&r is your &efirst electric multiblock&r! Congrats. It's used to process materials at high temperatures."
		""
		"You'll become familiar with the EBF to make &aAluminium&r and progress to &d&bMV Age&r. It can also make &7Steel&r faster than a PBF."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"It's important to keep in mind that the EBF is a beefy boy. The minimum power cost to run a recipe is &9120 EU/t&r! That's slightly under 4 &7LV&r Generators. This is why it was locked behind the Battery Quest. You may wish to consider building a separate power line, with separate Generators and Battery Buffer to run this."
	]
	quest.1E9BE8D3F8A602DC.quest_subtitle: "A big milestone!"
	quest.1EA89DD440FBA503.quest_subtitle: "Breed all the animals!(26)"
	quest.1EACE9E49BA4B753.quest_subtitle: "This blastproof alloy plate is going to be specially important with a specific process that will be booming."
	quest.1EACE9E49BA4B753.title: "Can we make a shield out of this?"
	quest.1EB61F477F73BCBD.quest_desc: ["Искажённая бородавка, которую можно получить с деревьев в искажённом лесу. Очень полезная вещь для алхимиков."]
	quest.1EB61F477F73BCBD.title: "Искажённая бородавка"
	quest.1EC6F3577F6413F2.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1EC9217BF9023978.quest_desc: ["bulb"]
	quest.1EC9217BF9023978.quest_subtitle: "Light Bulb"
	quest.1ECBA1CBFFB9F625.quest_desc: [
		"In the real world, iron isn't &oonly&r found as pure Iron Ore. Instead, it's found in a &avariety&r of &eoxide forms&r or &eminerals&r."
		""
		"You'll want to go and collect quite a bit of Iron, because you're going to need &9a bunch&r very soon. If you're struggling to find some, the &aOre Generation&r quest tab contains a lot of information on &eore veins&r. You may also want to check the Ore Spawn Information and Ore Byproduct List tabs in &2EMI&r."
		""
		"Any of the raw ores we're asking for can be directly smelted into Iron. That comes to &dfour different veins&r that can give you Iron."
		""
		"Lastly, Fortune &cdoes not&r work on GregTech ores, &7unfortunately&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Whilst it may be common habit to hoard ore in &bmodded Minecraft&r prior to unlocking some kind of &aore multiplication&r, don't worry about ore processing yet. Direct smelting remains the most efficient method for a long, &olong&r while, given how easy it is to obtain a lot of ore in a &emining trip&r."
		""
		"Gather &l&cany&r of the requested &dRaw Ores&r to complete this quest!"
	]
	quest.1ECBA1CBFFB9F625.quest_subtitle: "Isn't it ironic... don't you think?"
	quest.1ECBA1CBFFB9F625.title: "Iron, Iron, Iron!"
	quest.1F2359106FC95603.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3Rock Breaker&r generates different types of igneous Rocks. In order to operate, &9Water&r and &cLava&r (doesn't need to be source blocks) must both be adjacent to it. Those rocks might be pulverized and electrolyzed into certain materials."
		""
		"Certain rocks, such as &b&cRed Granite&r, need, at minimum, &5EV&r power to generate."
		""
		"&eAny&r Rock Breaker will complete this Quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Obsidian requiring Redstone to generate is in reference to an ancient Minecraft bug, &7MC-4239&f. Placing Redstone where the Cobblestone would go in a cobble generator would make it generate Obsidian instead. This bug was resolved in snapshot 14w25b for Minecraft 1.8, over 9 years ago at the time of writing!"
	]
	quest.1F2359106FC95603.quest_subtitle: "What is this, Skyblock?"
	quest.1F2359106FC95603.title: "Cobble is Life"
	quest.1F44B03267656D82.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.1F571B9E1555DA04.quest_desc: [
		"You're going to want to use the &3LCR&r recipe for your first &aEpichlorohydrin&r."
		""
		"This recipe requires &aPropene&r, which means that &dOil Processing&r and &dFuel Cracking&r are now necessary ventures. We're truly sorry if you've been dragging your heels!"
		""
		"It's quite important that you make your first &3Distillation Tower&r before progressing to the right."
		""
		"Last of all, if you haven't noticed, you can loop the &dSalt Water&r byproduct to bootstrap the &dSodium Hydroxide&r."
	]
	quest.1F571B9E1555DA04.quest_subtitle: "Putting the \"Epic\" in \"Epichlorohydrin\""
	quest.1F571B9E1555DA04.title: "Epichlorohydrin"
	quest.1F572D638AAACA21.quest_desc: [
		"Electrotine is important for progression in &6HV&r. It centrifuges into Electrum (a source of Gold and Silver), and Redstone."
		""
		"Saltpeter is used in a few reactions, and... the other two ores here are pretty average."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Does the word \"Nikolite\" ring a bell? It's pretty much Electrotine's great-ancestor, hailing from RedPower."
	]
	quest.1F572D638AAACA21.quest_subtitle: "Source of Potassium, Electrum"
	quest.1F572D638AAACA21.title: "Saltpeter"
	quest.1F6F9D8EB4E53575.quest_desc: ["The longbow has increased drawtime in comparison to a standard bow but it has much more strength and will do increased damage."]
	quest.1F6F9D8EB4E53575.title: "Longbow"
	quest.1F8C64E530FADD43.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.1FA308C8C319403E.quest_subtitle: "Found by using a brush on Suspicious Sand in the Desert."
	quest.1FA308C8C319403E.title: "Dig up a &eNecklace of the Desert"
	quest.1FA44E8FEE004AB4.title: "Rope coil"
	quest.1FBD746595917646.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of fabric will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from shepard villagers."
	]
	quest.1FCF2C103E25972B.quest_desc: [
		"&aBlue Alloy&r is an excellent Cable material for &6HV&r power."
		""
		"Nothing is preventing you from using it for &bMV&r power too! Make sure that you don't overvolt your machines, though."
		""
		"Superconductors for both &bMV&r and &6HV&r are unlocked... later."
		""
		"&aElectrotine&r is obtained from the &cNether&r, so don't craft it in the Mixer!"
		""
		"Furthermore, &aElectrotine&r can be separated for &dElectrum&r and &dRedstone&r."
	]
	quest.1FCF2C103E25972B.quest_subtitle: "You're blue now... that's my alloy"
	quest.1FCF2C103E25972B.title: "Blue Alloy"
	quest.1FEF7345C422F415.quest_desc: ["Создайте &bмогучую флейту сирены&r."]
	quest.1FFD2242B94A7378.quest_desc: [
		"&bFluid Pipes&r will transport &7Steam&r between machines for you."
		""
		"Each Pipe has a certain throughput in mB/t, and a &6Temperature Limit&r. This is relevant right now, as Steam will burn Wooden Pipes. Some pipes have &bspecial&r attributes you don't need to worry about for now."
		""
		"Each material has several sizes for Pipes. The bigger the Pipe, the &ahigher&r the throughput, but the more &dexpensive&r the craft. For example, a normal &6Bronze Fluid Pipe&r transfers 120 mB/t. (It also has a 1,200 mB internal buffer!)"
		""
		"Get any &6Bronze Fluid Pipe&r to complete this quest. The &6small&r and &enormal&r ones in particular are used in other recipes as well."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aReminder:&r 1 second = 20 ticks... assuming the server isn't lagging."
		""
		"&dNote:&r GT6-style Pipes are enabled. It means that placing Pipes connects them only to the block they were placed against. To open more connections, use your Wrench on the pipe."
		""
		"You can also shift-right click with your Wrench to disable input from a side. This can help counteract sloshing &7(liquids travelling in an undesired direction)&r."
	]
	quest.1FFD2242B94A7378.quest_subtitle: "Liquids, gases... we don't discriminate"
	quest.1FFD2242B94A7378.title: "Fluid Pipes"
	quest.2001CB4968D3E0A2.quest_desc: [
		"More GregTech tools are required for progression - here are the ones to lay eyes on."
		""
		"&9&lWrench:&r A crafting tool, but also the correct tool for GregTech machines... perfect if you think using pickaxes is unethical. It can also double as a &6wrench for other mods&r. Right-click allows you to set the output side of GregTech machines, and sneak-right-clicking rotates machines."
		""
		"&9&lFile:&r A crafting tool... and that's it. Yay!"
		""
		"&9&lSaw:&r Yet another crafting tool. If we were any more evil, we would force its use if you wanted to obtain 4 Planks and 4 Sticks from their respective crafting recipes. That being said, you can still use it to get &a6 Planks per Log&r, if you wish."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eNote:&r Any Quest with GregTech tools can be completed with the tool crafted from any material, not just the one displayed."
	]
	quest.2001CB4968D3E0A2.title: "Important Tools"
	quest.203A4D6E314685E3.quest_desc: ["Сэндвич из хлеба и мяса... Звучит забавно."]
	quest.203A4D6E314685E3.title: "Бутерброды"
	quest.2045E4A6728C750B.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &dдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.2045E4A6728C750B.title: "Броня из драконостали"
	quest.2050D2FF42E29F6D.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2050D2FF42E29F6D.quest_subtitle: "Getting these steel hatches will be essential for your quarry to use up their drills and give out their results."
	quest.2050D2FF42E29F6D.title: "Advance, advance, advance!"
	quest.206FE38B596D60E7.quest_desc: [
		"The Drawer Key will allow you to lock an item to a storage drawer slot. This will lock that item into that slot, even when all items are removed from the drawer."
		""
		"The Quantify Key will allow you to show/hide the storage drawer display of the number of items contained on the face of the drawer."
	]
	quest.2078EB76D829E0AB.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.208877D74542C6A7.quest_desc: ["bauxite :o"]
	quest.208DE0E29C636F41.quest_desc: [
		"It can combine Deuterium, Tritium, and/or Helium-3 into Helium Plasma, the most powerful fuel in the game!"
		""
		"However, it requires a large amount of energy to ignite the reaction."
	]
	quest.208DE0E29C636F41.quest_subtitle: "The Fusion Reactor is the ultimate energy source, to make it work requires a large amount of energy and it can combine Deuterium, Tritium, and/ or Helium-3 into Helium Plasma."
	quest.20A0931389DD2EA6.quest_desc: [
		"Press iron ingots and coal in a heated basin to create cast iron."
		"Press iron ingots by itself in a heated basin to create industrial iron."
	]
	quest.20AD73B935309188.quest_desc: [
		"Encoded templates must be delegated to template suppliers on the same network as the processing processor itself."
		""
		"When the processing processor then needs to process the main result of that template, it delegates this to the template supplier."
		""
		"Typically, the template supplier then sends the ingredients to a neighboring unit (such as a molecular assembler for recipe creation), and creation continues once the result is back on the network."
		""
		"This can be accomplished by sending the processing result back to the template provider, the ME interface, or any other method that would import the processing result into the network."
		""
		"Molecular assemblers are smart enough to automatically return the cooking result to the same template supplier that provided the ingredients."
	]
	quest.20AD73B935309188.quest_subtitle: "Recipes should be coded into templates so that they can be used when creating processors."
	quest.20B98506962B8B17.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Electric Blast Furnace&r requires a &3Muffler Hatch&r to run. This hatch must be &cunobstructed&r so it can output its beautiful smoke particles."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GregTech 5, polluting multiblocks had Muffler Hatches. The higher tier the hatch, the lower the Pollution output."
		""
		"&oPollution had... interesting... effects, such as turning grass and dirt into sand."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When a recipe is performed, there is a small chance for the &3Muffler Hatch&r to give bonus items - typically tiny Dusts of Ash. These items can be processed for some helpful resources."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Do &onot&r try to automate the extraction of items from the &3Muffler Hatch&r! It's not intended to be an automation challenge, as it voids excess contents when full, so don't worry about it stopping machines from running."
		""
		"Muffler Hatches in GTCEu are more about pure aesthetic (c'mon, you can't deny that those particles look good!) and small rewards, rather than punishing game mechanics."
	]
	quest.20B98506962B8B17.title: "Muffler Hatches"
	quest.20CE45C10A58D357.quest_desc: [
		"Don't think that's all—the “Create Aeronautics” mod has been added to the build, allowing you to build your own vehicles, structures, airplanes, and more."
		""
		"Currently, it works fairly well with “Create Big Cannons,” but it &4can cause the game to crash.&r"
	]
	quest.20CE45C10A58D357.title: "Transport"
	quest.20D6B44932002AC1.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.20E373424804CEDF.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.20F99CBAD8D587DA.quest_desc: ["Certus Quartz is the foundation of all Applied Energistics (AE2) technologies. It can be found as ore or grown from seeds."]
	quest.20F99CBAD8D587DA.title: "Certus Quartz"
	quest.2124BF15006733D5.quest_desc: [
		"This prospector boasts a &6higher range&r than its &7LV&r counterpart."
		""
		"Sneak right-clicking with the Prospector in your hand will change its mode to &6Fluid Prospection&r. This will instead display the base &dyield&r of Fluid veins, along with how full they are."
		""
		"&9Reminder:&r The yield of a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r is directly proportional to the \"fullness\" of the vein. When low enough, the output will default to a yield that can be defined in the CEu config."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Tip:&r When the fullness drops below 30% &7(alright, rough estimate)&r, you should consider moving to another vein for the sake of power-to-yield efficiency. Aiming for the &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r in &5EV&r may interest you, as not only does it significantly boost the output, but it also reduces the rate at which it drains the vein!"
		""
		"&cCaution:&r Due to a bug, the Prospector display may be offset by one chunk, so avoid placing your Rig in the corners of a fluid vein, or you may end up pumping the wrong fluid!"
	]
	quest.2124BF15006733D5.quest_subtitle: "Fluids just got easier"
	quest.2124BF15006733D5.title: "HV Prospector"
	quest.21257050C6608D6E.quest_subtitle: "The Energy Acceptor converts energy from external systems into AE and stores it in the network.The following energy systems are supported: Forge Energy / Redstone Flux 2 FE = 1 AE."
	quest.21257050C6608D6E.title: "Powering Your Network 1"
	quest.213211A0BC475C32.quest_desc: [
		"This was touched upon in the &5EV&r chapter, but we'll focus on what this distillation gets you here."
		""
		"The Nitrogen output is &bsubstantial&r, and can help you keep any &ePyrolyse Ovens&r running. You should buffer some of the Nitrogen so you can &aboost your EBFs&r - faster recipe times save your sanity and energy in equal measures."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Helium and Argon yields are low, but ideally you can run the Air Distillation as a &dpassive process&r every so often to keep your supplies topped up. Both are used to &aboost EBF speeds&r."
		""
		"&bCrushed Ice&r is... well, &bCrushed Ice&r. Maybe you could open a cocktail bar?"
	]
	quest.213211A0BC475C32.quest_subtitle: "Nitrogen, Helium, Argon...."
	quest.213211A0BC475C32.title: "Liquid Air"
	quest.2140BB56455664BA.quest_subtitle: "Use a Planar Stabilizer to craft a powerful belt attachment"
	quest.2144B6314F3B0C28.quest_desc: ["Создайте сыр из светящихся спор, которые можно собрать с адских деревьев."]
	quest.2144B6314F3B0C28.title: "Светящийся сыр"
	quest.21569BB793FFB579.quest_desc: ["Немалое количество листьев."]
	quest.21569BB793FFB579.title: "Чайный магнат"
	quest.215EF29F7DD6B37C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.216E5A3574AC08BF.quest_desc: [
		"This part of the chain starts by obtaining some &aRarest Metal Mixture&r."
		""
		"You'll need at least an &9IV&r &3Large Chemical Reactor&r, but the average power draw isn't too bad."
		""
		"&dChlorine&r is fully looped, and &dHydrogen&r is slightly negative &7(&ounless you put Acidic Osmium Solution in the Distillation Tower and electrolyze the water back... &8on second thoughts, don't do that&r&8)."
		""
		"&aIridium&r is required to progress through &9IV&r, so get your PGS line automated ASAP!"
	]
	quest.216E5A3574AC08BF.title: "Iridium and Osmium"
	quest.216F8320B52B65C1.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of wood will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from fletcher villagers."
	]
	quest.217123F78C8C807C.quest_desc: ["Из местного камня &eизвестняка&r, можно создать оружие дальнего и ближнего боя - копьё."]
	quest.2171AF09E76A5968.quest_desc: [
		"The de-facto Rare Earth vein for progression in &5EV&r... and onwards."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This vein was bugged for quite some time. It's never actually contained any Monazite, and nobody realised (well, nobody brought it up!) for many, many months. Did you notice?"
	]
	quest.2171AF09E76A5968.quest_subtitle: "Source of Rare Earth, Neodymium, Fluorine"
	quest.2171AF09E76A5968.title: "Bastnatite"
	quest.2188E4F0F1D67AF7.quest_desc: [
		"In these versions of the modpack, &4the story has not been fully developed&r. Please wait for updates!"
		""
		"The idea is that you will have to travel through different worlds in search of the &5Eternal Core&r in order to activate the mechanism and &5stop the paradoxes&r. "
	]
	quest.2188E4F0F1D67AF7.title: "Story"
	quest.2191CEB9D0802C27.quest_desc: ["Из некрома можно сделать прочные и эффективные инструменты."]
	quest.2191CEB9D0802C27.title: "Некромиевые интрументы"
	quest.219B4AC46BE85484.quest_desc: ["Специально для того, чтобы показать всем ваши творения."]
	quest.219B4AC46BE85484.title: "Выставка"
	quest.21A60BD5532EF9F6.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &bсамку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &bбестиарии&r."]
	quest.21A60BD5532EF9F6.quest_subtitle: "&bСинее"
	quest.21D02F5303F582A4.title: "Storage Upgrades"
	quest.21F70EACF6D81E6A.quest_desc: [
		"This jetpack enables flight, and requires energy."
		""
		"Charge it like you would charge a Battery."
		""
		"Press &4H&r (default) to enable Hover Mode."
		""
		"&o&8(Yeah, yeah, a jetpack is supposed to work off \"propellants\". Y'all are always here to nitpick.)&r"
	]
	quest.21F70EACF6D81E6A.quest_subtitle: "...still not quite there."
	quest.21F70EACF6D81E6A.title: "I Believe I Can Fly II"
	quest.220063A9A8F1D260.quest_desc: ["More chaotic, higher potential."]
	quest.2202AA5DC6DB0A26.quest_desc: [
		"&bMV&r Batteries will appeal to you if you want to buffer Energy, just like &7LV&r."
		""
		"The cost in &aSodium&r, &aLithium&r or &aCadmium&r jumps up to 8 dusts, so you should use whatever you have the most of. The difference in capacity isn't &7THAT&r huge, after all!"
		""
		"Get &eeither&r Battery to complete the Quest."
	]
	quest.2202AA5DC6DB0A26.quest_subtitle: "Baby Got Battery"
	quest.2202AA5DC6DB0A26.title: "Better Batteries"
	quest.221923EEDAEE1BEE.title: "Defeat the &6Sun Spirit"
	quest.2230589E0FCA8FDD.title: "Netherite-iron"
	quest.223778AA0A254150.quest_desc: ["Броня, принадлежавшая некогда очень опытному вору. Это идеально пошитый тканевый доспех не сковывает движений и позволяет оставаться незаметным даже на самых опасных заданиях. Поговаривают, что он даже приносит удачу владельцу."]
	quest.223778AA0A254150.title: "Поножи вора"
	quest.2242D415480E8057.quest_desc: ["Using fire ingots, create armour and tools with magical properties."]
	quest.225F57C95C6D7650.quest_desc: [
		"We know... this isn't actually gated behind &dIndium&r. However, you gotta trust us - this is the better recipe, so we don't want you wasting your time."
		""
		"&aQubit CPUs&r are used in the production of &1Quantum&r Processors."
	]
	quest.225F57C95C6D7650.quest_subtitle: "This actually has no relation to Quantum"
	quest.225F57C95C6D7650.title: "Qubit CPUs"
	quest.2262AB9F934165D0.title: "Steel Ingot"
	quest.226675C1209D3F9A.quest_desc: [
		"&dUr-Gast&r - A huge flying monster with immense strength and speed. He is able to summon small gasts in battle. "
		""
	]
	quest.226675C1209D3F9A.title: "Ur-Gast"
	quest.227177C9C7B62C0C.quest_desc: ["Half-size 2x2 storage drawers will store 4 stacks of an item per drawer (16 stacks overall)."]
	quest.227177C9C7B62C0C.title: "Half Storage Drawer: Four Items "
	quest.2273DD7E5CD49017.quest_desc: [
		"All four output Dusts obtained from Clay electrolysis are immensely useful."
		""
		"We'll ask you to give us a total of &a416 Clay Dust&r for this quest. You may also want to look into other sources of similar materials, such as &aSodalite&r. Check EMI for some ideas."
		""
		"You should use the Sodium and/or Lithium to make some &6MV Batteries&r."
		""
		"Grr, all this useless &dWater&r you're getting keeps clogging the machine! Maybe you should deal with it by using a &3Voiding Cover&r."
	]
	quest.2273DD7E5CD49017.quest_subtitle: "Clay is an extremely &mbalanced&r useful material for electrolysis"
	quest.2273DD7E5CD49017.title: "A Balanced Quest"
	quest.227A16C1E794FF69.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &2мирмекса&r."]
	quest.227D89550BB9BD55.quest_desc: [
		"&aRefinery Gas&r, &aLPG&r and &aMethane&r are &9Gas Fuels&r. LPG (Liquid Petroleum Gas) is a mix of hydrocarbons typically used in heating appliances."
		""
		"Refinery Gas is obtained either through &dNatural Gas&r or &dLight Oil&r, the latter yielding more, yet requiring an extra step of distillation."
		""
		"Use of a &3Centrifuge&r to separate into &aLPG&r and &aMethane&r should always be done, as it's practically free."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&a&aLPG&r and &aMethane&r are burned in a &3Gas Turbine&r. Among the other fuel options, they are the easier to set up which makes them excellent to get started. Their drawback is that they cannot be refined further, so upgrading the &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r may be a top priority if you stick to this fuel source."
		""
		"&aMethane&r can also be obtained from a few &anatural sources&r. &eBetween us&r, they're memes, but you can explore them if you wish. Ultimately, your power source is your choice."
	]
	quest.227D89550BB9BD55.quest_subtitle: "Whoever smelt it..."
	quest.227D89550BB9BD55.title: "The Church of Natural Farts"
	quest.227DBA8836021B0B.quest_desc: [
		"In Ars Nouveau, the power system for machines is called &9Source&r."
		""
		"To start collecting some Source, we'll need a Source Jar."
		""
		"Source can also be moved with buckets, or by breaking and picking up Source Jars."
	]
	quest.227DBA8836021B0B.quest_subtitle: "Storing Source"
	quest.228379C559E390B8.quest_desc: [
		"Nothing special here. Any ores that you don't wash in novelty chemicals simply need to be washed in water with an &dOre Washer&r. You should use Distilled Water, as it cuts the recipe time down by &650%&r. Set up a couple of Distilleries on-site and buffer into an appropriately-sized &aSuper Tank&r."
		""
		"If you don't care about the byproducts in this section, you can wash the ores in &bregular water&r without a configured circuit to process &225x&r faster, but &4without&r byproducts."
	]
	quest.228379C559E390B8.quest_subtitle: "The \"distinguished\" version of water"
	quest.228379C559E390B8.title: "Washing with Distilled Water"
	quest.22997534983F6812.quest_desc: [
		"Make the listed molds for future alloy smelting. Be sure to make &aMolds&r - don't make &cExtruder Shapes&r, as they're used in a different machine."
		""
		"The reward for this quest will alleviate &da lot of pain&r when it comes to crafting &bGears&r."
	]
	quest.22997534983F6812.quest_subtitle: "Reduce the amount of malding by molding"
	quest.22997534983F6812.title: "Malding"
	quest.22A1A629AF754066.quest_desc: [
		"The Autoclave is typically the last step of Gem Processing. It is used turn a select few &aGem Dusts&r back into regular Gems."
		""
		"It's veeeery slow - thus, it is generally not advised to crush gem ores at all, as the recovery process is too expensive."
		""
		"&9Note:&r In this modpack, the Autoclave is required to make &5Fluix Crystals&r if you're to progress in Applied Energistics. Sorry."
	]
	quest.22A1A629AF754066.quest_subtitle: "\"Oops, I turned my Diamonds into dust\""
	quest.22A1A629AF754066.title: "Basic Autoclave"
	quest.22A1CEAE96D66DC5.quest_subtitle: "A Player Transmitter will charge items in the player's inventory or equipped armor/trinkets."
	quest.22A1CEAE96D66DC5.title: "Walking Battery"
	quest.22B5AD670496C02D.quest_desc: [
		"We &lSINCERELY&r hope at &cno&r point you made the &7LV&r Extruder, because only the &bMV&r Extruder is actually useful. If you did, immediately &arecycle it&r through the Arc Furnace."
		""
		"The Extruder shapes solid materials into (almost!) any form using &aIngots&r. This is a great way to reduce the amount of microcrafting, as well as keeping a high conversion ratio."
		""
		"The Extruder can make &6Rods&r, &6Bolts&r, &6&6Small Gears&r, &6Gears&r, and &6&6Rings&r at the highest efficiency in a single step!"
		""
		"You may also like to use it for &dPipes&r, &dLong Rods&r, and &dRotors&r."
	]
	quest.22B5AD670496C02D.quest_subtitle: "The biggest upgrade you'll make"
	quest.22B5AD670496C02D.title: "Advanced Extruder"
	quest.22B7662B6ABBA0B6.quest_desc: ["Кузнечные шаблоны, которые можно найти по всему незеру."]
	quest.22B7662B6ABBA0B6.title: "Кузнечные шаблоны"
	quest.22D83509D938F039.quest_desc: [
		"If you heeded our suggestion for Peaceful mode, you shouldn't need to defend yourself from pesky mobs - but this armor provides some nice QoL that you may enjoy!"
		""
		"&9Helmet:&r Provides &dNight vision&r (the default keybind is &4M&r, but check for conflicts)"
		""
		"&9Chestplate:&r Provides nothing interesting right now, but can be further upgraded into the &aAdvanced&r version at the very end of &6HV&r."
		""
		"&9Leggings:&r Provides nothing special... perhaps we should have given it a small speed boost?"
		""
		"&9Boots:&r Provides &dStep Assist&r. Yes, you read that right!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This armor was inspired by IndustrialCraft, but its first implementation within the \"GTCE ecosystem\" came with Nuke Powered Utils, an addon mod to GTCE."
	]
	quest.22D83509D938F039.quest_subtitle: "GregTech and armour - a match made in heaven!"
	quest.22D83509D938F039.title: "Nanomuscles, son!"
	quest.22DBD0535B0A64C9.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.22E1A465FAF7EAA2.quest_desc: ["Fully absorbs your fall without dealing damage."]
	quest.23147B94406A7B99.quest_subtitle: "A Binding Card is used to connect a Player Transmitter to a machinery that can wirelessly connect to each other and charge. Only works in the same dimension."
	quest.2316F905D5CEF896.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.2316F905D5CEF896.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.233BA969DA5AA027.quest_subtitle: "Spawns randomly underground in boss rooms"
	quest.234F92A0F8D245E0.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &1морской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.234F92A0F8D245E0.quest_subtitle: "&1Тёмно-синяя"
	quest.234F92A0F8D245E0.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.235991BD8E068168.quest_desc: ["Улучшенная версия шотгана. Теперь его можно заряжать определённое количество раз, что позволит контроллировать мощность выстрела. Только не перестарайтесь."]
	quest.236C886D50A99785.quest_desc: [
		"Mine some &dSulfur&r from the Nether."
		""
		"If Lava is \"too hot to handle\", we've included a &6direct crafting recipe&r for &aPotions of Fire Resistance&r. EMI might look a little confusing, but don't worry - you can use &bWater Bottles&r in the potion recipe."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o With the existence of &6Small Sulfur Ores&f scattered in GregTech 5 ore veins, you could mine enough Sulfur in the Overworld to skip having to visit the Nether. Sounds broken, but it was still as much of a grind as Nether travel!"
	]
	quest.236C886D50A99785.quest_subtitle: "A little bit of exploring never hurt anyone"
	quest.236C886D50A99785.title: "S is for Sulfur"
	quest.237EEDF8D3F170DA.quest_desc: [
		"A feature of the &5Soft Mallet&r that you may be aware of is its ability to &6pause machines&r. However, did you know that if you &bsneak whilst pausing a machine&r, it'll tell the machine to continue operating until it finishes its recipe?"
		""
		"This is &2perfect&r if you need to make changes to a multiblock but don't want to &evoid items&r, as unforming a multiblock will void all inputs."
	]
	quest.237EEDF8D3F170DA.quest_subtitle: "Shoutout to Yung Onion"
	quest.237EEDF8D3F170DA.title: "I'm Fetching Me Mallet!"
	quest.23A7E6D95549B1F8.quest_desc: [
		"&aEnder Fluid Link Covers&r are &dGregTech&r's &r&3Ender Tanks&r. Each Cover sends fluids through a frequency defined by an &68-digit hexadecimal number&r (0-9, then A-F for each digit). That gives you &64.29 billion&r channels to work with! Ender fluid Link Covers work as long as their chunk is loaded - regardless of distance or dimension."
		""
		"Setting the mode to Import will &o&c&opull&r fluids from the world location it is attached to, while Export will &o&9&opush&r fluids to the world. Each channel has a buffer of &d64 buckets&r."
		""
		"You can also make similar &3Ender Item Link Covers&r to transport items, these have the same mechanics as the fluid ones. Craft any of them to complete this quest"
		""
		"Lastly, clicking on the &eLock&r in the ui lock the cover to your own &dprivate channel&r, which is helpful if you're playing on a server."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can assign a description to each channel in the cover, and list all of them. I recommend you set up a system to organise all those channels. I would also advise against using the default channel (FFFFFFFF) in all cases."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Before these were added to GTm, we had &dEnder Storage&r&o in the pack. If you are still using them we &lhighly&r&o recommend changing them over to the &aGregTech covers&r&o, which can be done in a crafting table."
	]
	quest.23A7E6D95549B1F8.quest_subtitle: "Ender? I ha- Ok, this joke is old"
	quest.23A7E6D95549B1F8.title: "Ender Fluid Linking"
	quest.23B078514FB4A215.quest_desc: [
		"The &3ME Tag Storage Bus&r is crucial to send tagged items to a desired destination. It does what it says in the tin - simply set its filter by clicking on it, then any items that enter your AE2 network that &ematch the programmed Item Tag&r will be sent to the inventory attached to the Bus."
		""
		"This can be particularly useful in the event that you wish to use a &afiltered subnet&r to process ore."
		""
		"Remember to set a &5high priority&r if you want to prioritise Ore Processing!"
	]
	quest.23B078514FB4A215.quest_subtitle: "Casting a Wider Net"
	quest.23B078514FB4A215.title: "Tag - You're It!"
	quest.2423918C4C6A18A5.quest_desc: [
		"The Advanced Nano Chestplate combines protection, a personal battery and an &6enhanced Jetpack&r, all in one."
		""
		"To &denable charging&r, sneak right-click with it in your hand, then equip it (There may be an occasional bug where it refuses to charge, but you'll forgive us, right?)."
		""
		"Note that this stores &oa lot&r of energy, and uses it fairly fast. You may want to invest in a &3HV Turbo Charger&r."
	]
	quest.2423918C4C6A18A5.quest_subtitle: "Quite the microcrafting project... but worth it"
	quest.2423918C4C6A18A5.title: "Better Flight!"
	quest.24366846FDA52CE3.quest_desc: [
		"Build the structure displayed with Fusion Glass in &aEMI&r."
		""
		"To save on Fusion Casings, fit Input + Output Hatches wherever you can (as displayed in the structure)."
		""
		"The &aFusion Reactor Mk2&r is even more expensive than the Mk1! The key difference is that it has a higher &6Energy To Start&r than the Mk1, allowing you to run new recipes."
		""
		"It can also overclock lower voltage recipes, such as those in the Mk1 reactor. See the Mk1's quest for how these mechanics work."
	]
	quest.24366846FDA52CE3.quest_subtitle: "Fusion just got more expensive..."
	quest.24366846FDA52CE3.title: "Fusion Reactor II"
	quest.24535DA01189CC75.quest_subtitle: "One of the most expensive drills to create, but it is useful for digging up iridium and uranium ores."
	quest.245946FF40FEFEE2.quest_desc: ["The Axe head allows you to chop tree logs and strip them just like vanilla axes."]
	quest.245FCF3E018D9760.quest_desc: [
		"In last update we added many artifacts They can make it easier to beat bosses—even if they're optional &0(for now)&r and simply make the gameplay more enjoyable"
		""
	]
	quest.245FCF3E018D9760.title: "Relics"
	quest.248343A8203E7CDC.quest_desc: ["Single Headed tools are the most simple tools you can make."]
	quest.24866E83B280C9AB.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cracker&r is a multiblock built with the sole purpose of cracking fluids. It comes with all the recipes of &3Chemical Reactor&r Cracking, but it is &6lossless&r."
		""
		"This is a great way to save a lot of Fuel in the long term!"
		""
		"Higher Coil tiers provide a small energy discount - up to 70% with the best Coils available."
	]
	quest.24866E83B280C9AB.quest_subtitle: "You Crack Me Up"
	quest.24866E83B280C9AB.title: "Multiblock Cracking"
	quest.249374557D095913.quest_desc: [
		"Use Mortars or a Macerator (your choice) to microcraft your way to Glass Dust, which you can then turn into a &aGlass Block&r."
		""
		"If you are lost, a more detailed guide for this process is on the next page, but &dwe urge you to nose around EMI&r and figure out the recipe on your own. Being able to navigate EMI and parse recipes is an &6essential skill&r for completing this pack."
		""
		"Glass will be easier later on. You've probably already noticed that juicy &3Arc Furnace&r recipe - don't worry, we'll get there soon."
		""
		"Glass tubes will be required for your first Electronic Circuit."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Lost? Worry not!"
		""
		"First, use a &3method of pulverisation&r to turn Sand into &9Quartz Sand Dust&r."
		""
		"Next, crush down some Flint into &9Flint Dust&r, and split this dust into tiny piles in a crafting grid."
		""
		"Combine the two into &9Glass Dust&r, which can be molded into Glass in an Alloy Smelter with a &9Block Mold&r."
		""
		"Finally, Glass!"
	]
	quest.249374557D095913.quest_subtitle: "Must be satisfying, right?"
	quest.249374557D095913.title: "Glass, at last!"
	quest.249B9E104CAF5FE6.quest_desc: [
		"&3Voiding Covers&r can be attached to GregTech Machines, Crates or Drums. They will void stuff you don't want. How fancy!"
		""
		"For machines, it will only void items in the Output slots. The Input slots are ignored."
		""
		"You can attach a &aFilter&r for more precise voiding."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"An advanced version also exists, which requires a &dMV Circuit&r. It enables voiding above a set threshold - great for for overflow control."
		""
		"&9Note:&r They default to being switched off, to prevent accidental voiding. Right-click them with a &5Soft Mallet&r to activate them."
		""
		"Obtaining &eany&r Voiding Cover will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.249B9E104CAF5FE6.quest_subtitle: "The best mechanic - making an item or fluid disappear!"
	quest.249B9E104CAF5FE6.title: "Voiding Covers"
	quest.249FA99AADAC3710.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLarge Titanium Boiler&r is yet another steam boiler. It's even more efficient than the previous ones, and produces more steam too. However, Steam &cbarely scales&r at this voltage."
		""
		"This thing absolutely isn't worth it, and there are so many better options for power by this point, so you should avoid making this. The better options require &9EV energy hatches&r, which are later in the chapter."
		""
		"&eNote&r: The LTB is so awful that we'll let you skip this quest (for completion progress) by clicking the Checkmark. You don't actually have to craft one."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT5u, players can construct another multiblock - the Large Heat Exchanger. It's also constructed with titanium, but produced Superheated Steam from hot IC2 coolant, or lava. This was a much better than regular steam, and was actually viable! This might make its way to CEu in the future."
	]
	quest.249FA99AADAC3710.quest_subtitle: "We're gonna need more charcoal"
	quest.249FA99AADAC3710.title: "Worse Combustion"
	quest.24A4F1AA0BFFE867.title: "Electric blast furnace"
	quest.24A90D07C3A35370.quest_desc: [
		"By collecting Air with a &6Gas Collector&r and cooling it to Liquid state with a &3Vacuum Freezer&r, you can then distill the liquid Air for a plethora of valuable resources."
		""
		"You thought that was all? Air collection isn't limited to the &2Overworld&r - whilst you'll require a higher-tier Distillation Tower to distill the \"higher\" tiers of liquid Air, you can also process air from the &4Nether&r and the &5End&r. This process is mostly optional, but you'll definitely find it to be a rewarding one."
	]
	quest.24A90D07C3A35370.quest_subtitle: "Things are up in the air right now..."
	quest.24A90D07C3A35370.title: "All Kinds Of Air (Distillation)"
	quest.24B4D9608718EE27.quest_desc: ["A rarely used machine. It uses magnetism to separate some Magnetic ores and gain additional &6Byproducts&r you would not obtain otherwise."]
	quest.24B4D9608718EE27.quest_subtitle: "Magnets... how do they work?"
	quest.24B4D9608718EE27.title: "Basic Electromagnetic Separator"
	quest.24F0454B9A090C44.quest_desc: [
		"This is the main material for &cZPM&r. Having this in stock will be a test of your Platinum processing, so this is a &6pre-emptive warning&r to stay on top of mining PGS-bearing ore."
		""
		"Prepare to make lots... after you make &9Fusion&r and &9Crystal Circuits&r. Tackle those before you try making this."
	]
	quest.24F0454B9A090C44.quest_subtitle: "Stargate's Strongest"
	quest.24F0454B9A090C44.title: "Naquadah Alloy"
	quest.25206FF0429DD30E.quest_desc: ["The Precision Mechanism is a complex component requiring multi-stage assembly using Deployers. It unlocks access to advanced Brass Age technologies."]
	quest.25206FF0429DD30E.title: "Precision Mechanism"
	quest.25289F9E8AE01C29.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack is intended as a guide on &b&lGregtech: Community Edition Unofficial Modern&r&r (also known as &aGTCEu Modern&r or &aCEu Modern&r), a continuation of &aGTCE&r - which is in itself a fork of Gregtech."
		""
		"New content has been added to every tier, even going up to &3Ultimate Voltage,&r and there is also a non-negligible amount of new &dQuality of Life&r."
		""
		"&aCEu Modern&r brings the mod up to date with &erecent versions&r of Minecraft &o(as of writing this)&r. You can open the questbook with the default keybind &6F4&r, but feel free to change it if it isn't to your tastes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This is a &2pure &lTech&r&2 modpack&r, focused on GregTech and its progression. You'll find &6no better place&r to learn about this mod and all the features it adds!"
		""
		"The questbook you're reading is &ebrimming with information&r to guide you through the modpack, so check it out if you find yourself getting lost.  We wrote it with both &dold-school veterans&r and &bnewcomers&r in mind."
	]
	quest.25289F9E8AE01C29.quest_subtitle: "We hope you enjoy your stay"
	quest.25289F9E8AE01C29.title: "Welcome to GregTech CEu!"
	quest.254982C1D77959B4.quest_desc: [
		"&dThe Twilight Forest&r is a world of eternal twilight, where many unknown creatures live. It is filled with magic and an atmosphere of mystery. You will have to fight many formidable opponents to get powerful artefacts."
		""
		"To open a portal to the twilight forest, you will need to break blocks of earth with 2x2 area, fill the resulting hole with water, plant flowers around this hole and throw a diamond into the water."
	]
	quest.254982C1D77959B4.title: "Enter to Twilight Forest"
	quest.2555C82BAA2865CD.quest_desc: ["Путешествуя в пустнях, вы сможете обнаружить загадочный храм со змеиными статуями. Отгодав загадки и пройдя тяжелые испытания, вы сможете попасть в подвал храма, где вас будет ждать &aмедуза горгона&r..."]
	quest.2555C82BAA2865CD.quest_subtitle: "Древнее существо, способная окаменять существ..."
	quest.255929EB845E200D.quest_desc: [
		"&lWhy go parallel?"
		""
		"&9-&r &4Parallelization is superior&r to overclocking! Take advantage of this for your passive setups such as Ore Processing or Oil Distilling."
		""
		"&9-&r &6Distinct buses&r: &3GCYM Machinery&r can accept multiple &3Input Buses&r. Use it for your pattern automation with &3Extruder&r, &3Engraver&r, and many other."
		""
		"Power cost is based on the current recipe being run, times the number of &4parallel&r being performed."
	]
	quest.255929EB845E200D.title: "Parallelisation"
	quest.2574E7CF699D5B45.quest_subtitle: "Breaking a log with an axe will destroy the entire tree attached. Sneaking while destroying a log will prevent this."
	quest.2574E7CF699D5B45.title: "Obtain a &2Wooden Log"
	quest.257DB4B39B2A928E.quest_desc: [
		"It's recommended that you &6put this machine off&r until you actually require it for for progression - explore elsewhere if you're fresh into &7LV&r."
		""
		"Some alloys previously made by hand can also be made in the mixer, except at &ahigher yield&r."
	]
	quest.257DB4B39B2A928E.quest_subtitle: "The Mixer mixes..."
	quest.257DB4B39B2A928E.title: "Basic Mixer"
	quest.2587BFD0D9F3FF4A.quest_desc: [
		"&aZPM Superconductors&r are a major gate between you and a &9Fusion Reactor Mk2&r, which uses copious amounts for its structure blocks."
		""
		"You can also use them to make &9Superconducting Coils&r for cheaper."
	]
	quest.2587BFD0D9F3FF4A.quest_subtitle: "Getting tired of all these pitch-black ingots yet?"
	quest.2587BFD0D9F3FF4A.title: "ZPM Superconductors"
	quest.258BFF29CB5486F8.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &bдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.258BFF29CB5486F8.title: "Инструменты из драконостали"
	quest.25966E7B57F97BA1.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &bчешую&r."]
	quest.25966E7B57F97BA1.quest_subtitle: "&bСиняя"
	quest.25A9FD3C44185B12.quest_desc: ["Из &cалых&r и &9лазурных&r магнитов можно создавать различные полезные и интересные вещи."]
	quest.25C5C1B8CDE2EB21.title: "Итальянская гаста"
	quest.25CC6F9D65A98A0E.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.25E90357BAFE1FF1.title: "Any valve handles"
	quest.25F5C7D646D4F0BE.title: "Атрибуты ведьмы"
	quest.260E516A219825A2.quest_desc: [
		"This vein is namely one of the few direct sources of Gold in the overworld."
		""
		"There are many other sources of Gold in GregTech, but you will likely see better yields of Gold if you obtain it by processing other resources."
		""
		"Vanadium Magnetite becomes more useful in &bMV&r, when you will centrifuge out the Vanadium within for Vanadium Steel."
	]
	quest.260E516A219825A2.quest_subtitle: "Source of Iron, Gold, Vanadium"
	quest.260E516A219825A2.title: "Magnetite"
	quest.2620A7CCFB446634.quest_subtitle: "As the name implies, Energizing Orb receives electric charge and uses it on items to upgrade machinery. The higher tier the material, the more power required to energize."
	quest.2625EC5BE51DE54D.quest_desc: [
		"Thermal Cells can be found in Ancient Bases as loot."
		""
		"They can be charged in Transfer Units attached to operating Core Extractor units. The side of the Transfer Unit must be pried off to be able to plug cells in."
	]
	quest.2625EC5BE51DE54D.title: "Thermal Cells and Recharging"
	quest.262AA679D42ECBF4.quest_desc: ["Очередные ингриденты для готовки."]
	quest.262AA679D42ECBF4.title: "Клубника и овёс"
	quest.26394C1290D70AB6.quest_desc: [
		"Alright... technically, obtaining &6HV&r Circuits and Stainless Steel lets you progress to &6HV&r - but let's not rush things."
		""
		"The first thing you should make with these is a &3MV Circuit Assembler&r to unlock the new tier of Circuits right away; cheaper recipes is the &dreal payoff&r here."
	]
	quest.26394C1290D70AB6.quest_subtitle: "...but hold on before getting too giddy"
	quest.26394C1290D70AB6.title: "First HV Circuits!"
	quest.264F1F2ED17FD212.quest_desc: [
		"To better navigate this dimension, you should create a &dmagic map&r!"
		""
		"&dFakelont&r - Roots of ancient trees that got their glowing property thanks to shards of magical stone that fell on them. Can be found underground."
		""
		"&dRaven Feather&r - Can be obtained by killing a raven that lives in the twilight forest."
		""
		"&dLightstone Dust&r - Can be obtained in Nezera by breaking a cluster of lightstone or by killing a firefly in the trees of the twilight forest with a bow."
	]
	quest.264F1F2ED17FD212.title: "Magic map"
	quest.264FA27F45BDDCFF.quest_subtitle: "Obtained by killing a Minotaur, found in swamp Labyrinths. Unlocks Hollow Hills."
	quest.264FA27F45BDDCFF.title: "Eat Meef Stroganoff"
	quest.2655B72C9FF3B372.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech doesn't provide ways to farm plants or trees, so we made a custom multiblock for the modpack!"
		""
		"The multiblock &3Greenhouse&r will be your source of &aWood&r and other plants if you wish."
		""
		"Its &aWood&r production should be enough to run &32 Pyrolyse Ovens&r at their lowest Power."
		""
		"You can also use this for automated &aResin&r. The yields are kept low to incentivize other rubber sources later in the game."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note: &rWith &d40 EU/t&r recipes, it needs either 1 &bMV&r energy hatch or 2 &7LV&r energy hatches. Multiblocks will &cnot&r use 2A of one tier to reach the next one for recipe voltage minimums. "
		""
		"In other words, the controller needs to say at least \"&bMV&r\" in the GUI to run recipes which say \"&bMV&r\" in EMI, even if they can draw enough EU/t with a lower tier hatch configuration."
		""
		"&9Note:&r The structure requires a lot of &9Wrought Iron&r. Make sure you have an &3Arc Furnace&r for that."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o We originally implemented a Chemical Reactor recipe for wood in the modpack to solve the tree problem. Our implementation turned out to be completely busted, so we decided that a rebalance was due. Hopefully, the Greenhouse is a happy middle ground."
	]
	quest.2655B72C9FF3B372.quest_subtitle: "The power of KubeJS"
	quest.2655B72C9FF3B372.title: "Greenhouse"
	quest.26575D4FEB3D3F62.quest_desc: [
		"A lot of &dKanthal&r will be required for the &aEV Motors&r. This may feel painful when you're on the edge of &5EV&r, but it won't be a problem later - trust us."
		""
		"&dNeodymium&r is the metal used for &aMagnetic Rods&r."
		""
		"&aAluminium Cables&r require &dPVC&r to be insulated."
		""
		"Lastly, you will need &4Radon&r for the &dQuantum Eyes&r in the &aEmitter&r recipe."
	]
	quest.26575D4FEB3D3F62.quest_subtitle: "Wait, no, don't leave!"
	quest.26575D4FEB3D3F62.title: "The \"Fun\" will never stop"
	quest.26667A49602865F4.quest_desc: ["Атмосферно."]
	quest.26667A49602865F4.title: "Кафе под открытым небом"
	quest.268A05DFD4D5427A.quest_subtitle: "Gatekeeper Houses can be found in most biomes"
	quest.268A05DFD4D5427A.title: "Obtain a &9Blue Journal &rfrom a Gatekeeper"
	quest.268C8F8048F99B46.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &dморской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.268C8F8048F99B46.quest_subtitle: "&dПурпурная"
	quest.268C8F8048F99B46.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.269C3BC39A0E74FD.quest_desc: ["Reveals more enchantment results in the enchanting table."]
	quest.269EBC3BD17F4D78.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони их хитина &eпустынного червя&r."]
	quest.269EBC3BD17F4D78.quest_subtitle: "&eТелесная"
	quest.269EBC3BD17F4D78.title: "Хитиновая броня"
	quest.26C43416F9427BB3.quest_desc: [
		"The &aPortable Scanner&r, or &aTricorder&r, is GTCEu's debug tool."
		""
		"Using it will show you a block's details, the details of the energy network, its current status and contents, and its impact on performance."
		""
		"It'll also display a percentage of fluid remaining in the fluid vein for the &3Fluid Rigs&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This little useful device comes from GregTech 5. It was extremely useful in the early days, because very little information (basically nothing) was given by GUIs or WAILA."
	]
	quest.26C43416F9427BB3.quest_subtitle: "For the nosiest GregTech players"
	quest.26C43416F9427BB3.title: "Tricorder"
	quest.26E587E34810A8FE.quest_desc: [
		"The Steam Quarry is a steam multiblock machine that consumes bronze drills, uses them to dig deeper than the bedrock and gives you back some ores, as you can see in REI."
		""
		"It's recommended that you have multiple SBFs running before you attempt to build it because it requires a lot of steel."
		""
	]
	quest.26E587E34810A8FE.quest_subtitle: "Here we are, it is time to assemble a Steam Quarry, an advanced machinery that uses bronze drills to dig for ores. This will be an expensive machinery but it will be one of your greatest investments of all."
	quest.26E587E34810A8FE.title: "Infinite resources?"
	quest.26E8E5C163340E5A.quest_desc: [
		"&bDigital fluid storage&r is pretty cool. Each &b1k ME Fluid Storage Cell&r holds up to &d5 types&r of fluid, and can hold &6over 8,000 buckets&r of those 5 fluid types! That's more than a &3Super Tank 2&r!"
		""
		"You may want to &4format&r Fluid Storage Cells to certain types to prevent the network from clogging. Make a &3Cell Workbench&r to do so."
	]
	quest.26E8E5C163340E5A.quest_subtitle: "\"Fluid Discretizer\"? Who's that?"
	quest.26E8E5C163340E5A.title: "Digital Fluid Storage"
	quest.26EA75D177BC496B.quest_subtitle: "Raids are started by killing Illager Captains, the same way as normal"
	quest.26EA75D177BC496B.title: "Defend a Village from a &4Raid"
	quest.26F5A04750F6B6DD.quest_desc: [
		"&3UV&r Components are a tad harder than &cZPM&r. "
		""
		"They use lots of &9Tritanium&r and &9Naquadria&r, so make sure your have enough Fusion Reactors, and a fast enough Naquadah Plant."
		""
		"They also need a lot more &9Computation&r, which means &3Advanced HPCA Components&r are now required!"
		""
		"Computation Needs for early &3UV&r:"
		""
		"- &a32 CWU/t&r: Basic &3UV&r Components and the Network Switch"
		"- &a48 CWU/t&r: &3UV&r Sensor, Emitter, and Field Generator"
	]
	quest.26F5A04750F6B6DD.quest_subtitle: "Prepare your Fusion Reactors!"
	quest.26F5A04750F6B6DD.title: "Total Euphoria"
	quest.271CE5C2B78A1EDC.quest_desc: [
		"This quest will cover the Tungsten Chain. &aTungsten&r is obtained from either &eTungstate&r or &eScheelite&r, which are part of the same vein in the End."
		""
		"Just like the &dRutile&r chain, you will only need to input one item type, and everything else will be looped perfectly!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You will need:"
		""
		"&9-&r One &3Chemical Bath&r, to make &dTungstic Acid&r."
		"&9-&r One &3Electrolyzer&r, to electrolyze &oboth&r Bath outputs."
		"&9-&r One &3Chemical Reactor&r, to loop &dHydrogen&r and &dChlorine&r back into &aHydrochloric Acid&r."
		""
		"You will be granted either Calcium or Lithium as a byproduct - it's on the house!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GTCE, Tungstate or Scheelite took 40sec and 4,000mB of Hydrogen @ 1920 EU/t to electrolyze into 1 Tungsten Dust. Even if it was simpler, it was much more expensive!"
	]
	quest.271CE5C2B78A1EDC.quest_subtitle: "All in one!"
	quest.271CE5C2B78A1EDC.title: "Tungsten Chain"
	quest.27239A694562172E.quest_desc: ["Трофеи за истребление хоглинов."]
	quest.27239A694562172E.title: "Убийца хоглинов"
	quest.27240865315F9530.quest_desc: [
		"Ever wanted your pipes to look &leven&r cooler? Now you can!"
		""
		"Fluid and Item Pipes can be placed inside of Frameboxes, giving your base an &6unparalleled level of beauty&r!"
		""
		"All you - dear player - need to do is right-click a frame onto a pipe &7(or a pipe onto a frame)&r, and you're done."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This is a GTCEu-original mechanic."
	]
	quest.27240865315F9530.quest_subtitle: "Spaghetti has never looked so swanky!"
	quest.27240865315F9530.title: "Aesthetic Ultra"
	quest.27BAA1F4DE80AC55.quest_subtitle: "Stores up to 200,000 AE. They do not accept power directly, but are used to add additional power storage to an already existing ME Network."
	quest.27BAA1F4DE80AC55.title: "Storing Energy 1"
	quest.27CD4319695039D1.quest_desc: ["The Large Cogwheel allows you to change the rotation speed when connected to a small cogwheel. This is a key element for controlling the speed of your mechanisms."]
	quest.27CD4319695039D1.title: "Large Cogwheel"
	quest.27D639418E232980.quest_desc: ["Из серебра можно сделать броню и оружие, включая метательные ножи."]
	quest.27D639418E232980.title: "Серебряное снаряжение"
	quest.27E4CBB51DBD27CD.quest_desc: [
		"Ropes are essentially reverse scaffolding: the can be continuously deployed downward from the same spot, and can be climbed without collision. This allows players to safely descend or ascend high altitudes, such as ravines or mountains."
		""
		"When placing Rope, you can use more ropes against the first one to deploy them downward. This will continuously extend a column of rope down to the bottom-most Y-level possible, allowing for easy and controllable descents into chasms, ravines or from high locations."
		""
		"To suppress rope deployment, simply sneak while placing it. If there's no space underneath to deploy, it will also place normally."
	]
	quest.286C78DD09FE49B1.quest_desc: [
		"The Workbench will be where all the magic will happen with Tetra."
		""
		"This block is created by right clicking a Crafting Table with the Wooden Hammer you just created."
		""
		"By right clicking the workbench it will open a menu where an item (which types can be seen below in the branching quests) can then be placed and modified."
	]
	quest.28847A536C38EEA0.title: "Transformer"
	quest.288CE4AA4C5AA8BF.quest_desc: [
		"Less common as a component, but used in a number of critical machines."
		""
		"When placed on a machine, conveyor modules will transfer items. You can configure them to import or export."
		""
		"They can also accept various &9Item Filters&r."
	]
	quest.288CE4AA4C5AA8BF.quest_subtitle: "A crafting component, but also a cover!"
	quest.28B46976C7954142.quest_desc: ["Броня, принадлежавшая некогда очень опытному вору. Это идеально пошитый тканевый доспех не сковывает движений и позволяет оставаться незаметным даже на самых опасных заданиях. Поговаривают, что он даже приносит удачу владельцу."]
	quest.28B46976C7954142.title: "Ботинки вора"
	quest.28ED66F775111A17.quest_desc: [
		"Yo, a quick note on &aIridium&r and &aOsmium&r. "
		""
		"We know, it's technically possible to obtain these materials now, but you should wait until you reach &9IV&r. Producing these materials will suck up a lot of your precious power... and you won't be able to smelt them into ingots until &9IV&r anyway!"
	]
	quest.28ED66F775111A17.quest_subtitle: "Hold your fire just for now"
	quest.28ED66F775111A17.title: "Iridium, Osmium, and EV"
	quest.292938760AB9A12B.quest_desc: [
		"Cells are an alternative form of Fluid storage. All Cell types with the same type and amount of Fluid inside them &6stack&r. They can be automatically filled with a &3Canning Machine&r."
		""
		"Cells hold &done bucket&r of Fluid."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Universal Cells hold up to &done bucket&r, but also can store &9fractions&r of Buckets. They're particularly ideal if you want to store leftover Fluid without crafting a whole Drum. "
		""
		"Cells made from higher tier materials can hold even more fluid, but &9Drums&r and &9Super Tanks&r will hold more by then."
		""
		"Like Drums, Cells can be placed into a crafting grid to clear their contents."
	]
	quest.292938760AB9A12B.quest_subtitle: "GTCE killed cell chemistry... GTCE killed Cells!"
	quest.292938760AB9A12B.title: "Dead Cells"
	quest.29379C91D6E00436.quest_desc: ["One of the cheapest - if not the cheapest - &7LV&r machine. Use this to make &6Redstone-free Magnetic Rods&r for your Motors. Whenever you start to batch your Motors, this machine will save you stacks and stacks of Redstone."]
	quest.29379C91D6E00436.quest_subtitle: "The Polarizer polarizes!"
	quest.29379C91D6E00436.title: "Basic Polariser"
	quest.295C77EEC89000FC.quest_subtitle: "Generates Source from Mob Deaths and Animal Breeding"
	quest.295C8DC11B22B1B6.quest_desc: ["Дьявольские яйца..."]
	quest.295C8DC11B22B1B6.title: "Дьявольские яйца"
	quest.29A1E1FF02BD9219.title: "Visit &6Starlight Forest"
	quest.29A484F12E8E0926.quest_desc: ["The primary building block for your first mechanisms."]
	quest.29A484F12E8E0926.title: "Andesite"
	quest.29B7D93D7F32DBA9.quest_desc: [
		"The &aCrystal SoC&r is used to make cheaper &9Crystal Circuits&r. Enjoy the discount!"
		""
		"Crystal SoCs require &9ZPM Emitters&r, which means you need a &9Data Orb&r for their research."
		""
		"In the future, these may become more difficult to make."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT5u, the texture for this item was red, and did not have the special design on it. There was a \"raw\" version with the design, but it was used for other unrelated things. Who knows why?"
	]
	quest.29B7D93D7F32DBA9.quest_subtitle: "When engraving it once isn't enough"
	quest.29B7D93D7F32DBA9.title: "Crystal SoC"
	quest.29B9E1247DE9901A.quest_desc: [
		"By using cables, you can divide/multiply voltage."
		""
		"Right-click a coil to set it as an output."
	]
	quest.29C2A82490261F1C.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &9Nano&r Circuit line."
		""
		"Starting from here, circuit progression will follow a pattern:"
		""
		"&9-&r Processor"
		"&9-&r Assembly"
		"&9-&r Supercomputer"
		"&9-&r Mainframe"
	]
	quest.29C2A82490261F1C.quest_subtitle: "Nano Age"
	quest.29C2A82490261F1C.title: "Craftable in &5EV&r"
	quest.2A1BFB2E0F1F3312.title: "Ammo"
	quest.2A358437484E61CF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2A9ECD745E15A5D8.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &5EV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"The pattern stays the same: the rightmost circuit comes in &dlarger quantities&r and is overall &aeasier&r to produce."
	]
	quest.2A9ECD745E15A5D8.title: "&5EV&r Circuits"
	quest.2AA2D0140E9B0F88.quest_subtitle: "Used to display inventories of ME Chests and to hold Storage Drives."
	quest.2ACF8F5EFD3C4AF7.title: "Boots"
	quest.2AD1B75D43A10E7A.quest_desc: ["Чашки адских супов."]
	quest.2AD1B75D43A10E7A.title: "Адские чашки"
	quest.2AD44111B9B39C90.quest_desc: [
		"A &7LV&r Battery Buffer and two &7LV&r Energy Hatches likely won't cut it anymore. Let's remedy that!"
		""
		"Upgrade your Electric Blast Furnace with a &3MV Energy Hatch&r. Now, you can run it with &bMV&r Generators without having to mess around with &3Transformers&r."
	]
	quest.2AD44111B9B39C90.quest_subtitle: "LV is so old-school!"
	quest.2AD44111B9B39C90.title: "Upgrade your EBF!"
	quest.2AE689F6495C83A6.quest_desc: [
		"The Distillery only gives you one oil processing output, but the tower gives you ONE PER LAYER!"
		""
		"To change the height of the Distillation Tower, right-click it with a screwdriver. This applies to other multiblocks with multiple shapes as well, such as the Kanthal tier EBF."
	]
	quest.2AE689F6495C83A6.quest_subtitle: "This is a very advanced machinery that is fairly tall with how they're able to assemble to an even taller machinery. If you would like to change the height, right click it with a screwdriver and it applies to other multiblocks with multiple shapes like the Kanthal tier Electric Blast Furnace!"
	quest.2B01BE60343D5839.quest_desc: ["Жаровня с сундуком - сокровищница, открыть которую можно только с помощью огня, полученного после боя с коварной свечёй. Хранит в себе очень много ценных вещей с давних времён."]
	quest.2B01BE60343D5839.title: "Пылающая сокровищница"
	quest.2B0219B675E3820F.quest_desc: ["Like other HV generators, it will produce 512 EU/t. This one will only accept regular steam."]
	quest.2B0219B675E3820F.quest_subtitle: "Another option for small setups is to use an HV steam turbine, they are not a joke with their production."
	quest.2B07F72462A04417.quest_desc: ["Apple Mash is obtained by pressing apples. Use it in fermentation barrels."]
	quest.2B07F72462A04417.title: "Apple Mash"
	quest.2B2B037180846FBA.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.2B2B037180846FBA.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.2B2C90A07E101ED4.quest_desc: ["Победите &dголемов&r, что охраняют эту крепость и заполучите ядро пустоты."]
	quest.2B30B5137906EE93.quest_desc: [
		"Ponder the Rotor and make your generator!"
		""
		"Keep in mind, it can explode, so be careful on how much RPM you put into it. (Min. 71rpm for it to work.)"
	]
	quest.2B3CB86820081AE2.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.2B5FCD2A3579C941.quest_subtitle: "Killing mobs with the &2Soul Stealing&r enchantment gives them a chance to drop &1Mob Souls&r. By clicking a &1Mob Soul&r onto an Inactive Spawner, the spawner will become active."
	quest.2B5FCD2A3579C941.title: "Craft an &cInactive Spawner"
	quest.2B641E7A30686BCF.quest_desc: [
		"Although somewhat similar to Fluix ME coated cables in appearance, they provide a diagnostic function by visualizing channel usage on the cables, channels are displayed as illuminated colored lines that run along the black band on the cables, giving you an idea of how your channels are being used on your network."
		""
		"The first four channels are displayed as lines that match the color of the cable, the next four as white lines."
	]
	quest.2B641E7A30686BCF.quest_subtitle: "A smarter cable?"
	quest.2B74E56C9E138F18.quest_desc: [
		"&6GregTech&r can quickly get &4overwhelming&r with the plethora of fluids it introduces, so you may be looking for a way to store them. "
		""
		"Introducing... &aDrums&r! They have large internal buffers, and any &aDrum&r can be broken and picked up and will &dkeep the fluid&r inside."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Additionally, &binternal tanks&r from machines will interact with items containing fluid. This is great for manual crafting - this means you can use fluid drums instead of multiple buckets in crafting. To &5void fluid&r contained in a Drum, place it alone in any crafting grid."
		""
		"&o&7Pssst:&8 &oA right-click with a Screwdriver allows a Drum to drain its content into another container placed under it. This is great if you want to keep your Liquid Boilers fueled for longer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o These drums are actually ported from GregTech 6."
	]
	quest.2B74E56C9E138F18.quest_subtitle: "Just kidding, tanks for fluids"
	quest.2B74E56C9E138F18.title: "Armoured Tanks"
	quest.2B7B214EDE0B45A2.quest_desc: [
		"&cTNT&r (Trinitrotoluene, to be pedantic) can't be prepared with the usual \"Gunpowder and Sand\" routine anymore. Instead, you'll have to produce &aGelled Toluene&r and react it with Sulfuric Acid to make TNT."
		""
		"Using the &3HV Chemical Reactor&r recipe will double the yield of &aGelled Toluene&r at the cost of requiring additional inputs."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"We don't have any easy tips to give you for &aToluene&r. We regret to inform you that making TNT is going to be tricky no matter which route you take."
		""
		"That being said, don't miss out on the direct &aHeavy Fuel&r to &aToluene&r recipe in the single block &3Distillery&r."
		""
		"&aToluene&r can also optionally be used in &5EV&r to make &dGasoline&r."
		""
		"&cTNT&r is used in the &3Implosion Compressor&r to make Gems. It also blows stuff (and your friends) up. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cITNT&r can also be used in the &3Implosion Compressor&r at a better rate but require &aNitration Mixture&r to make. It also ignites when punched so be careful when it is placed."
		""
		"Get &9either&r TNT or ITNT to complete this quest."
		""
		"Technically, Dynamite or Powerbarrels could also be used... but Dynamite is a pain to obtain, whereas Powerbarrels are weaker."
	]
	quest.2B7B214EDE0B45A2.quest_subtitle: "An explosive discovery"
	quest.2B7B214EDE0B45A2.title: "TNT"
	quest.2B98A58B036E1D9E.quest_desc: [
		"Создайте костюм &eхимзащиты&r."
		"\"Мы делаем сборку, Джесси\" - Стеф Уайт"
	]
	quest.2BB16260A76718B8.quest_desc: [
		"Woah! It's been tough to get here. You'll appreciate not having to make a new polymer for Circuits Boards."
		""
		"The &3IV Circuit Assembler&r unlocks the &1Quantum&r Circuit line."
		""
		"This also unlocks the &6best recipe&r for &dMV Circuits&r."
	]
	quest.2BB16260A76718B8.title: "IV Circuit Assembling"
	quest.2BBD3BC7D1B955C2.quest_desc: [
		"&aPlutonium-241&r is yet another requirement for the &9Fusion Reactor&r. It's very easy to make: just centrifuge some &9Pu-239&r to slowly separate some out."
		""
		"In the future, this material will require a &dNuclear Reactor&r to produce, but that's not in GTCEu yet."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT Impact, making Pu-241 was a challenge. Your first Pu-241 had to be produced as a byproduct of its very expensive Naquadah fuel process, and it could only be made independently with something post-fusion!"
	]
	quest.2BBD3BC7D1B955C2.quest_subtitle: "Spicy Plutonium Isotope"
	quest.2BBD3BC7D1B955C2.title: "Plutonium-241"
	quest.2BC7B74C1D405B3B.quest_subtitle: "To create a Twilight Forest portal, first make a 2x2 infinite water source. Then, place flowers on surrounding grass blocks and throw a diamond into the water."
	quest.2BC7B74C1D405B3B.title: "Enter &2The Twilight Forest"
	quest.2BDE73120475DD87.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &bчешую&r."]
	quest.2BDE73120475DD87.quest_subtitle: "&bБирюзовая"
	quest.2BE355672E638CF2.quest_desc: [
		"The quantity of 1 packet per tick is known as an Amp (1A for short)."
		""
		"Each single-block Generator in GregTech is configured to produce &91A&r of its voltage tier. For &7LV&r, that results in &232EU/t&r."
		""
		"If a machine requires 16EU/t, one \"packet\" of 32EU is sent &6every other tick&r (assuming no cable loss) - no more, no less."
		""
		"A Battery Buffer with &94&r Batteries can produce up to &94 Amps&r for &2128EU/t&r as &7LV&r power, which is important for the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r - or to run multiple machines simultaneously."
		""
		"Generic machines are configured to draw up to &92 Amps&r to account for cable loss. Other machines have specific &9Amps IN&r, which is described in their tooltip."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The most critical thing to know is that &acables&r have an &9Amperage &climit&r. Attempting to transport more Amps than this limit will &4burn your cable up&r."
		""
		"&9Amps&r are drawn &oonly&r through the &aCables&r connecting the Producers and Consumers directly, and only drawn if the Consumers are active."
		""
		"This means you can safely step down your Cables in certain places - feel free to experiment!"
	]
	quest.2BE8127E1180DA21.quest_desc: ["The main feature of Applied Energistics 2 is the ME (pronounced Emm- Eee and stands for Matter Energy) network, which is a set of interconnected blocks and cables grouped into a system where storage, power, and function interact between multiple components."]
	quest.2BE8127E1180DA21.quest_subtitle: "Use different interfaces and automate your network."
	quest.2BE8127E1180DA21.title: "Automation is the key to success!"
	quest.2BFFB238D31D61AB.quest_desc: ["The Hoe head will allow you to harvest crops and till soil to farm just like a standard hoe."]
	quest.2C0442E2897E8966.quest_subtitle: "The Wrench is a tool used to rotate powah machinery, config with energy cables and even link certain electric rods to energizing orbs."
	quest.2C0442E2897E8966.title: "Electrician's Right Hand"
	quest.2C70E297DBE3BDF2.quest_desc: [
		"There are many ways to automate Ordered Items: GT item pipes, Redstone, other mods, you name it! This quest will attempt to guide you through a setup using &3AE2&r."
		""
		"Have the Pattern Provider face an &3Item P2P&r. Set two output P2Ps: one into the first &3Input Bus&r, and the other into &3Item Pipes&r. Make your Item Pipes connect to all Input Buses including the first. Don't forget &dBlocking Mode&r! "
		""
		"With this setup, assembly items should be fully automated!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Whilst item automation was relatively simple, fluid automation is slightly harder."
		""
		"Fluid Pipes behave differently compared to Item Pipes, so you &4won't&r be able to use the same solution as above. "
		""
		"This quest won't explain how to do this entirely &7(due to it being off by default)&r, so the full solution is left as an exercise to the reader."
	]
	quest.2C70E297DBE3BDF2.title: "Understanding the Assembly Line"
	quest.2C75A50B17AA9AF1.quest_desc: [
		"Pyrolusite is what most people are here for. It smelts directly into Manganese, which you'll be needing in bulk for &6HV&r."
		""
		"Tantalite will eventually become extremely valuable, thanks to its Niobium byproducts, and its utility when crafting &bSMD Components&r."
	]
	quest.2C75A50B17AA9AF1.quest_subtitle: "Source of Manganese"
	quest.2C75A50B17AA9AF1.title: "Pyrolusite"
	quest.2C8BB51F8A0A4703.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.2CA6AAAD1281E63B.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.2CB8FCE09920042C.quest_desc: [
		"&aDuranium&r is a material from Star Trek, and is used for a few things in GT. It makes some pretty awesome pipes, but otherwise you won't need much of this quite yet."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In some versions of GT5u, this material was entirely white. In fact, most fusion materials and later were like this. Boring!"
	]
	quest.2CB8FCE09920042C.quest_subtitle: "Who needs Stargate, anyway?"
	quest.2CB8FCE09920042C.title: "Duranium"
	quest.2CE2E7816C6866AF.quest_desc: ["The book will help you understand the mod if needed."]
	quest.2CE2E7816C6866AF.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Powah! A generator mod used to power machinery of almost every tech available. Learning how to use them will give you the power to function your machinery without the need to use fuel."
	quest.2CE2E7816C6866AF.title: "Electrician's First Job"
	quest.2CEB4950E882EBB0.quest_desc: ["Светящиеся споры, которые можно собрать с адских деревьев."]
	quest.2CEB4950E882EBB0.title: "Споры"
	quest.2D00608E23BFE28D.quest_subtitle: "Enchant a stonecutter with the efficient enchantment to increase the amount of blocks broken in each sweep"
	quest.2D01E80DE837F6A6.quest_desc: [
		"When your power generation allows for it, &3HV machines&r are well worth using for on-demand processing. The quadrupled energy cost compared to their &7LV&r counterparts shouldn't bother you too much."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Crafting Hulls in the &3Assembler&r is slightly more efficient. Prioritise this recipe!"
	]
	quest.2D01E80DE837F6A6.title: "High Voltage Machines"
	quest.2D0CF18C8B2ABB7D.quest_desc: [
		"Placing this near growing plants or saplings will provide Source. Archwood trees provide more Source!"
		""
		"Note: Bonemealing does not produce Source."
	]
	quest.2D0CF18C8B2ABB7D.quest_subtitle: "Creates Source using the growth of Plants"
	quest.2D1E2B60A800EDDE.quest_desc: ["Давно утеряно в огромной &eзаброшенной пирамиде&f под охраной ужасного чудовища."]
	quest.2D30219AB7DF5C26.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.2D320F78629CC719.quest_subtitle: "The Steel Unpacker is a self-explanatory machinery that takes apart machine parts into other smaller pieces as a sort of recycling system, and the sibling of the Steel Packer."
	quest.2D320F78629CC719.title: "Unpack your bags, people!"
	quest.2D457E53BB6D63C7.title: "Visit &6Permafrost Forest"
	quest.2D4882ADCEA8C398.title: "Quest Book"
	quest.2D5BECC0AC0E316B.quest_desc: [
		"A NOR gate takes two input signals, and outputs a high signal only if both input signals are low."
		""
		"This doesn't matter for now though, and it's simply a more complex wafer."
		"It is used for the &aData Orb&r (a key component for when you get into &3Research&r), and in &5Nano&r Circuit production."
	]
	quest.2D5BECC0AC0E316B.title: "NOR Gates"
	quest.2D788BCA763E68F6.quest_desc: ["Обьедените меч из кости дракона и фантомный слиток, чтобы получить &bфантомный клинок&r."]
	quest.2D812FCB6A870A60.quest_desc: ["Wheat Seeds are the start of your agricultural path. Plant them on tilled soil next to water."]
	quest.2D812FCB6A870A60.title: "Wheat Seeds"
	quest.2D8EB2902477E0E0.quest_desc: [
		"This is an &zadventure&r modpack in which you will have to explore different worlds in search of &dstory items and resources&r"
		""
		"Various bosses are scattered throughout the worlds, from which you can find good loot."
		""
		"In the modpack, after exploring the world, you can cook food or make wine, and even build mechanisms that will make your life a little easier."
		""
		"We recommend reading further along the quest line about create and magic with the story."
		""
		"Have a good journey !"
	]
	quest.2D8EB2902477E0E0.title: "&5Steamcreate 2"
	quest.2D97125FB3DE9A31.quest_desc: ["&dNaga&r is a huge snake. It lives in its labyrinth and has been sleeping for many years. It has red eyes and green scales, which is very hard to penetrate."]
	quest.2D97125FB3DE9A31.title: "Naga"
	quest.2DB259568F347C0E.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3Turbo Charger&r charges &6RF and EU&r items such as &9Drills&r extremely quickly."
		"It accepts up to 4 Amps for every item it charges, making it &6twice as fast&r as the &3Battery Buffer&r. It cannot discharge, though."
		""
		"&eAny&r Charger will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.2DB259568F347C0E.quest_subtitle: "100% Battery"
	quest.2DB259568F347C0E.title: "Turbo Charger"
	quest.2DB4F8709A1E0F36.quest_subtitle: "Used to accelerate crystal growth, which allows you to create Certus Quartz Crystal andFluix Crystal from crystal dust. Must be powered by an ME Network via the top or bottom, and consumes a steady 8 ae/t while plugged in. Crystal Seeds must be in an adjacent water block to be effected, the seeds will shimmer more rapidly when in the presence of a powered Crystal Growth Accelerator. Can only connect to cables, or other networked machines on the top and bottom of the machine."
	quest.2DB9C3C383C91BC0.quest_desc: ["Don't break it with the wrench, use a pickaxe."]
	quest.2DB9C3C383C91BC0.quest_subtitle: "Is it a monkey or a wrench? Anyway this will be useful in rotating the machine or changing their input and output locations."
	quest.2DB9C3C383C91BC0.title: "Engineer's Toy"
	quest.2DDCD0D0F96DBC07.quest_desc: ["Используя железо и &bкровь дракона&r, создайте драконью сталь. А затем изготовьте из неё броню и инструменты."]
	quest.2DDCD0D0F96DBC07.quest_subtitle: "&bЛедяная драконья сталь"
	quest.2DE4C3DE6FC87007.quest_desc: ["Еда, которую можно найти в заброшенных бункерах токсичных пещер. Помогает регенерировать при облучении."]
	quest.2DE4C3DE6FC87007.title: "Радиоактивная еда"
	quest.2E00E10D4E92F64D.quest_desc: ["Circuits along this line are &cZPM&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."]
	quest.2E00E10D4E92F64D.title: "&cZPM&r Circuits"
	quest.2E0777FBD0476D75.quest_desc: [
		"Washing ores with Mercury where applicable instead of &3Distilled Water&r grants unique byproducts that may be difficult to obtain in other circumstances. It's usually worth doing this, as Mercury is readily available from centrifuging &cRedstone&r or &4Cinnabar&r &7(and in fact, Mercury is the &lonly&r&7 real usage of Cinnabar!)&r."
		""
		"Simply wash any &6Crushed Ore&r with a Chemical Bath."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Here is a non-exhaustive list of ores you likely want to wash in Mercury:"
		""
		"- Galena Ore"
		"- Tungstate Ore"
		"- Silver Ore"
		"- Bornite Ore"
		"- Magnetite Ore"
		"- Copper Ore"
		"- Gold Ore"
		"- Nickel Ore"
		"- Platinum Ore"
		"- Chalcopyrite Ore"
		"- Sheldonite Ore"
		""
		"These alternate \"&bwashing routes&r\" will increase your Gold, Silver, and Platinum Group yields significantly!"
	]
	quest.2E0777FBD0476D75.quest_subtitle: "Bathing with Venus"
	quest.2E0777FBD0476D75.title: "Washing with Mercury"
	quest.2E36E5755B2F551C.quest_desc: [
		"The Prospector is an amazing tool that'll help you find veins in no time."
		""
		"Its GUI is interactive. Right-clicking will scan for ores, displaying them on a dynamic map."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Back in OUR day, the portable Prospector was locked to &dLuV&f. Kids these days have it easy."
	]
	quest.2E36E5755B2F551C.quest_subtitle: "(Ok, maybe not)"
	quest.2E36E5755B2F551C.title: "This is Hacking"
	quest.2E47FB88AF4E02A4.quest_desc: ["Заполучите &dперчатку стража энда&r."]
	quest.2E4BF7CDD48F7ECA.quest_desc: ["На &aболотах&r обитает могучее существо - &aГидра&r, которое можно отрастить 9 голов. Из-за быстрой регенерации ей всё равно на любые раны, кроме &cогня&r."]
	quest.2E5A71CED4B01657.quest_desc: [
		"Your classic Redstone vein."
		""
		"Ruby is very important for the Chromium it contains. You'll quickly discover that you can never have too much Chromium!"
	]
	quest.2E5A71CED4B01657.quest_subtitle: "Source of Redstone, Ruby, Chromium, Mercury"
	quest.2E5A71CED4B01657.title: "Redstone"
	quest.2EC5E615489EDC1D.title: "Any wood"
	quest.2EDC7E875E426986.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.2EFC07A4615B8B12.quest_desc: [
		"This armor provides more QoL compared to the Nano suit."
		""
		"&9Helmet:&r Provides &dNight vision&r (default keybind &4M&r but check for conflicts), prevents harmful potion effects, and automatically eats for you!"
		""
		"&9Chestplate:&r Nullifies burning, but can be further upgraded into the &aAdvanced&r version at the very end of &dLuV&r. Note that this does NOT include a jetpack without the advanced upgrade."
		""
		"&9Leggings:&r Provides the speed boost which the Nano leggings did not."
		""
		"&9Boots:&r Provides &dStep Assist&r, nullifies fall damage, and increases jump height!"
	]
	quest.2EFC07A4615B8B12.quest_subtitle: "No, we didn't trademark this one"
	quest.2EFC07A4615B8B12.title: "QuarkTech"
	quest.2F11BBE61151DFAF.title: "Ruined Portal"
	quest.2F1CCFEBAB71B1F3.quest_desc: [
		"With &7LV&r power, the primary way of getting &aAluminium Dust&r is by electrolyzing &9Sapphire&r or &2Green Sapphire&r. Aluminium is the main &bMV&r material, similar to how Steel is crucial in &7LV&r, and Bronze is important in the &6Steam Age&r."
		""
		"It's possible to obtain Aluminium by processing ores such as &6Fullers' Earth&r, but the commitment required to see similar yields is more than sourcing your Aluminium from &3Sapphire&r. For this reason, you can &5skip the quest&r with the checkbox."
		""
		"It would be wise to obtain enough Sapphire to electrolyze into a full stack of &aAluminium Dust&r - it &lwill&r be useful very soon. Plus, bonus Oxygen is always nice."
	]
	quest.2F1CCFEBAB71B1F3.quest_subtitle: "One Step Closer To MV"
	quest.2F1CCFEBAB71B1F3.title: "Sapphire"
	quest.2F1DBF8A01DDC230.quest_desc: ["Доспех очень богатых жителей северных регионов. Выполнен на манер доспехов викингов. Обеспечивает хорошую защиту, но не замедляет владельца."]
	quest.2F1DBF8A01DDC230.title: "Шлем Золотого рога"
	quest.2F2F82D9DE3C798C.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest will be completed with &eeither&r a &3UV Energy Hatch&r&r... or a &3UV Dynamo Hatch&r for your Multiblock Generators."
		""
		"Don't forget that &d16 Amp&r variants exist!"
		""
		"Additionally, remember that these hatches require a &9Data Module&r for research."
	]
	quest.2F2F82D9DE3C798C.title: "Upgrading your Assembly Line III"
	quest.2F5A88568154E986.quest_subtitle: "Let's start small first. You never know how this will turn out."
	quest.2F6ED192CC3A9AF4.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2F6ED192CC3A9AF4.quest_subtitle: "I feel like we're creating a Steam Engine with how much bigger these boilers get. Anyway, this is an upgraded version of your already known boilers, they use up more fuel but their output is tremendous."
	quest.2F6ED192CC3A9AF4.title: "Can we boil our food now? No?"
	quest.2F7617C0C4B330DE.quest_desc: [
		"When placed on a machine, pumps will transfer fluid. You can configure them to import or export."
		""
		"It can accept a &9Fluid Filter&r."
	]
	quest.2F7617C0C4B330DE.quest_subtitle: "A crafting component, but also a cover!"
	quest.2F85E5A410CB7C52.quest_desc: ["С маленьким шансом, после убийства призрака, вы можете получить &bфантомный слиток&r."]
	quest.2F9D9AAB27E6534D.quest_desc: [
		"This part of the chain starts with &aInert Metal Mixture&r."
		""
		"The &dSulfuric Acid&r will be perfectly recycled. You will also produce excess &dOxygen&r and &dHydrogen&r that can be stored."
		""
		"&aRuthenium&r and &aRhodium&r will gate your progression into &9IV&r and &dLuV&r respectively. If you automate them now, you won't need to do it later!"
	]
	quest.2F9D9AAB27E6534D.quest_subtitle: "Ru-Rho, Rhaggy"
	quest.2F9D9AAB27E6534D.title: "Ruthenium and Rhodium"
	quest.2FB251E717EA2F3C.quest_desc: [
		"This block is not connected to any cables and is only registered as part of the network when creating a full bridge."
		""
		"This block list can contain only one quantum entangled singularity and is available for automation."
	]
	quest.2FB251E717EA2F3C.quest_subtitle: "One of these blocks, surrounded by a quantum ME ring, will create a Quantum Network Bridge."
	quest.2FB2FE782B1103D6.title: "Blast furnace"
	quest.2FC7B1E867E4194E.quest_desc: [
		"Multiblocks bear a large variety of interesting mechanics that might seem daunting, but don't worry - we've written a guide to help you learn."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a bunch of tutorials on Multiblocks in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check them out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.2FC7B1E867E4194E.quest_subtitle: "By the end of this, you'll be an expert"
	quest.2FC7B1E867E4194E.title: "Multiblock Techniques"
	quest.2FCBA0D780DBDA9E.quest_desc: [
		"&aNaquadah Coils&r crank up the Heat Capacity to &d7,200K&r."
		""
		"These coils are required for progressing to the second half of &dLuV&r and beyond."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Well... not some \"juicy GregTech lore\", but a cool space fact, owing to the fact you're beating the Sun's temperature with your EBF. The surface temperature of the Sun is 5,800K. We're taking this as an effective temperature - i.e. the radiative temperature of the Sun as if it were a perfectly \"black body\". Check out the Stefan-Boltzmann law if you're interested in some crude astrophysics."
		""
		"&oOh, and the \"photosphere\" (the part of the sun we're talking about when we mention its surface)? It's 400 kilometres thick. That's 250 miles. Damn!"
	]
	quest.2FCBA0D780DBDA9E.quest_subtitle: "Hotter than the surface temperature of the Sun!"
	quest.2FCBA0D780DBDA9E.title: "Naquadah Coils"
	quest.2FD75E4BD95F6645.quest_desc: [
		"&3High Pressure Boilers&r will be a better source of Steam for powering your Steam machines."
		""
		"Keep in mind that you will still be using Steam to power your Electric machines in &7LV&r via the miracles of energy conversion."
		""
		"&cNote:&r You will need more than a handful of &3HP Boilers&r. The more you make, the less you'll need to worry about running out of power."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &3Solid Boiler&r burns solid Fuel. It's self explanatory - better fuels last longer."
		""
		"The &3Liquid Boiler&r burns either &dLava&r or &dCreosote&r."
		""
		"The &3Solar Boiler&r burns nothing - it's fueled by the sun."
		""
		"Looking for a recommendation? Honestly, either goes, as all three boilers are equivalent in generation. Craft the boiler that best suits your preferred resource."
		""
		"Get &eany&r of the proposed boilers to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.2FD75E4BD95F6645.quest_subtitle: "Pressure! Pushin' down on me..."
	quest.2FD75E4BD95F6645.title: "High Pressure"
	quest.2FEC85DD348C7C1C.quest_desc: [
		"Items can be placed on the Cutting Board by using them on it. It always prefers receiving items from the off-hand, allowing players to hold their ingredients there while holding the tool in their main hand, processing the stack simply by holding the use button."
		""
		"When the correct tool is used on a valid item, it will be broken down into 1-4 different outputs, which are swiped sideways. Outputs always fly to the direction opposite to the Cutting Board's handle, allowing them to be collected by an item-capturing block, such as a Hopper or Basket. The tool receives 1 point of damage for each processed item."
	]
	quest.2FEC85DD348C7C1C.quest_subtitle: "The Cutting Board is a workstation where players can break down one item into many outputs, by using a valid tool on it."
	quest.300343A7965531DD.quest_desc: ["Only the 4 ME Quantum ring units adjacent to the ME Quantum Link camera will accept network connections, the 4 corner units cannot connect to cables."]
	quest.300343A7965531DD.quest_subtitle: "Eight of these blocks placed around the ME Quantum Link camera will create a quantum network bridge."
	quest.300348B1238BCB9A.quest_desc: [
		"If you already made and centrifuged &aRare Earth&r, that's great! If you haven't, you can obtain it as a &9Byproduct&r from various ores, or from centrifuging &dMonazite&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The elements you can obtain are:"
		""
		"&9-&r &aLanthanum&r is used in &3Fusion&r&r - you will eventually want a lot of it!"
		"&9-&r &aYttrium&r is used in &dYttrium-Barium-Cuprate-Oxide&r (YBCO), a wire material for &3UV&r."
		"&9-&r &aCerium&r is not particularly useful."
		"&9-&r &aSamarium&r is used for &dIV Superconductors&r and &dMagnetic Rods&r for &dLuV&r+ Motors."
		"&9-&r &aNeodymium&r normally makes the strongest magnets, but gameplay balance... y'know."
		"&9-&r &aCadmium&r is not particularly useful."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Rare Earth Elements (REE) contain a lot more metals than these, but we're struggling as is to give them use."
	]
	quest.300348B1238BCB9A.quest_subtitle: "It's got \"rare\" in the name... oh no."
	quest.300348B1238BCB9A.title: "Rare Earth"
	quest.301EAF236DC03E34.title: "autofocus"
	quest.307A7F690F13334A.quest_desc: ["Приготовьте &dамброзию&r."]
	quest.3081D7B146082323.quest_desc: ["Одолев сирену, вы можете получить её &bслезу&r. Которую можно использовать для создания магического артефакта."]
	quest.30A6EDDF25A5E5F8.quest_desc: [
		"50% of &aTungstensteel's&r composition is Steel... suffice to say, you'll need large quantities of both &aIron&r and &aTungsten&r!"
		""
		"Right now, &aTungsten&r is a crucial ingredient for the next tier of coils. You're one step closer to moving away from those pesky single block Generators!"
		""
		"Boosting the smelting recipe in the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r will require &eHelium&r. You can get an initial supply from &aextracting Monazite&r or &acentrifuging Endstone&r."
		""
		"In the long term, you will want to get Helium via &aLiquid Air Distillation&r."
	]
	quest.30A6EDDF25A5E5F8.quest_subtitle: "The main &9IV&r Material!"
	quest.30A6EDDF25A5E5F8.title: "Tungstensteel"
	quest.30C849D73754A0C0.quest_desc: ["&dGribotaur&r is an upgraded version of the Minotaur. He possesses a powerful weapon - the Legendary Diamond Axe. He has been guarding the valuable resources of the labyrinth for many years."]
	quest.30C849D73754A0C0.title: "Gribotaur"
	quest.30D81AF1E268C878.quest_desc: ["The ME Terminal gives you access to all items stored in your network. It requires one channel to operate."]
	quest.30D81AF1E268C878.title: "ME Terminal"
	quest.30FDAAAA8784A842.quest_desc: ["The Millstone allows you to grind resources into powders or flour. It is a more efficient way to process some materials in the early stages."]
	quest.30FDAAAA8784A842.title: "Millstone"
	quest.3103B2CFCFDB2173.quest_subtitle: "Found at the bottom of the &cCursed Pyramid&r, which spawns in deserts. Awaken the boss with the &eNecklace of the Desert&r. This boss is &lvery&r difficult and you will need to be properly prepared. Locate with an &eEye of Desert"
	quest.3103B2CFCFDB2173.title: "Defeat an &6Ancient Remnant"
	quest.3142A40E1EAEBAA3.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Dowsing Rod&r gives you Magic Find and Scrying when used."
		""
		"This allows you to see nearby magic creatures as well as helping you find amethyst!"
	]
	quest.3142A40E1EAEBAA3.quest_subtitle: "Magic Finder"
	quest.3144DC68B266730C.quest_desc: [
		"Grow &dRubber Trees&r and cut them down to get &aSticky Resin&r."
		""
		"If you're playing on a difficulty other than &bPeaceful&r, Sticky Resin can be obtained from Slimeballs."
	]
	quest.3144DC68B266730C.quest_subtitle: "Did you think we would force you to use treetaps...?"
	quest.3144DC68B266730C.title: "Sticky Resin"
	quest.315159E35808B405.quest_desc: ["Броня полководца, сражавшегося против сил тьмы. Очень яркий доспех, отражающий тактический гений носителя. Увеличивает максимальное здоровье владельца и усиливает его боевые навыки."]
	quest.315169840E06110F.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Laser Engraver&r engraves patterns into &9Silicon Wafers&r based on the type of &9Lens&r it is given. After the wafers are engraved, they must be passed through a &3Cutting Machine&r to turn them into components ready to be put into Circuits."
		""
		"Higher tier Engravers can etch more complex wafers for more efficient Circuits."
	]
	quest.315169840E06110F.title: "Laser Engraving"
	quest.315BE66F5DF44912.quest_subtitle: "Used to create Binding Cards."
	quest.315DBB3B23F95E0D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bronze&r is an &2alloy&r of Copper and Tin. Grind down 3 parts Copper and 1 part Tin into dust, then combine and smelt them. If you are confused on how this is done, take a look at the &o\"&dMore Tools&r&o\"&r quest."
		""
		"Don't spend your entire supply of Copper and Tin on Bronze right now! You'll soon be able to get a better ratio for your Bronze."
		""
		"&6&lThe progression now continues in the Steam Age chapter.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Bronze in real life is closer to a ratio of 7:1 for Copper to Tin. Here (and in most of modded Minecraft) this is &4not&f the case for the sake of game balance. There are a lot of things like this that need to be tweaked - &eno realism here&f."
	]
	quest.315DBB3B23F95E0D.quest_subtitle: "Humanity's first alloy - and yours too!"
	quest.315DBB3B23F95E0D.title: "Bronze Age? No, &6Steam Age&r!"
	quest.316FF60D6FFE97CE.quest_desc: [
		"EMI might look a little overwhelming here, so we'll go through the best path for Sulfuric Acid here."
		""
		"Making &eSulfuric Acid&r is a three step process. It is used in many important reactions, so you should automate its production ASAP."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To automate it, you will need &3three LV Chemical Reactors&r. We would recommend building a dedicated setup somewhere with &3a single LV Generator&r to power all three machines. You can then spaghetti your pipes to handle input and output &m...or simply use AE2&r."
		""
		"&9-&r Step 1: React &aSulfur&r with &bOxygen&r to form &aSulfur Dioxide&r."
		"&9-&r Step 2: React &aSulfur Dioxide&r with more &bOxygen&r to form &aSulfur Trioxide&r."
		"&9-&r Step 3: React &aSulfur Trioxide&r with &bWater&r to form &eSulfuric Acid&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5's Chemical Reactor only had one Fluid slot. To circumvent that, they would do &dcell chemistry&f. The way you would automate Sulfuric Acid was by having one cell travel from machine to machine and then loop back to its starting position. A somewhat fun and interesting automation challenge, but also a chore!"
	]
	quest.316FF60D6FFE97CE.quest_subtitle: "\"...what he thought was H2O was H2SO4!\""
	quest.316FF60D6FFE97CE.title: "Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.3182E8AF755104E4.quest_desc: [
		"When blocking damage, the &9Enchanter's Shield&r will give the user Mana Regen and Spell Damage for a short amount of time."
		""
		"Additionally, the shield will repair itself over time using the wearer's mana."
	]
	quest.31BCEF301071F67C.quest_desc: ["This advanced version can produce up to 1024 mb/t of steam!"]
	quest.31BCEF301071F67C.quest_subtitle: "My back is killing me! More boilers?! I might get a heatstroke at this rate!"
	quest.31E78478F7F43CBD.quest_subtitle: "ENERGY??"
	quest.31E7C56ABBA6A7B2.quest_desc: ["This combination allows your mount to be a lot more agile during travels. Since mounts eat a large volume of feed, the item does not need to be contained in a Bowl, saving some inventory space."]
	quest.31F7D7956905A110.quest_desc: ["В нашем мире с давних времён существует могущественная раса, которая стоит на вершине иерархии во всём мире - драконы. Они делятся на три типа: &6огненные&r, &bледяные&r и &dгрозовые&r. Их зубы могут прокусить металл, их когти могут срубить деревья."]
	quest.32226ED25E813908.quest_subtitle: "&6The Aether&r portal is built the same way as a Nether Portal, but instead of Obsidian you use Glowstone, and instead of a Flint n' Steel you use a water bucket."
	quest.32226ED25E813908.title: "Enter the &6Aether"
	quest.324B15844FC6C305.quest_desc: ["You can now automate double ingots and pipes, for example! Again, check REI."]
	quest.324B15844FC6C305.quest_subtitle: "The Steel Packer is a self-explanatory machinery that automates combining of certain machinery parts, the sibling of Steel Unpacker."
	quest.324B15844FC6C305.title: "Pack your bags, people!"
	quest.327C3E02CD751453.quest_desc: ["The &aZPM Mainframe&r is used to make the &3LuV Circuit Assembler&r (of course), but also allows you to step into &3Fusion&r."]
	quest.327C3E02CD751453.quest_subtitle: "Zero Point Module is (almost) mine!"
	quest.327C3E02CD751453.title: "First ZPM Circuits!"
	quest.328702B1D4999C5F.quest_desc: ["An upgraded Infused Hellshelf. provides increased stats."]
	quest.328CFD483C26EA44.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLarge Tungstensteel Boiler&r is the final Steam Boiler. It's even more efficient than the previous ones, and produces more steam."
		""
		"This thing is &la colossal noob trap&r, and you should &4ABSOLUTELY&r use something else. &cDon't&r make this, it's not good, not even as a meme! Steam &4doesn't&r scale beyond this point, and this boiler will likely be &3removed&r in the future."
		""
		"&eNote&r: This quest can be skipped &7(for completion progress)&r by clicking the Checkmark. You do not have to actually craft one."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o No one makes these in GT5u either... y'know, almost makes you feel sorry for the poor boiler."
	]
	quest.328CFD483C26EA44.quest_subtitle: "Good luck fueling this, lmao"
	quest.328CFD483C26EA44.title: "Worst Combustion"
	quest.3296B815876C3181.quest_desc: [
		"Whilst frolicking about on the surface, you may have spotted a couple of &dSurface rocks&r."
		""
		"These little guys indicate the type of veins that are below them. Just right-click &7(or mine!)&r the surface rock to receive a corresponding pile of &aTiny Dust&r. This will also add the vein to your minimap."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can now use &2EMI&r to learn more about the vein beneath your feet. Just press &dU&r on the Tiny Dust you mined from the rock, find the corresponding Raw Ore, and press &dR&r. From there, navigate to the &6Ore Vein Diagram&r. This page contains details on what &btypes of ores&r generate with it, their &3generation patterns&r, their &espawning dimension&r and &dY-level range&r, and their &aspawning weight&r, which is the chance it spawns."
	]
	quest.3296B815876C3181.quest_subtitle: "Awakening your inner geologist"
	quest.3296B815876C3181.title: "This Rocks!"
	quest.329A84D396DD4DC6.quest_desc: ["Из монстров &4забвенных пустот&r можно получать разные предметы, которые пригодятся в последующих крафтах."]
	quest.329DD575089DC2E5.quest_desc: ["Шотган - оружие, которое разрабатывалось в святилище душ. Стреляет плотью призраков."]
	quest.32B08E6F414A00C0.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Similar to the Centrifuge, this machine does a lot of things - we can't hope to list them all! Fortunately, it's one of the cheapest &7LV&r machines, so grab it as soon as it becomes necessary."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Okay, we lied. It's not &oexactly&r used for Ore Processing, it's actually used in the &adecomposition of Dusts&r. However, most of the useful electrolysis recipes are locked at &bMV&r. You can peep at the &emolecular formula&r in a dust's tooltip to see what you can get from electrolysis."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cTake caution!&r Due to how ores work, directly smelting dusts into Ingots can give higher metal yields than electrolysis. However, it means you lose the other products in the dust. You will have to decide whether you want to prioritise direct value, or byproduct count."
	]
	quest.32B08E6F414A00C0.quest_subtitle: "Separating anything you can think of"
	quest.32B08E6F414A00C0.title: "Basic Electrolyzer"
	quest.32EA7E81885C8E87.quest_desc: [
		"You could make any other &7LV&r Machine, but it would be easiest to start with the most useful one. We know, we know... you wanna make some of the crazier stuff first, but trust us, this is the best starting point."
		""
		"The Wiremill lets you make &6two Wires from one Ingot&r. That should be three times cheaper than what you were doing up until now! &8&oPlus, aren't you sick of crafting Wire Cutters?&r"
		""
		"To the right of this Quest, you'll find some important machines which will grant you cheaper intermediates."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Recipes inside &3LV Machines&r go up to a maximum usage of &a32 EU/t (LV)&r. Anything higher than that and you will need a &bMV&r (or better) Machine. Needless to say, we aren't quite there yet."
		""
		"You will need a &dProgrammed Circuit&r for certain recipes. We're sure you don't want to spend a precious Circuit to craft one, so &6read the dedicated quest for important details&r."
		""
		"With this machine safely crafted - welcome to the age of all things electric!"
	]
	quest.32EA7E81885C8E87.quest_subtitle: "No more painful wires!"
	quest.32EA7E81885C8E87.title: "Basic Wiremill"
	quest.330BDB559A7BAB35.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"You can make &6Paper out of Wood&r so that you no longer rely on &aSugar Canes&9*&r. You're probably sick of them by now, especially if you've played Nomifactory."
		""
		"There are some other less important recipes, such as applying colours to various items and blocks, or bleaching them."
		""
		"&9*&r &aSugar&r is still useful as a requirement for &cTNT&r production in &6HV&r, so don't dismantle your setups."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Some &aCrushed Ores&r have alternate routes when washed into &aPurified Ore&r, involving bathing in either &aMercury&r or &aSodium Persulfate&r. This step isn't really important, unless you really want that special &6Byproduct&r. This can be a nice alternate source of Gold (hint, hint!)."
	]
	quest.330BDB559A7BAB35.quest_subtitle: "The Chemical Bath bathes..."
	quest.330BDB559A7BAB35.title: "Basic Chemical Bath"
	quest.331A37777C92793B.quest_desc: ["Из &cалых&r и &9лазурных&r магнитов можно создавать различные полезные и интересные вещи."]
	quest.331F2C12C652D268.quest_desc: [
		"&9-&r If the recipe isn't happening, check if the Multiblock is properly plugged in (we all make these mistakes!)."
		""
		"&9-&r Remember to always perform the initial Maintenance \"routine\" at the appropriate hatch."
		""
		"&9-&r Verify the recipe's EU/t usage - the max EU/t provided to the multiblock has to be greater than that of the recipe."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9- &rCheck the special requirements the recipe may have (EMI always has some kind of indication if this is the case). Do you need to be in a Cleanroom, for example?"
		""
		"&9-&r Make sure the correct items are input into the buses/hatches. This is less obvious than in a regular machine, because you have to juggle between the Input Bus and Input Hatch."
		""
		"&9-&r Make sure there is space for an output. Maybe the multiblock formed, but you forgot a Hatch. The other biggest offender is the Output Hatches being too low tier and thus having too little capacity - this trips people up with the Greenhouse!"
	]
	quest.331F2C12C652D268.quest_subtitle: "It's not forming? We've all been there before."
	quest.331F2C12C652D268.title: "Troubleshooting Multiblocks"
	quest.33263404ED38C6D2.quest_desc: [
		"&oThe &3Large Boiler&r is an &6optional&r big-boy variant of the Small Boilers. It runs off solid or liquid fuel."
		""
		"If you want Steam-based power production, this will be your first port-of-call. Other power options are listed in the &bMV&r chapter, if you want to invest in those, you can &cskip this quest&r with the checkmark."
		""
		"One \"easy\" fuel option is producing &dCharcoal&r from &3Coke Ovens&r. One piece of Charcoal lasts 20s in the LBB and the wood can be sourced from a tree farm."
		""
		"&cImportant:&r This Boiler &lCAN&r also &cexplode&r similarly to the regular Boilers! Usually, the explosion can be rather devastating... but it's configured to not damage blocks or entities in this modpack."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cWater supply is &lcrucial&r&r. Dedicate a &3Primitive Pump&r with a &7LV&r Output Hatch in the &lsame chunk&r as the Boiler. Any biome will still be enough to supply enough water."
		""
		"Once fully heated up, the &3LBB&r produces 800 Steam per tick, which is &d400EU/t&r after conversion, or 12.5 Basic Steam Turbines. Such (relatively!) immense power comes at the cost of automating fuel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&5&lWith this in consideration&r, the GUI lets you &9throttle&r the Boiler down to 25% power for 200 Steam per tick. That's &d100EU/t&r, or slightly above 3 Basic Steam Turbines."
		""
		"&9Note:&r An in-depth tutorial about Multiblocks is given after you get the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r. We recommend you aim for that first."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The LBB used to be terrible, however it recently got rebalanced in 7.3.0 to make it actually viable to use."
	]
	quest.33263404ED38C6D2.quest_subtitle: "Boom, boom, boom, boom"
	quest.33334A51A383F8BE.quest_desc: ["Иногда вам могут попасться старые особняки, в которых остались призраки их &bхозяев&r, которые ночью могут встретится, защищая свой дом. "]
	quest.333C13FB45EE4774.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &9чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.333C13FB45EE4774.quest_subtitle: "&9Сапфировый комплект"
	quest.333C13FB45EE4774.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.33682F4B44950123.quest_desc: [
		"To gain further knowledge of spells, we'll need a specific type of magical wood!"
		""
		"Archwood Trees can be found in the overworld."
	]
	quest.33682F4B44950123.title: "Archwood logs"
	quest.336BB4A8E9DE0A95.quest_desc: ["Растения, которые нужны для приготовления напитков."]
	quest.336BB4A8E9DE0A95.title: "Полезные растения"
	quest.338FEC8C826F9B46.quest_desc: ["The void upgrade will void any items added to the drawer past its max capacity."]
	quest.3398FC108D9DCB46.quest_desc: [
		"How do you get Platinum?"
		""
		"&9-&r As a byproduct of &aNickel Ore&r processing, either with a &3Chemical Bath&r, or a &3HV Macerator&r"
		"&9-&r From &aSheldonite veins&r in the End"
		"&9-&r From &aPlatinum Group Sludge&r, a complicated chain granting all Platinum Group metals. Highly &cunrecommended until IV&r, but eventually required."
		""
		"Platinum is needed in small amounts for &dSMD Diodes&r, and for a plethora of recipes starting in &5EV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Mekanism's primary material was planned to be Platinum. However, GregoriusT didn't agree - the fact that such a rare material could be found all over the world wasn't quite to his tastes. The Mekanism devs thus opted to make the primary material Osmium."
	]
	quest.3398FC108D9DCB46.quest_subtitle: "Diamond and Pearl"
	quest.3398FC108D9DCB46.title: "Platinum"
	quest.33A1FF5C31EAF716.quest_desc: ["&aStem Cells&r are a major component of &4Wetware Circuits&r. Just don't question why these use Osmiridium."]
	quest.33A1FF5C31EAF716.quest_subtitle: "This texture used to be really ugly..."
	quest.33A1FF5C31EAF716.title: "Stem Cells"
	quest.33BF21CF8232FD35.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.33BF21CF8232FD35.quest_subtitle: "A huge multiblock that can dig for Crude Oil under the bedrock using fluid pipes. I hope we can sell all this oil for money... wait, do we have money at all?"
	quest.33BF21CF8232FD35.title: "Time to be rich!"
	quest.33DBE8E47A2000EC.quest_subtitle: "Energy Hoppers are used to charge items in a chest without the need to use an energizing orb."
	quest.33DCA1E150BE1ADB.quest_desc: ["The highest tier of bookshelf. Adds a higher, balanced spread of stats."]
	quest.3408F95596F372A9.quest_desc: ["Necessary material and block."]
	quest.343E1E09687C2717.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &cчешую&r."]
	quest.343E1E09687C2717.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасная"
	quest.34550EB511DF1DBC.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to view the contents of your network like other terminals, but also contains an area for creating templates."
		""
		"There are two modes of pattern encoding. Pattern creation and pattern processing."
		""
		"Processing patterns are designed for use with machines that do not use standard manufacturing recipes, such as kilns or other machines. "
		""
		"To select one of the modes, click the button to the right of the interface; when the standard crafting table is displayed, crafting patterns are created, and when the furnace is displayed, processing patterns are created."
	]
	quest.34550EB511DF1DBC.quest_subtitle: "A specialized version of the ME Crafting Terminal, designed to encode an empty template into a crafting template or a processing template."
	quest.348A80A550A14F5D.quest_desc: ["Told you the creosote was needed."]
	quest.34C8EE7B485AA260.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &7чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.34C8EE7B485AA260.quest_subtitle: "Серый комплект"
	quest.34C8EE7B485AA260.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.350E8A014DD8C838.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of running around your base yet? &3Travel Anchors&r make their introduction in the latest update!"
		""
		"Aim the &aTravel Staff&r at a placed Anchor, then &6sneak-right-click&r to teleport on top. You can &bcustomise the appearance&r of a Travel Anchor by right-clicking it with a block in your off-hand, and you can &9rename&r Anchors in their GUI. The effective tool for breaking them is the &bWrench&r."
		""
		"The &dEnder Pearls&r necessary to craft more Anchors won't be available yet - take a small handful of Anchors to make life a &olittle&r easier."
	]
	quest.350E8A014DD8C838.quest_subtitle: "pshhh... nothin personnel... kid"
	quest.350E8A014DD8C838.title: "Travel Anchors"
	quest.35105F4914FBEC3B.quest_subtitle: "The Charger provides a way to charge supported tools through the ME Network or manually using a crank. It can also be used to create Charged Certus Quartz Crystal from Certus Quartz Crystal, and Meteorite Compass from Compass."
	quest.35105F4914FBEC3B.title: "Preparing to Find Meteorites 1"
	quest.353C7E49ADF67BF3.quest_desc: ["Убивая приспешников королевы, вы будете получать хитин. Из которого можно создать &2броню мирмексов&r."]
	quest.35549F0404C87BCA.quest_desc: [
		"&3Dielectric PCB Coolant&r is used to maintain some highly advanced late and end-game machinery."
		""
		"You only need a little bit in &dLuV&r, but you'll want to automate it when you get to &cZPM&r."
	]
	quest.35549F0404C87BCA.quest_subtitle: "Absolutely beneficial for the environment"
	quest.35549F0404C87BCA.title: "Dielectric PCB Coolant"
	quest.3568BC9742092FC5.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cleanroom&r is a hollow multiblock free of contaminants. Going forward, most new &acircuit-related recipes&r, as well as some unique blocks like &3Fusion Casings&r, will need to be run in machines inside a Cleanroom."
		""
		"Creating it will put your &aPolyethylene&r automation to the test for all the &dPlascrete&r and/or &dCleanroom Glass&r you will make."
		""
		"We'll start you off with a 5x5x5 Cleanroom, but you should upgrade its size when you start feeling cramped."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on the Cleanroom in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Cleanroom comes from GregTech 5, but as is often the case, the GT5 implementation is much more punishing. The recipes would run without regard to cleanliness, but had a % chance of completion equal to the cleanliness of the Cleanroom. This caused a lot of accidental voiding."
		""
		"&oFurthermore, if the Cleanroom had a maintenance issue, the cleanliness would cap out at 90%, which means 10% of items would be voided."
		""
		"&oThe GTCEu Cleanroom will &6never void&f recipe outputs."
	]
	quest.3568BC9742092FC5.quest_subtitle: "They put me in a room... a clean room"
	quest.3568BC9742092FC5.title: "The Cleanroom"
	quest.3571E087401DC67E.quest_desc: ["An infused version of a Seashelf. To infuse a shelf, place it in an ehcnating table while you meet the required levels and enchanting stats. To see the requirements, click on the item image here, or search in JEI."]
	quest.3576A3E476D545DE.quest_desc: [
		"Создайте костюм &eхимзащиты&r."
		"\"Мы делаем сборку, Джесси\" - Стеф Уайт"
	]
	quest.357FAEECCD7CCB67.quest_desc: ["Смертоносное оружие ушедших эпох."]
	quest.357FAEECCD7CCB67.title: "Первобытное оружие"
	quest.358D742BF236AFA7.quest_subtitle: "Energy Cells are basically a bulk battery that can contain and transfer energy to other machinery connected to it when a machine is taking time to produce energy."
	quest.359121584E056022.quest_desc: [
		"The third circuit of the &4wetware&r line. Get some &bEuropium&r to make these."
		""
		"This is also the best &3UV&r circuit!"
	]
	quest.359121584E056022.quest_subtitle: "Sentience in circuit form"
	quest.359121584E056022.title: "Best UV Circuits!"
	quest.35BAD166CED7B37A.quest_desc: ["С незапамятных времён это око охраняет Иссушитель."]
	quest.35D4F93EFB6EACB6.quest_desc: [
		"&aMagnetic Samarium&r (which you'll need for your &dLuV&r components) requires an &3IV Polarizer&r."
		""
		"Even so, we hope you weren't running all the polarization off a single &6HV&r Polarizer. Were you?"
	]
	quest.35D4F93EFB6EACB6.quest_subtitle: "Feeling attracted yet?"
	quest.35D4F93EFB6EACB6.title: "IV Magnetism"
	quest.35DC92C0C706A260.quest_desc: [
		"Items created with Tetra will have several different ways of leveling with use or construction."
		""
		"Synergy is the most basic form of leveling up a tool that comes during construction. The inclusion of the same head twice (double head pickaxe and axe for example) will give special bonuses to the tool. These special bonuses can be checked in the holosphere."
		""
		"Settling occurs per tool part with use. When a part becomes settled it will grant bonuses to the tool such as increased integrity, though if you remove the part you will lose the bonus. There are some upgrades that never settle so don't expect everything to."
		""
		"Finally, Honing also occurs with further use of a tool with stable parts. Certain parts will become honed with use (can be checked by holding shift and hovering over the tool) where they will be able to have additional unique upgrades applied to them at a workbench. This is to encourage you to keep using and upgrading your tools. You will lose the Honing of a part by removing it so be careful and plan your upgrades."
	]
	quest.35DC92C0C706A260.title: "Tool Leveling"
	quest.35E7E45987D9B1F6.quest_desc: [
		"So, what's on the agenda today?"
		""
		"New Cutting Machine? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Lens? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Power Circuit? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New EBF Metal required? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Coil for Energy Hatch? &a✓&r"
		""
		"&9Note:&r If you haven't found a Jungle yet, you can &acentrifuge Stone Dust&r for &dMetal Mixture Dust&r. This doubles as a Brown Dye."
	]
	quest.35E7E45987D9B1F6.quest_subtitle: "No one machine should have all this power!"
	quest.35E7E45987D9B1F6.title: "Power Integrated Circuit"
	quest.35EFFA6C85EFCA58.quest_desc: ["Circuits along this line are &3UV&r, and are interchangeable for each other."]
	quest.35EFFA6C85EFCA58.title: "&3UV&r Circuits"
	quest.35F13B6D60361904.quest_desc: [
		"&aTritanium&r is a material from Star Trek, and is used for a few other things in GT. It, like &9Americium&r, requires two fusion steps!"
		""
		"You'll need this to get the next tier of circuits, and for &3UV&r components."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In some versions of GT5u, only Tritanium fluid was red. The material was otherwise white. In GTCEu, we decided to make the whole thing red instead. Much better looking!"
	]
	quest.35F13B6D60361904.quest_subtitle: "Star Trek strikes again!"
	quest.35F13B6D60361904.title: "Tritanium"
	quest.363455215C23E84E.quest_subtitle: "Using this very delicate material, it will be used to create the best of the best machinery for UNLIMITED POWER!!"
	quest.363455215C23E84E.title: "&dThe Endgame"
	quest.3640D08452F6CF1C.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.3647B1B964A15E4E.quest_desc: [
		"This Circuit Board is used to create &dMV Circuits&r!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r You have &ltwo&r options when making the Phenolic Printed Circuit Board. If you use &aSodium Persulfate&r or &aIron III Chloride&r, making boards takes &6only a quarter of the Silver&r as opposed to the crafting recipe."
		""
		"&lHowever&r, given how painful it may be for you to obtain these chemicals &oright now&r, you can simply use more Silver by mining most of a Galena Vein..."
		""
		"The quest for &aSodium Persulfate&r is in the &bMV&r chapter, if you're down for some light reading."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Back in GTCEu 1.12.2, these circuit boards were called \"&2Good Circuit Boards&f\". Not exactly a fitting name, as they're &4rather evil&f to craft."
	]
	quest.3647B1B964A15E4E.quest_subtitle: "A Good Board"
	quest.3693C3F67BD59401.quest_desc: ["This combination allows wolves to catch up a lot more easily with you or nimble opponents, as well as last longer in battle."]
	quest.36A99F64857B21D7.quest_desc: ["В &eпустынях&r и &aджунглях&r, можно найти логово мирмексов. Этим логовом управляет &6королева&r, все рабочии и стражники выполняют её приказы."]
	quest.36DD94945D5B4A80.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, we were generous enough to leave Wood-to-Plank-ratios &cuntouched&r, but this is GregTech - charcoal smelting is &4&lnot possible&r in a Furnace. You'll need to make a &d&lCoke Oven&r to get your grubby hands on some &6charcoal&r."
		""
		"Wooden planks are still pretty good as &6furnace fuel&r, especially since you get &l&3four&r from one log."
		""
		"If this displeases you - normally you'd be able to &brevert this back&r to vanilla behaviour in the &aGTCEu&r configs, but the configuration option is bugged. To &erevert&r the nerf, you can delete the \"charcoal.js\" script in &bkubejs/server_scripts&r!"
	]
	quest.36DD94945D5B4A80.quest_subtitle: "Not here!"
	quest.36DD94945D5B4A80.title: "Charcoal?"
	quest.36ECD7C06649DE78.quest_desc: [
		"Coke will be very useful for steel, but it is also a powerful fuel."
		""
		"I hope that you can find a convenient location for your input and output hatches so it will run smoothly."
	]
	quest.36ECD7C06649DE78.quest_subtitle: "The Coke Oven is meant to make coke fuel, not soda. Remember to power this oven with steam using the input hatch and it will give coke in the output hatch. Always carry a wrench in order to see the multiblock structure."
	quest.36ECD7C06649DE78.title: "This is not Coca Cola!"
	quest.370EE225E8140570.quest_desc: ["Its maximum production rate is roughly 1 MEU/t."]
	quest.370EE225E8140570.quest_subtitle: "Do not underestimate SCIENCE! Without it, we wouldn't have been able to create the best energy producer of the mod!"
	quest.370FC1CDF5F9A9CC.quest_desc: [
		"The second circuit of the &4wetware&r line."
		""
		"This is also the best &cZPM&r circuit!"
	]
	quest.370FC1CDF5F9A9CC.quest_subtitle: "Did that circuit just BLINK at me?"
	quest.370FC1CDF5F9A9CC.title: "Best ZPM Circuits!"
	quest.37307A46E70011D3.quest_desc: [
		"Make this machine when you feel like it's time you invested into Batteries."
		""
		"It'll also be required if you want to make Storage Disks from &bApplied Energistics 2&r."
	]
	quest.37307A46E70011D3.quest_subtitle: "This machine does nothing exciting"
	quest.37307A46E70011D3.title: "Basic Canner"
	quest.373668AE257A7A94.title: "Cartridge"
	quest.3746FD072D591CBB.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade a Mallet and use it to break open a Geode at a Workbench"
	quest.375684F9CBEF9132.quest_desc: ["A circuit component that you can now produce thanks to the &3MV Assembler&r and your shiny new &3Kanthal EBF&r."]
	quest.375684F9CBEF9132.title: "Moore's Law"
	quest.375CE372A0A91A71.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of scale will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from leatherworker villagers."
	]
	quest.378F0AFCF95354B2.quest_desc: [
		"Refining &9Naquadah&r into further products will be your next automation challenge. The primary outputs of this line are &aEnriched Naquadah&r, &aNaquadria&r, and &aTrinium&r. "
		""
		"This processing line - affectionately known as the \"Naqline\" - also produces many useful byproducts, such as Titanium and Indium."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aEnriched Naquadah&r currently isn't used for much, but will be integral to power generation in the future."
		""
		"&aNaquadria&r is a lategame material that you'll want to stockpile for your &3UV&r components."
		""
		"&aTrinium&r is the material you'll be wanting most right now. You'll use a lot of it to build your first Fusion Reactor, is used for the next set of Coils, and sees heavy usage in most &cZPM&r recipes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eNote&r: This processing chain presents more of a challenge than any chemistry you've dealt with so far."
		""
		"As usual, outputs in later steps can be sent back into previous processes... with the caveat that they lose a small amount of fluid with each loop."
		""
		"This can be challenging to automate. Good luck!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Many GregTech iterations have Naquadah processing. "
		""
		"&oThe first was likely Impact, with its own original Naquadah fuel process. "
		""
		"&oGregicality Legacy was hot on its heels with processes for making the Naquadah material (and variants) as well as Fuel. "
		""
		"&oAfter that, GTNH added their own Naquadah processes for the material and fuel. "
		""
		"&oLastly, GTCEu added the process you're about to set up!"
	]
	quest.378F0AFCF95354B2.quest_subtitle: "Do not touch the acid"
	quest.378F0AFCF95354B2.title: "Naquadah Chain"
	quest.379C8E43BFC6678D.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &1чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.379C8E43BFC6678D.quest_subtitle: "&1Электрический комплект"
	quest.37A995EE494248AB.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.37AAB88A9EDCC862.quest_desc: [
		"This is the main way of getting &9Power&r via the &aBiochemical&r route. Put Logs in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r for &9Wood Tar&r. The Charcoal you obtain can then be processed in &3Extractors&r for even more &9Wood Tar&r!"
		""
		"Check out the Distillation quest to see what you can do with this wondrous substance."
	]
	quest.37AAB88A9EDCC862.title: "Wood Tar"
	quest.37CD6EBB40276EE2.quest_subtitle: "3rd Tier Capacitors used to upgrade to Blazing Machinery."
	quest.37E4C4EFA9E20B79.quest_subtitle: "Found in Hollow Hills in swamps. Unlocks The Dark Forest."
	quest.37E4C4EFA9E20B79.title: "Defeat the &2Hydra"
	quest.37EC97FB0FC6C56D.quest_desc: [
		"Both Topaz ores are excellent subjects for eventual electrolysis."
		""
		"This makes this vein one of the best Fluorine sources."
	]
	quest.37EC97FB0FC6C56D.quest_subtitle: "Source of Copper, Fluorine"
	quest.37EC97FB0FC6C56D.title: "Topaz"
	quest.381693770EF21108.quest_subtitle: "One of the Quarry's drills."
	quest.381693770EF21108.title: "&6Gold Drill"
	quest.382A9CC6F9B5740F.title: "Helmet"
	quest.38320B67645DE351.quest_desc: ["In the underground fortress there are goblins, trolls and other monsters that carry pieces of knight metal. It can be used to create powerful equipment."]
	quest.383B789B654C4094.quest_desc: [
		"Quite a journey to get here."
		""
		"The &3EV Circuit Assembling&r \"unlocks\" the next tier of Circuits, &5Nano&r."
	]
	quest.383B789B654C4094.quest_subtitle: "Consider yourself firmly in EV!"
	quest.383B789B654C4094.title: "EV Circuit Assembling"
	quest.384E5189E0273AE7.quest_subtitle: "Dry ice is used to cool down Reactors, another alternative to using water as coolant."
	quest.385079198388468C.quest_desc: [
		"Before making bronze, we will need to create a Forge Hammer."
		""
		"You can put iron, copper and tin ore in the forge hammer and you will receive 2 raw ores per ore."
		""
		"You can increase this ratio by using a Hammer."
		""
		"The Hammer increases the ratio in the Forge Hammer and unlocks more recipes, at the cost of some durability"
	]
	quest.385079198388468C.quest_subtitle: "Such a piece of equipment is surely gonna be important for our uses! It feels like we're doing blacksmith work!"
	quest.385079198388468C.title: "Are we Blacksmiths?"
	quest.3856DBCCAA6D2A58.quest_desc: ["You're gonna need to start on your &dPlatinum&r processing, or \"&bPlatline&r\", if you want to get your hands on these."]
	quest.3856DBCCAA6D2A58.quest_subtitle: "Tungstensteel is dead, long live RTM"
	quest.386BB0A6D8D16F8D.quest_subtitle: "Used in the creation of Calculation Processors in an Inscriber."
	quest.38993B4697B0E16C.quest_desc: [
		"A specialized motor needed to make certain machines."
		""
		"One of the more intricate crafting components, as it's made using a motor."
	]
	quest.38993B4697B0E16C.quest_subtitle: "A crafting component - did you expect anything fancier?"
	quest.38A2EA4D5BB0035B.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.38B08A136E92B917.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of skin (leather) will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from leatherworker villagers."
	]
	quest.38C955F6CBDD95BD.quest_desc: [
		"Your one and only trusty source for Nickel."
		""
		"Cobalt makes for some pretty decent early-game item pipes too!"
	]
	quest.38C955F6CBDD95BD.quest_subtitle: "Source of Nickel, Cobalt"
	quest.38C955F6CBDD95BD.title: "Nickel"
	quest.38D1336DC84E03FE.quest_desc: [
		"As mentioned in the main sections of this quest book, this &5Indium setup&r has a limited lifetime, so don't stress over optimising every last detail."
		""
		"Simply mix &dPurified Galena&r and &eSphalerite&r together with some &aSulfuric Acid&r to obtain &9Indium Concentrate&r, then combine with Aluminium Dust in a Chemical Reactor for your prize!"
	]
	quest.38D1336DC84E03FE.quest_subtitle: "Getting your first Indium has never been so fun."
	quest.38D1336DC84E03FE.title: "Indium Processing"
	quest.38DD5AB82C03E70D.quest_desc: ["Одолейта &dстража края&r и заполучите &dмогущественный артефакт&r, способный притягивать множество существ."]
	quest.38DE506FF5B32031.quest_desc: [
		"&6The best MV Circuits&r! You will be making these for the remainder of the game."
		""
		"Eventually (in &9IV&r), they will become even cheaper."
	]
	quest.38DE506FF5B32031.quest_subtitle: "MV has peaked"
	quest.38DE506FF5B32031.title: "Best MV Circuits"
	quest.38E5B595C33A071C.quest_desc: [
		"Carbon Monoxide is useful when making &6Butyraldehyde&r for your Laminated Glass in &9late IV&r."
		""
		"&6Coal Gas&r can be processed in a Distillation Tower for a variety of useful outputs."
		""
		"Helium-3 is only used in &bFusion&r, and Neon is used to boost a single &aBlast Furnace&r recipe - &4UHV&r superconductors!"
		""
		"Ashes are always useful for the handful of resources they grant."
	]
	quest.38E5B595C33A071C.quest_subtitle: "Carbon, Coal Gas, Helium-3..."
	quest.38E5B595C33A071C.title: "Liquid Nether Air"
	quest.38F9192F665742BA.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.38F9192F665742BA.quest_subtitle: "Now we can force items to be transported! Remember to force a connection with the pipes into machineries so they will transport them when needed."
	quest.38F9192F665742BA.title: "Item Transportation"
	quest.390E59F05132FCB8.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Chemical Reactor&r unlocks a ton of new recipes. Ah, who doesn't love the ever-growing demand on more advanced Chemistry?"
		""
		"&9Note:&r We've actually unlocked a ton of new content by reaching &6HV&r. However, not every processing line or item is crucial right now. It'd make the &6HV&r chapter far too dense if we included everything!"
		""
		"You could still check out the &5EV&r Chapter if you want to push yourself."
	]
	quest.390E59F05132FCB8.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry-heads rejoice!"
	quest.390E59F05132FCB8.title: "High Voltage Chemistry"
	quest.391E853DCE86BFD0.quest_desc: [
		"Resistors are components that will be used to make your first Circuit."
		""
		"It wouldn't be unwise to prioritise the recipes that use &aFine Wires&r, as they'll save you more materials in the long run."
		""
		"Wires may be expensive right now, but they'll get a lot cheaper in &7LV&r."
	]
	quest.391E853DCE86BFD0.quest_subtitle: "The easier component for circuits"
	quest.391E853DCE86BFD0.title: "Electronics #1: Resistors"
	quest.394ED7E8D84C03E9.quest_desc: ["The Clock shows the current time of day. Useful to know when it's time to return home or prepare for a night hunt."]
	quest.394ED7E8D84C03E9.title: "Clock"
	quest.3978C2DBE1B61990.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.3988E16DAA388261.quest_desc: ["An updated version of the ME Terminal that has an integrated Craft grid with access to the ME Network storage."]
	quest.39A58AFE2E0C13EB.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know Lazurite and Sodalite can be used as substitutes for &9Lapis&r in enchanting?"
		""
		"Sodalite is the most valuable Ore here, thanks to its useful electrolysis recipe when you get to &bMV&r."
	]
	quest.39A58AFE2E0C13EB.quest_subtitle: "Source of Lapis Lazuli, Aluminium, Sodium, Chlorine"
	quest.39A58AFE2E0C13EB.title: "Lapis"
	quest.39A6BA59CA48DA92.quest_desc: [
		"Can store a large number of enchanted books in one location. Combines enchanted books automatically, and enchanted books can be withdrawn at any available strength easily. A must-have for enchanters with storage problems."
		"Can save you a significant amount of exp when combining enchantments."
	]
	quest.39CFF60D8B06E5A3.quest_desc: ["Can be socketed into a tool then tweaked in the tweaking menu of the workbench to change the level of a tools abilities."]
	quest.39E7997F3080250A.quest_desc: [
		"Even without channels, P2P Tunnels are still extremely important automation tools!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r There are many fantastic resources online to explain how P2P Tunnels work. The short description is that they allow transfer of things from 1 input to endless output. You can link them using a Memory Card."
		""
		"This Quest acts as a tutorial on how to use the P2P Tunnels to your own benefit."
	]
	quest.39E7997F3080250A.quest_subtitle: "Fear not, channels are gone"
	quest.39E7997F3080250A.title: "P2P Tunnels"
	quest.39FADF9C0442304F.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.39FADF9C0442304F.quest_subtitle: "Dust to dust! Clay to bricks! Making these bricks aren't particularly hard, just turn regular bricks into dust, mix it with some clay and smelt."
	quest.39FADF9C0442304F.title: "Where's the Fire in Fire Clay?"
	quest.3A39842BDBE00DB3.quest_desc: ["В магнитных пещерах, вы встретите два типа кристалла: &cалый неодим&r и &9лазурный неодим&r. Из котрых можно создать разные предметы."]
	quest.3A7491323AC5C70C.quest_desc: [
		"HSS-S is another &mcompletely fictional&r &7High Speed Steel&r, alloyed with Iridium and Osmium."
		""
		"&aHSS-S&r will be necessary to craft &dLuV Motors&r."
		""
		"This alloy has a great mining speed, which translates into extremely good &6efficiency&r when used as a &dRotor&r in &3Large Turbines&r."
	]
	quest.3A7491323AC5C70C.quest_subtitle: "We made this one up"
	quest.3A7491323AC5C70C.title: "HSS-S"
	quest.3A768E3EC544BDE4.quest_desc: [
		"The Toolbelt will allow you to have different addons such as carrying extra tools, items, and potions. It is curios compatible in the belt slot."
		""
		"Check your keybinds to be able to use the quick access function or access key."
	]
	quest.3A768E3EC544BDE4.title: "Rope Toolbelt"
	quest.3A8D7FC6F316C38C.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't made a &eMixer&r yet, you'll need it to craft this."
		""
		"For now, you should use &9Water&r for its recipes instead of trying to acquire Lubricant."
		""
		"The &3Cutting Machine&r additionally unlocks converting &6Rods into four Bolts&r."
		""
		"This machine is the only way to obtain &dGem Plates&r, which are needed to craft Filters, and by extension, the &3Gas Collector&r."
	]
	quest.3A8D7FC6F316C38C.quest_subtitle: "The Cutter... cuts..."
	quest.3A8D7FC6F316C38C.title: "Basic Cutter"
	quest.3A9803430D9E7F3F.quest_desc: ["Shafts transmit rotational power in a straight line. They are essential for connecting your power sources to consumers."]
	quest.3A9803430D9E7F3F.title: "Shaft"
	quest.3AB5C392A3F8E3E1.quest_desc: ["&6Флейта дракона&r нужна в том случае, если ваш дракон взлетел в небеса, а спускаться не хочет. Чтобы его опустить на землю достаточно посвистеть в флейту."]
	quest.3ABB26FB3088F27B.quest_desc: ["Осколок фазмо выпадает из Эктоплит в незере, из него создаются стрелы, которые могут нанести урон призракам."]
	quest.3ABB26FB3088F27B.title: "Призрачные вещи"
	quest.3AED592F764C56FC.title: "Void Worm Blade"
	quest.3B08D63022E8D6A7.quest_desc: ["Создайте &aполимерную&r пластину."]
	quest.3B2469805D2E4E2B.quest_desc: ["This upgrade template is the base of many upgrades that can be applied to storage drawers."]
	quest.3B26CA44EA955B07.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7This quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3Fisher&r catches fish from Water. It requires a 5x5 area of Water directly below to operate. It uses the same loot table as normal Fishing, so it can catch things like &dEnchanted Books&r. Each operation consumes 1 String and EU equivalent to its tier (32 for &7LV&r, etc.) That's about it."
		""
		"&eFish Oil&r can be extracted from Fish, which can be used for &6Bio Diesel&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r tier Fisher to complete this quest. (They only go up to &5EV&r. If you foresee needing enough Fish to justify an &1IV&r or higher Fisher, make a feature request on our GitHub or Discord.)"
	]
	quest.3B26CA44EA955B07.quest_subtitle: "Women want me, fish fear me"
	quest.3B26CA44EA955B07.title: "Fishing 50"
	quest.3B2D2C47BEBCFFA7.quest_desc: [
		"If you want a big boost to your processing abilities, look no further than these powerful Multiblocks!"
		""
		"Formerly known as &2Gregicality Multiblocks&r, the add-on has been fully integrated into GregTech CEu Modern!"
		""
		"You'll need to make use of many new &9alloys&r to build the new Multiblocks. Yay, more content!"
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on the GCYM mechanics in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.3B2D2C47BEBCFFA7.quest_subtitle: "We made it so far..."
	quest.3B2D2C47BEBCFFA7.title: "Gregicality Multiblocks"
	quest.3B35688E3F0A13C0.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.3B379794A3030C73.quest_desc: ["A pure, very rich Tin vein - excellent for early game. You'll be over the moon to find one of these in the &6Steam Age&r."]
	quest.3B379794A3030C73.quest_subtitle: "#1 Source of Tin"
	quest.3B379794A3030C73.title: "Cassiterite"
	quest.3B3987FFF0725FD1.quest_desc: ["A small cogwheel transmits rotation to adjacent shafts or wheels. It can also change the direction of rotation."]
	quest.3B3987FFF0725FD1.title: "Cogwheel"
	quest.3B436487305AEE38.quest_desc: [
		"Deepslate centrifuges into... you guessed it... Silicon Dioxide! You may want to set this up for the guaranteed Biotite output, as Biotite electrolyses into Fluorine."
		""
		"This is obviously a far better source of Biotite than Stone Dust. Hopefully, you didn't waste your time setting that up!"
	]
	quest.3B436487305AEE38.quest_subtitle: "Silicon Dioxide, Fluorine..."
	quest.3B49BD004F38E1A2.quest_desc: [
		"This is a huge accomplishment, nice job!"
		""
		"The only ingredient that should be new to you are the &4Tritanium Frames&r."
	]
	quest.3B49BD004F38E1A2.quest_subtitle: "The &6final&r circuit"
	quest.3B49BD004F38E1A2.title: "Wetware Mainframe - The UHV Circuit"
	quest.3B55C9A41E94825E.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &6мирмекса&r."]
	quest.3B72CFB9F466DD76.quest_desc: ["Some dusts in &bGregTech&r have little use other than to be processed in an &3Electrolyser&r for some nice bonus chemical outputs. You can either set a manual filter for the desired items in a &aStorage Bus&r, or provide the most vital dusts via ME Interface, for example."]
	quest.3B72CFB9F466DD76.quest_subtitle: "We don't need THIS much Cobaltite, right?"
	quest.3B72CFB9F466DD76.title: "Electrolyse what's left!"
	quest.3BCA8923DF575D5D.quest_desc: [
		"Andesite Dust will get you some delicious Asbestos Dust, and some Saltpeter Dust to boot."
		""
		"Asbestos is a slow source of Magnesium, and Saltpeter has a variety of uses in chemistry."
	]
	quest.3BCA8923DF575D5D.quest_subtitle: "Asbestos, Saltpeter... (No Create)"
	quest.3BD68E5909A97532.quest_desc: ["The &aNeuro Processing Unit&r serves as the CPU for &4Wetware&r. It also takes a circuit board in its recipe, but don't let that scare you."]
	quest.3BD68E5909A97532.quest_subtitle: "Neurons for computation"
	quest.3BD68E5909A97532.title: "It's Alive!"
	quest.3BE6E50AA8E0170D.title: "Defeat a &6Mimic"
	quest.3C12FD23932C3522.quest_desc: [
		"To make colored cables, surround any type of dye with 8 cables of the same type (the color of the cables doesn't matter, but they must be of the same type, glass, smart, etc). You can also dye the cables with any forge compatible brush in the world."
		""
		"You can make any colored cable with a bucket of water to remove the paint."
		""
		"You can coat the cable with wool to create a Fluix ME coated cable, and make a Fluix ME smart cable to get a better idea of what's going on with your channels."
	]
	quest.3C12FD23932C3522.quest_subtitle: "The easiest cable to manufacture for power transmission."
	quest.3C1D930613F170F9.quest_desc: ["When added to the Forge Hammer it allows upgrades made with the hammer to have better stats."]
	quest.3C36AA80FE51DA45.quest_desc: [
		"The default way to deal with ores at this step is usually with the &eThermal Centrifuge&r for its &bexclusive byproduct&r, but check around the above quest to make sure you're not missing something important."
		""
		"&9Al&rle&4z!"
	]
	quest.3C36AA80FE51DA45.quest_subtitle: "This isn't Thermal Expansion..."
	quest.3C36AA80FE51DA45.title: "Thermal Centrifuge"
	quest.3C70B0717E9377A4.quest_desc: [
		"&dPotin Fluid Pipes&r have a &avery high throughput&r for the material tier and cost. You may want to look into making some of these to aid with fluid logistics."
		""
		"To get &dPotin&r, you should start by crafting its &eDust&r form."
		""
		"Get a &dPotin&r pipe of any size to complete this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o &dPotin Fluid Pipes&f were first seen in &9GT++&f, an addon to GT5, and are a considerable power spike for players in a relatively unknown pack called &4GT:NH&f. We wanted to spread some of that joy."
		""
		"&oIn the real world, &dPotin&f is an alloy used in coins, not pipes. GTCEu just gets more unrealistic by the day..."
	]
	quest.3C70B0717E9377A4.quest_subtitle: "...I'm going into battle, and I need only your finest Potin."
	quest.3C70B0717E9377A4.title: "Potin Seller..."
	quest.3CAD0701EC16C2D8.title: "Visit &6Dark Swamp"
	quest.3CBDB45D65737212.quest_subtitle: "found by stepping on &6Infested Sculk"
	quest.3CBDB45D65737212.title: "Defeat a &7Shriek Worm"
	quest.3CCD98E7139BA564.quest_desc: ["Whilst the majority &7(if not all)&r of the listed steps can be automated &3using GregTech alone&r, savvy players may wish to use &dAE2&r for all their logistics needs. Here, we'll cover some methods you may not be aware of to help you elevate your &aOre Processing&r to the next level."]
	quest.3CCD98E7139BA564.quest_subtitle: "Let's look at what AE2 can do for you!"
	quest.3CCD98E7139BA564.title: "Applied Energistics 2"
	quest.3CDA855A045A9F4D.quest_desc: [
		"&aUV Superconductors&r show up a lot in recipes when making a &9Fusion Reactor Mk3&r. Better get ready to make a boatload..."
		""
		"You can also use them to cheapen &9Superconducting Coils&r even further."
	]
	quest.3CDA855A045A9F4D.title: "UV Superconductors"
	quest.3CEBC51DB3555C3E.title: "Netherite Ingot"
	quest.3CECB3BAFED1E23D.quest_desc: ["Убив плотоядного червя, вы получите &eхитин&r. Который можно использовать для создания брони."]
	quest.3CF550B81716B8B9.quest_desc: [
		"Crafting Vacuum Tubes might make you question your existence. Sorry about that."
		""
		"This is mostly due to the fact that Wires and Rods are &7(sadly)&r very expensive right now, but they'll get cheaper in &7LV&r."
		""
		"Vacuum Tubes are also technically your first Ultra Low Voltage (&8ULV&r) Circuit! Congratulations! You won't find very much use for these by themselves, though."
	]
	quest.3CF550B81716B8B9.quest_subtitle: "The harder component for circuits"
	quest.3CF550B81716B8B9.title: "Electronics #3: Vacuum Tubes"
	quest.3D069ACDFD3F9EC5.quest_desc: ["Ancient Debris is a rare ore from which you can obtain Netherite. Look for them on the lower levels of the Nether."]
	quest.3D069ACDFD3F9EC5.title: "Ancient Debris"
	quest.3D09FAAE6A19976D.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &2мирмекса&r."]
	quest.3D1578DF95F261ED.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.3D18246B76F2B0E4.quest_desc: ["tomato"]
	quest.3D1F53C06B660F96.quest_subtitle: "Found in &fYeti Lairs &rin the &fSnowy Forest&r. Unlocks the &f&lSnow Queen&r."
	quest.3D1F53C06B660F96.title: "Defeat the &f&lAlpha Yeti"
	quest.3D4D88B8BE881351.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to cast better spells, you'll need a &6Scribe's Table&r to unlock new glyphs for your spellbook."
		""
		"There are 3 tiers of glyphs to unlock, and each one requires some experience and items."
		""
		"The Scribe's Table is also used to attach spells to Spell Parchments. To do this, place a Spell Parchment on the table, select the spell in your Spellbook, then sneak right-click the book on the table."
		""
		"To create a Glyph, right-click on the Scribe's Table with your spellbook. Search for the glyph you want to make, then click Select at the bottom. Right-click the table with the items required, and the glyph will be created. Use the glyph to learn it."
		""
		"Note: The table can pull items from nearby inventories."
	]
	quest.3D4D88B8BE881351.quest_subtitle: "Upgrading Spells"
	quest.3D523C82C9F7F64C.quest_desc: [
		"При помощи стола исследователя можно изучать способности реликвий найденных по всем мирам."
		"Чтобы им воспользоваться нужно положить реликвию на стол, нажав ПКМ по столу держа в руках реликвию."
		"После этого нажать Shift + ПКМ и откроется интерфейс. "
		"У реликвий есть своя система опыта, чтобы его получать вам нужно обычный опыт конвертировать в опыт для реликвий через стол исследователя. "
		"Также внизу интерфейса показаны способности реликвии, которые можно улучшать и прокачивать."
	]
	quest.3D550CD9EEE29E6F.quest_subtitle: "Medium tier processor."
	quest.3D5BF7E05FE7FF71.quest_subtitle: "Redstone is a component when creating Processors."
	quest.3D63DAC3E66CF7D8.quest_subtitle: "Use a Bolt to bind a tool or a sword, then use the tweak tab in a workbench to change the stats of the item"
	quest.3D6E4F18F20D4D9C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.3D862A3D3F83CA26.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Enchanting Apparatus&r is used to craft various items within the mod. It requires Source to work."
		""
		"It is also a multiblock structure that utilizes Arcane Pedestals to craft."
		""
		"Start by placing an Arcane Core in the ground, then place the Enchanting Apparatus on top of it. Surround the Apparatus with Arcane Pedestals."
		""
	]
	quest.3D862A3D3F83CA26.title: "Enchanting Apparatus"
	quest.3D90929CDE45D3D0.quest_subtitle: "Magmators use lava to generator power. The higher the tier, the more power and efficiency used from lava."
	quest.3D98819A799D2E64.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Chemical Reactor&r will be required for &la lot&r of recipes."
		""
		"Let's give it a spin - why don't we use your freshly made Chemical Reactor to unlock a new, &6better recipe for Rubber&r? Rubber is &dunusable&r as a Fluid, so you will need to make another machine to process it further."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can't make Rubber using the Chemical Reactor alone, so here are some &aother machines&r you might want to aim for: "
		""
		"A &3Solidifier&r is useful to solidify your Rubber directly into &aRubber Sheets&r. You'll want these moving forward."
		""
		"You could then make use of an &3Assembler&r to use your molten Rubber for &aCables&r. This isn't important for Tin Cables, but better cables will &eneed&r to be made in the Assembler."
		""
		"&eNote:&r Submit a fluid by having it stored in a &lbucket&r in your inventory. Sorry - it's an FTB Quests quirk."
	]
	quest.3D98819A799D2E64.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry for dummies"
	quest.3D98819A799D2E64.title: "Basic Chemical Reactor"
	quest.3D9D27F29D9D12F6.quest_desc: [
		"The &aUV Lapotronic Orb&r is even better than the &cZPM&r one! It of course comes at a price..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Imagine making 512 &1IV&f Orbs, or 64 &dLuV&f Orbs... or 8 &cZPM&f Orbs.... for just one of these! See the Lore for the LuV orb for details."
	]
	quest.3D9D27F29D9D12F6.quest_subtitle: "It holds way too much power!"
	quest.3D9D27F29D9D12F6.title: "Ultimate Battery?"
	quest.3D9E045B8D3F2B85.quest_desc: [
		"Some Gem ores - namely &cRuby&r, &9Sapphire&r, and &2Green Sapphire&r - can be mixed with Aqua Regia in their crushed form to obtain Slurry."
		""
		"When electrolysed, the Slurry has some interesting byproducts. Namely, it's one of the few ways to obtain &dTitanium Dust&r without macerating Titanium ingots!"
	]
	quest.3D9E045B8D3F2B85.quest_subtitle: "Not quite like Mekanism"
	quest.3D9E045B8D3F2B85.title: "Slurry Processing"
	quest.3DA4F9C4BFF85392.quest_desc: [
		"Создайте костюм &eхимзащиты&r."
		"\"Мы делаем сборку, Джесси\" - Стеф Уайт"
	]
	quest.3DAB175493B08089.quest_subtitle: "Found in Dark Oak Forests"
	quest.3DAB175493B08089.title: "Defeat the &8Conjurer"
	quest.3DC21B6F47A253E4.quest_desc: [
		"Provide it with items and energy, and watch your resources GO BRRR!"
		""
		"Its structure is exactly the same as the Steam Quarry's."
	]
	quest.3DC21B6F47A253E4.quest_subtitle: "The electric equivalent of the Steam Quarry."
	quest.3DC2E82860976E05.title: "Cardboard Armor"
	quest.3DD457633883E2A3.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони их хитина пустынного червя."]
	quest.3DD457633883E2A3.quest_subtitle: "Белая"
	quest.3DD457633883E2A3.title: "Хитиновая броня"
	quest.3DE11C6E8AACD30D.quest_desc: ["Elytra allow you to soar in the air using wind currents. This is the fastest and most convenient way to move between the islands of the End."]
	quest.3DE11C6E8AACD30D.title: "Elytra"
	quest.3DE7A2B91CFF48F6.quest_desc: [
		"When placed on a machine, Robot Arms are a more configurable version of a Conveyor Module. They allow you to transfer items in specific batches, at specific rates, or keep a certain amount of items stocked."
		""
		"Practical uses for the Robot Arm will be explained in future Quests as a tutorial."
		""
		"&9Note:&r The functionalities provided by the Robot Arm work &lonly&r if it is &lrequired&r to perform the operation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5 had blocks such as the Buffer, Filter and Type Filter to allow fine control over items. In GTCE it's all been replaced by the almighty Robot Arm and various Filter Covers. Much more compact!"
	]
	quest.3DE7A2B91CFF48F6.quest_subtitle: "You're going to hate making these"
	quest.3DEEF330074DD80C.quest_subtitle: "2nd Tier Capacitors used to upgrade to Hardened Machinery."
	quest.3DFFA8F91452C62A.quest_desc: [
		"A Circuit Component that you can now make thanks to the &3MV Assembler&r."
		""
		"If you want the cheapest recipe, &aNickel-Zinc Ferrite&r is the way to go."
	]
	quest.3DFFA8F91452C62A.quest_subtitle: "Z = jwL"
	quest.3DFFA8F91452C62A.title: "Inductors"
	quest.3E2E161F8CE35138.quest_desc: [
		"Don't panic! We'll mostly be doing this to get hydrocarbons."
		""
		"There are many ways to acquire &dEthylene&r from Oil processing. It's easy to get lost in all the options and recipes!"
		""
		"The best way is to steam-crack &aNaphtha&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r. Be sure to make the &aSeverely Steam-Cracked&r version for a higher yield of Ethylene."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once in &6HV&r, you'll have the option to do this recipe in the &3Cracking Unit&r at 100% efficiency. Unfortunately, the recipes you are doing with the Chemical Reactor have a loss of &450%&r."
		""
		"&9Note:&r All of this looks and feels terribly inefficient - we hope that's strong motivation to tier up! The &3Distillation Tower&r will be a huge upgrade for petrochem, but you're not quite there... yet. Right now, you'll have to use a &3Distillery&r to get &dEthylene&r."
	]
	quest.3E2E161F8CE35138.quest_subtitle: "Fuel and oil cracking can get complicated..."
	quest.3E2E161F8CE35138.title: "Fuel Cracking"
	quest.3E31CABE22FEB919.title: "Executioner Blade"
	quest.3E3EB69F34F50A9C.quest_desc: ["Marble Dust isn't anything to write home about, yielding Calcite and Magnesium."]
	quest.3E3EB69F34F50A9C.quest_subtitle: "Calcite, Magnesium..."
	quest.3E6DC423FE4A99F7.quest_desc: [
		"&aBatteries&r can be put into the energy slot at the bottom middle of machine GUIs, or in a &3Battery Buffer&r."
		""
		"When inside your inventory, they can be sneak-right-clicked to allow the batteries to &dcharge&r your EU items."
		""
		"&7LV&r, &bMV&r, and &6HV&r Batteries come in three forms, allowing you to pick the one you find the best depending on materials you have. &dLithium&r has the best capacity, followed by &dCadmium&r, then &dSodium&r."
		""
		"Our recommendation? Find a Salt vein, and either &aelectrolyze Salt&r for &dSodium&r, or &awash crushed Lepidolite&r for &dLithium&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r &aBattery&r to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.3E6DC423FE4A99F7.quest_subtitle: "Batteries for storing energy!"
	quest.3E6DC423FE4A99F7.title: "Batteries!"
	quest.3E869581140512FE.quest_desc: [
		"An upgraded bookshelf which add increased Eterna and some Quanta. Increases maximum Eterna."
		"Can be mixed with Seashelves for more balanced enchanting."
	]
	quest.3EA1138EA494F1C0.quest_desc: ["A Furnace is needed for smelting ores and preparing food. A basic survival essential."]
	quest.3EA1138EA494F1C0.title: "Furnace"
	quest.3EA48F9716705F18.quest_desc: ["Full-size 2x2 storage drawers will store 8 stacks of an item per drawer (32 stacks overall)."]
	quest.3EA48F9716705F18.title: "Full Storage Drawer: Four Items "
	quest.3EA4CB4D9C90B767.quest_subtitle: "Found in &eIllusioner Towers&r"
	quest.3EA8F4022DEEE82F.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.3ECD9C9B909CCCCC.quest_desc: [
		"&dSneak right-click&r when in hand to activate your Magnet. Do it again to deactivate. The battery capacity of your magnet depends on the battery used to craft it."
		""
		"If you're worried about getting overwhelmed by Cobblestone or Netherrack, use the trash can from FTB Utilities (top left corner of your inventory) to void them"
		""
		"&9Note:&r The magnet has a whitelist filter turned on by default (in other words, it's not going to pick anything up.) Right-click the magnet to tinker with the item filter settings. There's even a &ctag filter&r - you could, for example, whitelist only &braw ores&r!"
	]
	quest.3ECD9C9B909CCCCC.quest_subtitle: "Why can't these items I mine behave and enter my inventory!?"
	quest.3ECD9C9B909CCCCC.title: "Magnet"
	quest.3ED18704C8F9E5E9.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.3ED18704C8F9E5E9.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.3ED40CE1E4476C99.quest_desc: [
		"A goal if you really want to make a point."
		""
		"If you make this in a &3UV&r machine, it'll take you 10 days."
		""
		"If you overclock a Gregicality Multiblock to UEV (by using a 4A &4UHV&r hatch), you'll still be waiting for 2.5 days!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The NAN Certificate comes from Crops++, a GT5u addon that adds a wide variety of IC2 crops."
	]
	quest.3ED40CE1E4476C99.quest_subtitle: "Obtain for G.O.A.T Status"
	quest.3ED40CE1E4476C99.title: "Certificate of not being a Noob anymore"
	quest.3EDD50F03E605456.quest_desc: ["Steel is a durable alloy needed for creating heavy equipment and advanced mechanisms. Produced in a blast furnace."]
	quest.3EDD50F03E605456.title: "Steel Ingot"
	quest.3EEDC2C14BD73F44.quest_desc: ["Оружие, основанное на явлении радиоактивности."]
	quest.3EEDC2C14BD73F44.title: "Ядерная мощь"
	quest.3F058322E1A8D5EC.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &afinal silicon boule&r, which will allow you to produce a ton of wafers."
		""
		"It also unlocks the recipe for the &aHighly Advanced SoC&r, which is used to make cheaper &4wetware circuits&r."
	]
	quest.3F058322E1A8D5EC.quest_subtitle: "Neutron -> Electron Holes"
	quest.3F058322E1A8D5EC.title: "Neutronium-doped Silicon Boule"
	quest.3F123950216DF93B.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Packager&r compresses &aTiny Dusts&r and &aSmall Dusts&r into &afull Dusts&r, which can be compressed further into Ingots."
		""
		"It can also work in reverse, change between sizes of Wires, and much more..."
		""
		"Unpacking Cables back into Wires and Rubber will be &every useful&r once you rewire your Energy Network."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&oYeah, we know...&r the 3x3 compacting recipes don't seem useful, because you can just use a Crafting Table. We urge you to consider the utility of this machine when used for &9automation&r purposes."
		""
		"For an &9automated&r Dust setup, route &aTiny Dusts&r into a buffer inventory (a chest will do) placed next to your &3Packager&r."
		""
		"Next place a &3Robot Arm&r and configure it to \"&dImport&r\", and \"&dSupply Exact 9&r\". Finally, let the Machine auto-output on another side."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GTCE, the reverse operation required a separate machine - the Unpackager."
	]
	quest.3F123950216DF93B.quest_subtitle: "Look who's packing"
	quest.3F123950216DF93B.title: "Basic Packer"
	quest.3F31E99D0284A60A.quest_desc: [
		"Doping &9Silicon&r with &9Naquadah&r will give a better &aSilicon Boule&r."
		""
		"Use it for higher yield on &dWafers&r."
		""
		"This will also unlock the &6best recipe&r for &6HV&r Circuits in the &3LuV Circuit Assembler&r. You're probably going to want to mass produce these for the many &dLapotronic Energy Orbs&r that'll be required moving forwards."
	]
	quest.3F31E99D0284A60A.quest_subtitle: "Doper than ever before"
	quest.3F31E99D0284A60A.title: "Naquadah-doped Silicon Boule"
	quest.3F6DE3A5F00BD543.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.3FD702B5AB006402.quest_desc: [
		"Have you ever wanted to just hover everywhere you go?"
		""
		"This belt allows you to levitate. To activate, just sneak while in the air, either while falling or from jumping."
	]
	quest.40018C0546454CD9.quest_desc: [
		"While distilling &aWood Vinegar&r gives &aAcetone&r, the yield is low and might not meet your needs."
		""
		"You might want to use the direct &3LCR&r recipe from &aAcetic Acid&r to obtain &aAcetone&r."
		""
		"If you want to be fancy, you can also use the good old &aAcetic Acid&r -> &dDissolved Calcium Acetate&r -> &aAcetone&r loop, which does not require a &3LCR&r, but still recycles the Calcium compound perfectly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"We've been talking about Acetic Acid, but we're yet to tell you how to obtain it. Wouldn't that be great?"
		""
		"&aAcetic Acid&r can be synthesized in the &3Chemical Reactor&r. Our favorite recipe is from &dEthylene&r."
	]
	quest.40018C0546454CD9.title: "Acetone"
	quest.402245A432850997.quest_desc: ["Деликатес для богатых"]
	quest.402245A432850997.title: "Мидии"
	quest.4024C831C77101CA.quest_desc: [
		"If you've killed an Enderman before, you may have noticed it dropped &aEnderpearl Dust&r instead of an Ender Pearl. In order to get &aEnder Pearls&r, you must make them from Enderpearl Dust in the &3Implosion Compressor&r."
		""
		"&9Pro tip for non-Peaceful players&r: Trapping Endermen in Boats makes them much easier to kill! They also have a higher spawn rate in &dWarped Forests&r in the &4Nether&r compared to other locations before &9The End&r."
		""
		"In the long term, &aEnderpearl Dust&r should be made in an &3HV Mixer&r."
	]
	quest.4024C831C77101CA.quest_subtitle: "Darn \"artificial gating\""
	quest.4024C831C77101CA.title: "Ender Pearls"
	quest.4032D56BB750AAE8.quest_desc: ["The Pickaxe head is.... a pickaxe head. It allows you to mine just like you would expect it to do."]
	quest.40408FFD02134148.quest_desc: [
		"&aPolyvinyl Chloride (PVC)&r is the 3rd-most produced plastic in real life. Here in CEu, it can be substituted for Polyethylene in the production of &aPlastic Circuit Boards&r and other items to increase the yield. It is required from &5EV&r onwards to wrap Cables."
		""
		"PVC item pipes also have the &6highest throughput&r available for a while, but most of your setups right now won't need such speed. Still, it's good to keep this knowledge in your pocket."
		""
		"&9Pro tip:&r The fluid form of PVC is never used in base GTCEu, so feel free to solidify all of it into sheets."
	]
	quest.40408FFD02134148.quest_subtitle: "You've already made one polymer, what's two?"
	quest.40408FFD02134148.title: "Polyvinyl Chloride"
	quest.40727B8380F9A2D7.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.4073577B7EF9B593.quest_desc: [
		"Many materials going forward cannot be smelted directly from any Ores! They are instead obtained as byproducts from processing of other ores. Gallium and Arsenic are &4among&r these materials."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For &dGallium&r, you may, ranged from worst to best (compromising difficulty and yields):"
		""
		"&9- &3Electrolyze &aSphalerite&r for a low chance of dust. Note that you lose out on direct smelting value."
		""
		"&9-&r Put &aCrushed Bauxite&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r. Note that this requires &9Sodium Persulfate&r."
		""
		"&9-&r Obtain it as a Byproduct of &aSphalerite&r Ore Processing in the &3Thermal Centrifuge&r or &3Centrifuge&r."
		""
		"For &dArsenic&r, you will have to mine and &3centrifuge&r &aRealgar&r."
	]
	quest.4073577B7EF9B593.quest_subtitle: "I hate byproducts, they're awesome"
	quest.4073577B7EF9B593.title: "Gallium Arsenide"
	quest.409FDC9E0FBF40CB.quest_desc: ["The main feature of Applied Energistics 2 is the ME (pronounced Emm- Eee and stands for Matter Energy) network, which is a set of interconnected blocks and cables grouped into a system where storage, power, and function interact between multiple components."]
	quest.409FDC9E0FBF40CB.title: "Crystals are the way to go"
	quest.40A80DABB31AE408.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.40B20CED5F5F034A.quest_desc: ["Убейте кораблекрушителя - ужасного монстра, живущего в подводной бездне."]
	quest.40B20CED5F5F034A.title: "Гроза морей"
	quest.40B40DF0D1295A90.quest_desc: [
		"The vein to mine for &bAluminium&r and &dTitanium&r if you're a well-adjusted person."
		""
		"Ditch those Mica veins - Bauxite is the future!"
	]
	quest.40B40DF0D1295A90.quest_subtitle: "Source of Aluminium, Titanium, Gallium"
	quest.40B40DF0D1295A90.title: "Bauxite"
	quest.40BC67BDEE15D1DE.quest_desc: ["To create Source Gems, we'll need to put either Lapis or Amethyst Shards into the Imbuement Chamber. Over time, these will convert to Source Gems!"]
	quest.40BC67BDEE15D1DE.title: "&5Source Gems"
	quest.40DE888E6025C646.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Primitive Blast Furnace&r (&3PBF&r for short) is a multiblock you will become very familiar with in the next few hours."
		""
		"It is &cimportant&r that you get a &3Macerator&r before tackling this quest - if you haven't made one yet, this multiblock will be &lfour times as expensive&r."
		""
		"Using your fancy new &3Macerator&r, you'll need to process &d132 Clay&r, split into &d66 Clay Dusts&r and &d66 Brick Dusts&r."
		""
		"Build the structure using &4EMI's Multiblock preview tab&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Steel will be &9of utmost importance&r throughout the entire game, so make sure you keep that PBF running. We should clarify that the PBF isn't the only way to get Steel throughout your playthrough, though!"
		""
		"Steel also has &6double the durability&r compared to regular Iron for GregTech tools. It also provides &6Diamond mining level&r, and is much faster."
	]
	quest.40DE888E6025C646.quest_subtitle: "Steel Yourself for Greater Things"
	quest.40DE888E6025C646.title: "Primitive Blast Furnace"
	quest.40EEB0207CDFD670.quest_desc: ["The Smart Chute allows you to filter items passing through it. This greatly simplifies resource sorting."]
	quest.40EEB0207CDFD670.title: "Smart Chute"
	quest.40FB56274D296BFC.quest_desc: [
		"To turn a P2P Tunnel into a &aGTEU P2P Tunnel&r, right-click it in the world with a &dWire&r or &dCable&r."
		""
		"This is ideal in lategame situations to negate Cable or Transformer spam. You can also use them in conjunction with the AE2 Quantum Bridge to power your high tier Miners and Drills outside your base."
		""
		"There is a &45% Voltage Tax&r on the output side of the P2P, resulting in 5% energy loss."
	]
	quest.40FB56274D296BFC.quest_subtitle: "Unfortunately, unavailable to any British players"
	quest.40FB56274D296BFC.title: "EU P2P Tunnels"
	quest.4105C6C9192BBFF7.quest_desc: ["Убив &dпикси&r, вы получите пыльцу, из которой можно будет приготовить &dамброзию&r."]
	quest.4116E36045C3B3C3.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.4136E21A1E21C5FA.quest_desc: ["Да - это они."]
	quest.4136E21A1E21C5FA.title: "Бабушкины закрутки"
	quest.41616C31D9C08648.quest_desc: [
		"A decent alternative to the pure Tin vein if you haven't found one yet."
		""
		"The other ores are as good as decoration."
	]
	quest.41616C31D9C08648.quest_subtitle: "Source of Tin"
	quest.41616C31D9C08648.title: "Cassiterite Sand"
	quest.41730E340B3D8EDA.quest_desc: [
		"Some of the details are repeated from the introduction quest, but we feel like we needed to expand on the explanation if you want to know all the details!"
		""
		"Ready for some \"light\" reading?"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each vein can contain up to four different ores."
		""
		"Ore veins generate in a &4Grid&r. Every vein is spaced by 3 chunks from one to another in a cardinal direction. Each vein generates in an individual \"pattern\" - some are &6round&r, some are &asnakey&r, and others you'll discover for yourself."
		""
		"They spawn at the &4Center&r of the Chunks which have both their X and Z coordinates be at &b1 plus a multiple of 3&r (-8, -5, -2, 1, 4, 7, ...). You will typically find two veins in the selected chunk - one will be in the Stone layer, and the other vein lays deeper in the Deepslate layer."
		""
		"However, Ore veins may be deleted by caves, Oil deposits, or from trying to generate above the ground."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"It's a good practice to make &dWaypoints&r to every vein you find, and to label their type. You may want to come back to it several times."
		""
		"A classic Ore vein is &d7 blocks&r tall, and ores generate in 4 different patterns:"
		"- The &9Top Ore&r generates in the higher 4 layers of the vein."
		"- The &9Bottom Ore&r generates in the lower 3 layers of the vein."
		"- The &9Between Ore&r generates in the middle 3 layers of the vein."
		"- The &9Sporadic Ore&r generates anywhere in the vein. There will be the least amount of this ore in a vein."
		""
		"The same ore type can be in 2 different generation patterns, such as in Cassiterite veins."
	]
	quest.41730E340B3D8EDA.quest_subtitle: "You'll be an expert by the time you finish reading this!"
	quest.41730E340B3D8EDA.title: "Ore Generation"
	quest.419F7B74E30C2AF4.quest_subtitle: "A specialized drill used to dig for crude oil and only useful in an Oil Drilling Rig."
	quest.419F7B74E30C2AF4.title: "&bAluminum Drill"
	quest.41A0BE357C8A74E1.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Alchemical Sourcelink&r produces Source from adjacent potion jars."
		""
		"The amount of source varies per potion and complexity."
	]
	quest.41A0BE357C8A74E1.quest_subtitle: "Power through Potions"
	quest.41A1EAE9CF93D9C6.quest_desc: ["Самые редкие вещи подводной бездны."]
	quest.41A1EAE9CF93D9C6.title: "Подводные сокровища"
	quest.41A5B68621213ED8.quest_desc: ["The other Cable Hubs work the same way, just a matter of materials and aesthetics."]
	quest.41AF664375E88893.quest_desc: ["Create a set of Yeti armour."]
	quest.41AF664375E88893.title: "Yeti Armour"
	quest.41B99DBD03EB74FF.title: "Improved Blast Furnace"
	quest.41D32C5178760F47.quest_desc: [
		"Regardless of whether you're playing on Peaceful or not, you will have to defeat the &4Ender Dragon&r to return to the Overworld safely."
		""
		"Prepare yourself with a bow, a few arrows, a blade, and some beds &7(speedrunner strats!)&r."
		""
		"This quest will print the &alocation of the nearest Stronghold&r in chat. This &cwon't work&r if you have cheats disabled, unfortunately."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9The End&r has even more new veins and materials to harvest, such as &ePlatinum&r and &7Naquadah&r! Similar to Nether ores, End ores are &6worth two Overworld ores&r."
		""
		"&aEyes of Ender&r are additionally used in crafting certain components, or for creating &5Quantum Eyes&r."
	]
	quest.41D32C5178760F47.quest_subtitle: "...but not the end of your playthrough"
	quest.41D32C5178760F47.title: "The End of an Era"
	quest.41DD503169987D50.quest_desc: [
		"&3Concrete&r and &3Studs&r are two decorative block families added that increse your speed when walking on them, with &3Concrete&r increasing your speed more."
		""
		"Get &9either&r of them to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.41DD503169987D50.quest_subtitle: "Subsonic!"
	quest.41DD503169987D50.title: "Gotta go fast"
	quest.41F0B8A5BEB41CC0.quest_desc: ["Много-много разных рулетов."]
	quest.41F0B8A5BEB41CC0.title: "Рулеты из лавомерки"
	quest.422E7B7E24ADCE47.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.4231410A54694CFE.quest_desc: [
		"Crush dirt for nitrate, crush sulfur for... sulfur..."
		""
		"Then, just mix with water!"
	]
	quest.423CB9115B942CEA.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		""
	]
	quest.4252B1AF36FFB4F6.quest_desc: [
		"Early game Circuits are hand craftable."
		""
		"Pick up the &3Circuit Assembler&r to make them a lot more efficient."
	]
	quest.4252B1AF36FFB4F6.quest_subtitle: "Hand crafted and artisanal"
	quest.4252B1AF36FFB4F6.title: "Craftable in &6Steam Age&r and &7LV&r"
	quest.42721BC1F7734286.quest_desc: ["It is used to print products using various lettering plates."]
	quest.42760D3A86EFDCA3.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Data Bank&r is a multiblock capable of storing huge amounts of data. You can fill it with &aData Access Hatches&r, and fill those with &aData Storage Items&r."
		""
		"After that, you'll need power, and then a way to connect it to your Assembly Line! This is done through &3Optical Fiber Cables&r, which can be used to link &3Optical Data Hatches together&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"An &9Optical Transmission Hatch&r is used to send data (like an output), and an &9Optical Reception Hatch&r to recieve the data (like an input). "
		""
		"Optical cables have some restrictions however. They can only connect &eone input to one output&r. The Data Bank is your answer to this, since you can place many hatches on them to route your data anywhere."
		""
		"You can use this behavior to &echain&r Data Banks as well. Connecting one Data Bank to another, and then one of them to an Assembly Line will provide the data of both banks!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eNote: &rThis multiblock will be required later on in progression, but is very useful to set up early."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This multiblock also originates from TecTech, but part of its mechanics required optical cables to be painted as well. You don't have to do that here, but it looks really nice if you do!"
	]
	quest.42760D3A86EFDCA3.quest_subtitle: "Time for a server room"
	quest.42760D3A86EFDCA3.title: "Mass Data Storage"
	quest.427E6091713399FE.quest_desc: [
		"You'll want to send off the following ores to &aPlatinum Group Processing&r:"
		""
		"- Purified Chalcopyrite Ore"
		"- Purified Tetrahedrite Ore"
		"- Purified Chalcocite Ore"
		"- Purified Bornite Ore"
		"- Purified Sheldonite Ore"
		"- Purified Pentlandite Ore"
		""
		"Treat these ores with &eNitric Acid&r to receive your &5Platinum Group sludge&r, alongside a Sulfuric byproduct fluid. What you do with these &boutputs&r... is up to you to figure out!"
		""
		"&8(Hint: It's in the EV chapter.)"
	]
	quest.427E6091713399FE.quest_subtitle: "Quite the rabbit hole to jump down..."
	quest.427E6091713399FE.title: "Platinum Group Processing"
	quest.428C62749A1A1BAB.quest_desc: ["The &aCreative Energy Cell&r is one of the few craftable creative items. It provides infinite energy to your AE system, so you don't have to worry about blackouts or power anymore."]
	quest.428C62749A1A1BAB.quest_subtitle: "Ok, maybe there are Creative items."
	quest.428C62749A1A1BAB.title: "Creative ME Energy"
	quest.42A4FAD05869BF4A.quest_subtitle: "Silicon can be crafted by smelting Certus Quartz Dust. It's used alongside an Inscriber and Inscriber Silicon Press to create Printed Silicon."
	quest.42B5FA94E571CC7E.quest_desc: ["В бункерах подводной бездны вы сможете найти &6водолазные костюмы&r, чтобы быстрее и удобнее передвигаться под &bводой&r."]
	quest.42B5FA94E571CC7E.title: "20 тысяч блоков под водой!"
	quest.42CD789B8C40E424.quest_desc: [
		"The first circuit of the &9Crystal&r line."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The concept of a Crystal Circuit has existed since the very early versions of GregTech. We're still not entirely sure if they exist in real life."
	]
	quest.42CD789B8C40E424.quest_subtitle: "I know where this is going!"
	quest.42CD789B8C40E424.title: "Best IV Circuits!"
	quest.42F579E53977DF2C.quest_desc: ["Вам придётся убить огромную змею в &aСумеречном лесу&f, чтобы заполучить это око."]
	quest.42F91220B6FA66FC.quest_desc: ["Multiple &don-tier machines&r are never a bad idea, but you should definitely consider using the Large multiblock variants of the singleblock machines from &aGregicality Multiblocks&r. They're significantly easier to upgrade as you progress through the later tiers of the mod (would you rather make a &616A LuV Energy Hatch&r, or &b16 LuV Macerators&r?!), and plus... they look rad as hell."]
	quest.42F91220B6FA66FC.title: "How would I boost my processing power?"
	quest.42FB276AB16258D9.quest_desc: [
		"Fluorine is the rarest gas to obtain from electrolysis in this game."
		""
		"You can obtain it from &aLepidolite&r, &aBastnatite&r, and &aMica&r, but the best source is from &aTopaz&r."
	]
	quest.42FB276AB16258D9.title: "Fluorine"
	quest.4300E87679E7D662.quest_desc: ["You have reached the very edge of the world. Void reigns here, inhabited by strange creatures, and at the center of it all — the mighty dragon."]
	quest.4300E87679E7D662.title: "The End"
	quest.4329D355F5B2E80D.quest_subtitle: "Used alongside an Inscriber and Inscriber Engineering Plate to create a Printed Engineering Circuit."
	quest.433BE663989445B9.quest_desc: [
		"Some stages listed on this page output Small/Tiny Dusts, or Nuggets. These have little use in such a form, so it's never a bad idea to route these into a &dPacker&r to \"&7compress&r\" them into their full forms."
		""
		"If you're having problems with the Packer filling up with too few Nuggets and clogging your buffer, then you may want to consider using a &6GregTech Robot Arm&r set to \"Supply Exact\". Send your Nuggets in 9 at a time, and you can consider this a problem solved!"
	]
	quest.433BE663989445B9.quest_subtitle: "With our powers combined..."
	quest.433BE663989445B9.title: "Do we need to package?"
	quest.4343746E706264E6.quest_desc: [
		"&aAmmonia&r is &doptional&r in &6HV&r."
		""
		"You may use it in the production of:"
		""
		"&9-&r Nitric Acid, although we don't recommend this."
		""
		"&9-&r Rocket Fuel, required for Nether Stars in &1IV&r."
		""
		"&9-&r Polybenzimidazole (now THAT'S a tongue twister!) in &1IV&r."
		""
		"The \"least painful\" recipe should be the one in the &3HV Chemical Reactor&r. Make sure your &aHydrogen&r production (mostly from &aWater electrolysis&r) is enough to support the demand."
		""
		"You could also obtain &aAmmonia&r as a waste product from &dPlatinum Group Sludge&r processing."
	]
	quest.4343746E706264E6.quest_subtitle: "The Nectar of the Gods"
	quest.4343746E706264E6.title: "Ammonia"
	quest.4347E50649ED9BCC.quest_desc: ["The Grapevine Pot allows you to grow grapes right in your home or basement. Provide it with support for growth."]
	quest.4347E50649ED9BCC.title: "Grapevine Pot"
	quest.4353AB0E20601AEC.quest_desc: [
		"&aSodium Persulfate&r can be used in &9Ore Processing&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r to get various bonus outputs you would not normally obtain. It's completely optional, but pretty rewarding."
		""
		"&lWait, stop! That's only a distraction&r - the real topic of this Quest is..."
		""
		"&aSodium Persulfate&r and &aIron III Chloride&r are used to make cheaper &9Good Circuit Boards&r, as their inclusion cuts Silver usage by a factor of four."
		""
		"They're also &drequired&r to make &9Plastic Circuit Boards&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Making &aSodium Persulfate&r will yield &aHydrochloric Acid&r as a coproduct, which you may re-use to make &aIron III Chloride&r. This should the best approach right now, but the decision is entirely yours."
		""
		"With more automation later in the game, Iron III Chloride will be the cheaper and more straight forward path."
		""
		"This Quest requires &eboth&r Fluids to complete. You'll need both anyway..."
	]
	quest.4353AB0E20601AEC.quest_subtitle: "Let's etch some Copper off Circuit Boards!"
	quest.4353AB0E20601AEC.title: "Sodium Persulfate / Iron III Chloride"
	quest.436A76A36A764C00.title: "Anvil"
	quest.4384068C4517F3D9.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Charcoal Pile Igniter&r is a particularly unique multiblock. You can use it to produce &aCharcoal&r faster than &3Coke Ovens&r, but this comes with the trade-off of &amanual labor&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To operate the Igniter, dig a big pit into the ground - up to &e9x9x5&r blocks in size. Line the floor of the pit with vanilla &aBrick blocks&r, then fill the remaining space entirely with &aLogs&r. After that, &esurround the filled pit&r with Grass, Dirt, or other natural groundcover. In the layer with the roof, place the Igniter! To start it, light it with &aFlint and Steel&r."
		""
		"Once the process completes, open up the pit for your reward - &aBrittle Charcoal&r. This can be mined with a Shovel (or Spade!), and each block drops 1.4 Charcoal on average. Assuming 1 Log converts into 1 Brittle Charcoal, we're sure you can see the efficiency boost!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eNote&r: The pit must be &cfull to the brim&r with Logs - Air blocks will prevent this Multiblock from forming."
		""
		"&eNote&r: This quest is &boptional&r. If you would like to skip this quest, hit the checkmark instead."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This multiblock originated in GT5u, but did not require a fire-starting item to start."
	]
	quest.4384068C4517F3D9.quest_subtitle: "I'm the trouble starter, punkin' instigator..."
	quest.4384068C4517F3D9.title: "Fuel Pit"
	quest.43A2E8E5E1F40FD5.quest_desc: ["Фаршированный хоглин - это вкусно."]
	quest.43A2E8E5E1F40FD5.title: "Фаршированный хоглин"
	quest.43A98A87D1245D4E.quest_desc: ["Заберите &dдревние артефакты&r, что были запечатаны в пустотном черве."]
	quest.43D5A5F95EEB339C.quest_desc: [
		"Pulverise your Diorite into Dust, then centrifuge for Mirabilite Dust and Clay Dust."
		""
		"Mirabilite yields minimal Sulfur, but Clay Dust is the real treasure here. When electrolysed, you'll get some Aluminium for your troubles. Not bad!"
	]
	quest.43D5A5F95EEB339C.quest_subtitle: "Mirabilite, Clay..."
	quest.43DA52F807C059C5.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект инструментов из кости &6дракона&r и кости &6иссушителя&r."]
	quest.43DA52F807C059C5.title: "Оружие из кости дракона"
	quest.43F43FB0B9ED0818.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.43F43FB0B9ED0818.quest_subtitle: "A Steel Wiremill will be useful to create even more sophisticated machinery, but also remember that you need some raw synthetic oil and paper to make rubber sheets and more."
	quest.43F43FB0B9ED0818.title: "Do not tangle up the wires, okay?"
	quest.44266A4B1118A31E.quest_subtitle: "5th Tier Capacitors used to upgrade to Spirited Machinery."
	quest.444C900DAF64643F.quest_desc: ["Ядро - основной компонент шотгана, стреляющего плотью призраков. "]
	quest.445395C4CC42250D.quest_desc: ["Полезные вещи для интерьера."]
	quest.445395C4CC42250D.title: "Интерьер пекарни"
	quest.447D1005B0881D70.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Knife on grassy plants will yield Straw, a useful building and composting material. Early on, it's best used to craft some Ropes."
		""
	]
	quest.44875B6FA3D7CE74.quest_desc: ["Shields will be the best way to protect yourself outside of armor."]
	quest.44937B2D2EB38094.title: "Craft a &6Warden Helmet"
	quest.44B22A645FC94C64.quest_desc: ["Converts energy from external systems into electrical energy and stores it in the grid."]
	quest.44C8C983C934BEB0.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.44EE18F81A61FCEE.quest_subtitle: "Capacitors are the next parts that are used to create a variety of electric machinery, you can either combine two capacitors to get a large one or cut one to get two tiny capacitors."
	quest.44EE18F81A61FCEE.title: "Secondary Parts"
	quest.451C8D5D92F1BAED.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4527D540B69980FD.title: "Simply Swords"
	quest.452EF09F6CB4AD99.title: "Wire Relay"
	quest.452FE521007EE0D9.quest_subtitle: "To craft a meteorite compass, charge a normal compass in a Charger. This can be done very early by using a Wooden Crank.The Meteorite Compass points in the direction of the nearest Meteorite within a range of 2,700 blocks. If the compass is spinning rapidly there is Sky Stone in your chunk! If the compass is spinning slowly, then you need to explore more because you're out of range of the nearest Meteorite."
	quest.452FE521007EE0D9.title: "Preparing to Find Meteorites 2"
	quest.455276A3C6A12E55.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.4555AD508D9C6CEB.quest_desc: [
		"It has the ability to sort and search and filter using the view cell. It requires a channel to function."
		""
		"It can be upgraded into a terminal to create ME."
	]
	quest.4555AD508D9C6CEB.quest_subtitle: "HID that gives you access to items stored on your ME network. This will also include items accessible via the ME Storage Bus."
	quest.45656B8C14DF42BE.title: "Craft &6Warden Leggings"
	quest.4575644C7E5F2DEE.quest_subtitle: "The Mixer will help you mix dusts or fluids for a cheaper price. Just don't put your food ingredients in here, or it'll smell bad."
	quest.4575644C7E5F2DEE.title: "Is this for baking?"
	quest.45769156F4253C86.quest_desc: [
		"&aDiesel&r is a &dOil-based &9Combustion Fuel&r."
		""
		"To mix &aLight Fuel&r and &aHeavy Fuel&r, the right ratio for &3Distilleries&r is &63:2&r from &dOil&r or &dRaw Oil&r."
		""
		"This would necessitate 3 Distilleries for Light Fuel, or 2 Distilleries for Heavy Fuel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can cut the amount of &dOil&r required &6drastically&r by using &dHeavy Oil&r for &aHeavy Fuel&r specifically. &dOilsands&r is a great option if you wish to go down this route!"
		""
		"&o(For the math nerds, you go from 8.33 Oil -> 6 Diesel, to 5 Oil + 0.4 Heavy Oil -> 6 Diesel)&r"
		""
		"&eNote:&r Do &cnot attempt&r to put Oil in the &3Distillation Tower&r You might think it's a good idea because it gives both Light Fuel and Heavy Fuel. However, this process requires a lot of overclocking to be worth your time, and you will lose more energy than what the byproducts are worth."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In general, it is better to prioritize placing down more machines (&dparallelisation&r) over overclocking the recipes. That way, you end up losing less energy processing the resources."
		""
		"&aDiesel&r is burned in a &3Combustion Generator&r. It can be further refined to &6Cetane-Boosted Diesel&r in &6HV&r. Compared to the other power sources, it is generally more efficient, but a more demanding processing line. If you take the &eOil&r route for &aPolyethylene&r, this can work great with existing infrastructure. Ultimately, the power source you want to use is your choice."
	]
	quest.45769156F4253C86.quest_subtitle: "Mother, how is diesel made?"
	quest.45769156F4253C86.title: "The Church of Diesel"
	quest.457DE8C154641437.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Ritual Brazier&r is used to cast rituals. It can also be used for decoration. If you want to light the Brazier, use a Light spell on it."
		""
		"To perform rituals, you'll need Arcane Pedestals as well. As there are so many rituals to cast, make sure to check out each of them using the &6Worn Notebook&r!"
		""
		"This can be done by holding Ctrl on the Ritual Table while the book is in your inventory."
	]
	quest.45969FFBF88F4FBB.quest_desc: [
		"More resources are always nice. You're getting close to entering the &6age of Steam&r - Copper and Tin are required in many &6Steam Age&r machines, so check the ore tab to find out what veins they can be found in, and get mining!"
		""
		"If the different ore names are &bconfusing&r, you can tell which elements an ore holds at a glance by reading the &dmolecular formula&r in its tooltip. Copper is &oCu&r, Tin is &oSn&r, Iron is &oFe&r, and you can consult a &3periodic table&r for the rest. It's time to brush up on your chemistry - you'll need it for &llater&r."
		""
		"This quest can be completed with &9either metal&r, so you can claim the metal you're missinng as the reward. Be sure to find a source of both soon, as a &a&ocertain&r&a Copper-Tin alloy&r will be needed to get through the &6Steam Age&r."
	]
	quest.45969FFBF88F4FBB.quest_subtitle: "Gather more resources!"
	quest.45969FFBF88F4FBB.title: "Onwards to the Age of Bronze!"
	quest.45B62B35180593EA.quest_desc: [
		"Almost a pure Copper vein. Damn you, Stibnite, ruining our purity!"
		""
		"You can hardly complain about its presence, though - Stibnite smelts directly into Antimony, which you will want in &7LV&r for your Batteries."
	]
	quest.45B62B35180593EA.quest_subtitle: "Source of Copper, Antimony"
	quest.45B62B35180593EA.title: "Tetrahedrite"
	quest.45B71324028F6E68.quest_desc: [
		"As mentioned in the previous quest, electrolyse the &1Sapphire Dust&r to get your &bAluminium Dust&r."
		""
		"Now all you need is an EBF! If you haven't started to work towards one, move to the right on this quest page and you'll end up there."
	]
	quest.45B71324028F6E68.quest_subtitle: "Aluminium, not \"Aluminum\""
	quest.45B71324028F6E68.title: "Aluminium Dust"
	quest.45CA8DCA8226945A.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &bMV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"The pattern stays the same: the rightmost circuit comes in &dlarger quantities&r and is overall &aeasier&r to produce."
	]
	quest.45CA8DCA8226945A.title: "&bMV&r Circuits"
	quest.45DC77C714EB294E.title: "Katana Blade"
	quest.45E300FD7CD05A37.quest_desc: ["The &3Data Module&r is required for Endgame Research. &aAssembly Lines&r cannot read from it using &aData Access Hatches&r directly, and instead require the &9Data Bank&r."]
	quest.45E300FD7CD05A37.quest_subtitle: "Data storage sure is expensive..."
	quest.45E300FD7CD05A37.title: "Data Module"
	quest.45E97F13A097FB32.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &cдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.45E97F13A097FB32.title: "Броня из драконостали"
	quest.45F9AAE4ABE32033.quest_desc: [
		"By this point, normal Cables have such insignificant loss that superconductors aren't a requirement."
		""
		"You can use those as a flex!"
		""
		"Superconductors are still required to craft &aField Generators&r."
	]
	quest.45F9AAE4ABE32033.title: "HV Superconductors"
	quest.45FBEABEBA7CC09E.title: "Visit &6Sunken city"
	quest.4600221BF0A30C3A.quest_desc: [
		"At this point, you have all the tools available to start making Plastic Boards. Higher-tier polymers in future will increase your PCB yields substantially."
		""
		"The recipe chains are starting to get pretty long, so we recommend processing large batches in two dedicated &3Chemical Reactors&r."
	]
	quest.4600221BF0A30C3A.quest_subtitle: "It's a Casio on a Plastic Board"
	quest.4600221BF0A30C3A.title: "Plastic Boards"
	quest.4623789A4EE01FDA.quest_desc: ["После победы над грозовым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &7драконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.4623789A4EE01FDA.quest_subtitle: "&7Чёрная"
	quest.46319F2AE2F90532.quest_subtitle: "A new multiblock made of titanium that can turn water into HP (high pressure) water, steam into HP steam, and the other way around."
	quest.46319F2AE2F90532.title: "Stop giving me peer pressure!"
	quest.46367A76755866D9.quest_desc: [
		"Here are the four most relevant &dHydrocarbons&r you will be obtaining from distilling Steam-Cracked Fuels."
		""
		"You will want to set this up &lbefore&r moving to &1IV&r."
		""
		"&aSteam-Cracked Light Fuel&r as input is probably the most favorable, but you are free to experiment."
		""
		"We know what you're thinking - something along the lines of \"&7&oThat Carbon output is just SO infuriating! It's ruining my automation!&r\"."
		""
		"Enable Item Voiding (in the controller GUI) if you don't want to build an Output Bus."
	]
	quest.46367A76755866D9.title: "True Distillation: Fuel"
	quest.4661838E492BDE53.quest_desc: ["Steam machines will accept inputs from any side, be it items, steam or another fluid. You can lock their slots by clicking on the lock in the interface. Locked slots only accept one type of item or fluid."]
	quest.4661838E492BDE53.quest_subtitle: "Full Steam Ahead! You have now made it to this point of learning how tech works, are you ready for more?"
	quest.4661838E492BDE53.title: "&6Your First Bronze!"
	quest.466AC4DD902115EF.quest_desc: [
		"When running the &3Extreme Combustion Engine&r, you're gonna want to boost it! &m&7Why bother otherwise?&r"
		""
		"Get yourself a &34A IV Dynamo Hatch&r as the output, and set up a &3Vacuum Freezer&r to provide &aLiquid Oxygen&r."
		""
		"You should now be wielding the equivalent of 1 &dLuV&r Amp, all whilst burning fuel at &6200% efficiency&r!"
		""
		"Don't forget to keep it supplied with a small amount of &aLubricant&r."
		""
		"The &3ECE&r is also void-free, unlike Large Turbines. Any energy that cannot be output will momentarily pause the multiblock."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The ECE comes from GT:NH. However... its implementation wasn't so rosy at first. The stats on the tooltip looked similar to this one - so far, so good."
		""
		"&oThe bad part came when crunching the numbers. Players ended up realizing they needed to run around 16 whole &6HV&f Vacuum Freezers to keep up with the Liquid Oxygen demand..."
		""
		"&oThe one and only fuel it would accept is High Octane Gasoline, which was stated to be burned at 300% efficiency when boosted, but the UI was lying. The efficiency remained at 100%."
		""
		"&oThe GT:NH team eventually decided to rework the ECE among other power options... phew!"
	]
	quest.466AC4DD902115EF.quest_subtitle: "The ultimate Combustion generator!"
	quest.466AC4DD902115EF.title: "Extreme Combustion Engine"
	quest.466BE34F78A7FC03.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.468E6FCD361B1404.title: "Netherite-iron armor"
	quest.468EEFD9D2F69014.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Research Station&r is the upgrade to the Scanner. It's used for more advanced forms of research, and will finally allow you to perform research which requires &aData Orbs and Modules&r."
		""
		"When running the &3Research Station&r, energy and &9Computation&r is needed. The latter is provided through an &9HPCA&r, which is explained in the next quest. It is recieved with a &3Computation Data Reception Hatch&r. Note that only one Reception Hatch is allowed in a Research Station."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This multiblock needs computation &dsporadically&r, which means the recipe will not reverse progress if you don't supply enough - it will simply halt in-place. However, the machine will still draw energy constantly, even when recieving no computation."
		""
		"To scan items, the process is relatively similar. In the &3Object Holder&r, place the target item in the center slot, and the data storage item in the other slot. Then provide computation, and the data storage item will be updated upon completion. When running, the target item will be Locked and cannot be removed."
		""
		"&eNote&r: To form this multiblock, the &3Object Holder&r must face the controller."
	]
	quest.468EEFD9D2F69014.quest_subtitle: "Your research adventures continue!"
	quest.468EEFD9D2F69014.title: "Research Station"
	quest.469641436BC858D3.title: "Guide"
	quest.46A5FB31B70E248C.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &1чешую&r."]
	quest.46A5FB31B70E248C.quest_subtitle: "&1Тёмно-синяя"
	quest.46AD7A6F3B6775F5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Superconductors&r are special Wires available for each Voltage tier. They don't come with a Cable counterpart, but that isn't necessary, as they have absolutely &6zero cable loss&r."
		""
		"They also won't damage you when you touch them. This makes them the best choice for wiring, if not a little expensive in comparison to the other wires."
		""
		"If you weren't already enamoured, the 1x variant also covers 2 Amps. Isn't that nice?"
		""
		"Now is a good time to replace your crappy &aTin Cables&r. Recycle them in the &3Packager&r to recover both the Tin and Rubber used to craft them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Can't figure out how to make some of these? Here's a hint - &eTricalcium Phosphate&r and &2Pyrolusite&r ought to help."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o No version of GregTech has had actual Superconductors for &7LV&f up until Gregicality and GTCEu, though some modpacks had lossless cables."
	]
	quest.46AD7A6F3B6775F5.quest_subtitle: "We aren't losing a single Amp more"
	quest.46AD7A6F3B6775F5.title: "LV Superconductor"
	quest.46B3BB368D86D931.quest_desc: [
		"The Electromagnetic Separator is an interesting machine that skips &6two processing stages&r, but usually returns &2unique&r byproducts that aren't usually too simple to obtain. You'll need to process down pure dusts to use this - so &bmake sure&r you route any desired ores correctly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You may &bappreciate&r performing this stage of processing on the following ores:"
		""
		"- Bastnasite Ore &7(This is particularly strong for Neodymium!)&r"
		"- Naquadah Ore &7(The Enriched Naquadah byproduct is very powerful!)&r"
		"- Nickel Ore"
		"- Tin Ore"
		"- Goethite Ore"
		"- Hematite Ore"
		"- Chromite Ore"
		"- Ilmenite Ore"
		"- Pyrite Ore"
		"- Yellow Limonite Ore"
		"- Glauconite Sand Ore"
		"- Magnetite Ore"
		"- Vanadium Magnetite Ore"
		"- Granitic Mineral Sand Ore"
		"- Basaltic Mineral Sand Ore"
	]
	quest.46B3BB368D86D931.quest_subtitle: "Maximising Naquadah"
	quest.46B3BB368D86D931.title: "Electromagnetic Separator"
	quest.46C7E1D5E37B1ED2.quest_desc: [
		"You can now remotely expand your AE2 network if you're looking to move bases."
		""
		"A full set of two &3Quantum Tunnels&r is no slouch to craft, so you'll need to break a sweat if you want them."
	]
	quest.46C7E1D5E37B1ED2.quest_subtitle: "[-h^2/2m∇^2 + V(x,t)]ψ(x,t) = iht'ψ(x,t)"
	quest.46C7E1D5E37B1ED2.title: "Quantum Tunnel"
	quest.46D1B23EA92DFBC0.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &6чешую&r."]
	quest.46D1B23EA92DFBC0.quest_subtitle: "&6Бронзовая"
	quest.46E386050F3DA112.quest_desc: ["The Water Wheel is one of the simplest sources of rotational power. Place it next to flowing water to start it spinning."]
	quest.46E386050F3DA112.title: "Water Wheel"
	quest.47087361D6DE7DCF.quest_desc: ["Cheaper &dLuV&r circuits! These'll take some of the edge out of those brutal Robot Arm recipes."]
	quest.47087361D6DE7DCF.quest_subtitle: "Yup... another circuit upgrade"
	quest.47087361D6DE7DCF.title: "Even more LuV Circuits"
	quest.47123B901690686D.title: "Saber Blade"
	quest.471B85B964C578A7.quest_desc: [
		"Yup - &brenewable&r Glass."
		""
		"Glass'll always be useful throughout your playthrough in a variety of recipes."
	]
	quest.471B85B964C578A7.quest_subtitle: "Glass Hurts, doesn't it..."
	quest.4734E8ED60D024D5.title: "Explore the World"
	quest.474222302C8257C4.title: "Gold Armor"
	quest.47450E3E6F80ED9F.quest_desc: ["Can remove curses from an item. Used in an anvil with a cursed item. Consumes levels on use."]
	quest.474E2DF13B4D268C.quest_desc: ["На равнинах и горах, можно изредка встретить пасущих овец и других животных, &6циклопа&r. Они обладают большими размерами силой, что ставит их чуть ниже драконов."]
	quest.4752C473CA8ED916.quest_desc: ["&dAlpha Yeti&r is a huge Yeti who lives in a small snowy hill with his younger brothers. He possesses ice magic, which makes him a dangerous opponent."]
	quest.4752C473CA8ED916.title: "Aplha Yeti"
	quest.4775178C26F9B458.quest_desc: ["Some crafts have been changed in the modpack so that you can explore other mods. More changes are planned for the future"]
	quest.4784E2B69A5E19DA.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.478A5773B71C3151.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.478A5773B71C3151.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.478A7F7565AFC8A8.quest_desc: ["From now onwards, you'll be sending &ball of your ores&r towards &6all kinds of places&r, depending on how far you are through your playthrough. Quests will unlock around this node when you &aunlock the ability&r to deal with them, so check back occasionally if you're feeling bored."]
	quest.478A7F7565AFC8A8.quest_subtitle: "Started from the Raw Ore, now we here"
	quest.478A7F7565AFC8A8.title: "We've got some Purified Ore - what's next?"
	quest.478B0D55369C0F7F.quest_desc: [
		"The &3EV Mixer&r is required for more alloys."
		""
		"This is important if you want to get your hands on some &dTungstensteel&r."
	]
	quest.478B0D55369C0F7F.quest_subtitle: "Beginning to notice a pattern?"
	quest.478B0D55369C0F7F.title: "Extreme Mixing"
	quest.4795979571F1FAEA.quest_subtitle: "A modified furnace capable of generating AE Power instead of smelting ores. When placed on an ME Network it will charge Energy Cell or power other Network Devices.The Vibration Chamber will burn almost any solid burnable fuel for power. It will slow, or accelerate the burn depending on how much power it is able to store vs what is wasted. Generates between 1 and 10 AE/t depending on its burn speed."
	quest.4795979571F1FAEA.title: "Powering your Network 2"
	quest.47A8E5DC11E846C5.quest_desc: ["Forge mod?"]
	quest.47C361784A461BE4.quest_desc: [
		"RU - Бросьте вверх и направляйтесь туда куда полетело око эндера. Возможно придется копать вниз!"
		""
		"EN - Throw it up to see the way, it is located underground"
	]
	quest.47CEF7F4A5DE9EBF.quest_desc: ["Here are all the basic ways to store your resources and organize your warehouse."]
	quest.47CEF7F4A5DE9EBF.title: "Storage"
	quest.47D4545452F05E37.quest_desc: [
		"The &aFluid Regulator&r is sort of the equivalent to a &9Robot Arm&r for Fluids."
		""
		"It can transfer fluids, but has two useful modes:"
		""
		"&9-&r &dSupply Exact&r will transfer the amount of specified Fluid per tick if available. No more, no less."
		"&9-&r &dKeep Exact&r will make sure the exact amount of Fluid in the attached machine is being kept."
	]
	quest.47D4545452F05E37.quest_subtitle: "A cover!"
	quest.48141DBA683F6B5A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Distillation Tower&r is a multiblock that will help you extract the most out of fluids. In &3Distilleries&r, you had to pick only one product to output. DTs output &6all of it at once&r!"
		""
		"&9Note the special placement rules:&r Energy, Items, and Fluid Inputs can only be placed on the bottom layer. Maintenance can be placed anywhere. Fluid Outputs can only be placed starting on the second vertical layer, and only allow one per layer as well."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &3DT&r can form at any height from &c&c3&r to &c13&r blocks, allowing 2 to 12 Fluid Outputs. Fluid will always output on the layer corresponding to the recipe in &2EMI&r."
		""
		"The &3DT&r has one more &9special&r rule. You can deliberately build it too short, and it will &cvoid&r whichever Fluid should have been output at the top layers that were removed. This can be useful in some very niche situations."
		""
		"It is a good idea to use &3Super Tanks&r as the output for every layer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cNote:&r Using the &3Distillation Tower&r for Oil -> Fuel -> Diesel is &cnot&r worth it! You will spend more energy overclocking the Multiblock than what you would get back from the products. It would be better to wait until you can make the &3Large Distillery&r (&1IV&r) for large scale Diesel production. "
		""
		"However, the DT is &6very valuable&r when extracting Cracked Fuels and Pyrolyse products."
	]
	quest.48141DBA683F6B5A.quest_subtitle: "Time for a real oil refinery!"
	quest.48141DBA683F6B5A.title: "Distillation Tower"
	quest.4823F73FBA0274DF.quest_desc: [
		"To use the zoom you will need a &3spyglass."
		""
		"(opens with the C key)."
	]
	quest.4823F73FBA0274DF.title: "Zoom"
	quest.4826DCD2FC457EA5.quest_desc: [
		"A great vein for the early game. Copper and Tin to make Bronze, Realgar for your first source of Arsenic, and Zeolite for... nothing much."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o As GregTech used to auto-generate its recipes, Zeolite used to electrolyze in batches of 141 dust at a time. Whoops!"
	]
	quest.4826DCD2FC457EA5.quest_subtitle: "Source of Copper, Tin"
	quest.4826DCD2FC457EA5.title: "Chalcopyrite"
	quest.4847BA675A04852F.quest_subtitle: "The most powerful machine upgrade ever. Have a look for yourself, maybe you can create a Replicator?"
	quest.488477D975B8C132.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.48A284AAE8CE703D.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &dчешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.48A284AAE8CE703D.quest_subtitle: "&dАметистовый комплект"
	quest.48AED37B4E20A99A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bAlloy Smelter&r is used for, well, alloys. You'll want it for the efficient &6Bronze&r recipe, and for &4Red Alloy&r in the near future."
		""
		"Out of all the &6Steam Age&r machines, this is the most steam-hungry. If you ever find yourself running out of steam, give your machine a &alove-tap&r with &dany Soft Mallet&r to momentarily pause it."
	]
	quest.48AED37B4E20A99A.quest_subtitle: "The Alloy Smelter makes alloys..."
	quest.48AED37B4E20A99A.title: "Steam Alloy Smelter"
	quest.48DEABA155605D23.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest will be completed with &eeither&r an &3IV Energy Hatch&r&r... or an &3IV Dynamo Hatch&r for your Multiblock Generators."
		""
		"Don't forget that &d4 Amp&r variants exist! However they require &aNiobium-Titanium Cables&r, which need &9Polyphenylene Sulfide&r."
		""
		"Look down in the &dLuV&r Chapter for that (don't worry... it's easy to obtain)."
	]
	quest.48DEABA155605D23.quest_subtitle: "This is second nature at this point"
	quest.48DEABA155605D23.title: "Upgrading your EBF for the millionth time"
	quest.492CEF5FB6C065B7.quest_desc: ["При &9удачном&r изучении таблички вы узнаете информацию о пещерах, покрытых магнитными кристаллами, хранящих много древних технологий."]
	quest.492CEF5FB6C065B7.quest_subtitle: "Магнитные пещеры"
	quest.4946FC5BCA4CCA88.quest_desc: [
		"The &e&lCoke Oven&r will likely be your first &aGregTech&r multiblock. Congratulations!"
		""
		"It is used to make &aCoke&r from &eCoal&r, or &aCharcoal&r from &eWood&r, in addition to &dliquid Creosote&r as a &3bonus&r output."
		""
		"Take a look at the &6Multiblock Preview&r tab in EMI (press &dU&r over the controller block of any Multiblock!) to see the structure pattern."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r &lAny&r Brick block can be replaced with a &3Coke Oven Hatch&r. You can have up to five of them."
		""
		"The Hatch allows for automation - it'll &dauto-export&r both Fluid and Items! It also works for insertion into the Coke Oven (you can use Hoppers)."
		""
		"If the Coke Oven happens to fully fill up on &eCreosote&r that you are not using, break and replace the Coke Oven block. &3Automated fluid voiding&r is available later in the game."
		""
		"&lTip:&r A bucket of Creosote fuels a furnace for &c32&r items! Take full advantage of this to stop burning planks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The concept of multiblocks is a modded Minecraft classic. Think of IC2's Nuclear Reactor, or Railcraft's Coke Oven - truly revolutionary at the time!&r"
	]
	quest.4946FC5BCA4CCA88.quest_subtitle: "Your first big project... hopefully"
	quest.4946FC5BCA4CCA88.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.49761EAAB5D1F6A6.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &cчешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.49761EAAB5D1F6A6.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасный комплект"
	quest.49761EAAB5D1F6A6.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.497EA4E350997965.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.499506BBA2F2BF14.quest_subtitle: "Thermo Generators use heat sources under them to generate power and use water to cool down. The higher tier, the more power generated from heat."
	quest.49973B0404761173.title: "Defeat the &6Eye of the Storm"
	quest.49997B92CC48A598.quest_desc: ["The max redstone upgrade will output a redstone signal equivalent to how full the most filled drawer."]
	quest.49A04E63F40D65C0.quest_desc: [
		"Don't worry, these crafts are actually useful - you'll be required to make &ehundreds more&r of these components. It's good to start building the habit."
		""
		"It's generally wise to get familiar with the idea of &o\"&bbulk-crafting&r&o\"&r - if you need 1 plate, try making 8, etc. This means you'll have lots of these &dintermediates&r ready for future crafts. It might seem unreasonable to craft &astacks of rods&r or &ascrews&r especially this early on, but they will always end up being used, saving you a lot of micro-crafting in the future."
		""
		"If you needed &6any more&r convincing, take a peek at the &drewards&r for this quest."
	]
	quest.49A04E63F40D65C0.quest_subtitle: "Put your micro-crafting talent to the task!"
	quest.49A04E63F40D65C0.title: "A Minor Test of Strength"
	quest.49C1D61741AA288E.quest_desc: [
		"The first Circuit of the &1Quantum&r line. This is the last \"easy\" circuit line - things are about to get hectic."
		""
		"If you wish, you could go even further and aim for &dAdvanced SMDs&r to make these Circuits cheaper. "
		""
		"Doing so will require &9PBI&r... and Alloys that require &aHSS-G Coils&r in your EBF."
	]
	quest.49C1D61741AA288E.quest_subtitle: "Quantum Processing"
	quest.49C1D61741AA288E.title: "Best EV Circuits!"
	quest.49D7C5EE6E5F3DBB.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &4брони&r, а также &4лук&r из теневого шёлка и других ресурсов &4забвенных пустот&r."]
	quest.49D7C5EE6E5F3DBB.title: "Жуткое оружие"
	quest.49DC0BD7DC1B893C.title: "Visit &6Abyss"
	quest.49DCD65D23BB72C4.title: "Find &4Citadel"
	quest.49E6DC9CF4CAAAD9.quest_subtitle: "Obtained by mining spawners. The level of Fortune on your pickaxe affects how many fragments drop from a spawner."
	quest.49E6DC9CF4CAAAD9.title: "Obtain &8Spawner Fragments"
	quest.4A041E600B41F4C3.quest_subtitle: "Used alongside an Inscriber and Inscriber Calculation Plate to create a Printed Calculation Circuit."
	quest.4A365A7CC9E374F9.quest_desc: [
		"This hammer isn't quite like the ones you'll use for crafting. It actually works as a &d3x3 pickaxe&r!"
		""
		"If you're familiar with &a&lTinker's Construct&r, it behaves &esimilarly&r to hammers from that mod."
		""
		"Shift-right-click with a mining hammer in your hand to adjust the area of effect."
		""
		"Make &bgood use&r of these hammers! They'll help you to clear out an entire vein in &6record time&r."
		""
		"&eNote:&r Any quest with GregTech tools can be complete with tools crafted from any material - not just the one displayed."
	]
	quest.4A365A7CC9E374F9.quest_subtitle: "Mining just became efficient"
	quest.4A365A7CC9E374F9.title: "Hammer down!"
	quest.4A7379ED5BC0C161.quest_desc: ["A very nice volcanic stone hammer, stonger than most metals."]
	quest.4A92AFD2532EED26.quest_desc: [
		"If you're wanting to dive into &bMV&r, start here."
		""
		"The dusts created in an &3MV Mixer&r have great utility."
	]
	quest.4A92AFD2532EED26.quest_subtitle: "Mixing more complex alloys"
	quest.4A92AFD2532EED26.title: "Advanced Mixer"
	quest.4A96337843BAC13A.quest_desc: ["Amperage goes up - we're now at a whopping &e6A&r per Superconductor."]
	quest.4A96337843BAC13A.quest_subtitle: "Power Creep"
	quest.4A96337843BAC13A.title: "EV Superconductors"
	quest.4A993CC40AB6D35C.quest_desc: [
		"With your first &8Steel&r under your belt &7(ha!)&r, you can make a &bTool Belt&r to free up inventory space from all those pesky GT tools. It can be equipped in its own &ddedicated Curio slot&r."
		""
		"By default, the hotkey to open the belt is &eR&r, but you can rebind it if you prefer. From this GUI, you can place tools inside the belt's storage, and swap them with your &dmain-hand tool&r whenever is convenient."
		""
		"The belt has a small initial inventory of a single tool. This can be expanded by combining the belt with &bBelt Pouches&r in an &aAnvil&r - the maximum slottage is &69 slots&r."
	]
	quest.4A993CC40AB6D35C.quest_subtitle: "Take some weight off your inventory"
	quest.4A993CC40AB6D35C.title: "Tool Belt"
	quest.4AAB3899F530CC19.title: "Chute"
	quest.4AABEFF8E855D8D8.quest_subtitle: "Fluix ME Glass Cable is the simplest cable to make, transfers power and up to 8 Channels. It comes in 17 different colors, the default being Fluix, and can be dyed any color using any of the 16 dyes."
	quest.4AC1C083537E8706.quest_desc: [
		"Assemble and power it with the camera or generators from other mods."
		""
		"You can also power it manually with the crank handle "
	]
	quest.4AC1C083537E8706.quest_subtitle: "Provides the ability to charge supported instruments via the ME network."
	quest.4ACC10C8890C306E.quest_desc: ["Use a mains powered charger to charge the Certus Quartz Crystal."]
	quest.4AD93229344EA0BE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4AD93229344EA0BE.quest_subtitle: "The Bronze Furnace is just as slow as a normal furnace, but it uses steam instead of any other fuel source, and cheaper as well."
	quest.4AD93229344EA0BE.title: "Is it to steam food?"
	quest.4AEAC79007790BD8.quest_desc: [
		"At the cost of 16x the drilling Power, the &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig II&r will be gaining &664x the output&r in Fluid."
		"The depletion of veins is also slashed to an eighth of what it was before. This means you will get a total of &6128x&r as much Oil (or whatever fluid) as the regular rig from a bedrock fluid vein until depletion!"
		""
		"Even when depleted, you can safely use this and be very much power positive."
		""
		"One single &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig II&r should be enough to last you until the end of the game, for whatever fluid you drill."
	]
	quest.4AEAC79007790BD8.quest_subtitle: "This thing is completely ludicrous!"
	quest.4AEAC79007790BD8.title: "Ludicrous Fluid Drilling"
	quest.4AFD3073C731A1E4.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &5EV&r Circuit gets a unique texture. If you still consider yourself to be in &bMV&r, &ahold off&r on making too many of these, as they won't benefit you right now. We can't stop you from making these if you &djust wanna flex&r on us, though."
		""
		"It'll be needed in &6HV&r."
	]
	quest.4AFD3073C731A1E4.quest_subtitle: "Standing out amongst the rest"
	quest.4AFD3073C731A1E4.title: "First EV Circuits!"
	quest.4B0041B9D9DEED73.quest_desc: ["The Compass always points to your world spawn point. Helps find your way back if you get lost."]
	quest.4B0041B9D9DEED73.title: "Compass"
	quest.4B2D031595A25305.quest_subtitle: "A component used in the creation of an ME Terminal."
	quest.4B486C7CC66F1745.title: "Netherite-emerald armor"
	quest.4B656D6D4F32D64E.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &4брони&r, а также &4лук&r из теневого шёлка и других ресурсов &4забвенных пустот&r."]
	quest.4B8D66A65F102D7E.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Diode&r (the block, not the component) accepts energy inputs from 5 sides, but only outputs through a single side."
		""
		"Its main purpose is to &dlimit Amperage&r. It'll help you regulate any centralised power generation, so you can distribute your power everywhere without having to math out what cable size is safe depending on consumers..."
		""
		"They can also be used as an electric equivalent to Repeaters when the voltage loss from Cables (or GTEU P2P tunnels - more on that later!) gets too high."
		""
		"You can use a &5Soft Hammer&r to change the Amperage limit of the output."
		""
		"&eAny&r of the listed Diodes will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.4B8D66A65F102D7E.title: "Diode"
	quest.4B979482EF026BFF.quest_desc: [
		"We made it to &7LV&r! Give yourself a pat on the back!"
		""
		"Just kidding &7(lol)&r, you actually need three Circuits to get started anywhere relevant in &7LV&r. Thankfully for you, someone left this spare circuit laying around."
		""
		"We also want you to make an &aLV Machine Hull&r for this quest. You'll need one if you're to make any &7LV&r machine. We're feeling generous enough that this quest will grant you a second Hull, free of charge!"
		""
		"Circuits are an integral part of progression in GregTech, so keep climbing."
		""
		"&6Once you complete this Quest and the LV Motor Quest, you are ready to move on to the LV Age.&r"
	]
	quest.4B979482EF026BFF.quest_subtitle: "Your first &aElectronic Circuit&r!"
	quest.4B979482EF026BFF.title: "Electronics #4: The Circuit"
	quest.4BBF987FEF639801.title: "Alloy Kiln"
	quest.4BEC7C7000CA0094.quest_desc: [
		"- Axe efficieny can be bought from fletcher villagers. "
		""
		"- Hammer efficieny can be bought from metal working villagers."
		""
		"- Cut efficiency can be bought from leatherworker villagers."
	]
	quest.4BEC7C7000CA0094.quest_subtitle: "Can be bought from villagers"
	quest.4BEC7C7000CA0094.title: "Treatise: Tool efficiency"
	quest.4C2E8CAE784BD9D1.quest_desc: ["Тёмный лорд - порождение Бездны. Именно он вёл в бой Легион Затмения, пытаясь принести мир в жертву Бездне. Его доспех - прямое воплощение ужаса и боли всех, кто пал от его рук. Увеличивает урон носителя, заставляя проливать всё больше крови во имя тьмы."]
	quest.4C36EF046EC72D6D.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &2мирмекса&r."]
	quest.4C3805F75C9EE3DD.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSMD&r (surface-mount device) &aComponents&r are CEu-exclusive components that are required for the next tier of circuits (&5Nano&r). They can also be used in place of their non-SMD counterparts in most Circuit recipes."
		""
		"Of course they're more complicated to make, this is GregTech! What did you expect?"
		""
		"Invest in automation for these - you won't stop needing them."
	]
	quest.4C3805F75C9EE3DD.quest_subtitle: "Alternate components!"
	quest.4C3805F75C9EE3DD.title: "SMD Components"
	quest.4C7C0F6A6598BC24.quest_desc: [
		"&aTrinium Coils&r bring up the Heat Capacity to &d9,001K&r."
		""
		"These coils are required for progressing to the second half of &cZPM&r, and beyond."
	]
	quest.4C7C0F6A6598BC24.quest_subtitle: "IT'S OVER 9000!!!"
	quest.4C7C0F6A6598BC24.title: "Trinium Coils"
	quest.4C7D95C00F276FC9.quest_desc: ["Can be used to make a very powerful digging tool."]
	quest.4CBD140354E40E45.quest_desc: ["Почему?"]
	quest.4CD9F6D1B4CC7D81.quest_desc: [
		"Obtain &aPhenol&r from:"
		""
		"&91 -&r &aWood Tar&r distillation."
		""
		"&92 -&r Reacting &aBenzene&r with &dChlorine&r and &dSodium Hydroxide&r This should be performed in an &3LCR&r, and the Chlorine is perfectly looped."
		""
		"&93 -&r Shortcutting the above recipe by ignoring the &dSodium Hydroxide&r. This is net negative on &dChlorine&r."
		""
		"&94 -&r Reacting &aBenzene&r, &dPropene&r and &dOxygen&r using a small amount of &4Phosphoric Acid&r - normally a catalyst, but consumed here in small quantities. This is called the Cumene process."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you're having trouble deciding between the options presented, here's the appeal of each route:"
		""
		"&91 -&r Great if you're willing to set up a &3Pyrolyse Oven&r + &3Distillation Tower&r combo."
		""
		"&92 -&r This one's our preference! You can use the &dSalt&r to make more &dSalt Water&r, then electrolyze to create a loop."
		""
		"&93 -&r Very appealing if you have an infinite supply of &dChlorine&r. You could achieve this by setting up a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r on a Salt Water vein."
		""
		"&94 -&r ...&4Phosphoric Acid&r is a pain to produce. You'd be mad to consider this."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Benzene + Oxygen recipe was added in GTCE with the intent of fixing missing chemical recipes, as the Large Chemical Reactor didn't exist. Now that CEu provides more realistic options, we may remove the recipe in future."
	]
	quest.4CD9F6D1B4CC7D81.quest_subtitle: "But that's just how I Phenol"
	quest.4CD9F6D1B4CC7D81.title: "Phenol"
	quest.4CFBDAACE5C7ABE5.quest_desc: [
		"EN - You can also raise other animals"
		""
		"RU - Вы также можете разводить других животных"
	]
	quest.4CFBDAACE5C7ABE5.title: "Any fence"
	quest.4D00501812196BAE.quest_desc: ["Отличный мод для тех, кто любит безалкогольные напитки."]
	quest.4D276E4B462C4A60.title: "Wooden Tools"
	quest.4D34DB2A28C1B0DA.quest_desc: ["Can be attached to a Forge Hammer or a Transfer Unit to increase its efficiency."]
	quest.4D457489109A6432.quest_desc: ["&6Глаз циклопа&r владеет особым свойством. Победите циклопа и заполучите его глаз!"]
	quest.4D45782462BF69DA.quest_desc: ["Данные предметы можно получить из разных видов призраков в незере."]
	quest.4D45782462BF69DA.title: "Остатки призраков"
	quest.4D76C334B251EB3A.quest_desc: [
		"Platinum starts seeing usage in &5EV&r."
		""
		"The Platinum Group Sludge chain becomes a requirement in &1IV&r, and Sheldonite is the best ore to kickstart your processing."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The real-world name for Sheldonite ore is actually Cooperite. GregoriusT thought it was \"haha, funny\" to make it a reference to Sheldon Cooper, despite &lnot&r&o being the person the ore was named after!  We kept the \"haha, funny\" joke going."
	]
	quest.4D76C334B251EB3A.quest_subtitle: "Source of a lot, again..."
	quest.4D76C334B251EB3A.title: "Sheldonite"
	quest.4D7A771B67DAFC6F.quest_desc: [
		"You may be wondering how to obtain &6large quantities&r of common resources used in &bGregTech&r. This might be old news to seasoned players, but it's actually possible to set up &dpassive processes&r to make various materials and chemicals &2fully renewable&r."
		""
		"We've added this chapter to lead you towards some setups that you &7&omight&r desire. Obviously, there's no need to do all of these, but who doesn't love &2\"free\" resources&r."
		""
		"&9&lA footnote:&r There's no way we could document all of the renewable routes in &bGregTech&r. This quest page merely serves as a primer to lead &6newer players&r through their options. Not every option listed in this quest book is optimal, so we urge you to experiment!"
	]
	quest.4D7A771B67DAFC6F.quest_subtitle: "Very conscious of you!"
	quest.4D7A771B67DAFC6F.title: "Promoting a Sustainable Playthrough"
	quest.4DCFE7721417E669.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4DCFE7721417E669.quest_subtitle: "Cable networks have limitations on the amount of energy they will pull into the network depending on tier."
	quest.4DCFE7721417E669.title: "Energy Transfer"
	quest.4E0F2BFF1BF61BBC.quest_subtitle: "Thermo Plates are an essential part used to create and upgrade your generators."
	quest.4E7331F85C954C6F.quest_desc: ["Your most basic enchanting item. Can provide a max of 15 Eterna, allowing for enchantments up to lv30. Provides no Quanta or Arcana benefits. Fewer than the vanilla number are required before the maximum is reached, so can be mixed with other items to gain more Quanta and Arcana until higher level bookshelves are available."]
	quest.4E7439769A073494.title: "Leggins"
	quest.4E7E0575C1DEA958.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.4E9415FC5D3711EB.quest_subtitle: "Use something found up in the sky to break into a vault deep underground. Can burn through the spiny foliage of the Thornlands."
	quest.4E9415FC5D3711EB.title: "Find and use the &6Lamp of Cinders"
	quest.4E9605F744F69B14.quest_desc: ["Лавомерку тоже можно порубить на мясо."]
	quest.4E9605F744F69B14.title: "Нарезка лавомерок"
	quest.4E9DED9569AA17F5.quest_desc: [
		"Use this turbine to extract very large amounts of power from plasma!"
		""
		"&aHelium Plasma&r is the best fuel for its cost."
		""
		"If you're the type to question how realistic Plasma Turbines are... look up Magnetohydrodynamic Generators if you want something that bends fact into fiction."
	]
	quest.4E9DED9569AA17F5.quest_subtitle: "Plasma? Turbine?! How?"
	quest.4E9DED9569AA17F5.title: "Large Plasma Turbine"
	quest.4EAC2783BE9D4065.quest_desc: ["После победы над ледяным драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &bдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.4EAC2783BE9D4065.quest_subtitle: "&9Сапфировая"
	quest.4EB437CB7EEF956D.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.4EBD5363B552085D.quest_desc: ["In most cases, you can use the key from Create. But this one will allow machines to prioritize."]
	quest.4ED5A9AEF7B928BA.quest_desc: [
		"Macerate Wood into Wood Pulp, then compress it into Wood Plates. Combine it with Resin to make an empty board."
		""
		"Stick in some expensive Copper Wires (these'll get cheaper in &7LV&r) and you've got the base for your first &aCircuit&r."
		""
		"Almost there!"
	]
	quest.4ED5A9AEF7B928BA.quest_subtitle: "The circuit-er part of circuits..."
	quest.4ED5A9AEF7B928BA.title: "Electronics #2: Circuit Boards"
	quest.4F01823ED05E226D.quest_desc: ["Создайте &9глубоководные&r суши."]
	quest.4F01823ED05E226D.title: "Глубоководные суши"
	quest.4F02FD27A3688E42.quest_desc: ["The fourth level of storage upgrade will increase the storage of a drawer block by 16 times."]
	quest.4F3D82EDD1A2D7D2.title: "Iron Armor"
	quest.4F3FC2A1A6B1EEE6.quest_desc: ["Заберите &dдревние артефакты&r, что были запечатаны в пустотном черве."]
	quest.4F6275DED10DAB34.quest_desc: ["В &bморях&r и &bокеанах&r, можно найти небольшие островки на которых живут русалки и поют песни своим прекрасным голосом. Но когда, кто-то рядом с ними проплывает их голос начинает воздействовать на их мозг заставляя самостоятельно двигаться к ним. А потом они показывают своё истинное лицо &bсирены&r."]
	quest.4F6E351C5F676618.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations on making it this far!"
		""
		"Progressing into &dLuV&r will require more than &aRhodium Plated Palladium&r and &9LuV Circuits&r alone. You'll also need the &3Assembly Line&r."
		""
		"The &4resource costs&r for components will also start to increase &4significantly&r as you work towards &eFusion&r."
		""
		"If you haven't got automation for nearly everything, now (in &1IV&r) is a good time to do it. Take advantage of the power granted by &2Gregicality Multiblocks&r!"
		""
		"If your power generation relies on &3Large Turbines&r, you can pick up the &3LuV Rotor Holder&r."
	]
	quest.4F6E351C5F676618.quest_subtitle: "The main &dLuV&r material"
	quest.4F6E351C5F676618.title: "Rhodium-Plated Palladium"
	quest.4F71C6C67FB2F2A0.quest_desc: ["Доспех очень богатых жителей северных регионов. Выполнен на манер доспехов викингов. Обеспечивает хорошую защиту, но не замедляет владельца."]
	quest.4F71C6C67FB2F2A0.title: "Поножи Золотого рога"
	quest.4F742FFEFAFC2273.quest_desc: ["Создавайте броню легендарных героев прошлого с помощью необычных кристаллов, всё ещё хранящих память о тех давних временах."]
	quest.4F742FFEFAFC2273.title: "Fantasy Armor"
	quest.4FC668EF2BF294ED.quest_desc: [
		"You may already have boatloads of Iron by the time you make it here, but don't overlook the utility of this vein."
		""
		"Chromite is an excellent source of Chromium, and Vanadium is needed in higher quantities in the late game."
	]
	quest.4FC668EF2BF294ED.quest_subtitle: "Source of Iron, Vanadium, Gold, Chromium"
	quest.4FC668EF2BF294ED.title: "Magnetite"
	quest.4FFA7AF20E05678A.quest_desc: ["После победы над огненым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &cдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.4FFA7AF20E05678A.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасная"
	quest.501B670CACF1CD84.quest_subtitle: "Dielectric Casing is a material that is required on all machinery to function as they always contain one in each recipe and upgrade."
	quest.501B670CACF1CD84.title: "Heart of the Machine"
	quest.50258A19B61FD013.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.502836411CA028B9.quest_desc: ["&bPolybenzimidazole&r is the best material for &6Soft Mallets&r in vanilla GTCEu. Show us that you're on top of your PBI supply by spending some of it on a &dsuperfluous tool upgrade&r."]
	quest.502836411CA028B9.quest_subtitle: "Life would be boring without silly quests..."
	quest.502836411CA028B9.title: "The Mallet to End All Other Mallets"
	quest.50326B1D6EE8FA0B.title: "Accumulator"
	quest.503765686BCC67C1.quest_desc: ["A Buckler shield will give you a passive armor bonus when hend in your offhand but cannot be used to actively block."]
	quest.503C907A60861EE9.quest_desc: ["После победы над огненым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &6драконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.503C907A60861EE9.quest_subtitle: "&6Бронзовая"
	quest.5055AEE9D91172A0.quest_desc: ["Броня полководца, сражавшегося против сил тьмы. Очень яркий доспех, отражающий тактический гений носителя. Увеличивает максимальное здоровье владельца и усиливает его боевые навыки."]
	quest.5063FDFFBE3E4855.quest_desc: [
		"Better &6HV&r Circuits - much &dcheaper&r and easier to make than before."
		""
		"Before you move on to &6HV&r, make sure you have scaled up your Power Production, and automated the most important processes with AE2!"
	]
	quest.5063FDFFBE3E4855.quest_subtitle: "On that HV grind"
	quest.5063FDFFBE3E4855.title: "More HV Circuits"
	quest.50674FE3C6BE9990.title: "Visit &6Dense Forest"
	quest.509D66EBD410E270.title: "Visit a &8Brass Dungeon"
	quest.50BFFEAF92B72965.title: "Coke oven"
	quest.50C9CB8FB16E453D.title: "Find &6Burning arena"
	quest.51162B9185A45BB1.quest_desc: [
		"This bow can be inscribed with a spell using a Scribe's Table."
		""
		"At the cost of mana, arrows will become Spell Arrows and will apply the spell on their target."
		""
		"If you have no arrows, a spell arrow that deals 0 damage will be cast. If there is not enough mana, regular arrows will be fired instead."
		""
		"The &9Enchanter's Bow&r can also use special Augment Arrows that empower the inscribed spell."
	]
	quest.512456BD9ECF113E.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.51262C602F3BEF9E.quest_desc: ["Can be placed one-block away from the enchanting table, up to two-blocks high to add a small amount of Quanta. Good for mixing with bookshelves and candles early game to gain a better mix of enchanting potential."]
	quest.514ADF2A6EE7538C.quest_desc: ["A Heater shield can only be used for so long before going on cooldown for further use."]
	quest.517B6A6E04F4E4C8.quest_desc: ["A side product of sifting is the production of &dpure dusts&r. These shouldn't be sent back to your main storage, because they can't be used in recipes... and &3centrifuging&r them will give you a sweet, sweet extra byproduct."]
	quest.517B6A6E04F4E4C8.quest_subtitle: "Fear not! We have our solution!"
	quest.517B6A6E04F4E4C8.title: "Oh no! Pure dust?!"
	quest.517D50E748A129AB.quest_desc: [
		"Your ticket into &bApplied Energistics 2&r is nestled deep within a Certus Quartz vein."
		""
		"Alongside this, note that Barite electrolyses into Barium, which you will eventually need to make some higher tier Superconductors."
	]
	quest.517D50E748A129AB.quest_subtitle: "Source of AE2, Barium"
	quest.517D50E748A129AB.title: "Certus Quartz"
	quest.51821FFF001A051C.quest_desc: ["Зелья, дающие серьёзное преимущество в бою."]
	quest.51821FFF001A051C.title: "Необычные зелья"
	quest.5193DD03C0742548.quest_desc: [
		"Rubber Trees can be found in &aForest&r, &2Jungle&r or &aSwamp&r biomes."
		""
		"Breaking Rubber Logs will yield &6Sticky Resin&r, which will be important moving forwards."
		""
		"The logs also offer &duseful resources&r when processed in future."
	]
	quest.5193DD03C0742548.quest_subtitle: "No, this isn't IC2"
	quest.5193DD03C0742548.title: "Gettin' Shaded under a Rubber Tree"
	quest.519BAC5CAE362B19.quest_desc: [
		"- You can reach a new level of enchantment with the &zApothic Enchanting&r mod"
		""
		"- &dApothic Spawners&r allows you to obtain mob eggs and upgrade spawners"
	]
	quest.519BAC5CAE362B19.quest_subtitle: "May be deleted in the future"
	quest.519BAC5CAE362B19.title: "Enchanting and Spawners"
	quest.51B07F08608F0587.quest_desc: [
		"By breaking this block, you will receive molds for creating various items from the &5AE2&r mod."
		""
		""
	]
	quest.51F4741C1ABAB3FF.quest_subtitle: "Found upon his throne in &eSavanna &rbiomes"
	quest.51F7173FC0885F08.quest_desc: ["Works like an exhaust, but holds more and can be stacked on top of each other."]
	quest.52049B8E4CB25B43.quest_desc: [
		"Combat mechanics were altered by the &eBetter Combat&r mod."
		""
		"- Weapons Each weapon has its own attack animation and time."
		""
		""
		"- Hold to attack You can hold the attack button to keep attacking continuosly."
	]
	quest.52049B8E4CB25B43.title: "Combat Mechanics"
	quest.5230976ED3D20025.quest_desc: [
		"One of the important things in the assembly is the backpack. "
		""
		"When equipped, press &bB&r for easy access"
	]
	quest.5230976ED3D20025.title: "Backpack"
	quest.5244B2D6B5FA0487.title: "Visit &6 Crystallized Desert"
	quest.525B255172C03A7E.quest_desc: ["При &4удачном&r изучении этой таблички вы узнаете информацию о тёмных пещерах, в которых обитают ужасные монстры."]
	quest.525B255172C03A7E.quest_subtitle: "Забвение пустоты"
	quest.5263F866638D875C.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Oh boy, what can't this machine do? Decomposition recipes to separate dust types, separating air, do your taxes, and many others..."
		""
		"The list is too long! Let's just say &cyou need the Centrifuge&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"This takes &aImpure Dust&r or &aPurified Dust&r and turns them into clean Dust, plus an added tiny Dust &6Byproduct&r. This is outside of the optimal chain for Byproducts, but this is also the cheapest Ore Processing machine of the presented array to run and to setup on a small scale."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In base GTCE, this was objectively the strongest Ore Processing machine as it was fairly easy to use, and gave three tiny dusts, just like the Ore Washer or the Thermal Centrifuge. We tuned it down in favor of diversity."
	]
	quest.5263F866638D875C.quest_subtitle: "Jack of Many Trades"
	quest.5263F866638D875C.title: "Basic Centrifuge"
	quest.52868F643F0A1007.quest_desc: [
		"Just Forge Hammer that Cobblestone and you'll get some &dGravel&r."
		""
		"Gravel macerates into &6Stone Dust&r, but with a low chance of Flint when the recipe is performed in a &6HV Macerator&r or above. You probably want to sift for Flint, anyway!"
		""
		"Flint Dust centrifuges into &aSilicon Dioxide&r, which is then electrolysed for Silicon and Oxygen."
	]
	quest.52868F643F0A1007.quest_subtitle: "cp_gravelpit"
	quest.5289D5049A236D55.quest_desc: [
		"Your one-stop-shop for sources of Chlorine."
		""
		"If you're pining after Lithium, note that it can be obtained from Lepidolite Ore Processing."
	]
	quest.5289D5049A236D55.quest_subtitle: "Source of Salt, Chlorine, Lithium, Fluorine"
	quest.5289D5049A236D55.title: "Gamer Rage"
	quest.528CE69DA4358B2E.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Large Chemical Reactor (LCR)&r is a multiblock &3Chemical Reactor&r with more input/output slots. Its Teflon casings allow it to process extra recipes."
		""
		"The &3LCR&r can perform some exclusive reactions which allow you to combine multiple normal &3Chemical Reactor&r steps into a &6single step&r. Examples below:"
		""
		"&9-&r &aNitrogen Dioxide&r (for Nitric Acid and Dinitrogen Tetroxide)"
		"&9-&r &aSulfuric Acid&r"
		"&9-&r &aPhenol&r"
		"&9-&r &aEpichlorohydrin&r (you need it for Epoxy!)"
		"&9-&r &aEpoxy&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are also &3LCR&r exclusive recipes. For example, &dRadon&r can only be made in the LCR right now."
		""
		"All &dOverclocks&r in the &3LCR&r are &6100% efficient&r (known as Perfect overclocks); each overclock will &5quadruple the speed&r, as opposed to doubling it."
		""
		"The &3LCR&r has yet another &6advantage&r. You can use &32 Energy Hatches&r to allow it to run recipes of the &5next tier&r, similar to the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Tip:&r Given the amount of LCRs you may end up using, why not try utilising &dwallsharing&r to its full potential?"
		""
		"You could share one 2A (standard) &3Energy Hatch&r between 2 LCRs."
		""
		"You might want to share &3Input/Output Hatches&r, but make sure each LCR is running the correct recipe."
		""
		"Keep in mind Maintenance hatches cannot wallshare."
	]
	quest.528CE69DA4358B2E.quest_subtitle: "The Magic Box to end all Magic Boxes"
	quest.528CE69DA4358B2E.title: "Large Chemical Reactor"
	quest.5295C4AEFA8417F3.quest_desc: [
		"The worst Iron vein. It's helpful in the early game, but that's about it."
		""
		"We love you anyway, Mineral Sand vein!"
	]
	quest.5295C4AEFA8417F3.quest_subtitle: "Source of Iron"
	quest.5295C4AEFA8417F3.title: "Mineral Sand"
	quest.52AA00F57CB1E360.quest_desc: ["Хранится в аду под защитой самого &bБога Пламени."]
	quest.52B54E2CE151772D.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of bone will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from butcher villagers."
	]
	quest.52B6116AD14A0D31.quest_desc: ["The illumination upgrade will make the item and number count on the front of the drawer glow, being more visible in less lit areas."]
	quest.52D00CD3E8D1E293.quest_desc: [
		"The &aUHPIC&r unlocks &3ZPM Energy Hatches&r and &3Dynamos&r, as well as the Active Transformer. "
		""
		"You may know the drill, but do you know the screwdriver?"
	]
	quest.52D00CD3E8D1E293.title: "Ultra High Power Integrated Circuit"
	quest.52D952ADBEB67454.quest_desc: ["This Superconductor will be required for progression during &dLuV&r... when you delve deeper into &bResearch&r."]
	quest.52D952ADBEB67454.quest_subtitle: "So you're telling me an Ivy conducted this Super?"
	quest.52D952ADBEB67454.title: "IV Superconductors"
	quest.5310B93F2821826A.quest_subtitle: "A Processing Unit is used to create highly sophisticated machine parts and even highly advanced drills that are already difficult to make use of."
	quest.5310B93F2821826A.title: "Computer Brain"
	quest.53154550397E9704.title: "Kill &6Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.5359D0A924DCDF71.quest_desc: ["Доспех очень богатых жителей северных регионов. Выполнен на манер доспехов викингов. Обеспечивает хорошую защиту, но не замедляет владельца."]
	quest.5359D0A924DCDF71.title: "Ботинки Золотого рога"
	quest.536D62D580B9CD42.title: "Any chest"
	quest.53724A1FE29BFB20.quest_desc: ["Bows can be upgraded into a number of unique forms with their own advantages."]
	quest.53724A1FE29BFB20.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade a bow in a workbench"
	quest.538C44EB20C90EFE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.538C44EB20C90EFE.quest_subtitle: "&6Burns the target"
	quest.538F41CD0B583574.quest_desc: ["Spears are a basic weapon that can easily be made."]
	quest.53915852B9422EE2.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.53915852B9422EE2.quest_subtitle: "&6Burns the attacker"
	quest.539CF1B85725786D.quest_desc: [
		"&3Item Pipes&r are a simple yet effective way to move items around &dinstantly&r, but with throughput limitations."
		""
		"Higher tier pipes provide ridiculously large throughput - a rare sight in modded Minecraft!"
		""
		"Item Pipes &9do not pull&r, but they will push any item inserted into them to other connected inventories, prioritizing &9the closest inventory&r first."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The priority mechanics are &osomewhat complicated&r, so skip ahead if you aren't interested:"
		""
		"A &eDestination&r will have a &dRouting Value&r calculated, which is the sum of all \"Routing Values\" of the individual Pipes to that Destination. Whichever Destination has the &clowest &dRouting Value&r will be the one selected for Insertion."
		""
		"&3Restrictive Pipes&r typically have the lowest Priority for insertion due to their higher Routing Value."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Right now, you can use them in combination with &6Hoppers&r, but you will also be able to use them with Conveyor Modules, Output Buses, and machine Auto-Outputs all in the LV age."
		""
		"&9Note:&r GT6-style Pipes are &denabled&r. It means that placing Pipes connect them only to the block they were placed against. To open more connections, use your &5Wrench&r on the grid."
		""
		"You can also shift-right click with your Wrench to force items to flow in a certain direction. This can help counteract backflow (items being transported in an undesirable direction.) It also prevents the common issue of your &eCoke Oven Hatches&r trying to export charcoal/coke into your hoppers!"
		""
		"Get &eany&r of the suggested Item Pipes to complete this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Oooooh, YEAH! Item Pipes were in GregTech 5, and for whatever reason they weren't kept for GTCE, so you had to use other mods to transport items. Who does that!? Jokes aside, we hope you enjoy Item Pipes being back in GregTech!"
	]
	quest.539CF1B85725786D.quest_subtitle: "All your logistics woes are solved"
	quest.539CF1B85725786D.title: "Item Pipes"
	quest.53B0D08DB90EC369.quest_desc: [
		"Aluminium Cells are a big upgrade over the Steel Cells or Universal Fluid Cells."
		""
		"They can hold any fraction of Fluid - up to &d32 buckets&r!"
	]
	quest.53B0D08DB90EC369.quest_subtitle: "Like cells... only larger!"
	quest.53B0D08DB90EC369.title: "Large Cells"
	quest.53C5504730842406.quest_desc: ["Ничего необычного. Просто чай."]
	quest.53C5504730842406.title: "Обычный чай"
	quest.53DC6E32C41C94C3.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Pyrolyse Oven&r is an electric equivalent to the &3Coke Oven&r. It can produce &9Coal Coke&r and &9Charcoal&r with a &9Creosote&r byproduct just as before, but also has additional &6Organic Byproducts&r, the most beneficial of these being &aWood Tar&r."
		""
		"Another product is &aBiomass&r, which is more pertinent for your progression as of this moment."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The byproducts can be Distilled for an array of organic resources, with &odifferent&r byproducts giving &odifferent&r ratios of &odifferent&r chemicals."
		""
		"You will need to take a peek at the &9Distillation&r Quest to get to grips with the power of distillation..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&9Note: &rWith &d40 EU/t&r recipes, it needs either 1 &bMV&r energy hatch or 2 &7LV&r energy hatches. Multiblocks will &cnot&r use 2A of one tier to reach the next one for recipe voltage minimums. "
		""
		"In other words, the controller needs to say at least \"&bMV&r\" in the GUI to run recipes which say \"&bMV&r\" in EMI, even if they can draw enough EU/t with a lower tier hatch configuration. On the bright side, if you're using two &7LV&r hatches, you can choose to only power one, leaving the other disconnected - as long as you supply enough EU."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Pyrolyse Oven remains &doptional&r, should you choose to use Breweries instead. However, it is very rewarding to construct one either for Power, or for the various Byproducts, and we highly recommend you give it a look."
		""
		"There are recipes that can accept &bNitrogen&r to double the speed. This isn't quite worth pursuing right now, but Nitrogen will eventually be free and infinite."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT5u, the structure for the Pyrolyse Oven was infamously a giant box with only 9 coils inside. Players usually spent several minutes debugging what is wrong due to a lack of a EMI preview."
	]
	quest.53DC6E32C41C94C3.quest_subtitle: "Thermal Decomposition"
	quest.53DC6E32C41C94C3.title: "Pyrolyse Oven"
	quest.5401AB5E399E7BEA.quest_desc: [
		"Making &aAE2 Presses&r will unlock all the &9Processors&r from AE2. This opens up &9ME Drives&r, &9ME Pattern Providers,&r &9ME Crafting CPUs&r... that's almost the rest of AE2 at your fingertips! &7(Or at least... not until you obtain Silicon Ingots.)&r"
		""
		"AE2 &9Printed Circuits&r are now made in the &3Forming Press&r."
	]
	quest.5401AB5E399E7BEA.quest_subtitle: "Who likes meteor hunting, anyway?"
	quest.5401AB5E399E7BEA.title: "Pressing Matters"
	quest.542C6D76B579886C.quest_desc: [
		"When your Magebloom seeds.... bloom, you can use the Magebloom to create Fibers."
		""
		"These are used to craft several items, including your first set of magical armor!"
	]
	quest.5449DD547EE49B49.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.54540C05EA956E7F.quest_desc: ["Броня полководца, сражавшегося против сил тьмы. Очень яркий доспех, отражающий тактический гений носителя. Увеличивает максимальное здоровье владельца и усиливает его боевые навыки."]
	quest.5455DBF690ED02F4.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &2чешую&r."]
	quest.5455DBF690ED02F4.quest_subtitle: "&2Зелёная"
	quest.546CC03435E763CF.quest_desc: [
		"First things first - build the version of the structure that uses Fusion Glass in &aEMI&r. It's far cheaper right now."
		""
		"To save on &3Fusion Casings&r, fit Input/Output Hatches wherever you can (as displayed in the structure)."
		""
		"The &bFusion Reactor&r will pick a free Output Hatch from the many that are available. In order to \"&6force&r\" the Reactor to use a particular Output Hatch, you can always &alock all of the hatches&r to an irrelevant fluid (we usually use &9Water&r)."
		""
		"This time, we'll try something new: we're gonna explain the &3Lore&r at the same time as the mechanics."
		""
		"Enjoy the ride!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5's &3Fusion Reactor&f stores EU you feed it in its internal buffer. The maximum capacity is determined by the amount of &3Energy Hatches&f in the structure."
		""
		"&oRecipes can only start if the &9\"EU to start\"&f is stored internally, which will be &cconsumed&f. With this stored energy, the reactor can keep running recipes until it goes idle. At this point it will need to be topped up on EU to start again."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&oShadow of Greg's &3Fusion Reactor&f (which is now GTCEu's Fusion Reactor) comes with an added mechanic called &4Heat&f."
		""
		"&oWhen the reactor is running, the &9EU to start&f is converted to &4Heat&f. That Heat is preserved until the Reactor goes idle, at which point it will slowly go down."
		""
		"&oNext time a recipe is found, it will use all possible Heat and deduct it from the &9EU to start&f, allowing you to save Energy for short pauses."
		""
		"&oThe &3Fusion Reactor I&f can only run recipes up to a required EU of 160 MEU to start. It will also overclock up to &dLuV&f at best, even if you upgrade to ZPM Hatches, so don't stress over attempting this."
	]
	quest.546CC03435E763CF.quest_subtitle: "Stellar power"
	quest.546CC03435E763CF.title: "Fusion Reactor I"
	quest.5480AF2EDEDB6A36.quest_desc: [
		"&3Long-Distance Fluid Pipes&r can be used to send fluids across great distances. Place one endpoint at each end, and connect them with pipeline blocks."
		""
		"These pipes instantly transfer from the input side to the output side."
		""
		"They also have a minimum distance between pipe endpoints, so you can't use these for short-range operations."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"These pipes have a reputation of being &4buggy&r to set up. If they don't seem to work at first, try rotating the endpoints with a &eWrench&r."
	]
	quest.5480AF2EDEDB6A36.quest_subtitle: "Wondering how to move that oil around?"
	quest.5480AF2EDEDB6A36.title: "Long-Distance Fluids"
	quest.54AF8696674766B4.quest_desc: [
		"&4Red Alloy&r is an alloy of Copper and Redstone, prized in the GregTech universe for its conductivity."
		""
		"You will need some for &9Electronic Circuits&r."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This material originally comes from RedPower - what a throwback!"
	]
	quest.54AF8696674766B4.quest_subtitle: "A completely fictional alloy"
	quest.54AF8696674766B4.title: "Red Alloy"
	quest.54BCBA93CF61381B.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &2морской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.54BCBA93CF61381B.quest_subtitle: "&2Зелёная"
	quest.54BCBA93CF61381B.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.54CA210F1FB2DA3B.quest_desc: ["Доспех полководцев Легиона Затмения. Ходят слухи, что этот доспех ковался в самой Бездне и до сих пор черпает из неё силу, увеличивая запас здоровья владельца. Обеспечивает отличной защитой в бою."]
	quest.54CB4EF25126011A.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &7чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.54CB4EF25126011A.quest_subtitle: "&7Серебряный комплект"
	quest.54CB4EF25126011A.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.54CF2016ED44CC45.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &6HV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"The pattern stays the same: the rightmost circuit comes in &dlarger quantities&r and is overall &aeasier&r to produce."
	]
	quest.54CF2016ED44CC45.title: "&6HV&r Circuits"
	quest.54D282CDE4B4C938.quest_desc: ["А куда же без этого настоящему пекарю."]
	quest.54D282CDE4B4C938.title: "Инструменты пекаря"
	quest.54D73D049F8CD9FE.quest_desc: ["Cobblestone is just the start of things. Let's make a Cobbleworks!"]
	quest.54D73D049F8CD9FE.quest_subtitle: "Oh, we're only just getting started."
	quest.54D73D049F8CD9FE.title: "The Joy of Cobblestone"
	quest.54DE75E97153E455.quest_desc: [
		"Why does every machine have a million variants across each tier? We'll let you in on an industry secret - overclocking is one of the main reasons."
		""
		"Overclocking is a mechanic that happens when you try to run a recipe in a machine &dthat is higher tier than the recipe itself.&r The recipe will use an increased amount of energy, but the recipe time will be cut based on how many tiers you're overclocking by."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GTCE overclocking was extremely awkward. If the recipe consumed 16EU/t or below, it would do a classic 2.0x overclock. However if the recipe consumed more than 16EU/t, every Overclock would be 2.8x faster! GTCEu has a config to select the Overclock speed bonus."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A pro tip - for automated setups, overclock as little as possible!"
		""
		"Machines have a side menu to set the maximum voltage tier it will overclock to. Click on it to cycle through all the available Voltages and choose a limit."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each tier above the recipe tier allows one overclock. Each overclock implies:"
		""
		"&9-&r &a2x&r recipe speed"
		"&9-&r &a4x&r power consumption"
		"&9->&r &c2x&r total energy cost"
		""
		"As you can see, there are upsides and downsides. It is a game of balance: ask yourself if you want faster recipes at the cost of greater power consumption."
	]
	quest.551562CB9D0696B5.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.55552589C581EE9E.quest_desc: ["&aEnergium Crystals&r store a significant amount of &9EU&r. They're also arguably cheaper."]
	quest.55552589C581EE9E.quest_subtitle: "Science-fiction batteries!"
	quest.55552589C581EE9E.title: "Super Batteries"
	quest.5570F02C03267B36.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest will be completed with &eeither&r a &3UHV Energy Hatch&r&r... or a &3UHV Dynamo Hatch&r for your Multiblock Generators."
		""
		"These are the final energy hatches in GTCEu. It's been a pleasure upgrading our multiblocks together o7"
		""
		"Don't forget about the &d16 amp&r versions!"
	]
	quest.5570F02C03267B36.title: "Upgrading your Assembly Line for the Last Time"
	quest.55AF1779E7AE28A7.quest_desc: ["When consumed, it will remove a single random negative effect from the player, keeping positive ones untouched. This provides a simple use for Cocoa Beans in difficult, risky trips."]
	quest.55D51B6115A8B474.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.55D8E30978CBBC0D.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, the Rock Crusher - such an unassuming machine that initially appears to only really be a builder's best friend. Who could look past infinite Cobblestone, Deepslate, or Obsidian?"
		""
		"Don't be fooled, though, as this little machine might just shock you with the array of materials it makes renewable when you macerate its rocks down to dust form. The surrounding quests will clue you in."
	]
	quest.55D8E30978CBBC0D.quest_subtitle: "More like game breaking, am I right?"
	quest.55E245DFAC86BC77.quest_desc: ["Некром - это сплав серебра и незерита, что делает его очень прочным."]
	quest.55E245DFAC86BC77.title: "Некром"
	quest.55EBD8B1F83A6956.quest_desc: ["Убив плотоядного червя, вы получите &eхитин&r. Который можно использовать для создания брони."]
	quest.55ED05A197F8D24A.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.55ED05A197F8D24A.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Turbine uses steam to produce electricity. But there will be more upgrades to this certain turbine so remember to make a lot of these to power your electrical machinery."
	quest.55ED05A197F8D24A.title: "Is this my electric fan?"
	quest.562693D791F828A0.quest_desc: ["The Fermentation Barrel turns fruit mash into juices and wines. Patience is the key to obtaining a quality drink."]
	quest.562693D791F828A0.title: "Fermentation Barrel"
	quest.563C96885A227C9F.quest_desc: [
		"Wrought Iron has a very low carbon content, but that's enough to make it &btougher&r than regular Iron."
		""
		"&aGregTech&r tools made of Wrought Iron are &650% more durable&r than their Iron cousins. You might want to consider using Wrought Iron until you unlock &2something better&r."
		""
		"To obtain Wrought Iron, you can &6smelt&r Iron Nuggets into Wrought Iron Nuggets, then recombine them into an ingot. Make sure you don't convert all of your Iron supply, as the two &4&laren't&r interchangeable."
		""
		"This may be time-consuming, but rest assured, you'll unlock a &ebetter way&r to produce Wrought Iron before long."
	]
	quest.563C96885A227C9F.quest_subtitle: "Murder, she Wrought"
	quest.563C96885A227C9F.title: "Better Than Iron"
	quest.5649FC1867467561.quest_desc: ["Half-size 1x1 storage drawers will store 16 stacks of an item."]
	quest.5673089822BFCA70.quest_desc: [
		"You may recall that regular Steam machines had a duration penalty, and were twice as slow. Not great."
		""
		"&5High Pressure&r Steam machines no longer bear a &bduration penalty &rfor recipes, making them objective upgrades."
		""
		"Make &eone&r of the proposed HP machines to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.5673089822BFCA70.quest_subtitle: "Pressure can be good sometimes"
	quest.5673089822BFCA70.title: "No More Penalty"
	quest.5683C69200EBC4CD.quest_desc: ["The main feature of Applied Energistics 2 is the ME (pronounced Emm- Eee and stands for Matter Energy) network, which is a set of interconnected blocks and cables grouped into a system where storage, power, and function interact between multiple components."]
	quest.5683C69200EBC4CD.title: "Storage and transportation"
	quest.56A515610D242E28.title: "Magic Inc"
	quest.56B56E26B8F48D4F.quest_desc: ["Глубоко под землёй находится древний город. Ходят слухи о жутком существе, что обитает там. Кто знает, может оно охраняет именно это око?"]
	quest.56D3BC7D09F900CA.quest_desc: [
		"Rich Soil is an enhanced type of dirt, more fertile and durable to the elements."
		""
		"Rich Soil cannot be directly crafted. To make it, you must craft Organic Compost and place it into the world, letting it decompose over time."
		""
		"Organic Compost will decompose more easily under sunlight and moisture from nearby water, but doesn't actually hydrate like farmland. It can also be gently accelerated by placing activators next to it, in a 3x3x3 area centered on itself."
		""
		"Currently, the following blocks behave as activators for Organic Compost:"
		"- Brown and Red Mushrooms, and their Colonies;"
		"- Podzol and Mycelium;"
		"- Other blocks of Organic Compost;"
		"- Rich Soil, normal or tilled."
	]
	quest.56E7A3A0CC690C8A.quest_desc: [
		"Making &aNitrobenzene&r will boost the energy efficiency of &aBenzene&r roughly &6fourfold&r. You love to see it."
		""
		"The catch here is that it takes &dDistilled Water&r, and consumes a bit of &dSulfur&r with every step."
	]
	quest.56E7A3A0CC690C8A.quest_subtitle: "Click this link for free Nitro"
	quest.56E7A3A0CC690C8A.title: "Benzene Nitro"
	quest.5720372F5FE12A07.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &6мирмекса&r."]
	quest.572B673C0CBC834D.quest_desc: ["Отправляйтесь в глубины самых отдалённых пещер этого мира с модом &2Alex's Caves&f. Вас ждёт незабываемое приключение, куча сокровищ и серьёзные испытания."]
	quest.572B673C0CBC834D.title: "Alex's Caves"
	quest.573AC9DC73B2CCE8.quest_desc: ["Use the ingots of &6ignitium&r to create a powerful piece of equipment. It will definitely not let you down in battle...."]
	quest.573C2242EAB85B49.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.573DD5834B321D0A.title: "Visit &6Acropolis"
	quest.5742702B8021B1F5.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest requires the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r and is &doptional&r, yet convenient."
		""
		"The first four fluids are the important products of &aWood Tar&r Distillation:"
		"&9-&r Phenol: useful for Epoxy and PBI"
		"&9-&r Benzene: an important hydrocarbon"
		"&9-&r Toluene: useful for TNT"
		"&9-&r Dimethylbenzene: useful for PBI"
		""
		"Unlike Oil, putting &aWood Tar&r in the &3Distillation Tower&r for the byproducts, and using &dNitrobenzene&r for power is arguably worth it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The bottom three are the important products from &aWood Vinegar&r Distillation:"
		"&9-&r Acetic Acid: useful to make more Acetone"
		"&9-&r Methanol: a moderately important hydrocarbon"
		"&9-&r Acetone: useful for Epoxy and Gasoline"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"It's also possible to use a \"full combo\" of 4 &3DTs&r -  input &aCharcoal Byproducts&r into a first tower, splitting into &aWood Tar&r, &aWood Gas&r and &aWood Vinegar&r."
		""
		"This isn't the most efficient cost-to-production ratio, but the option is there if you get bored."
	]
	quest.5742702B8021B1F5.title: "True Distillation: Organic"
	quest.57545605AB3B88EF.quest_desc: ["Броня рыцарей Легиона Затмения. Когда-то в мире произошла большая война, в которой этот легион сражался за приход вечной ночи. Является довольно лёгким, тем самым не сковывая движений владельца."]
	quest.57545605AB3B88EF.title: "Ботинки солдата Затмения"
	quest.575B07D390D9D079.quest_desc: [
		"Underground, you may come across pure Oilsands ore veins. You can &3centrifuge&r the Dust to get &aOil&r."
		""
		"&9&lNote:&r&l The Oil path is one path towards &9&lEthylene&r&l. The other paths involve getting natural with some Ethanol.&r"
		""
		"For now, Oil is &doptional&r. It becomes mandatory much later when you get to &5EV&r."
		""
		"Oil can also be refined in the form of &aLight Fuel&r, &aDiesel&r or even &aGasoline&r, which are excellent power options."
		""
		"If you chose this path, you should use it for both Power and Ethylene."
		""
		"Oilsands are a &6great starting point&r - they'll tide you over until you unlock Fluid Drilling Rigs."
	]
	quest.575B07D390D9D079.quest_subtitle: "This quest was sponsored by the US Military"
	quest.575B07D390D9D079.title: "America Simulator"
	quest.5766C8B9E850C186.quest_desc: [
		"To create one of the main crafting items in Ars, the &9Source Gem&r, we'll need to make an &6Imbuement Chamber&r."
		""
		"The Imbuement Chamber requires Source to imbue items. It produces a small amount of Source by itself, but can also use Source Jars as a power source."
		""
		"Several recipes also require Arcane Pedestals to be placed around it as well."
		""
		""
	]
	quest.5766C8B9E850C186.quest_subtitle: "Creating Source Gems"
	quest.57A5FFB72BB92BDA.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.57A69B644B88B0BA.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.57A69B644B88B0BA.title: "Ironwood tools"
	quest.57CBC122D021798F.title: "Sopchisticated Storage"
	quest.57D4E09A9CAB150C.quest_desc: [
		"The &aPlatinum Group Metals&r are six rare metals with useful catalytic properties. In no particular order, they are &3Ruthenium&r, &dRhodium&r, &7Palladium&r, &9Osmium&r, &bIridium&r, and &ePlatinum&r."
		""
		"You will need to &4automate&r their processing lines, as every single one of these metals will be used extensively in the late game."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To begin, treat various PGM-bearing &aPurified Crushed Ores&r with &dNitric Acid&r to produce &aPlatinum Group Sludge&r."
		""
		"Then, centrifuge it with &dAqua Regia&r to produce the various PGM salts."
		""
		"&dChlorine&r can be perfectly recycled from the &eRaw Platinum Powder&r."
		""
		"&dNitric Acid&r is &osort of&r recycled from &7Raw Palladium Powder&r through &dAmmonia&r, though we'd recommend keeping the excess Ammonia for other uses (Rocket Fuel and PBI)."
		""
		"The other PGM salts have their own special mini-chain associated to them - more on this in the next quests."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r &ePlatinum&r and &7Palladium&r can also be obtained from The End or through normal Ore Processing."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Heard of the infamous \"Platline\" from either Gregicality or GregTech: New Horizons? The extremely daunting chain was added in GT:NH through Bartworks. The concept is amazing, but we had to tune it down significantly to make entering late game in GTCEu much smoother."
	]
	quest.57D4E09A9CAB150C.quest_subtitle: "Platline in 50 hours"
	quest.57D4E09A9CAB150C.title: "Platinum Group Processing"
	quest.57DE7059D524FAE9.quest_desc: [
		"Simply put, Gregicality Multiblocks are larger versions of the GregTech machines you might be familiar with. The obvious increase in resource cost is worth your time, as they can be upgraded to gain the ability to process recipes in parallel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"They also introduce Machine Modes - depending on the configured machine mode, the Multiblock will use a different recipe type when processing materials. You can change this from the machine GUI by clicking on the Robot Arm button."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"By including Parallel Control Hatches in your Gregicality Multiblocks, you can grant them parallel processing capability. There are 4 tiers of hatch, each further increasing parallel capability by an factor of 4."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Batch mode can be enabled on a multiblock to merge together an amount of one recipe together into one recipe up to 5 seconds. This does not change the overall speed of one recipe like overclocking, but is useful to stop machine flickering."
		"This is not strictly gated by Gregicality Multiblocks, but is extremely useful with them. "
	]
	quest.57EC19AF87A32930.quest_desc: ["Spraying &3Input Buses&r and &3Hatches&r the same color will treat them as one &3Hatch&r in the &5Multiblock&r. With distinct mode enabled on the &3Buses/Hatches&r, the &5Multiblock&r will only search for a recipe using ingredients from one color group. With this enabled the &5Multiblock&r will try to match the color of the &3Output Hatch&r to the color group used for the inputs."]
	quest.57EC19AF87A32930.quest_subtitle: "Color by number multiblocks"
	quest.57EC19AF87A32930.title: "Colored Buses"
	quest.57FD6DFF7B7647D0.quest_subtitle: "Found in Dark Towers in The Dark Forest."
	quest.57FD6DFF7B7647D0.title: "Defeat the &fUr-Ghast"
	quest.580A89FDD1401BF4.quest_desc: ["Компас. который можно найти в старой часовне в аду. Ведёт к давно заброшенному святилищу."]
	quest.580AF20D915596F0.quest_desc: [
		"An upgraded bookshelf which provides Greater Eterna and some Arcana."
		"Increases max Eterna."
		"Can be mixed with Hellshelves for more balanced enchanting."
	]
	quest.581CDF545E1EA1FD.quest_desc: [
		"Build this machine next to your &3Chemical Reactor&r to automatically solidify Rubber into &aRubber Sheets&r."
		""
		"You can make your Chemical Reactor auto-output if you &dwrench&r the side of your &3Chemical Reactor&r and enable Fluid &9auto-output&r."
		""
		"There will be more Fluids to solidify, so you may re-purpose your &3Fluid Solidifier&r when not crafting Rubber - or make a second one!"
	]
	quest.581CDF545E1EA1FD.quest_subtitle: "The Fluid Solidifier solidifies..."
	quest.581CDF545E1EA1FD.title: "Basic Fluid Solidifier"
	quest.583AA3AED6ADAD73.quest_desc: ["Improved Endshelf with better stats."]
	quest.583D0CC4FAA4FC98.quest_desc: [
		"Higher-tier Generators will increase their fuel consumption proportionally to their Generation rate, keeping the duration of fuels and the specific amount of energy from fuels the same. The &3Advanced Steam Turbine&r will use &d5,120 mB Steam&r per second, equivalent to &d256 mB/t&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r of the generators to complete this quest, but you may prefer starting off with the &3Advanced Steam Turbine&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are a few new power options available for &bMV&r. Selecting the Generators and pressing &4U&r will let you see which fuels count as &aCombustion&r or &aGas&r."
		""
		"Quests in the top left corner of this Chapter are for the valuable Power options."
		""
		"If you stick to &9Steam&r for your Power generation, you'll probably need a &3Large Boiler&r."
	]
	quest.583D0CC4FAA4FC98.quest_subtitle: "Things are 'boutta get rough"
	quest.583D0CC4FAA4FC98.title: "Electricity Generation in MV"
	quest.58580EAC2879DDCB.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.586CB8FEAA0A50C6.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.586CB8FEAA0A50C6.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Blast Furnace has a similar structure like the Coke Oven, but this is used to create steel. Perhaps this is where the next stage comes."
	quest.586CB8FEAA0A50C6.title: "Sauna but for metals"
	quest.5898743D8D6C2690.quest_desc: [
		"If you've tried to distill an Oil into &eLight Fuel, Heavy Fuel&r, etc., you might've realised that you can't. Instead, you've gotten this &6sulfurized&r version of it. How dreadful!"
		""
		"To fix this, we'll need to &6desulfurize&r it. Combine whatever you'd like to desulfurize with &9Hydrogen Gas&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r to produce the pure product, along with a byproduct of &aHydrogen Sulfide&r. What now?"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Luckily, &aHydrogen Sulfide&r is perfectly &drecycled&r in an &3Electrolyzer&r."
		""
		"To automate this process, simply place your &3Chemical Reactor&r and your &3Electrolyzer&r next to each other. Be sure to &cenable input from the output side&r. We've graciously provided a &3Fluid Filter&r so that your desulfurized prize doesn't go into your Electrolyzer too - remember to set it to filter both input/extract so that the right fluids can flow both ways!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"But now, how do we get our refined goodies out of our &3Chemical Reactor&r? This is where the Electric Pump comes in - use it on a different face of the Chemical Reactor and extract your prize!"
		""
		"&l&bTip&r&r: You only need two buckets of &9Hydrogen Gas&r. The easiest way of obtaining it is by electrolyzing water. You don't need to mass-produce Hydrogen (yet), don't worry!"
	]
	quest.5898743D8D6C2690.quest_subtitle: "Waiter! Why is there Sulfur in my soup?"
	quest.5898743D8D6C2690.title: "Desulfurization"
	quest.58BA62A3A8A32C24.quest_desc: [
		"This machine combines washing for simple automation, but also advanced and precise washing for byproducts."
		""
		"Washing a &aCrushed Ore&r will grant a &aPurified Ore&r which can be refined further, some useless stone, and more importantly, the first &6Byproduct&r!"
		""
		"Any Ore will give at &9minimum 2/3rd of a Dust&r of this Byproduct through washing. Prioritize this step the most."
		""
		"Using Distilled Water over Water cuts recipe duration in half, but it's also more difficult to produce."
	]
	quest.58BA62A3A8A32C24.quest_subtitle: "Wash that mouth out"
	quest.58BA62A3A8A32C24.title: "Basic Ore Washing Plant"
	quest.58BBD540D7D4FF01.quest_desc: ["Save two of these for the &3IV Circuit Assembler&r."]
	quest.58BBD540D7D4FF01.quest_subtitle: "I LuV GregTech"
	quest.58BBD540D7D4FF01.title: "First LuV Circuits!"
	quest.58D9B4E20FADDCF1.quest_desc: ["Зелья, дающие ещё более серьёзное преимущество в бою."]
	quest.58D9B4E20FADDCF1.title: "Большие необычные зелья"
	quest.58E51E027525C66D.quest_desc: [
		"Tetra includes a number of additional methods to better your tools. These schematics/treatises must be placed around a workbench in a 5x5x5 square of the space two above the workbench (so four blocks up the wall and two blocks off each side)."
		""
		"The way to find these new items are indicated in the quests."
		""
		"* Note: When you will pick up one scroll from category it will auto-complete the whole quest. So these quests are more like overview of scrolls available."
	]
	quest.58E51E027525C66D.title: "Scrolls, Schematics, and Treatises"
	quest.58EC47584C773B82.quest_desc: [
		"Using our Enchanting Apparatus structure, we'll want to craft our first seed, the &5Magebloom Seed&r."
		""
		"This will be used to create us some magical clothing!"
	]
	quest.58EC47584C773B82.quest_subtitle: "Growing Magic"
	quest.58EC47584C773B82.title: "Magebloom Seed"
	quest.591D9D37D588E02A.quest_desc: ["The Rack, when placed on the wall in a 3x3 area behind a workbench, will allow tools placed on it (right click while holding tool) to be used in the workbench. "]
	quest.592BD683A48C2AA2.quest_desc: [
		"The bucket recipe has been &d&lchanged.&r It now requires plates - &owahoo&r."
		""
		"Plates are used absolutely &beverywhere&r in &aGregTech&r. Combining two ingots with your new &9hammer&r in a crafting table will make a plate. This ratio is kind of &cexpensive,&r but better recipes for plates will come later."
		""
		"Take this &6Wooden Barrel&r full of &bWater&r as a reward. Huh... isn't that an odd reward? We just wanted to show you that all &aGTCEu&r tanks are portable."
	]
	quest.592BD683A48C2AA2.quest_subtitle: "#realism"
	quest.592BD683A48C2AA2.title: "Greg has struck"
	quest.594D84730913698A.quest_desc: ["Emerald is the useful ore here. It's used in small quantities in &bMV&r, and is a part of the Crystal process for Crystal and Wetware circuits much later on."]
	quest.594D84730913698A.quest_subtitle: "Source of Beryllium, Emerald, Thorium"
	quest.594D84730913698A.title: "Emerald"
	quest.5962DB7143D9AD5F.quest_subtitle: "Inscriber Presses are found in the Sky Chest at the center of a Meteorite. They can be used to create circuits in an Inscriber."
	quest.5962DB7143D9AD5F.title: "Inscriber Presses"
	quest.59747E4FED7FF46F.quest_desc: ["При &bудачном&r изучении этой таблички вы узнаете информацию о подводной бездне, скрытой под толщей воды."]
	quest.59747E4FED7FF46F.quest_subtitle: "Подводная бездна"
	quest.5979B0E13A1EDC9C.quest_desc: [
		"The &aAlloy Blast Smelter&r is the only main &2GCYM&r machine available in &5EV&r. You can use it to produce any alloy that you'd normally use the Mixer for. "
		""
		"Instead of producing &6Hot Ingots&r, the ABS produces &9Molten Fluids&r if the recipe is \"hot\" enough. These fluids require cooling with a &bVacuum Freezer&r. Otherwise, it produces regular liquids."
		""
		"Don't let the long smelting times scare you off. This machine incorporates the &dMixer step&r directly into the smelting recipe, and actually saves you quite a bit of time over smelting the dust in an EBF!"
		""
		"Nearly every &2GCYM&r material is produced in this machine, so if you have trouble finding a Mixer recipe, look for a Molten Fluid!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This multiblock was inspired by GT++. It didn't use any heating coils, had no temperature requirements, and only produced regular liquids for all materials. It was pretty OP back in the day, but it eventually got restricted to only a single Energy Hatch to balance it out. For some reason, it also allowed you to melt any dust... into liquid...?"
	]
	quest.5979B0E13A1EDC9C.quest_subtitle: "Visions of GT++"
	quest.5979B0E13A1EDC9C.title: "So Many Alloys!"
	quest.59B6D295D8F2F07D.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &1самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &1бестиарии&r."]
	quest.59B6D295D8F2F07D.quest_subtitle: "&1Электрическое"
	quest.59BEB2AA9598A21D.quest_desc: [
		"This is a &4meme&r quest - check the recipe requirement for the teddy."
		""
		"Yes... this will take you an entire year to craft in an &7LV&r Compressor. How long would this take you to craft when overclocked to the highest possible value?"
		""
		"&7Definitely don't worry about making this now... take the hint and wait for a heavy overclock."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The main developer of this pack spent far too long fixing the model files to customise this thing.&7.&8. If you're wondering why there's a random Pokemon doll, it's my Minecraft skin!"
	]
	quest.59BEB2AA9598A21D.quest_subtitle: "Got enough time on your hands?"
	quest.59BEB2AA9598A21D.title: "And they say GregTech is grindy..."
	quest.59C29E3B955B8449.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &6мирмекса&r."]
	quest.59DFC4DA7D29C315.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium requires a slightly more &binvolved&r process than the previous materials to process. To get started, you'll need &aRutile&r, which can be obtained by processing &aBauxite&r."
		""
		"Once you've gotten enough &5Rutile&r, your journey to &6Titanium&r continues in the next quest. There's no need to rush things."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You may have already noticed that Bauxite is also an &6excellent source of Aluminium&r."
		""
		"Visiting &dThe End&r allows you to access a richer Bauxite vein, as well as &9Ilmenite&r - an even better source of Rutile."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r Ore processing for &aBauxite&r is ridiculously good! Including the &3Thermal Centrifuge&r step easily &6triples&r your &aRutile&r yield."
		""
		"&9Bonus Tip:&r There is also an alternate route you can process &aPurified Bauxite&r in a &3Mixer&r and process into a greater return of &aRutile&r, however this is much harder to initally batch so it is more ideal to use when you set up a dedicated Titanium processing line."
	]
	quest.59DFC4DA7D29C315.quest_subtitle: "...means it WASN'T Titanium!"
	quest.59DFC4DA7D29C315.title: "Almost Titanium"
	quest.59E718E171670BF2.quest_desc: ["Доспех полководцев Легиона Затмения. Ходят слухи, что этот доспех ковался в самой Бездне и до сих пор черпает из неё силу, увеличивая запас здоровья владельца. Обеспечивает отличной защитой в бою."]
	quest.59F0060B55307311.quest_desc: [
		"By clicking the &6Circuit Configuration Slot&r in machines, you can create a &bghost Programmed Circuit&r. "
		""
		"This is a \"&7fake circuit&r\" that allows you to select a configuration for recipes. There's no need to spend your circuits crafting &bProgrammed Circuits&r anymore."
		""
		"The purpose of this ghost circuit is to prevent &drecipe clashes&r - for example, the same Wiremill can produce wires of different thicknesses, with the same material!"
		""
		"&dElectric Machines&r and &dItem Input Buses&r will have a Ghost Circuit Slot."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This feature is originally from GTNH."
	]
	quest.59F0060B55307311.quest_subtitle: "Don't want to spend your circuits to select recipes?"
	quest.59F0060B55307311.title: "Programmed Circuits"
	quest.5A27B361EF71A4DF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5A27B361EF71A4DF.quest_subtitle: "The Macerator is an interesting machine that allows the recycling of materials and powder them into dust and be reused again."
	quest.5A27B361EF71A4DF.title: "Reduce, Reuse, Reforge"
	quest.5A393255C66CECCE.title: "Tomahawk"
	quest.5A8BCC3C79020C3C.quest_desc: ["Создавайте броню легендарных героев прошлого с помощью необычных кристаллов, всё ещё хранящих память о тех давних временах."]
	quest.5A8BCC3C79020C3C.title: "Fantasy Armor"
	quest.5A8F0124E07D5025.quest_desc: [
		"Good news - we're going to start to cut down on the amount of components you'll need to submit for quests as you progress further into the modpack. Remember that &2EMI is your true mentor&r if recipes are getting overwhelming."
		""
		"Getting back on topic, set yourself up for &7LV&r by crafting six &aLV Electric Motors&r! This may seem like a lot, but that's the bare minimum required to get to the good stuff in &7LV&r."
		""
		"&6Once you complete this Quest and the Electronic Circuit Quest, you are ready to move on to the LV Age.&r"
	]
	quest.5A8F0124E07D5025.quest_subtitle: "Low Voltage beckons..."
	quest.5A8F0124E07D5025.title: "The First of Many Motors"
	quest.5A92BB6310082A88.quest_desc: ["Тёмный лорд - порождение Бездны. Именно он вёл в бой Легион Затмения, пытаясь принести мир в жертву Бездне. Его доспех - прямое воплощение ужаса и боли всех, кто пал от его рук. Увеличивает урон носителя, заставляя проливать всё больше крови во имя тьмы."]
	quest.5AA75E6F5C50AFB7.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &6самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &6бестиарии&r."]
	quest.5AA75E6F5C50AFB7.quest_subtitle: "&6Бронзовое"
	quest.5AA98D1298FD90BA.quest_desc: [
		"Your one and only &9Tungsten&r source! Whilst you could technically get your Tungstate from macerating &eEnd Stone,&r the yield is tiny. Process these ores instead!"
		""
		"An extremely important vein, as Tungsten is used in vast amounts in &9IV&r and onwards."
	]
	quest.5AA98D1298FD90BA.quest_subtitle: "Source of Tungsten, Lithium"
	quest.5AA98D1298FD90BA.title: "Scheelite"
	quest.5AB202F6C0B34BF3.quest_desc: [
		"Sodium Persulfate isn't as simple to obtain as Mercury, but you'll probably find yourself making some when crafting Circuit Boards. Set up a &6Chemical Reactor&r/&bElectrolyser&r combo with a Level Emitter attached if you want to keep some in stock, and then you can wash any Crushed Ore with a &aChemical Bath&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You'll want to use &3Sodium Persulfate&r when processing:"
		""
		"- Tin Ore"
		"- Aluminium Ore"
		"- Cobalt Ore"
		"- Cobaltite Ore"
		"- Bauxite Ore"
		"- Tetrahedrite Ore"
		"- Pentlandite Ore"
		"- Sphalerite Ore"
		"- Stibnite Ore"
		"- Yellow Limonite Ore"
		"- Malachite Ore"
		"- Iron Ore"
		""
		"Enjoy your byproducts!"
	]
	quest.5AB202F6C0B34BF3.quest_subtitle: "Sulfium Persodate"
	quest.5AB202F6C0B34BF3.title: "Washing with Sodium Persulfate"
	quest.5AB8DB04F4DA2F40.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5ABD56ACA65AC114.quest_desc: ["Декоративные черепа со свечами. Отлично подойдут для интерьера вашего дома."]
	quest.5ABD56ACA65AC114.title: "Свечи на черепах"
	quest.5AD9884E7BFB2510.quest_desc: [
		"Unfortunately, this is only an &lEmpty&r Spray Can, which you have to fill with Chemical Dye before using."
		""
		"&aSpray Cans&r do not provide any functionality involving machines, but can be quite &bvisually appealing and useful&r!"
		""
		"Any &7(or almost any)&r GregTech tile entity &7(machine, pipe, cable...)&r can be &6painted&r to one of the 16 colors of your choosing. This is great for screenshots, or to separate different setups for convenience in a Multiplayer base. They also help with distinguishing between pipelines and cables."
		""
		"Holding the &aSpray Can&r in the offhand will automatically paint any block you place."
	]
	quest.5AD9884E7BFB2510.quest_subtitle: "Time for server tag wars"
	quest.5AD9884E7BFB2510.title: "Spray Can"
	quest.5ADF05F11C9318F3.quest_desc: ["После победы над ледяным драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &bдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.5ADF05F11C9318F3.quest_subtitle: "&bСиняя"
	quest.5AEDD4540682A8BB.quest_desc: ["A more powerful version of the Water Wheel, producing more energy."]
	quest.5AEDD4540682A8BB.title: "Large Water Wheel"
	quest.5AEF483DC14DC7A7.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект &6морской брони&r из блестящей чешуи, а также чешуи левиафана."]
	quest.5AEF483DC14DC7A7.quest_subtitle: "&6Бронзовая"
	quest.5AEF483DC14DC7A7.title: "Морская броня"
	quest.5B07279B08BF8DDE.quest_desc: [
		"&o&7\"250,000,000 EU in a Battery? That's 25 minutes of Power when drained constantly.\""
		""
		"The &aLapotronic Energy Orb&r should be the beginning of the end of your energy storage struggles."
		""
		"This form of Energy Storage is perfect if your Power Generation is inconsistent, or if you need to buffer large amounts due to the nature of &3Large Turbines&r."
		""
		"Such a boost in power does not come cheap. Each &dLapotronic Energy Orb&r is worth &a8 Lapotron Crystals&r."
	]
	quest.5B07279B08BF8DDE.quest_subtitle: "It's amazing!"
	quest.5B07279B08BF8DDE.title: "Insane Batteries"
	quest.5B0AC445672E14B6.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &1IV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"The pattern stays the same: the rightmost circuit comes in &dlarger quantities&r and is overall &aeasier&r to produce."
	]
	quest.5B0AC445672E14B6.title: "&1IV&r Circuits"
	quest.5B1664C5DEB1160D.quest_desc: ["Full-size 1x2 storage drawers will store 16 stacks of an item per drawer (32 stacks overall)."]
	quest.5B182959C194C268.quest_desc: ["Постройте рамку портала в Незер и активируйте портал с помощью огнива."]
	quest.5B1D88BFEA39DBAE.quest_desc: ["Fluix Crystals are obtained from the reaction of Certus Quartz, Redstone, and Nether Quartz in water. This is a key element for creating cables and processors."]
	quest.5B1D88BFEA39DBAE.title: "Fluix Crystal"
	quest.5B20FAAB0E962133.title: "Блюда из гасты"
	quest.5B2696206205CB2E.quest_desc: [
		"&8Wait, we're not in the Steam Age anymore!"
		""
		"The reason we didn't present &7LV&r versions of &6Steam&r machines is because they are &4NOT&r required. You might not want to invest into an upgrade that does next to nothing. Except for &othis one&r specifically, because it's a big improvement over the &6Steam Age&r."
		""
		"The &3Basic Extractor&r gains Fluid capabilities, which enables &aFluid Extraction&r. Use it to melt Rubber that you previously solidified, to &dmelt Soldering Alloy&r for your circuits, and to &dmelt Red Alloy&r for the &6best Vacuum Tube recipe&r in the &3Assembler&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Did you notice this machine doubles as both an Extractor and a Fluid Extractor? The two of them were separate machines in previous versions of GregTech."
	]
	quest.5B2696206205CB2E.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Extractor extracts..."
	quest.5B978E6C5FE55BEB.quest_subtitle: "An exclusive ingredient used to create Player Transmitters."
	quest.5BACED5AE350EAB1.quest_desc: [
		"Nitric Acid's fumes are extremely toxic! It's also a very potent oxidizer."
		""
		"&aNitric Acid&r is used in:"
		""
		"&9-&r Cetane-Boosted Diesel, a better Diesel fuel that you'll get to soon."
		"&9-&r Nitrobenzene, a better Gas fuel that we're not far off making."
		"&9-&r The optional gem slurry chains."
		"&9-&r The Platinum Group Sludge chain in &1IV&r."
		"&9-&r Polybenzimidazole (try saying that ten times fast!) in &1IV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are two main ways to make &aNitric Acid&r - &othe &agood&f way and the &4bad&f ways!&r"
		""
		"Therefore, we'll point you towards the best method:"
		""
		"Get a &3Large Chemical Reactor&r and use it to make &aNitrogen Dioxide&r. From there, react it in a regular &3Chemical Reactor&r with more &dOxygen&r and &dWater&r and you got yourself some &aNitric Acid&r!"
		""
		"This requires a lot of &dOxygen&r. Refer to its own Quest in &7LV&r for the most efficient ways to obtain in large amount. Notice that this is Hydrogen free!"
	]
	quest.5BACED5AE350EAB1.quest_subtitle: "This won't eat your skin"
	quest.5BACED5AE350EAB1.title: "Nitric Acid"
	quest.5BBFE222190891DE.quest_desc: [
		"&cZPM&r Components thankfully aren't too much harder than &dLuV&r. "
		""
		"They use lots of &9Osmiridium&r, so make sure your platinum refining process is up to the task."
	]
	quest.5BBFE222190891DE.quest_subtitle: "Prepare your platline!"
	quest.5BBFE222190891DE.title: "Absolute Elation"
	quest.5BDDB91816287CD1.quest_desc: ["Blaze Rods drop from Blazes in fortresses. They are needed for brewing and creating Eyes of Ender."]
	quest.5BDDB91816287CD1.title: "Blaze Rod"
	quest.5C17BF90DA2AAEEE.quest_desc: [
		"The Integrated Logic Circuit is an alternate &7LV &aCircuit&r, which is easier to mass-produce, and can be upgraded to &bMV&r (and then &6HV&r)."
		""
		"&9Note:&r This is not a strict upgrade to the cost of Circuits - you would need to get to the next Tier for that, just slightly further down in &bMV&r. It is still an important upgrade, and is required to get to &6HV circuits&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The circuit progression in GTCEu is mostly based on GT5u's progression. It has been rebalanced to not be as painful. &lSpecifically&r&o this circuit tier, which was a trap!"
	]
	quest.5C17BF90DA2AAEEE.quest_subtitle: "You have unlocked a new tier of Circuits!"
	quest.5C17BF90DA2AAEEE.title: "More LV Circuits"
	quest.5C27111CCD5A67DA.quest_desc: ["Получите всевозможное оружие из морской бездны."]
	quest.5C27111CCD5A67DA.title: "Глубинное оружие"
	quest.5C3501DD3B4788FA.quest_desc: [
		"More tools - they're not critically important right now, but you'll need to make these at some point."
		""
		"&9&lScrewdriver:&r A crafting tool. It's used for special configuration of machines and covers."
		""
		"&9&lWire Cutter:&r A crafting tool. You'll need it if you want to configure wire connections. Right-clicking on wires will enable or disable connection to other blocks."
		""
		"&9&lMortar:&r A crafting tool, used to grind various things down into dust form."
		""
		"&9&lKnife:&r A pretty mediocre weapon, better suited as - &oyou guessed it&r - a crafting tool!"
		""
		"&9&lSoft Mallet:&r A tool to toggle machine operation with a simple right-click."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are a couple of other tools that are quite niche, but deserve a mention."
		""
		"&9&lCrowbar:&r A helpful tool that can remove covers from &aGregTech&r machines by right-clicking the side."
		""
		"&9&lScythe:&r A powerful farming tool that can automatically replant your crops in a large area. It's also a surprisingly good weapon!"
		""
		"&9&lPlunger:&r A tool to clear stuck fluids from GregTech&a machines."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e&lNote:&r This quest's reward is &3Damascus Steel&r - a rare material which can only be found as overworld loot. It far surpasses the materials you have now, so be sure to use it."
	]
	quest.5C3501DD3B4788FA.title: "More Tools"
	quest.5C3C55360EAE3AE1.quest_desc: ["После победы над грозовым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &6драконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.5C3C55360EAE3AE1.quest_subtitle: "&6Медная"
	quest.5C3FF43CF16BCF30.quest_desc: ["With Source Gems, you can get started crafting the various machines by creating &5Sourcestones&r."]
	quest.5C3FF43CF16BCF30.quest_subtitle: "Formerly known as \"Arcane Stones\""
	quest.5C3FF43CF16BCF30.title: "Sourcestones"
	quest.5C593430DA232A34.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &7самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &7бестиарии&r."]
	quest.5C593430DA232A34.quest_subtitle: "&7Серебряное"
	quest.5C78BBC3403DFB6F.quest_subtitle: "This Binding Card will allow wireless charging across dimensions, but must use a binding card on an Enderman to work."
	quest.5C78BBC3403DFB6F.title: "Bounded Through Dimensions"
	quest.5C8D7BD3DA61109F.title: "Electric quarry"
	quest.5C94CF50090D7DA0.quest_desc: [
		"This kind soul&r will mine ores for you when placed above a vein."
		""
		"Vertical range is unlimited below the miner. Horizontal range is displayed in the tooltip."
		""
		"The &bMV&r variant may not have the range to mine a full vein, but the &6HV&r variant does, so you may wish hold off for now. Get &eeither&r to complete this Quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You will need &9Power&r. &aCharged Batteries&r may work, but they tend to run out of power, which is a bit inconvenient."
		""
		"Our top suggestion is to use a filled &3Drum&r of some kind of fuel &7(if you're using Steam, no dice!)&r and a &3Generator&r. "
		""
		"Place the Drum above your Generator and right-click it with a &5Screwdriver&r to auto-output into the Generator."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cNote:&r Do not forget to &dchunkload&r all 9 chunks of the ore vein with FTB Utilities &7(open the map in the top left corner, claim the chunks with left-click, and enable force loading with shift-left-click)&r."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r You can either use an &3ME Chest&r or a &32x2 Drawer&r as the output inventory to make transporting the ores back home a simple task. The &3ME Chest&r can be powered with EU directly."
	]
	quest.5C94CF50090D7DA0.title: "Digital Miner"
	quest.5CA86A333670A55C.quest_desc: [
		"Tungstensteel under your belt? Nanoprocessor Mainframes on demand? Let's make some machinery."
		""
		"The &3IV Assembler&r is required to unlock &3IV Energy and Dynamo Hatches&r, as well as &3HSS-G Coils&r."
		""
		"Upgrading this to its &2GCYM&r variant isn't a bad idea."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Did you know that GTCE's content stopped at &5EV&r&o, and all content up to &3UV&f was provided by Shadows of Greg, a third party mod?"
	]
	quest.5CA86A333670A55C.title: "IV Assembler"
	quest.5CAF5670B1E622EC.title: "Backpack Upgrades"
	quest.5CBBBFD1FBBE95CE.quest_desc: [
		"The &3MV Cutter&r is required to cut &7Silicon Boules&r to prepare them for &aLaser Engraving&r."
		""
		"We recommend you supply this machine with a steady stream of &dLubricant&r to cut down on the processing time."
		""
		"Lubricant can be &3brewed&r from &eOil&r and &aTalc&r, &2Soapstone&r or &cRedstone&r."
	]
	quest.5CBBBFD1FBBE95CE.quest_subtitle: "Upgrades, people, upgrades!"
	quest.5CBBBFD1FBBE95CE.title: "Advanced Cutter"
	quest.5CC9B0E832545569.quest_desc: ["Entering &1IV&r with these Circuits shouldn't be too painful."]
	quest.5CC9B0E832545569.quest_subtitle: "Set sail, IV is on the horizon"
	quest.5CC9B0E832545569.title: "More IV Circuits"
	quest.5CE0B928479D8535.quest_desc: [
		"Let's go over some uses!"
		""
		"&2Blank Pattern Storage:&r"
		""
		"Right-clicking with the tool in your hand will open a GUI where you can insert &9Blank Patterns&r. There's a considerable amount of storage space for transport of Patterns!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2Bulk Pattern Modification:&r"
		""
		"Inserting &9Encoded Patterns&r instead of blank ones will allow you to multiply/divide them all at once in bulk. This is particularly useful when multiplying up your Patterns for parallel on-demand machinery."
		""
		"Patterns can also be cleared in bulk with the \"Clear\" button. There isn't any confirmation after clicking it, so use with caution."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2Item Search and Replace:&r"
		""
		"Right-clicking the tool and clicking the &aChange Mode button&r will bring up a new GUI. This GUI will allow you to replace all occurances of one item with another for the &9Encoded Patterns&r stored within the tool."
		""
		"This is particularly useful for &eupgrading GT circuits&r, such as transitioning from Nano to Quantum &5EV&r circuits."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2Easy Pattern Transfer:&r"
		""
		"Shift-left-clicking Patterns will move them between the Player Inventory and the Modifier where possible. This means you can easily move Patterns around between Pattern Providers and Terminals without clogging your inventory."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&bLore&r: Neeve, the author of the NAE2 mod which this originated from, suggested tiering this item at &eUXV&r tier, because it \"gives the player way too much power.\" For reference, &eUXV&r is 4 tiers past &3UV&r tier - two tiers before &c&lMAX&r voltage."
	]
	quest.5CE0B928479D8535.quest_subtitle: "The &aPattern Modifier&r does A LOT!"
	quest.5CE0B928479D8535.title: "Pattern Modifier"
	quest.5CEF21E35885E955.quest_subtitle: "Found in &fsnowy&r biomes"
	quest.5CF50859A98E45FB.quest_desc: [
		"They are always produced in matched pairs to create a connection point between 1 pair of quantum entangled Singularities with a ME bridge quantum entanglement chamber on each side."
		""
		"They are created by the interaction between an Ender Pearl or Ender Dust and a Singularity. Any explosive force should be enough to cause a reaction."
		""
		"Almost any explosion - even vines - will work."
		""
		"Always produced in pairs, but only require one specialty."
		""
		"It might be a good idea to provide names for them when you create them with vanilla anvil."
	]
	quest.5CF50859A98E45FB.quest_subtitle: "Required to create a connection between bridges of a quantum network."
	quest.5CFBA24B3E0CDEDD.quest_desc: [
		"While holding your Spellbook, you can press C to open up the spell creation page."
		""
		"Each spell must have a form. You start off with 3 basic forms: Projectile, Self-cast, and Touch."
		""
		"For the Effect, this determines what happens when you cast the spell. You can have up to 9 effects per spell."
		""
		"For starters, you have Harm and Break."
		""
		"Select one Form and one Effect, name your spell, and click create!"
		""
	]
	quest.5CFE6E363FC52BDD.quest_subtitle: "Most Advanced Processor."
	quest.5D17DFCF6672404C.quest_desc: [
		"With a very small percentage of carbon in its mass, Steel is significantly tougher than Iron or Wrought Iron.&r"
		""
		"One &3PBF&r most likely won't cut it moving forwards. Make another one, and you'll effectively halve the time spent waiting for Steel."
		""
		"To save the most time, use blocks of &aCoke&r and &eWrought Iron&r - this generates a block of Steel every 270 seconds. Not bad!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Just to check - did you know GregTech multiblocks can &dshare walls&r? This could save you a whole 12 Firebricks for your second PBF. &7There may be more efficient setups, but don't stress out over figuring them out.&r"
		""
		"What you &omay&r also do is upgrade to four &3PBFs&r. It just depends on how much time you want to dedicate to resource collection, but more PBFs are always nice. We won't force you to make them, don't worry."
		""
		"&9Note:&r The &3PBF&r cannot be (reasonably) automated, but putting blocks of Iron and Coke or Charcoal will guarantee it will run for a long time without needing to be babysat."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o  In GregTech 5, one single Ingot of Steel would take you &d360 seconds&f in the PBF when using Coal or Charcoal! That's over &e6 hours&f for a whole stack! Of course, with 4 PBFs, that would cut it down to &3around 1.5 hours&f."
		""
		"&oPollution was also (infamously) a thing, so four of these monsters would guarantee your character would periodically get negative effects such as slowness, mining fatigue, or even nausea and poison."
		""
		"&oPollution is actually integrated into GregTech Modern, but we've graciously disabled it in the configs. You can re-enable it if you're up for a challenge."
	]
	quest.5D17DFCF6672404C.quest_subtitle: "Steel, Schrödinger's alloy"
	quest.5D17DFCF6672404C.title: "We Need More Steel!"
	quest.5D77F808FB789F64.quest_desc: ["Создайте &dволшебную палочку пикси&r."]
	quest.5D82F035B9D23B6E.title: "Time to sleep"
	quest.5D87088E8D71DB9B.title: "Energy Crystal"
	quest.5D89C7F9261D1E74.quest_subtitle: "Find a chapter of Tools of War in a bastion remnant, or barter for one with a piglin"
	quest.5D9D01EF219A31C5.quest_desc: [
		"Put your previously made &aBiomass&r into a &3MV Distillery&r to make &aEthanol&r."
		""
		"You will need this for &dEthylene&r by reacting it with &aSulfuric Acid&r in a &3MV Chemical Reactor&r... unless you chose to go down the Oil path."
		""
		"Once you have a hefty starting stock of Ethanol, consider making and distilling &9Fermented Biomass&r in a &3Distillation Tower&r (when you get there!) for extra chemicals."
		""
		"&cDo not try&r to use Ethanol as a Power source... it's quite possibly its worst use. If it's organic &9Power&r that you want, we suggest taking a look at &dBenzene&r instead!"
	]
	quest.5D9D01EF219A31C5.quest_subtitle: "Yo, wait - that's alcohol!"
	quest.5D9D01EF219A31C5.title: "Ethanol"
	quest.5DB4107A4B371F98.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.5DBBD9B1F5B01F4E.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLow Power Integrated Circuit&r requires an &3HV Cutting Machine&r inside your &3Cleanroom&r."
		""
		"&3HV Energy Hatches&r will be nice additions so you can run your Multiblocks (mainly your Electric Blast Furnace and Large Chemical Reactor) directly off a &6HV&r line."
		""
		"You'll need to upgrade your EBF with &32 Energy Hatches&r to obtain &eNichrome coils&r - fun!"
	]
	quest.5DBBD9B1F5B01F4E.quest_subtitle: "Noticing a pattern here?"
	quest.5DBBD9B1F5B01F4E.title: "Upgrade your EBF II"
	quest.5DD49D500327A0E2.quest_desc: [
		"The &dSolid Boiler&r is the only available Boiler for now, as the &aGlass&r needed for the others is not available just yet. You can get by with only one, but we would recommend making at least two."
		""
		"Important: Boilers can explode! This still catches out &eexperienced GT players&r, so keep this warning in mind when setting your Boiler up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Water does not gel well with &6high temperatures&r, and a &cSteam Explosion&r &7(Launch!)&r may occur under the following conditions:"
		""
		"- The Boiler is &4overheating.&r Its temperature is indicated by the &cred bar&r in the GUI."
		"...and..."
		"- The Boiler does not have any &bwater&r. This is signified by the absence of a &bblue bar&r in the GUI."
		"...AND..."
		"- The Boiler receives water whilst &6both&r conditions are &2true&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can avert catastrophe by filling the boiler with water before heating it up, and making sure the water supply is constant. The drain is slow - &b1 mB&r of Water boils into &7160 mB&r of Steam - so you shouldn't have to worry about running out."
		""
		"The Boiler can auto eject steam on all its faces except the bottom. For automated Water input, use the bottom face."
		""
		"&3Note:&r In this modpack, explosions are configured to &cnot&r damage any block or entity, but you'll &dstill lose&r your machine."
	]
	quest.5DD49D500327A0E2.quest_subtitle: "Putting the Steam in Steam Age"
	quest.5DD49D500327A0E2.title: "Pressure Cookin'"
	quest.5DE127A09C08A509.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.5DE71164950E8FE9.quest_desc: ["Welcome to hell! The Nether is a dangerous place full of fire and monsters, but here you can find the rarest resources, like Netherite."]
	quest.5DE71164950E8FE9.title: "Visit the Nether"
	quest.5E1D79B76A1A2D3A.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.5E21323CD1DA1EB1.quest_desc: ["После победы над ледяным драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &bдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.5E21323CD1DA1EB1.quest_subtitle: "Серебряная"
	quest.5E4FBB2287D9E635.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Integrated&r Circuit line may not be a strict upgrade in terms of cost, but will tide you over as a stepping stone towards the next tier."
		""
		"They will require a MV &3Laser Engraver&r and a MV &3Cutting Machine&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In Omnifactory, and in previous Gregicality, this circuit line was called &9Refined&f and was standardized like further tiers."
	]
	quest.5E4FBB2287D9E635.quest_subtitle: "Integrated Dynamics"
	quest.5E4FBB2287D9E635.title: "Craftable in &bMV&r"
	quest.5E540531298FE9FF.quest_subtitle: "wizards mod"
	quest.5E6BA54E8A5BEBDE.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have &aEpoxy&r, you can make &aAdvanced Circuit Boards&r! The next Circuit tier is oh so close, so keep pushing."
		""
		"&9&lTips:&r"
		""
		"- Consider using &dElectrotine decomposition&r and &dOre Processing&r for &eElectrum&r."
		"- Consider using the &3Chemical Bath&r with &dMercury&r for &eGold&r, from a wide variety of ores."
	]
	quest.5E6BA54E8A5BEBDE.quest_subtitle: "Quite the gold cost..."
	quest.5E6BA54E8A5BEBDE.title: "Advanced Circuit Boards"
	quest.5E76D4C24026157D.quest_desc: [
		"&6The best LV Circuits&r! You can start to churn these guys out, as you'll be making them for the rest of the game."
		""
		"Try to keep a stockpile of these crafted at all times - making these on-demand can take a while."
		""
		"Reaching &5EV&r will unlock methods to make them even cheaper."
	]
	quest.5E76D4C24026157D.quest_subtitle: "It Feels Good to be the Best"
	quest.5E76D4C24026157D.title: "Best LV Circuits"
	quest.5E7AF7CD58AEB1CD.quest_desc: ["Бомбы из чернил спрутов."]
	quest.5E7AF7CD58AEB1CD.title: "Глубинные бомбы"
	quest.5E89BDA8943534AF.quest_desc: [
		"After &lmany&r requests, &6Sophisticated Backpacks&r has now been integrated!"
		""
		"Backpacks scale alongside &aPortable Cell&r tiering, with modular upgrades that can be inserted to provide new &dBackpack functionalities&r."
		""
		"Before you reach &7LV&r, the upgrade options are &cquite limited&r. However, you should be able to upgrade the starter backpack &eonce&r before you make your first electric machine!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Just so you know - backpacks have been configured and will &cnot&r interact with a connected &bStorage Bus&r. If you want the power of digital storage, you'll have to work for it!"
		""
		"Oh, and holding one too many backpacks will &6slow you down&r."
	]
	quest.5E89BDA8943534AF.quest_subtitle: "A lower-tech Personal Cell!"
	quest.5E89BDA8943534AF.title: "Backpacks"
	quest.5ED483A04095EFA3.quest_desc: [
		"The one and only vein for Uranium!"
		""
		"Uranium has a few minor uses in &5EV&r and beyond."
		""
		"Did you know that Nuclear Reactors might be making their way to &bGTCEu&r in the future?"
	]
	quest.5ED483A04095EFA3.quest_subtitle: "Source of Uranium, Thorium, Lead"
	quest.5ED483A04095EFA3.title: "Pitchblende"
	quest.5ED6B16E5C7303AF.quest_desc: ["Use the ingots of &6ignitium&r to create a powerful piece of equipment. It will definitely not let you down in battle...."]
	quest.5ED7707B0ECF2207.quest_desc: [
		"&aLuV Superconductors&r are necessary if you're eyeing a &9Fusion Reactor&r. "
		""
		"Don't ignore our warning here - you're gonna need &ea lot&r&r of them. Luckily, any &5Indium&r shortages will be solved by your Naquadah line."
	]
	quest.5ED7707B0ECF2207.quest_subtitle: "Be glad these don't use pumps"
	quest.5ED7707B0ECF2207.title: "LuV Superconductors"
	quest.5F074BD9298F0DA0.quest_desc: ["Пицца из незерских ингридиентов. Довольно вкусная!"]
	quest.5F320AFEF6F41AAF.quest_desc: [
		"Multiblocks do not look at the voltage of recipes when trying to craft. Instead, they simply check if they are being provided with enough Power."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Be wary of Cable &closses&r bringing the actual power input below the recipe requirement! We &lhighly&r recommend either placing your &3Battery Buffer&r next to the &3Energy Hatches&r for the minimum cable length, or looking around this questbook to see if there are better alternatives to Cables."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The EBF needs a minimum of &4120EU/t&r power input to run its recipes. This can be achieved with &3two LV Energy Hatches&r. Each one takes 2 Amps of LV, so that's 4 Amps of LV for 128EU/t maximum power."
	]
	quest.5F320AFEF6F41AAF.title: "Powering Multiblocks"
	quest.5F52B24FFE2DDD86.quest_desc: ["It doesn't have many recipes yet, but it is already useful to automate Motors!"]
	quest.5F52B24FFE2DDD86.quest_subtitle: "The Polarizer is a unique machinery that adds in magnet like properties to certain machinery parts that will be essential."
	quest.5F52B24FFE2DDD86.title: "Can we create Magnemite?"
	quest.5FE2E98F31F86843.quest_desc: ["Не каждый ел такое."]
	quest.5FE2E98F31F86843.title: "Люксовая еда"
	quest.5FEA2252462284A4.quest_desc: ["Brass Casing is used to create more advanced mechanisms. Applied to stripped logs just like Andesite Casing."]
	quest.5FEA2252462284A4.title: "Brass Casing"
	quest.601FE17AA8C90316.quest_subtitle: "Found by opening underground Strongholds in the Dark Forest with a trophy. Unlocks the Ur-Ghast Tower."
	quest.601FE17AA8C90316.title: "Slay the &8Knight Phantoms"
	quest.602DA4B4820E9088.quest_desc: ["The &aQuantum Bridge Card&r is an upgrade to the &9Quantum Link Tunnel&r, which gives &9Wireless Terminals&r access to your AE system with unlimited range, and from any dimension."]
	quest.602DA4B4820E9088.quest_subtitle: "Bridge over Troubled Water"
	quest.602DA4B4820E9088.title: "Infinite Wireless Range"
	quest.60415FF25D84D1D9.quest_desc: ["Тёмный лорд - порождение Бездны. Именно он вёл в бой Легион Затмения, пытаясь принести мир в жертву Бездне. Его доспех - прямое воплощение ужаса и боли всех, кто пал от его рук. Увеличивает урон носителя, заставляя проливать всё больше крови во имя тьмы."]
	quest.60852BB9DAB419FA.quest_desc: ["An unusual booskelf. Decreases Eterna slightly, but makes enchanting less random."]
	quest.60D7F6C1EE918B66.quest_desc: ["The &bMV&r Circuit for the Integrated Tier."]
	quest.60D7F6C1EE918B66.quest_subtitle: "More... I demand more!"
	quest.60D7F6C1EE918B66.title: "More MV Circuits"
	quest.60E012BBFD9C07E2.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.60EB85A31AA3EC1F.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.61444A4D9FA7B3DA.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &9самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &9бестиарии&r."]
	quest.61444A4D9FA7B3DA.quest_subtitle: "&9Сапфировое"
	quest.6153EB0873A1A74E.quest_desc: ["Отыскав &dдвенадцать&r очей края, а также найдя крепость края, вы можете смело отправляться в мир, где практически всё состоит из пустоты - &dКрай&r."]
	quest.616DB394EB7D81D6.quest_desc: [
		"You probably don't even need these, but &aUHV Superconductors&r exist, and are used for a few things, which you also probably don't need..."
		""
		"Craft these if you feel like flexing."
	]
	quest.616DB394EB7D81D6.quest_subtitle: "Is Neutronate even a real thing?"
	quest.616DB394EB7D81D6.title: "UHV Superconductors"
	quest.6175CD799995E927.quest_desc: ["The conversion upgrade will convert materials from different mods to a single type. (You should not run into this in this pack)."]
	quest.617C44FC794E91B9.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.6191E10B6F79AC20.quest_desc: ["Броня, принадлежавшая некогда очень опытному вору. Это идеально пошитый тканевый доспех не сковывает движений и позволяет оставаться незаметным даже на самых опасных заданиях. Поговаривают, что он даже приносит удачу владельцу."]
	quest.6191E10B6F79AC20.title: "Нагрудник вора"
	quest.61972B16805FC9EE.quest_desc: [
		"Distillating &aOil&r will give you Fuel that you will need to desulfurize."
		""
		"&aHydrogen Sulfide&r is perfectly &drecycled&r in an &3Electrolyzer&r."
		""
		"To automate this process, simply place your &3Chemical Reactor&r and your &3Electrolyzer&r next to each other. Be sure to use your &5Screwdriver&r to &4enable input from the output side&r."
		""
		"&aLight Fuel&r is a good &9Power&r option, but there's something even greater... check the Quest to the left."
	]
	quest.61972B16805FC9EE.quest_subtitle: "Turn up the Lights in here, baby"
	quest.61972B16805FC9EE.title: "Light Fuel"
	quest.619A52669514E850.quest_desc: [
		"Feasts are not edible directly as an item; they must be placed down as a block first. When placed, players can use (right-click) them with Bowls to serve themselves with a consumable portion."
		""
		"The existing feasts in Farmer's Delight provide 4 servings in total. Plated feasts will also leave behind leftovers in the form of a dirty plate; right-clicking or mining it will retrieve the original Bowl, and any bones or food scraps left behind."
	]
	quest.619A52669514E850.quest_subtitle: "Feasts are very large meals, which can be placed as a block to provide multiple servings to players."
	quest.619E47CCB5F361E9.quest_desc: [
		"В тёмном дубовом лесу обитает раса фей, именуемых&d пикси&r. Они живут в маленьких домиках в виде пеньков, а также грибов. Они умеют делать волшебную, вкусную пыльцу. А также они любят красть вещи у людей..."
		"Также вы можете подружится с пикси и сделать ее своим другом, покормив ее тортиком."
	]
	quest.619E47CCB5F361E9.quest_subtitle: "Друг или враг?"
	quest.61A0AF3A1C32CD19.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.61D2494A05ED6BFE.title: "Netherite-gold"
	quest.61E553A98BE5C2EC.quest_desc: ["The storage downgrade will drop the storage of the drawer it is installed in to one stack."]
	quest.61FED75EFA6555EC.quest_desc: [
		"You have likely realised by now that the Energy system in &2GregTech&r is &cnowhere near as simple&r as the &1RF&r you may be used to using in modded Minecraft."
		""
		"The energy unit of GregTech is the EU."
		""
		"&1EU&r mechanics have a certain flair to them, and are not dissimilar to real-world electricity. They can also be &4dangerous and punishing&r if mishandled. However, the power system gives GregTech players a lot of &6satisfaction&r when harnessed well."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Amperage bug, exploit or feature (call it whatever you want!) from 1.12.2 GTCE has been &lfixed&r&o in GTCEu. The Energy network now works as intended."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let's go over some basic physics:"
		""
		"° &9Power&r = &2Voltage&r * &dAmperage&r"
		"° &1Energy&r = &9Power&r * &6Time&r"
		""
		"&8Resistance&r is an excluded concept in GregTech, instead being partially simulated as cable loss."
		""
		"The units are defined as such:"
		""
		"- &1EU&r is the unit of &1Energy&r."
		"- &9EU/t&r is the &9Power&r."
		"- &dA&r or &dAmp&r is the &dAmperage&r."
		"- &2V&r &owould&r be the &2Voltage&r, but we prefer referring to it as &7LV&r, &bMV&r, &6HV&r... as those are the relevant values for gameplay (technically: &7LV&r = 32V = 32EU/t/A)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Electricity in GregTech travels in \"packets\". The size of each packet is equivalent to the voltage of its tier."
		""
		"Taking an LV packet as an example, this \"packet\" would carry 32EU. Multiple blocks are capable of producing these EU packets, and packets are only produced if they are able to access a destination."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Every &6tick&r, &1EU&r &apackets&r attempt to transfer themselves from Energy Producers to Consumers. These &apackets&r have two parameters: a &2Voltage&r tier determined by the tier of the Producer, and &dAmperage&r. This determines how much &9Power&r can actually be transferred. "
		""
		"There are no partial Amps, meaning Energy is transferred only if the full Amp &apacket&r can be received. You might notice this from your machines sitting just below full EU capacity - they will only accept EU when they are missing at least 1A of their input voltage."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If a &3Machine&r receives a &2higher Voltage&r than its Tier, it'll &cexplode&r. Kaboom! Any excess &dAmperage&r won't have an adverse affect, as machines only consume as they need."
		""
		"The machine explosion would usually also damage terrain, but we have disabled that feature in this pack."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In summary, Energy is transported in &apackets&r of &132EU&r for &7LV&r, &1128EU&r for &bMV&r... so on and so forth. The amount of energy that is actually received by a machine can end up being lower than energy sent, due to cable loss."
		""
		"Machine Energy Input is limited by &2Voltage&r (too high and, well, &6boom&r!), and by &dAmperage&r. Thus, a &bMV&r Machine with &d2A&r Input connected to a &7LV&r line will never accept more than &964EU/t&r."
		""
		"It is still possible to run &bMV&r Machines on &7LV&r lines, but only if the recipes are low enough &9Power&r, or if you have a &3MV Battery&r in the charging slot. The machine will only accept &d1A&r when idle, and so the &3Battery&r will recharge at a maximum rate of &932EU/t&r."
	]
	quest.61FED75EFA6555EC.title: "Electricity"
	quest.62133878B524E274.quest_desc: ["Находится далеко в заснеженных землях под защитой могучего зверя."]
	quest.62212F2B51AC779E.quest_desc: [
		"Iron, Copper and Tin will only get you so far. &4Redstone&r and &bDiamond&r will occasionally be required during the &6Steam Age&r, whereas Nickel, Lead and Silver are also nice to have. All will come in handy &asoon enough&r."
		""
		"&o&8Consult the ore tab if you're struggling to find these materials!&r"
	]
	quest.62212F2B51AC779E.quest_subtitle: "Sometimes, you gotta be inefficient... to be efficient!"
	quest.62212F2B51AC779E.title: "Early Investments"
	quest.6238B2A7ED1BE5A1.quest_desc: [
		"Distillating &aOil&r will give you Fuel that you will need to desulfurize."
		""
		"&aHydrogen Sulfide&r is perfectly &drecycled&r in an &3Electrolyzer&r."
		""
		"To automate this process, simply place your &3Chemical Reactor&r and your &3Electrolyzer&r next to each other. Be sure to use your &5Screwdriver&r to &4enable input from the output side&r."
		""
		"&aNaphtha&r is a good &9Product&r source. Keep following the quests to the right for more details."
	]
	quest.6238B2A7ED1BE5A1.quest_subtitle: "We're still confused on how this is pronounced"
	quest.6238B2A7ED1BE5A1.title: "Naphtha"
	quest.624FD51FE060AADC.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the Infused Seashelf. Provides higher stats."]
	quest.6291071778065BC1.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.6291071778065BC1.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.629E023752317A31.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &9Wetware&r Circuit line."
		""
		"It will be the biggest automation challenge to face in this modpack. Best of luck."
	]
	quest.629E023752317A31.quest_subtitle: "Soft and Wetware"
	quest.629E023752317A31.title: "Craftable in &cZPM&r"
	quest.62A893EB7E47BFB4.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект инструментов из кости &6дракона&r и кости &6иссушителя&r."]
	quest.6314525E36DEA54B.quest_desc: ["The Singularity is the answer: this immensely powerful ball of matter has very useful quantum physics applications with the proper stabilizing materials."]
	quest.6314525E36DEA54B.quest_subtitle: "I wonder if creating a miniature black hole is safe? Ah well, it'll be useful for quantum physics."
	quest.6314525E36DEA54B.title: "Are we gonna fix history for Humanity?"
	quest.6314B892B569A0A5.title: "&6Stalight"
	quest.63256ED95F17B242.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Arc Furnace&r uses a lil' bit of &9Oxygen&r to smelt items in a different fashion than Furnaces."
		""
		"You can use it to make easier &aWrought Iron&r, double your &aGlass&r, and gain access to &aAnnealed Copper&r."
		""
		"It can also recycle various components and machines back to their original material."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Previous versions had both the Arc Furnace and the &bPlasma Arc Furnace&f. In that case, why not use one machine for both? Well, that's exactly what we thought - but we ultimately decided to remove one of the two &bplasma&f recipes. And then the other &bplasma&f recipe. "
		""
		"&oIn short, the &bPlasma Arc Furnace&f is &4gone&f. RIP."
	]
	quest.63256ED95F17B242.quest_subtitle: "Here lies Plasma Furnace"
	quest.632BC46928CC9A8C.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Enchanter's Mirror&r will apply a self spell when used."
		""
		"Spells cast with this mirror are discounted and gain additional bonus duration."
		""
		"To apply a spell, use a Scribe's table. Create a spell without using a form."
	]
	quest.63362CC33B39C627.title: "Visit &6Starlit Sea"
	quest.633851529C3BB554.quest_desc: ["Из монстров &4забвенных пустот&r, можно получать разные предметы, которые пригодятся в последующих крафтах."]
	quest.63535BCF692E1F53.quest_desc: ["Доспех Героя, сразившего Тёмного Лорда в жестокой битве. После этого силы тьмы отступили обратно в Бездну и больше не предпринимали попыток нападения. Этот доспех впитал в себя сущность того героя и наделяет владельца силой и регенерацией."]
	quest.637B8123F0E769C6.quest_desc: ["Further improves Rectification"]
	quest.637D255E6F4459DB.quest_desc: ["Дрожжи нужны не для того, чтобы кидать в унитаз."]
	quest.637D255E6F4459DB.title: "Подготовка к выпеканию"
	quest.63A87C9303D54487.quest_desc: [
		"&aNano CPU Wafers&r are made by infusing regular &aCPU Wafers&r with &dGlowstone&r and &9Raw Carbon Fibers&r."
		""
		"They will be needed in large quantities when making the &5Nano&r line of Circuits."
		""
		"Higher-tier polymers will increase your yield of &9Raw Carbon Fibers&r. One &dEpoxy&r is enough for a full stack."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r Don't like mining &dGlowstone&r? Check out Redstone ore processing."
	]
	quest.63A87C9303D54487.title: "Nano CPUs"
	quest.63AE94F1F504DE76.quest_desc: [
		"In this quest, we'll bestow upon you &5cursed wisdom&r... the ability to easily automate the Electrolyzer."
		""
		"The &9Smart Item Filter&r is a filter that recognises Recipe Maps. When placed on the side of a machine, you can set it to \"&3Electrolyzer&r\" to allow insertion of electrolyzable items specifically. You heard that right - no need to filter manually!"
		""
		"Oh, and it only gets &abetter&r. If you combine this bad boy with a &aRobot Arm&r, it'll only supply the &6exact amount&r of items required for a successful recipe to the machine."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Place the &aRobot Arm&r on your Electrolyzer, open its GUI, then place the &9Smart Filter&r inside. Ensure that the Smart Filter is set to Electrolyzer."
		""
		"Next, configure it to &d&lImport&r and &d&lSupply Exact&r. Finally, attach any inventory &7(a chest will do)&r onto the side where you placed the &aRobot Arm&r. Ta-dah! You've figured out how to handle &6all&r Electrolyzer recipes!"
		""
		"What about the output of the &3Electrolyzer&r? You may want to route the Fluids to several Tanks - or even &3Super Tanks&r if you've gotten that far. We highly recommend that you avoid any methods involving voiding Fluids.&7.&8. except for Water for obvious reasons."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r The Robot Arm has to facilitate the item transfer for its filtering functionality to work! Inserting directly into the machine &7(for instance, pushing with a Hopper!)&r will ignore the Robot Arm's &dSupply Exact&r setting."
	]
	quest.63AE94F1F504DE76.quest_subtitle: "Knock, knock - who's that? It's MENSA!"
	quest.63AE94F1F504DE76.title: "200IQ"
	quest.63AFDDFB959D5158.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.63CB3C9F5A61E0C4.quest_desc: [
		"This vein is very rare! Congratulations on stumbling upon one."
		""
		"&8(Or at least... it should be rare.)&r"
		""
		"View the contents of this vein as \"&7&obasically Molybdenum, and some other stuff&r\". Yeah, Molybdenum is what's important here."
	]
	quest.63CB3C9F5A61E0C4.quest_subtitle: "Source of Molybdenum"
	quest.63CB3C9F5A61E0C4.title: "Molybdenum"
	quest.63CD0236B337EAAD.quest_desc: [
		"While this is an extremely &9important&r machine for progression, this will &9&lnot help you immediately&r as it is &cexpensive.&r Most of the recipes you will want to pursue require &cfluids&r. Set up a little bit more infrastructure before rushing this."
		""
		"With that out of the way, the &3Assembler&r is crucial to gameplay. Consider it as important as a Crafting Table, except... well, it's a machine, duh."
		""
		"We as \"modpack developers\" also love to use this to include all sorts of custom recipes - and speaking of custom recipes, the Assembler now unlocks &dApplied Energistics 2&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once you have enough infrastructure you will be able to make use of better recipes for:"
		""
		"&9-&r &6Vacuum Tubes&r, giving over double the previous yield"
		""
		"&9-&r &6Resistors&r, granting 4 resistors per craft!"
		""
		"&9-&r &6Circuit Boards&r, greatly reducing copper used"
		""
		"Wahoo!"
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Back in the days of GregTech 2, the Assembling Machine only had two slots, and was only really used for alternate Circuit and Hull recipes."
	]
	quest.63CD0236B337EAAD.quest_subtitle: "Assemblers, Avenge!"
	quest.63D55699D4BB8848.quest_subtitle: "Charged Snowballs carry enough energy to cause a lightning strike when hitting a mob or hitting the ground."
	quest.63DC162144871509.quest_desc: [
		"Think this pack is &atoo easy&r? Wanting some unique experiences to sink your teeth into?"
		""
		"We've gathered some GTCEu Modern-flavored recommendations in this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lMonifactory&r"
		"&dMonifactory&r is a 1.20.1 modpack based on &eNomifactory CEu&r (which was on 1.12.2!). It aims to streamline and simplify the earlier parts of GregTech, while interweaving other tech mods into GTCEu Modern's progression. It also features a &2Hard&r and an &aExpert&r mode for the challenge-minded!"
		""
		"In its current state, the pack is on the cusp of a pack-changing update, 0.13. Any worlds at &cHigh Voltage&r or higher will likely need a fresh restart."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lCosmic Frontiers&r"
		"- &7Ghostipedia et al."
		""
		"&dCosmic Frontiers&r is a 1.20.1 modpack with gameplay &ba little more difficult&r than this pack, and a focus on interactions between many mods and GTCEu Modern. You'll explore the stars above and travel to the depths below, all whilst tackling &eintricately woven&r progression that ties together the &7mechanical&r and the &5arcane&r."
		""
		"In its current state, the pack is considered to be in &2early alpha&r. However, progress has been curated through &3LuV&r. It's an experience like no other!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lAll the Mods: Gravitas 2"
		"- &7ATMTeam"
		""
		"Starting from &6primitive Stone Age technology&r, hand-knapping your tools and foraging for food, you'll need to progress through the ages covering many &bclassic and new&r mods. This is seamlessly complemented by mods such as TerraFirmaCraft, Create New Age, Stargate Journey and &8(obviously)&r GregTech."
		""
		"You'll find yourself transitioning from a &2primitive beginning&r, smashing rocks together, to smashing atoms together, soon &dpowering your voyages&r to the stars and beyond!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lStar Technology"
		"- &7trulyno"
		""
		"&6Star Technology&r is more of a laid-back GregTech &dskyblock modpack&r where you play as a scientist stranded in an &balternate dimension&r after a dimensional travel experiment &4catastrophically fails&r."
		""
		"Progression in this pack will take you above and beyond &3UHV&r, with numerous unique &aStargates&r to craft, and even a remixed &o\"Gregified\"&r Mystical Agriculture."
		""
		"Once again, this pack features a Hard mode, and a Desert mod (called Abydos!)."
		""
		"Note that the pack is still under &eheavy development&r, but you should be able to achieve the &o\"Classic Stargate\"&r as of version Zeta!"
	]
	quest.63DC162144871509.title: "What Else Can I Play?"
	quest.63F9531F391040B2.quest_desc: [
		"The chances you are having TPS issues playing this modpack are slim - this Quest is more suited for late game bases with GregTech and AE2."
		""
		"If you run the command &9/forge tps&r, you will be given the current &4TPS&r and the &4tick time&r in milliseconds."
		""
		"If the tick time exceeds 50ms, the server is under too much load, and won't be able to keep up with a steady 20 TPS."
		""
		"Any machine will add up to the tick time, but don't be too scared of adding machines. Most of the lag usually comes from things that are unoptimized."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Things to &cavoid&r in general:"
		""
		"&9-&r Entities are pretty bad. Ground items or mob entities should be kept as low as possible at any given time. Thankfully, this shouldn't be an issue in this modpack."
		""
		"&9-&r Building everything packed together in a small space. Note that this does &onot&r affect TPS, but you will suffer FPS drops instead."
		""
		"&9-&r Huge walls of drawers, as iterating through every single one of them for insertion and extraction can be pretty taxing."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Things to&c avoid&r with AE2:"
		""
		"&9-&r ME Import and Export Buses on large networks. Use ME Interfaces instead."
		""
		"&9-&r Crafting Cards to passively do large requests."
		""
		"&9-&r Recursive insertion and/or extraction through sub-networks. If you use sub-networks, make them do very specific things rather than interacting with another AE2 network."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Things to &cavoid&r with GregTech (GTCEu has received a lot of improvements over GTCE, but it is possible to destroy your TPS, as with any mod):"
		""
		"&9-&r Many EU Producers connected to many EU Consumers in the same line. Instead, use a Diode or Battery Buffer to separate your line of generators to your line of machines."
		""
		"&9-&r Large amounts of Fluid Pipes. They are &onot&r laggy individually, but they can add up if you have thousands of them."
		""
		"&9-&r Big Item Pipe networks. Small networks are better, to reduce the number of iterations over inventories."
	]
	quest.63F9531F391040B2.quest_subtitle: "They call me 007 - 0 Naquadah, 0 EU/t, 7 TPS"
	quest.63F9531F391040B2.title: "Combatting Lag"
	quest.6401C96CA77FEE8E.quest_subtitle: "Found in the &1Frosted Prison&7, in the Overworld in Snow Biomes. Locate with an &1Eye of Curse"
	quest.64074C9DBD0F7C94.quest_desc: ["A Tower shield allows you to block indefinitely but it takes more integrity of the overall shield."]
	quest.641BB9E51338D0CC.quest_desc: ["Из монстров &4забвенных пустот&r можно получать разные предметы, которые пригодятся в последующих крафтах."]
	quest.641BB9E51338D0CC.title: "Кусочки насекомых"
	quest.641CF8A1AF736C82.quest_desc: ["Cursed eyes can lead you to various dungeons scattered around the world."]
	quest.6431381FBE07D6EF.quest_desc: [
		"By itself, the Battery Buffer does nothing. However, if you place batteries inside its internal storage, it will act as a power buffer."
		""
		"The &3Battery Buffer&r handles &9two Amps in&r, and &9one Amp out&r, &dper Battery&r. The output side has the dot, and all other sides are used as inputs."
		""
		"Our recommendation is to have your generators input energy into it, and power your machines from the output side. This is because the Battery Buffers will demand many Amps of power when it charges, and this could prevent you from using your other machines if it's set up in a way where it can divert power from your other machines to itself."
		""
		"&6It'll also charge &lboth&r EU and RF Tools inside it&r."
		""
		"This is a must have if you don't have unlimited power at hand. Get &eany&r &7LV&r Battery Buffer to finish the quest. However, the 16 slots variant is likely overkill at this stage."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Don't loop your lossy Cables back to your Battery Buffer! If you think about it, you'll just end up voiding energy."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o To be frank with you, the GTCE Battery Buffer was... mediocre. It's been reworked in GTCEu to provide a mix between GT5 and GTCE's functionality. Energy now splits evenly across all batteries!"
	]
	quest.6431381FBE07D6EF.title: "Battery Buffer"
	quest.644C12D0FA5ADD13.title: "oil"
	quest.6450F9CA932E4E8C.quest_desc: ["Это око находится в древнем затопленном городе под охраной ужасного &5порождения бездны."]
	quest.648BCF486E16CCB2.quest_desc: [
		"&7LV&r will require you to craft a lot of different machines! You may also find it useful to have multiple of the same machine, set to different programmed circuit values."
		""
		"Here's a friendly tip if you're struggling to set goals: pick an item in a later quest and go backwards from there."
		""
		"With that in mind... why don't we start with a &5Fusion Reactor&r? Never mind, slightly too ambitious - let's check a closer goal instead. Ah, yes, the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r - the main \"end goal\" of &7LV&r - should be a good target."
		""
		"The EBF is &aexpensive&r, which is why you should initially focus on machines to make components and materials cheaper. We'll do our best to guide you in the right direction with these quests."
		""
		"Other important goals are crafting the &3LV Assembler&r and making your first &aMV Circuits&r."
	]
	quest.648BCF486E16CCB2.quest_subtitle: "Too many options, too little time!"
	quest.648BCF486E16CCB2.title: "Progressing Through LV"
	quest.649045BE6DED01C9.quest_subtitle: "This crystal possesses the unique ability to absorb and convert energy from one form to another, and is the foundation of all ME technology. Fluix Crystal is crafted by placing Charged Certus Quartz Crystal , Nether Quartz and Redstone Dust in water. It will quickly start to react, and result in a Fluix Crystal."
	quest.64BACF5B60AD2406.quest_desc: ["Smelting stainless steel dust in an EBF will give you hot ingots, which you can cool back into regular ingots with a Vacuum Freezer."]
	quest.64BACF5B60AD2406.quest_subtitle: "Stainless Steel, another necessary ingot used for new stuff. Wait.. I see a stain here!"
	quest.64BACF5B60AD2406.title: "Squeaky Clean"
	quest.64BE381FFF7D45F7.quest_desc: ["Убив левиафана, вы получите его &dчешую&r."]
	quest.64BE381FFF7D45F7.quest_subtitle: "&dПурпурная"
	quest.64CACABB48635904.quest_desc: [
		"Obtain &9Hydrochloric Acid&r by mixing &aHydrogen&r and &aChlorine&r."
		""
		"This acid is also obtained as waste from a lot of reactions involving &aChlorine&r. Depending on your setups, you may never need to produce it directly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cNote:&r We have a $medicine command on our Discord:"
		""
		"\"&b&oDo not attempt this in real life - it is not only illegal, but also stupidly dangerous&r\"."
		""
		"This applies to toying with chemicals. Please don't do it."
		""
		"Side note - we can guarantee you have a sample of this with you right now! It's in your stomach as a part of gastric acid."
	]
	quest.64CACABB48635904.quest_subtitle: "You'll need a lot of this!"
	quest.64CACABB48635904.title: "Hydrochloric Acid"
	quest.64D0E66CB4FBEC82.quest_desc: [
		"To get started, you'll need to craft yourself a &6Novice Spellbook&r."
		""
		"This is where you create and store your spells."
		""
		"Hitting the &9C&r key will open up the \"Create a Spell\" page. On the left, there are several tabs, but the main 3 are: Spell Creation, Color Picker, and Familiars."
		""
		"This spellbook will only allow you to create and use Tier 1 Glyphs. To create better spells, you'll need to upgrade your Spellbook!"
	]
	quest.64D0E66CB4FBEC82.quest_subtitle: "Our First Spellbook"
	quest.64E1E87B8AF72968.quest_desc: [
		"All machines typically have one &7Front Face&r, and one &9Output Face&r."
		""
		"The &7Front Face&r should be obvious.\\nThe &9Output Face&r is the face with a dot or hole on it. By default, this is at the back of the machine as you place it."
		""
		"Machines can &aauto-output&r through their output face. To enable auto-output, click the appropriate button in the GUI. Fluid and item auto-outputs are toggled separately. Further control over outputs can be achieved with &dFilters&r and &dCovers&r, which are explained in the quest to the upper left of this one."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Right-clicking a machine with a &5Wrench&r changes the output side, and shift-right-clicking changes the front side. Keep in mind that the front side &ccannot&r also be the output side! "
		""
		"By default, items and fluids cannot be inserted through the output side, but this can be toggled with a &5Screwdriver&r. Either right-click the output face directly, or shift-right-click on the grid corresponding to the side of the output."
		""
		"There are unique machines that do not process recipes, such as the &3Pump&r, &3Miner&r, &3Fisher&r, &3Item Collector&r, etc. These machines will output on their &7Front Face&r (which is still marked as a dot)."
	]
	quest.64E1E87B8AF72968.quest_subtitle: "Let's learn."
	quest.64E1E87B8AF72968.title: "Machine Auto-Output Behaviour"
	quest.64EA73FAB2A51850.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest will be completed with &eeither&r a &3ZPM Energy Hatch&r&r... or a &3ZPM Dynamo Hatch&r for your Multiblock Generators."
		""
		"Don't forget that &d16 Amp&r variants exist!"
		""
		"Don't forget that these hatches require a &9Data Orb&r for research."
	]
	quest.64EA73FAB2A51850.title: "Upgrading your Assembly Line II"
	quest.651EA35917084F06.quest_desc: ["Создайте &eпервобытную&r броню."]
	quest.65333CAC62E70C32.title: "Netherite-diamond"
	quest.653345427522D728.quest_desc: [
		"&3Long-Distance Item Pipes&r can be used to send items across great distances. Place one endpoint at each end, and connect them with pipeline blocks."
		""
		"These pipes instantly transfer from the input side to the output side."
		""
		"They also have a minimum distance between pipe endpoints, so you can't use these for short-range operations."
	]
	quest.653345427522D728.quest_subtitle: "Wondering how to move those ores around?"
	quest.653345427522D728.title: "Long-Distance Items"
	quest.6551184966D3FB8D.quest_desc: ["A Heavy blade will turn a sword into a Greatsword that does large sweeping attacks with a full charge attack."]
	quest.659E1EE75343D327.quest_desc: ["Создайте &eпервобытную&r броню."]
	quest.65A04D599786005E.quest_desc: ["Броня полководца, сражавшегося против сил тьмы. Очень яркий доспех, отражающий тактический гений носителя. Увеличивает максимальное здоровье владельца и усиливает его боевые навыки."]
	quest.65B818D879FA7E4F.quest_subtitle: "The 6th Tier Capacitor used to upgrade to Nitro Machinery, the final tier."
	quest.65CAB2210849D027.title: "Shipwreck"
	quest.65CB5CA13FBD010E.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.65CB5CA13FBD010E.quest_subtitle: "Turbo Upgrades will be useful to speed up your machinery when right clicked with it while the Advanced Machine Hulls will be used on machines to accept MV only as they're a higher tier. Both can be removed using a crowbar when necessary."
	quest.65CB5CA13FBD010E.title: "More upgrades!"
	quest.65EAE938D91FF0F5.quest_desc: ["Убив &dпикси&r, с маленьким шансом вы можете получить её крылья. Их можно использовать для создания волшебной палочки."]
	quest.66041DE10C882382.quest_desc: [
		"Regular &o&dGregTech&r Fluid Pipes can only transport one fluid type at a time."
		""
		"&3Quadruple Fluid Pipes&r can transfer four different types of fluids. &3Nonuple Fluid Pipes&r can transfer nine different types! Useful for compact setups."
		""
		"&3Nonuple Fluid Pipes&r will be useful in &5EV&r for handling the many outputs of the &3Distillation Tower&r."
		""
		"Get &eeither&r to finish this quest."
	]
	quest.66041DE10C882382.quest_subtitle: "\"I thought channels were disabled!\""
	quest.66041DE10C882382.title: "Multiple Channel Pipes"
	quest.66153EDBD5BC8DC5.quest_desc: ["&dThe Twilight Lich&r is a necromancer who lives in his tower in the twilight forest. He possesses four staffs that make him a very strong and powerful boss!"]
	quest.66153EDBD5BC8DC5.title: "Twilight Lich"
	quest.6615AB6958CDE71C.quest_desc: ["Порции фаршированного хоглина."]
	quest.6615AB6958CDE71C.title: "Нарезанный хоглин"
	quest.6644AAD403127EFB.quest_desc: [
		"Maintenance in GregTech is not as bad as you think (promise!), and adding a Maintenance Hatch to your multiblocks makes them look pretty industrial!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Most Multiblocks require a &3Maintenance Hatch&r. You will need to perform Maintenance for the Multiblock to begin operating."
		""
		"This is done by having a &9Wrench&r, a &9Screwdriver&r, a &9Soft Mallet&r, a &9Hammer&r, a &9Wire Cutter&r, and a &9Crowbar&r in your inventory, opening the Maintenance Hatch and &eclicking the center spot once&r. &cThere's no need to move tools individually&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Alternatively, you can circumvent these problems by placing a &9Tape&r in the Maintenance Hatch, but a lot of people would jump at the chance to tell you that Tape is &o\"unethical\"&r - plus, tape is gated behind some polymers starting from &bMV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Maintenance problems have a &d5%&r chance of occuring every &dhour of multiblock activity&r. Needless to say, they are &6very&r rare. Each maintenance problem increases the recipe duration by &c10%&r. Fixing these problems is done the same way as above."
		""
		"At &6HV&r, you'll unlock other Maintenance Hatches that do not require manual repairs."
	]
	quest.6644AAD403127EFB.title: "Maintenance Hatches"
	quest.6656A5E5D8FDABE9.title: "Netherite-diamond armor"
	quest.66805BB78A828C00.quest_desc: [
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You might find Kanthal around the home. Due to its excellent thermal conductivity and intermediate electric resistance, Kanthal is usually found in toasters and heaters!"
		""
		"&oBet you didn't expect your toaster to be at &bMV&f before you!"
	]
	quest.66805BB78A828C00.quest_subtitle: "That's just how I FeAlCr"
	quest.668A8BDDEE17865E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Stone Dust&r can be centrifuged in &bMV&r for a wide range of miscellaneous materials. It's a slow and expensive process, but you may wish to check it out."
		""
		"Obviously, Quartzite is Quartzite. Did you know that you could extract any excess Quartzite into &eLiquid Glass&r?"
		""
		"&aPotassium Feldspar&r electrolyses into some incredibly useful resources."
		""
		"You also have a (low) chance for &dBiotite&r, which notably electrolyses for a very slow source of &bFluorine&r."
		""
		"Finally, &aMetal Mixture dust&r is useless until you can centrifuge it at &5EV&r. Pretty much all of its outputs when centrifuged are very useful."
	]
	quest.668A8BDDEE17865E.quest_subtitle: "Small Stone, Big Byproducts"
	quest.66A23AC2EE9BC4AE.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the &9Quantum&r Circuit line."
		""
		"You may want to invest in &aPBI&r at this point, as &dAdvanced SMDs&r will skyrocket your circuit production."
	]
	quest.66A23AC2EE9BC4AE.quest_subtitle: "GregTech gets Quantum"
	quest.66A23AC2EE9BC4AE.title: "Craftable in &1IV&r"
	quest.66C4F35670A11042.quest_desc: ["Сахарный диабет передёт привет."]
	quest.66C4F35670A11042.title: "Тортики"
	quest.66D26625F2F9CB42.quest_desc: ["The Drawer Controller is the brain of your storage system. It unites all connected drawers into one network, allowing you to quickly store and retrieve items."]
	quest.66D26625F2F9CB42.title: "Drawer Controller"
	quest.6708D4288C5B1F71.quest_desc: ["Абсолютно не связанные между собой блюда."]
	quest.6708D4288C5B1F71.title: "Каменный суп"
	quest.673067D1EF14C18C.quest_desc: ["Броня, принадлежавшая некогда очень опытному вору. Это идеально пошитый тканевый доспех не сковывает движений и позволяет оставаться незаметным даже на самых опасных заданиях. Поговаривают, что он даже приносит удачу владельцу."]
	quest.673067D1EF14C18C.title: "Капюшон вора"
	quest.676667089653641C.quest_desc: [
		"This one's nothing but a meme. It's literally called a Lubricant vein."
		""
		"With that being said, Lubricant is always useful for your &eCutting Machines&r to keep your factory running smoothly."
	]
	quest.676667089653641C.quest_subtitle: "Source of Lubricant"
	quest.676667089653641C.title: "Soapstone"
	quest.6779ED5EB60CF3AB.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &6чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.6779ED5EB60CF3AB.quest_subtitle: "&6Бронзовый комплект"
	quest.6779ED5EB60CF3AB.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.6781213726919716.quest_desc: [
		"The &6System-on-Chip&r (or &bSoC&r) is a specialty component that miniaturizes all the typical circuit components (like SMDs) onto a single chip."
		""
		"These are very useful as they unlock the most efficient recipes for creating &6Refined&r, &6Micro&r, and &6Nano Circuits&r."
		""
		"Each SoC-based circuit recipe requires a different minimum tier of &aAssembling Machine&r, with the Nano Circuits requiring you to hit &dLuV&r. &aSystem on Chip&r unlocks the best recipe for &dLV Circuits&r."
	]
	quest.6781213726919716.quest_subtitle: "Where's the Chip on System?"
	quest.6781213726919716.title: "System on Chip"
	quest.678CABA03E17516A.quest_desc: [
		"The final circuit board - it's been a long time coming! As you can see, this board is &cmuch&r more expensive than the other ones, but you should be alright. You're a pro now!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GTNH, these circuit boards require LuV Sensors, instead of IV. This means that Wetware LuV circuits, needed other (crystal) LuV circuits!"
		""
		"Additionally, because Wetware was so expensive, using Crystal was preferred unless UHV wetware circuits were needed. Thankfully, CEu does not have this problem, and LuV Wetware Circuits are worth making."
	]
	quest.678CABA03E17516A.quest_subtitle: "The board of life itself"
	quest.678CABA03E17516A.title: "Wetware Printed Circuit Board"
	quest.679909A9D331AAAD.quest_subtitle: "I Know What You're Thinking"
	quest.679955AA48F79365.quest_desc: ["The main feature of Applied Energistics 2 is the ME (pronounced Emm- Eee and stands for Matter Energy) network, which is a set of interconnected blocks and cables grouped into a system where storage, power, and function interact between multiple components."]
	quest.679955AA48F79365.title: "Security, wireless and more"
	quest.679AA7BD4B13282D.quest_desc: ["Это око охраняет огромный древний голем в аду."]
	quest.67CB9892113FA601.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &6чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.67CB9892113FA601.quest_subtitle: "&6Медный комплект"
	quest.67FA1292129370E6.quest_subtitle: "Sky Stone Blocks are crafted by melting Sky Stone in a furnace."
	quest.681F1423A36FD4FF.quest_desc: [
		"&3ME Hatches&r directly connect to your &aAE System&r, allowing you to skip placing interfaces directly on buses and hatches."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This feature originally comes from GTNH!"
	]
	quest.681F1423A36FD4FF.quest_subtitle: "No more interfaces on buses"
	quest.681F1423A36FD4FF.title: "ME Hatches"
	quest.68268257BA98FBC0.title: "Meteorite"
	quest.6827A0BFE8BBD247.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из чешуи дракона, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.6827A0BFE8BBD247.quest_subtitle: "Белый комплект"
	quest.6827A0BFE8BBD247.title: "Броня из чешуи дракона"
	quest.682C26579EDDCA76.quest_desc: [
		"Vanadiumsteel is required in small quantities in progression. It's &6nearly four times as durable&r as Steel if used in GregTech tools. The Vanadium comes from &aVanadium Magnetite&r, which you may have encountered in Magnetite veins."
		""
		"Other Steel alloys include Blue Steel, Red Steel, and Black Steel!"
		""
		"Take some Blue Steel free of charge - it's twice as durable as Steel."
	]
	quest.682C26579EDDCA76.quest_subtitle: "Steel Your Heart"
	quest.682C26579EDDCA76.title: "Steel Alloys"
	quest.682D1178AF51998C.title: "Runes"
	quest.68445BB069625244.quest_desc: ["The Electron Tube is used in logic circuits and advanced Create components. It's made by polishing Rose Quartz and combining it with an iron nugget."]
	quest.68445BB069625244.title: "Electron Tube"
	quest.68487E90AA4A1FC5.quest_subtitle: "The ME Chest is the simplest way to use a Storage cell, it will give you direct access to the contents of the cell placed inside. It can be powered stand alone with external power, or as part of a ME Network. When on a network, the storage of the chest will be available to any other devices in the same network using an assigned Channel. When used without a network, the chest will not transfer full stacks at once, capping transfers at 38 items instead."
	quest.6863855483D18530.title: "Netherite-emerald"
	quest.686528C6DC3955B0.title: "Certus Quartz"
	quest.68789BCAD0BF39ED.quest_desc: [
		"If desired, you can enable the mini-map, but it is disabled by default."
		""
		"(World map opens with the &2M&r key)."
	]
	quest.68827799A12D6F5C.quest_desc: ["В &bморях&r и &bокеанах&r обиют морские драконы, именуемые левиафанами. Они очень быстры и сильны, а также гигантских размеров!"]
	quest.68841C26A41D419B.quest_desc: ["Can be used to upgrade a quiver to automatically pull arrows from it."]
	quest.68B2D3B985FC1378.title: "Visit &6Torreya Forest"
	quest.68BD457258EC8CBF.quest_subtitle: "Can split materials into their different parts using strong electric currents."
	quest.68E3010C08DB6C3B.quest_desc: ["Антидоты являются аналогами зелий, но имеют другое применение. Антидот позволяет получить иммунитет от какого-либо эффекта на длительное время."]
	quest.68E3010C08DB6C3B.title: "Создатель антидотов"
	quest.68E8311AC3140A56.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.68E8311AC3140A56.quest_subtitle: "Now this is a perfect machine used to save your materials from being wasted! Use it to cut into any machine part you need, at the cost of some lubricant."
	quest.68E8311AC3140A56.title: "I'll cut you!"
	quest.6902AED5587882DC.quest_desc: ["Победив &bсирену&r, вы получите её чешую, которую можно будет соеденить с &bчешуёй левиафана&r и создать мощную броню."]
	quest.6906121936A688C0.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &9Crystal&r Circuit line."
		""
		"It's locked behind &3Fusion&r."
	]
	quest.6906121936A688C0.quest_subtitle: "Crystallisation"
	quest.6906121936A688C0.title: "Craftable in &dLuV&r"
	quest.690A51204DF5D469.quest_desc: [
		"The &aZPM Lapotronic Orb&r is even better than the &dLuV&r one! It of course comes at a price..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Imagine making 64 &1IV&f or 8 &dLuV&f Orbs for just one of these! See the Lore for the &dLuV&f orb for details."
	]
	quest.690A51204DF5D469.quest_subtitle: "A power singularity!"
	quest.690A51204DF5D469.title: "Mega Batteries"
	quest.690B35169E2F654D.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &rсамку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &rбестиарии&r."]
	quest.690B35169E2F654D.quest_subtitle: "Белое"
	quest.690E013DFCB060ED.quest_desc: [
		"The &aSterilized Cleanroom&r is required to produce the next tier of circuits. Nearly every step must be performed inside of one. Good luck fitting everything into such a tight space!"
		""
		"If you only have one &3Cleanroom&r, you'll need another for &aSterilized&r recipes."
		""
		"&eNote&r: Normal Cleanroom recipes cannot run in the Sterilized Cleanroom, so you can't just \"upgrade\" your old Cleanrooms."
	]
	quest.690E013DFCB060ED.quest_subtitle: "Comes with disinfectant!"
	quest.690E013DFCB060ED.title: "Sterilized Cleanroom"
	quest.692F4312B3F73FAF.quest_desc: ["A standard Iron vein. It's a good target when you need to replenish your supply."]
	quest.692F4312B3F73FAF.quest_subtitle: "Source of Iron, Copper"
	quest.692F4312B3F73FAF.title: "Limonite"
	quest.693E05A909195578.quest_desc: ["You can use it to make carbon dust and unlock better recipes for steel and silicon."]
	quest.693E05A909195578.quest_subtitle: "Splits items by spinning them very fast."
	quest.6942ADE3BA8910F6.title: "Quarter Staff"
	quest.6958029B5514D4EC.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Vacuum Freezer&r is a multiblock used to cool down &eHot Ingots&r. All ingots made in the EBF with a temperature above &d1750K&r will need it."
		""
		"Most of the time, your &3Electric Blast Furnace&r will be the bottleneck, so you don't need to worry about overclocking your freezer."
		""
		"Since &eHot Ingots&r &churt you&r when held, item routing will be very useful."
	]
	quest.6958029B5514D4EC.quest_subtitle: "Did you know vacuums actually make things hotter?"
	quest.6958029B5514D4EC.title: "Ice Cold"
	quest.69597F2A6D80AE29.quest_desc: [
		"Range and power consumption are determined based on the number of wireless amplifiers installed in the ME Wireless Access Point."
		""
		"A network can have any number of ME Wireless Access Points with any number of wireless amplifiers in each, allowing you to optimize power consumption and range by changing the settings."
		""
		"It is required that the channel be operational."
	]
	quest.69597F2A6D80AE29.quest_subtitle: "Provides wireless access via a wireless terminal."
	quest.696536A55ED81D6B.quest_desc: ["The network requires power, which can be provided by various units, and may require ME controller(s) if you require more than 8 channels on a single network."]
	quest.6966F57E97BB934C.quest_subtitle: "Use a workbench to restore the sweeping capabilities of the Holosphere Ccanner, the Ccanner makers it easier to find Ancient Ruins."
	quest.6975F16F5B50F17F.quest_desc: [
		"The &aSimple System on Chip&r will be used for the best &dULV Circuit&r recipe."
		""
		"We'd also recommend going out of your way to make all the other useful colored Lenses ahead of time. They are listed here in an &eoptional&r task."
	]
	quest.6975F16F5B50F17F.quest_subtitle: "...and it's beautiful"
	quest.6975F16F5B50F17F.title: "I see the world in colour"
	quest.69855EE51B48E6B7.quest_desc: [
		"Compacting drawers are a special drawer that will hold a specific material type and allow it to be changed between its different material amounts."
		""
		"For example, loading this drawer with a iron block will allow you to pull the iron block, 9 iron ingots, or 81 iron nuggets from it with no crafting required."
	]
	quest.6988AE94BE7B461F.quest_desc: [
		"Remember &aDarmstadtium&r tools from &3GTCE&r? Well then... guess who's back?"
		""
		"&aDarmstadtium&r is the main material for &3UV&r hulls. It is yet again made with Fusion."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&bFun Fact&r: Arsenic does not exist as a liquid at standard conditions. It sublimates directly into a gas! \"Realism\", my ass."
	]
	quest.6988AE94BE7B461F.quest_subtitle: "I want my particle accelerator back..."
	quest.6988AE94BE7B461F.title: "Darmstadtium"
	quest.698B5F65F2DE4439.quest_desc: [
		"Better &9IV&r Circuits. "
		""
		"Your march through &9IV&r continues. Stay strong, soldier."
	]
	quest.698B5F65F2DE4439.quest_subtitle: "IV, but it's green now"
	quest.698B5F65F2DE4439.title: "Even more IV Circuits"
	quest.698D3529F746CA03.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &7самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &7бестиарии&r."]
	quest.698D3529F746CA03.quest_subtitle: "&7Чёрное"
	quest.69E384F389B0D07B.quest_desc: [
		"The best battery-like item for &5EV&r!"
		""
		"Making a &aLapotron Crystal&r will require quite a bit of nested crafting, so craft these in large batches - or, of course, automate everything with &bAE2&r patterns."
	]
	quest.69E384F389B0D07B.title: "Extreme Batteries"
	quest.6A12B1FE7B703F9D.quest_subtitle: "When equipped, press &bB&r for easy access"
	quest.6A12B1FE7B703F9D.title: "Craft a &2Backpack"
	quest.6A1C0B17B22CE50F.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Amulet of Mana Boost&r gives a boost to max mana."
		""
		"The &6Amulet of Mana Regen&r gives a boost to your mana regen."
	]
	quest.6A1C0B17B22CE50F.title: "The Amulets"
	quest.6A26F923739785B5.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		""
	]
	quest.6A304E453D74C57C.quest_desc: [
		"Before we start, here's some important information if you're aiming to make Ethylene:"
		""
		"Taking the &aOil&r route will require &oat least&r a &3LV Distillery&r."
		""
		"With the &aBiomass&r route, you will &lneed&r a &3MV Distillery&r."
		""
		"Get &eeither&r to complete this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Got all that? &6Alright&r! Let's discuss a complex topic: &9Distillation&r. We'll try to help you understand how and why the &aEMI&r recipes are the way they are, so stick with us."
		""
		"Nearly all the &3Distillery&r recipes are duplicates from the &3Distillation Tower&r, except that they only have one Fluid output, and void everything else."
		""
		"In other words, you could argue the &3Distillery&r is an &dinferior&r &3Distillation Tower&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This doesn't mean that the &3Distillery&r is the worse of the two. It is unlocked earlier, and it is &dsmaller&r, &dcheaper&r, and &dmore energy efficient&r per recipe."
		""
		"Hell, in many cases, you won't even mind losing the other Fluids."
		""
		"&3Distilleries&r are an essential component for power generation, whether you pick &aDiesel&r or &aBenzene&r."
		""
		"You'll probably want many of them at as low-tier as possible to avoid the energy losses from Overclocking."
	]
	quest.6A304E453D74C57C.quest_subtitle: "The Illusion of Free Choice"
	quest.6A304E453D74C57C.title: "Distillery"
	quest.6A723769F45D3B57.quest_desc: [
		"Pump crude oil out from the pumpjack base by connecting it with pipes. The crude oil needs to be pumped into the Steel Distillation Controller, not the tank itself. "
		""
		"Pump each individual oil type out of the outputs into different tanks. "
		""
		"You can burn the ones you don't need with a flarestack."
	]
	quest.6A723769F45D3B57.quest_subtitle: "It's Time..."
	quest.6A723769F45D3B57.title: "Oil Tank"
	quest.6A8464695BDD9B9D.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню и инструменты из &bдраконьей стали&r."]
	quest.6A8464695BDD9B9D.title: "Броня из драконостали"
	quest.6A94B4DB9DDAEDEB.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.6ACBF71317EB9937.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6ADFD817111E5435.quest_desc: ["Can be placed surrounding the enchanting table one-block away and up to two-blocks high to add a small amount of Arcana. There is no limit beyond how many you can fit. Placing multiple on the same block provides no additional benefit."]
	quest.6AE569FB246DF219.title: "Diamond Armor"
	quest.6AF3A40BC9CE7122.quest_desc: [
		"&aTritanium Coils&r bring the Heat Capacity to &d10,800K&r."
		""
		"These coils aren't needed for much, but they'll provide another perfect overclock for most recipes!"
	]
	quest.6AF3A40BC9CE7122.quest_subtitle: "Why would you even need something this hot?!"
	quest.6AF3A40BC9CE7122.title: "Tritanium Coils"
	quest.6AFDA523304711DB.quest_desc: [
		"Production of &aSterilized Growth Medium&r is the final processing line in GTCEu, for now."
		""
		"You will need this for your first &4Wetware Circuits&r."
		""
		"Producing it won't be as much of a hassle as PBI, but nearly every step requires a Sterilized Cleanroom. This means you'll have to get creative with how you use your space."
		""
		"Make sure to scrutinise every step of the chain. Some recipes are much more efficient than others!"
		""
		"&ePro Tip&r: You can wall-share cleanrooms with doors in-between too if you want more space."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GTCEu's Sterilized Growth Medium chain is loosely based off of Bartworks' from GTNH. The main difference is that GTNH required a Bacterial Vat multiblock, which was more complex than the ordered Assembly Line. GTCEu is considering adding a multiblock like it but with their own spin in the future."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3More Lore:&r&o In Gregicality Legacy, the Sterilized Growth Medium production chain was very different. It was one of the most difficult processes in the mod, with over 30 complicated steps! It was based off of producing different real-life vitamins and nutrients."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Even More Lore:&r&o In Shadows of Greg, this was made with just Distilled Water and Mince Meat. How far we've come..."
	]
	quest.6AFDA523304711DB.quest_subtitle: "The final processing line, at last!"
	quest.6AFDA523304711DB.title: "Sterilized Growth Medium"
	quest.6B05C72FF31E104D.title: "Raw Iridium"
	quest.6B08799BCFD01D3D.quest_desc: [
		"&3Nichrome Heating Coils&r increase the temperature of your &3Blast Furnace&r to &d3,600K&r."
		""
		"Despite not being required &oyet&r, it's still a good idea to upgrade your primary &3EBF&r for those sweet, sweet &6Coil bonuses&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In the original GregTech 5, there were only three types of coils. This was the last tier."
	]
	quest.6B08799BCFD01D3D.quest_subtitle: "A long way to go before we beat the Sun"
	quest.6B08799BCFD01D3D.title: "Nichrome Coils"
	quest.6B093C1DD6F02BCE.quest_desc: ["The base for backpack upgrades. With it, you can add functions like a magnet, auto-feeding, and more to your backpack."]
	quest.6B093C1DD6F02BCE.title: "Upgrade Base"
	quest.6B11B8A209763B36.quest_subtitle: "Can make items and fluids react with each other."
	quest.6B128610C7D2825D.quest_desc: [
		"&aNether Stars&r are used for high tier &dSensors&r, &dEmitters&r and &dField Generators&r."
		""
		"You can also use them for &dBeacons&r if you desire the permanent potion effects. Finally, a vanilla multiblock!"
		""
		"We've added a recipe for Nether Star Dust in this pack. &7(Yes - without any tweaks, GTCEu expects you to farm Withers ad nauseam.)"
		"&r"
		"On the topic of the &aNether Air&r which is required in the recipe: take a look at &9Liquid Nether Air&r distillation at your own leisure. It's quite rewarding."
		""
		"&o&8Did you know the vanilla Nether Star texture isn't centred? :)"
	]
	quest.6B128610C7D2825D.quest_subtitle: "Jump Up, Superstar"
	quest.6B128610C7D2825D.title: "Nether Stars"
	quest.6B15091EC1B119B0.quest_subtitle: "Kanthal Coils are used by the Electric Blast Furnace to produce more materials as they are powerful enough to do so."
	quest.6B1595678ECB7AC8.quest_desc: [
		"The next &3Circuit Assembler&r. This tier of Circuit Assembler is only required for one type of Circuit - your first ever &aMainframe&r."
		""
		"You can put this off until &5EV&r."
	]
	quest.6B1595678ECB7AC8.title: "HV Circuit Assembler"
	quest.6B15F03E2B2FE389.quest_desc: ["Из меди можно сделать ящик, в который можно положить до 9 различных инструментов, в том числе серебряных."]
	quest.6B15F03E2B2FE389.title: "Серебряные инструменты"
	quest.6B2B5078EBFA806B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6B511C8B572E8940.quest_desc: [
		"In the bottom left of your screen, you'll see a bar. This bar is your mana pool!"
		""
		"There are several ways to increase your mana pool, or increase the efficiency of your spells as you progress through the mod. Upgrading your spellbook can also increase your mana!"
	]
	quest.6B511C8B572E8940.quest_subtitle: "Mage Power"
	quest.6B522DC6845DB558.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6B522DC6845DB558.quest_subtitle: "You are almost there! With oil processing, you're a few steps closer to making even more advanced machinery."
	quest.6B522DC6845DB558.title: "Upgrades!"
	quest.6B6E7C58587ED44B.quest_desc: ["Святилище душ - давно заброшенная крепость, в которой когда-то проводились эксперименты с душами. После неизвестного события все обитатели святилища бесследно исчезли, оставив после себя только старые записи с исследованиями."]
	quest.6B6E7C58587ED44B.title: "&bНайдите:&r Святилище"
	quest.6B7762F672BAE76F.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Macerator&r finally unlocks more of the slots shown in EMI. With this, the first &9three&r slots are now available. This allows you to receive the &6unique ore Byproduct&r from macerating &dThermal &dCentrifuged Ore&r."
		""
		"Macerating Ores costs &a32 EU/t&r with &5two overclocks&r, which makes this machine able to fit in &7LV&r lines - very, very convenient."
		""
		"Despite the signicant improvements this machine provides, it still isn't completely worth it to set up advanced processing for every single ore. Energy and time are still things to consider, so only process the ores that produce &6Byproducts&r you care for."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GregTech 5u, the &6HV&r&o Macerator only gave two slots. Urgh... we weren't planning on using that Stone Dust, anyway..."
	]
	quest.6B7762F672BAE76F.quest_subtitle: "Shredding your Ores with byproducts"
	quest.6B7762F672BAE76F.title: "Universal Macerator"
	quest.6BB13E775A579F2E.quest_desc: [
		"Need to handle &6multiple&r fluid inputs and outputs? Look no further - these &aFluid Hatches&r can handle more than one fluid at once!"
		""
		"These cannot be used in a &bDistillation Tower&r, but may be particularly useful in &5Large Chemical Reactors&r."
	]
	quest.6BB13E775A579F2E.quest_subtitle: "One-To-Many, Many-To-One"
	quest.6BB13E775A579F2E.title: "Multiple Fluid Hatches"
	quest.6BB98D128822730E.quest_desc: [
		"Our warmest congratulations on making it here."
		""
		"The way you should obtain &aEthylene&r was described in the previous Quest, depending on the route you chose."
		""
		"&aEthylene&r will shortly be used in polymer production. It's also useful in a few other reactions."
	]
	quest.6BB98D128822730E.quest_subtitle: "One of many hydrocarbons"
	quest.6BB98D128822730E.title: "Ethylene"
	quest.6BBB3BDE124D2C16.quest_desc: ["Can be added to a Forge Hammer to increase its hammer rank by 1 but it may light blocks around it on fire."]
	quest.6BBD04C132F40318.quest_desc: ["The skin of the innocent..... oh boy that sounds bad....."]
	quest.6BD42073B410FD59.quest_desc: ["Adds Rectification to your enchanting setup. Rectification decreases the potential for quanta to curse items or offer lower-level enchantments. Max Rectification turns Quanta into a purely beneficial stat. Rectification level can be see when hovering over an enchantment in the enchanting GUI."]
	quest.6BE44648875B11C5.quest_desc: ["При помощи &6рога дракона&r, вы можете поместить в него дракона и освободить в любой нужный момент."]
	quest.6BEB4461CA08633F.quest_subtitle: "Oh dear me, this was such a headache, but now we're going even further beyond? I hope I don't get a headache.."
	quest.6BEB4461CA08633F.title: "&bI want a car now!"
	quest.6BFDAA5B3D799150.quest_desc: ["В первобытных пещерах растёт дерево араукарии. На нём можно найти вкусные орехи."]
	quest.6BFDAA5B3D799150.title: "Дерево Ауакария"
	quest.6C1822FED0613FAF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6C1822FED0613FAF.quest_subtitle: "A specialized chestplate that is used to grant the wearer fall damage protection and creative flight, but will not protect the wearer from any external damage. It must be powered in order to use."
	quest.6C1822FED0613FAF.title: "Iron Man"
	quest.6C20A9A64C1BE0BF.quest_desc: [
		"&3Transformers&r allow you to step up and down safely between Voltage tiers. They convert the power they receive into an equivalent amount of power 1 voltage tier above or below the input voltage."
		""
		"Apart from running machines on different voltage tiers, Transformers come in handy for transporting power across longer distances, as cable loss has less of an effect at higher voltages. Just like real life!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Transformers have 5 low voltage sides, and 1 high voltage side."
		""
		"The &9normal&r Transformer can only do 1A <-> 4A conversion, but &9Adjustable&r Transformers can be changed between 1A <-> 4A, 2A <-> 8A, 4A <-> 16A, and 16A <-> 64A conversions. "
		""
		"Use a &aSoft Hammer&r to change between transforming up and down, and a &aScrewdriver&r on Adjustable Transformers to change the amperage."
		""
		"Higher tier Transformers will require &9Coils&r."
	]
	quest.6C20A9A64C1BE0BF.quest_subtitle: "LV In Disguise"
	quest.6C20A9A64C1BE0BF.title: "Transformers"
	quest.6C241455C5434C2E.quest_desc: [
		"If you say the name 3 times in front of a mirror, you summon a CEu dev."
		""
		"&aMulti-Layer Fiber-Reinforced Printed Circuit Boards&r are the next step in your circuit journey. They're not particularly interesting compared to the previous boards: just two of the previous stuck together."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In Gregicality Legacy, these circuit boards were much more complicated. They required Kapton, a dual polymer material. It was a challenge to say the least. In the future, the GTCEu team might make these boards somewhat more involved to produce."
	]
	quest.6C241455C5434C2E.quest_subtitle: "M-L F-R PCB"
	quest.6C241455C5434C2E.title: "Multi-Layer Fiber-Reinforced Printed Circuit Boards"
	quest.6C248355DABE9A13.quest_desc: ["&dHydra&r - A powerful serpent with three heads. When one head is destroyed, two more appear in its place. To defeat it you need to repel its fireballs at it."]
	quest.6C248355DABE9A13.title: "Hydra"
	quest.6C25D11A26306168.quest_desc: [
		"&o...or little brother. Don't let him know!&r"
		""
		"The &3Steam Oven&r is a great multiblock option if you need &6effortlessly smelt large quantities of items.&r No more lines of furnaces that you have to manually empty and refuel!"
		""
		"It effectively behaves as a parallel furnace, smelting up to 8 items at a time for a low cost of Steam."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This Multiblock - despite being very similar to its brother, the Steam Grinder - isn't ported from a GregTech version or addon. Its actual progenitor is the Steam Oven from Railcraft, which dates back to 1.4.7!"
	]
	quest.6C25D11A26306168.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Grinder's big brother"
	quest.6C25D11A26306168.title: "Steam Oven"
	quest.6C53B01A05FFF1DC.quest_desc: [
		"No, but seriously."
		""
		"This is the &cu&6l&et&ai&bm&9a&5t&4e&r portable Fluid storage solution. &64,000 buckets of storage&r - in one single block!"
		""
		"Like Drums, Super Tanks &6keep their fluids when broken&r, and can be cleared in the crafting grid."
		""
		"If you hunger for &9even more&r storage, take a look at higher tier Super Tanks or AE2 Fluid Storage Cells."
	]
	quest.6C53B01A05FFF1DC.quest_subtitle: "Super Tanks are OP!"
	quest.6C53B01A05FFF1DC.title: "Super Tank"
	quest.6C7A7F08F1F4FD1C.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &6самку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &6бестиарии&r."]
	quest.6C7A7F08F1F4FD1C.quest_subtitle: "&6Медное"
	quest.6C8789A7B8946CFF.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Electric Blast Furnace&r, &3Pyrolyse Oven, &b&aMulti Smelter&r, and &3Cracking Unit&r all require Heating Coils. But why should you bother upgrading to higher tiers of Coil?"
		""
		"Coil progression can be viewed in the Milestones tab."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For the EBF, things get slightly complicated. The EBF smelts items at a certain &dtemperature&r. This is mainly determined by the tier of heating coil used - &r&6Cupronickel&r smelts at &d1800K&r, &bKanthal&r at &d2700K&r, etc. Additionally, starting from &6HV&r, each tier of energy adds &d100K&r to the temperature."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"How does this affect you? Each EBF recipe has a certain base temperature. For example, &bAluminium&r is smelted at &d1700K&r. If the EBF temperature is not high enough, the recipe won't happen. If the EBF temperature is high enough, 2 different bonuses are applied:"
		""
		"&9-&r For every &d900K&r above the recipe temperature, the amount of energy required is multiplied by &a0.95x&r - which stacks."
		"&9-&r For every &d1800K&r above the recipe temperature, a single additional overclock will be &6100% efficient&r; in other words, it will &5quadruple the recipe speed&r, instead of doubling it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Pyrolyse Oven is much more simple in comparison to the EBF."
		""
		"Cupronickel coils apply a &c+25% penalty&r to recipe duration - effectively, recipes are slower than listed if one uses Cupronickel coils."
		""
		"Kanthal coils restore recipe duration to a regular length of time."
		""
		"However, coils above Kanthal apply an &aadditive -50% bonus&r to recipe duration!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Cracker is much more simple."
		""
		"Every coil tier post-Cupronickel will reduce its energy usage by 10%."
		""
		"Coils in the Multi Smelter reduce the amount of energy per operation whilst also increasing the number of items that can be processed in parallel."
	]
	quest.6CD359CE6901E99E.quest_desc: ["Только не переборщите."]
	quest.6CD359CE6901E99E.title: "Кофемашина"
	quest.6CF436D4831F590C.quest_subtitle: "A wrench made of Certus Quartz Crystal or Nether Quartz. Useful for rotating blocks, and removing individual parts from cables."
	quest.6CF436D4831F590C.title: "Rotating Your Machines"
	quest.6D0310EF6A259AC8.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6D0310EF6A259AC8.quest_subtitle: "These tools will be powerful and potentially replace your pickaxe and shovel. The jetpack will also fly faster with better fuel, handle with care."
	quest.6D0310EF6A259AC8.title: "&bIs it a Jet Engine or a Diesel Engine?"
	quest.6D076A95C8A45A1E.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.6D0EB1A5C4C4A913.quest_desc: ["Знаменитый завтрак с видом на Незер."]
	quest.6D0EB1A5C4C4A913.title: "Адский завтрак"
	quest.6D12CE80F92FC485.quest_desc: [
		"Some specific fluids are &dCryogenic&r, which are too cold for ordinary pipes. "
		""
		"Thus... you need to pick the right pipe for the job."
		""
		"Not many pipes support cold fluids, so you'll want to give &aStainless Steel&r or &aIridium&r a try. Later on you can use &aNaquadah&r or most of the fusion materials when you get there."
		""
		"&cWARNING:&r&r Cryogenics in the wrong pipes will cause &cvoiding&r, &cpipe freezing&r, and high rates of &cdeath&r! Be careful."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This is the first time GregTech has cryogenic mechanics, a GTCEu-original feature!"
	]
	quest.6D12CE80F92FC485.quest_subtitle: "You won't find it here"
	quest.6D12CE80F92FC485.title: "This isn't Cryotheum!"
	quest.6D17293BBEDF3958.quest_subtitle: "A component used to create an ME Terminal."
	quest.6D179594F4C5F517.quest_subtitle: "Find a gilding scroll in a nether fortress"
	quest.6D1F10543A391940.quest_desc: ["&aNaquadria&r is an isotope of Naquadah, Nq-522. It's highly unstable, but it'll still be used for &3UV&r components, &9Fusion Mk2&r, and when fusing Neutronium."]
	quest.6D1F10543A391940.quest_subtitle: "Naquadah, but radioactive-er!"
	quest.6D1F10543A391940.title: "Naquadria"
	quest.6D231D21FE4502B0.quest_desc: [" After the potion, feed him with this apple! Don't waste your time, the potion won't last forever!"]
	quest.6D86B78C1DA0BB65.quest_desc: ["Когда-то драконов в мире было намного больше, но рыцари-драконоборцы очень сильно сократили их популяцию. Теперь найти настоящего древнего дракона - большая редкость. Эта тяжёлая древняя броня,, принадлежавшая когда-то одному из сильнейших драконоборцев, впитала в себя силу поверженных драконов. Обеспечивает огромную защиту против драконов."]
	quest.6D86B78C1DA0BB65.title: "Шлем драконоборца"
	quest.6D9D54FAB21EC086.quest_desc: [
		"Make some Battery Alloy, used for Battery Hulls."
		""
		"Antimony is found in the &cNether&r, so don't forget to check its Ore Tab."
		""
		"&9Note:&r This quest does &lnot&r contain functional Batteries - head downwards for that."
	]
	quest.6D9D54FAB21EC086.quest_subtitle: "Batteries are great!"
	quest.6D9D54FAB21EC086.title: "Battery Preparations!"
	quest.6DA28F169CED9C7D.quest_desc: [
		"Scanning is the first step for research. Take the item shown in EMI and put it with a &3Data Stick&r to scan it. This will &4consume&r the item and put Data on the Data Stick. Pretty straightforward, right?"
		""
		"You will need at least an &6HV Scanner&r to progress to &dLuV&r, an &5EV Scanner&r for &aLuV Energy Hatches&r, and an &1IV Scanner&r for &aFusion Reactors&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Later on, recipes will require different &aData Storage Items&r for research, such as the &3Data Orb&r. This process will remain the same, but will use different Data Storage Items instead. They can also be copied the same way, but you cannot copy between different types of storage items."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Eventually, you'll want multiple Assembly Lines, but you won't want to re-scan for every Research. This is why you can also use the &3Scanner&r to &dCopy Data&r. Place the data stick you want to copy in one slot, and a blank one in the other. This will copy the contents of the first stick into the second!"
		""
		"&4Important&r: Using two different data sticks with data on them will cause one to &4overwrite&r the other. Be careful!"
	]
	quest.6DA28F169CED9C7D.quest_subtitle: "Implemented At Last"
	quest.6DA736BAF10D92E2.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.6DAA82B5F94AF9F8.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Jar of Light&r summons a floating light source that follows you."
		""
		"The &6Jar of Voiding&r destroys items you pick up in exchange for mana. This can be filtered."
		""
		"To add or remove an item to be detroyed by the jar, use the jar with the item in your off hand, or use an item on the Scribe's Table with the jar placed on it."
		""
		"The jar must be on your hotbar to function."
	]
	quest.6DBF61D4F94BC851.quest_desc: [
		"&6Neutronium&r is a hyper-dense material normally found in the hearts of neutron stars: the collapsed cores of stars between ten and thirty times the size of the sun. It is the final primary material in GTCEu."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GCYL, Neutronium is unlocked at UMV-tier (called UXV in CEu). There is also Cosmic Neutronium, which is equivalent to Avaritia's Neutronium in GT5u, which was unlocked even later in GCYL!"
		""
		"&l&3More Lore:&r&o Fun Fact: a single Neutronium block is approximately 2884 million metric tons and somewhere around 600000K, yet you're somehow capable of holding one with your bare hands. Don't think about it too much."
	]
	quest.6DBF61D4F94BC851.quest_subtitle: "Pure Neutrons"
	quest.6DBF61D4F94BC851.title: "Neutronium"
	quest.6DDDE2268B691F74.quest_desc: [
		"At its lowest power (Cupronickel coils and &7LV&r Voltage), the &dMulti Smelter&r smelts 32 items in just 12 seconds - equivalent to &926.7 Furnaces&r, or 3.3 Steam Ovens!"
		""
		"If that wasn't already enough to convince you, standard &aoverclocks&r can be applied with sufficient voltage."
		""
		"And even better - higher tier &3Coils&r increase the amount of items it can smelt in &dparallel&r!"
	]
	quest.6DDDE2268B691F74.quest_subtitle: "Possibly the most powerful furnace you've seen"
	quest.6DDDE2268B691F74.title: "Ultimate Smelter"
	quest.6DFE4E05FBAC9A3C.quest_desc: ["The Machete blade allows the breaking of web and plants in an area."]
	quest.6E0E13806F388D7E.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to &aArs Nouveau&f!"
		""
		"Ars Nouveau is a magic mod that allows you to create custom spells with the different Glyphs made within the mod!"
	]
	quest.6E186F9C57155BFA.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Steam Turbine&r is the only Generator you can realistically use in &7LV&r. &2Later, you'll unlock more interesting Power options&r, such as natural gases or petrols."
		""
		"When provided Steam, the turbine will output EU at a ratio of &d2 Steam = 1 EU&r."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks two new tutorials on Electricity and Cables in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check them out to learn more!&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you're using a single &3Steam Turbine&r, you only need &a1x Tin Cables&r. On the other hand, if you upgrade to &32 Steam Turbines&r, you should use &a2x Tin Cables&r - else they may end up &cburning&r."
		""
		"This is because of the &9Amperage&r mechanic... but that will be explained later so you can enjoy playing. Don't worry!"
	]
	quest.6E186F9C57155BFA.quest_subtitle: "You must construct more turbines"
	quest.6E186F9C57155BFA.title: "Electricity Generation"
	quest.6E7D3242496F4501.quest_subtitle: "Spawns in &6Deeplands"
	quest.6E7D3242496F4501.title: "Defeat a &6Shattered"
	quest.6E8F257261F93501.quest_desc: [
		"Crafting the &aUltimate Battery&r marks the end of GTCEu and the GregTech Community Modpack. &6Congratulations!&r"
		""
		"Now that you've finished the mod, there's a few things you should do:"
		""
		"- &9Join the GTCEu Discord&r and tell us about how your playthrough went! Feel free to show off your battery :) "
		""
		"- &eGo outside&r (and start playing GregTech in real life, right?). Integrate back into regular society."
		""
		"- &cBlow up your world with TNT and GT Dynamite&r. &nPlease, please, PLEASE make a backup first!!!&r"
		""
		"&6&lThank you for playing the pack! :D&r"
		"- The GregTech Community Pack Dev Team"
	]
	quest.6E8F257261F93501.quest_subtitle: "Is this... the end?"
	quest.6E8F257261F93501.title: "The Finale"
	quest.6E8F5B69CC8AFF2A.quest_subtitle: "Found inside the Monastery, a structure that spawns in the &bFrozen Peaks&r biome"
	quest.6E9E15DA847DD0A1.quest_desc: [
		"A circuit component that you can now produce thanks to the &3MV Assembler&r!"
		""
		"Capacitors are commonly used in computers to store information during power failures, amongst many other uses."
	]
	quest.6E9E15DA847DD0A1.quest_subtitle: "No cap, bussin frfr"
	quest.6E9E15DA847DD0A1.title: "Capacitors"
	quest.6EB68C28BEE24DEF.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the &2natural&r Ethylene route! This method uses &9plant matter&r to produce Ethanol."
		""
		"Before we get ahead of ourselves, &aSugar Cane&r works fine in a &3Brewery&r for a decent yield of Biomass."
		""
		"Othe&rrwise, you could try the \"&o&dPlantball into Bio Chaff&r\" route, and then turn it into Biomass, either in the &3Brewery&r or the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r - the latter being more efficient."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Only one Bio Chaff can be obtained from maceration until you make the &3HV Macerator&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You may recognise Plantballs from IndustrialCraft2! In IC2 Experimental, there was this rather... obscure way to turn Biomass into Biogas for power, which sadly required too much investment to be really worth it."
	]
	quest.6EB68C28BEE24DEF.quest_subtitle: "Plants aren't industrial enough!"
	quest.6EB68C28BEE24DEF.title: "Biomass"
	quest.6EB8D1C82A0C63F0.quest_desc: ["При &aудачном&r изучении этой таблички вы узнаете информацию о токсичных пещерах, заражённых радиацией."]
	quest.6EB8D1C82A0C63F0.quest_subtitle: "Токсичные пещеры"
	quest.6EBB48BD21BE7EDD.quest_desc: ["Матча или..."]
	quest.6EBB48BD21BE7EDD.title: "Люксовый чай"
	quest.6ECD212BB01F3B55.quest_desc: ["&dThe Phantom Knight Squad&r is a squad of ancient world travellers who met their end in one of the countless dungeons of the twilight forest."]
	quest.6ECD212BB01F3B55.title: "Phantom Knight Squad"
	quest.6EDC503C8C472640.quest_desc: ["Убив &aгидру&r, вы получите её &aсердце&r, что является могучим артефактом."]
	quest.6EE547AB2CA24377.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6EE547AB2CA24377.quest_subtitle: "&6Burns the attacker"
	quest.6EFE154D32A2155E.quest_desc: [
		"Both Sapphire variants serve as your primary source of Aluminium until you can unlock other electrolysis recipes in &bMV&r."
		""
		"The other two gems are mediocre at best."
	]
	quest.6EFE154D32A2155E.quest_subtitle: "Source of Aluminium"
	quest.6EFE154D32A2155E.title: "Sapphire"
	quest.6F1588945003CB8F.quest_desc: ["A recurve bow will decrease the draw time of a bow but make it do slightly decreased damage."]
	quest.6F15D7574B8F6DB5.quest_desc: [
		"The amount of EU this battery can store is the max value of a Long Integer in Java."
		""
		"Don't try to win Minecraft - you can't."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You're probably tired of this by now, but things are different with the battery lore this time. We promise."
		""
		"&oGTCEu's ultimate battery uses 16 &3UV&f orbs. GTNH's only uses 8. However, GTNH also has a &lReally Ultimate Battery&r&o made of 8 Ultimate Batteries! It's not useful at all, but still exists..."
		""
		"&oThey also added an &lExtremely Ultimate Battery&r&o made of 8 Really Ultimate Batteries, which is ludicrously expensive."
	]
	quest.6F15D7574B8F6DB5.quest_subtitle: "Consider touching some grass"
	quest.6F15D7574B8F6DB5.title: "Ultimate Battery!"
	quest.6F4AE13DA520109C.quest_subtitle: "It is time to upgrade your bronze machinery into their steel variants, they have evolved even further than you can imagine."
	quest.6F4AE13DA520109C.title: "You Live, You Learn, You Upgrade"
	quest.6F57A2A5AA6E3F49.title: "Oil Drilling"
	quest.6F6196A606D3A8EF.quest_desc: ["Remember, this guidebook is very very important in order to progress in case you're lost on what to do. Please take the time and read them when needed."]
	quest.6F6196A606D3A8EF.quest_subtitle: "Hello, young technician! I am here to help guide you through the factory world of Modern Industrialization. It may be a bit overwhelming at first, but it won't hurt too much, right?"
	quest.6F6196A606D3A8EF.title: "Engineering School?!"
	quest.6F6898DC529D1120.title: "Steam Querry"
	quest.6F6D2829FC42F21C.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Ruby Lens, engrave a Silicon Wafer into an ILC Wafer."
		""
		"This can be processed in a Cutter for IC Chips, which are important components that will be precious when improving upon your circuit crafting capabilities."
	]
	quest.6F6D2829FC42F21C.quest_subtitle: "I C U"
	quest.6F6D2829FC42F21C.title: "IC Chips"
	quest.6FA956DAA72D6139.quest_desc: [
		"This Jetpack takes most &aCombustion Fuels&r (excluding oils) to enable a primitive form of flight."
		""
		"Fill it like you would fill a Drum, or with a &3Canning Machine&r."
		""
		"Press &4H&r (default) to enable Hover Mode."
	]
	quest.6FA956DAA72D6139.quest_subtitle: "...well, almost Fly"
	quest.6FA956DAA72D6139.title: "I Believe I Can Fly"
	quest.6FD2FD1F7F98537C.quest_desc: ["Use a Photoelectric Pane on an Enderman or Endermite."]
	quest.6FD2FD1F7F98537C.quest_subtitle: "A Lens of Ender allows a Solar Panel to see through blocks which allows it to absorb sunlight while under a block."
	quest.6FE12FF0EFEE7525.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект инструментов из кости &6дракона&r и кости &6иссушителя&r."]
	quest.6FE1CBDF3A7515EC.quest_subtitle: "A component used to create an ME Terminal."
	quest.6FEF59B8F571359D.quest_desc: [
		"You probably have some old machines lying around, right?"
		""
		"You most likely know by now that Arc Furnaces can recycle machines, but by &5EV&r, they upgrade to &a9 slots&r!"
		""
		"&eNote&r: This quest accepts either an &5EV&r or &9IV&r Arc Furnace. You don't have to make both."
	]
	quest.6FEF59B8F571359D.quest_subtitle: "I never liked them anyway..."
	quest.6FEF59B8F571359D.title: "Getting Rid of Those Old Machines"
	quest.70072763767DCB9A.quest_desc: [
		"When crafting tool upgrades they will require tools of various specialities to be worked into their final forms."
		""
		"Wood materials will require axes, metals and stones will require hammers, and organic materials will require cutting tools such as swords to be able to be crafted."
		"For progressively higher levels of materials the required tool level will equally be as high, this drives you to equally maintain your tool levels in order to keep progress moving."
		""
		"So keep upgrading those hammers to keep getting the best gear!"
	]
	quest.70072763767DCB9A.title: "Repairing 2"
	quest.701BCADAE5CF6CA5.quest_desc: [
		"This quest is a light look over the &dfull scale of regular Ore Processing&r. Why \"regular\"? Some ores require special treatment, but that's a topic for much later. Oh no, we're already getting carried away!"
		""
		"Each quest surrounding this one gives a different machine that has some involvement in Ore Processing."
		""
		"&cNote:&r Don't get too preoccupied with Ore Processing! It's very slow at this point, and somewhat power hungry. Around 90% of ores are not important enough to warrant going out of your way to obtain their byproducts. &7That's a legitimate stat, by the way.&r"
	]
	quest.701BCADAE5CF6CA5.quest_subtitle: "You can't escape Greg..."
	quest.701BCADAE5CF6CA5.title: "What is this Mess?: Part Two"
	quest.70252B72F7728EFD.quest_desc: [
		"Hey, anyone remember Forestry?"
		""
		"This is pretty much the one vein you want to tap in for Phosphorus - which requires quite a few steps of processing to obtain."
		""
		"Pyrochlore will eventually become extremely valuable, as it's a good source of Niobium."
	]
	quest.70252B72F7728EFD.quest_subtitle: "Source of Calcium, Phosphorus, Niobium"
	quest.70252B72F7728EFD.title: "Apatite"
	quest.7033A24F37F9B9B9.quest_desc: ["The &aLuV Electric Prospector&r is a major upgrade from the &eHV&r one. With its huge range, it'll make finding Fluid and Ore veins very easy."]
	quest.7033A24F37F9B9B9.quest_subtitle: "If you're yet to strike gold, you will now"
	quest.7033A24F37F9B9B9.title: "LuV Prospector"
	quest.70432F650591353C.quest_desc: [
		"Gotta say, Cupronickel ingots look pretty tasty."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o IRL, Cupronickel usually contains additional elements such as Iron or Manganese to improve its strength. The Cupronickel in GregTech is probably more like Constantan (55:45 Copper:Nickel)."
	]
	quest.70432F650591353C.quest_subtitle: "Legally distinct Constantan"
	quest.704CCA2CEAB23B4D.title: "Enter The &6&lOtherside"
	quest.707AFB8F32C608EE.quest_desc: ["The Sequenced Gearshift allows you to create complex sequences of movements for your constructions."]
	quest.707AFB8F32C608EE.title: "Sequenced Gearshift"
	quest.70A66D9B5E2627C0.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.70BBF00528C68A05.quest_desc: [
		"&9Drills&r are electric tools which come in different tiers. The &7LV&r Drill is quite good: mining a 3x3x1 area. Higher-tier drills can mine 3x3x3, 5x5x5, and up to 9x9x9 to make huge holes!"
		""
		"This suggested drill is with a Diamond tip, which might be the best material for it right now."
		""
		"&9Note 1:&r All Electric Tools have a lot more durability than indicated, as they use Energy to prevent damage from being applied! On top of that, they can be enchanted as Pickaxes can."
		""
		"&9Note 2:&r Drills can now be configured to different ranges, not just the maximum or a single block."
		""
		"&9Note 3:&r You can now craft electric versions of other tools too! Hooray for less Wire Cutter crafting!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Up until GTCEu, Electric tools required Stainless Steel, which locked players out of experiencing their glory until &6HV&f!"
	]
	quest.70BBF00528C68A05.quest_subtitle: "We Drill Now? We Drill Now."
	quest.70BBF00528C68A05.title: "Oh Yeah, we Drillin'"
	quest.70CD9F0D26A75E13.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.70CD9F0D26A75E13.quest_subtitle: "This is a miner's trusty item that will mine tunnels in a 3x3 manner. Remember to always refuel with water and coal like a steam engine!"
	quest.70CD9F0D26A75E13.title: "My Drill Will Pierce the Heavens!"
	quest.70CDA5F1593DB4B2.title: "Visit &6Cursed pyramid"
	quest.713C8D6A20BF3A0E.quest_desc: [
		"&aSoldering Alloy&r is used solely as a &9Fluid&r, and in most cases is &dinterchangeable&r in circuit recipes as a cheaper alternative to Tin&r."
		""
		"The choice is yours. Save more materials? Make Soldering Alloy. Spend less time crafting materials? Tin is the way to go."
	]
	quest.713C8D6A20BF3A0E.quest_subtitle: "I got soul but I'm not a solder"
	quest.713C8D6A20BF3A0E.title: "Soldering Alloy"
	quest.713D81FCECD1A537.quest_subtitle: "Dielectric Rods are one of the main building parts in creating another piece of machinery part."
	quest.713D81FCECD1A537.title: "Initial Parts"
	quest.71412502C81F21C1.quest_desc: [
		"&9Silicon Boules&r are made in the &3EBF&r with half a stack of &aSilicon Dust&r and a pinch of &aGallium Arsenide&r. Their primary purpose is engraving &6Circuit Wafers&r."
		""
		"After making the Boule, process it in the &3Cutter&r to get 16 Silicon Wafers ready for engraving."
		""
		"The recommended &aSilicon&r source at this point would be... hm, either &dGlass Dust&r or &dSodalite&r."
		""
		"&cWarning:&r Each Silicon Boule takes &47.5 minutes&r to make at 120 EU/t, or 1,080,000 EU! If the EBF loses power midway, the recipe will start to &close progress&r."
		""
		"With that being said, Silicon Boules take an absolute age to craft, so consider parallelizing the recipe in multiple &3EBF&rs and stockpiling them."
	]
	quest.71412502C81F21C1.quest_subtitle: "These wafers are fully fungible"
	quest.71412502C81F21C1.title: "Silicon Lottery"
	quest.7149FE98D0E105CE.quest_subtitle: "Found in forests. Unlocks Labyrinths and Yeti Lairs."
	quest.7149FE98D0E105CE.title: "Defeat the &eTwilight Lich"
	quest.7153C282E7490BD6.quest_desc: ["После победы над грозовым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &dдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.7153C282E7490BD6.quest_subtitle: "&dАметистовая"
	quest.7158BB4DFD87109C.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.717099CE2CB9A0ED.quest_desc: [
		"&oThis is a guide on how to automatically route &lall&r&o your Hot Ingots to your Vacuum Freezer while keeping everything automated perfectly fine.&r"
		""
		"You already know the drill from the Chemical Bath, so let's get right to the chase."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Install an &aItem Tag Filter&r Cover on the &3Input Bus&r of your &3Vacuum Freezer&r, open it and set to whitelist &e&lhot_ingots&r. The slot is to &dtest&r items to make sure you configured the Filter properly in case you forgot. Drag ingots from EMI!"
		""
		"From here, you now have the option to route either with &9Item Pipes&r or &9AE2&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2With Item Pipes&r, connect the output of your &3EBF(s)&r to the input of your &3Vacuum Freezer&r and the output dump (Chest, Crate, or ME Interface)."
		"You can also have a &dRestrictive Pipe&r in front of the output dump to ensure the Vacuum Freezer will be prioritized."
		""
		"&2With AE2&r, place a &3ME Storage Bus&r on top of your Cover and set to very &dhigh priority&r. Any hot ingots entering your ME system will automatically be moved into the Vacuum Freezer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&9Note:&r If you wish to know more tags for future automation setups, they will display if you press Shift when hovering over an item. For instance, an item tagged with &e&o#forge:plates/copper&r would be filtered as &e&lplates/copper&r."
		""
		"&9Other Note:&r The Item Tag Filter partially supports &dregex&r. Hover over the info icon for more information."
	]
	quest.717099CE2CB9A0ED.quest_subtitle: "Can we get much smarter? Apparently so"
	quest.717099CE2CB9A0ED.title: "300IQ"
	quest.71972471AFB97BB2.quest_desc: [
		"By placing some Redstone Dust into your Rock Breaker, you'll find yourself making some Obsidian."
		""
		"Obsidian Dust is quite useful, as it electrolyses into Iron."
	]
	quest.71972471AFB97BB2.quest_subtitle: "Fallout: New Vegas, Iron..."
	quest.71C41E71CF881A59.quest_desc: ["The third level of storage upgrade will increase the storage of a drawer block by 8 times."]
	quest.71C9599025F42AFB.quest_desc: ["Убивая приспешников королевы, вы будете получать хитин. Из которого можно создать &6броню мирмексов&r."]
	quest.71D13F8ED724184A.quest_desc: ["Хоглин, как оказалось, очень даже полезен."]
	quest.71D13F8ED724184A.title: "Огромный адский свин"
	quest.71ED2850DB4D0528.quest_desc: ["Learn the basic mechanics of Create. Hover over an item and hold 'W' to see a visual guide (Ponder)."]
	quest.71ED2850DB4D0528.quest_subtitle: "Hover over an item and hold down the W button to see how it works."
	quest.71ED2850DB4D0528.title: "Guide"
	quest.71EDE15818D4C2A1.quest_desc: ["The Blast Furnace is a complex structure for obtaining steel from cast iron or industrial iron using coal coke."]
	quest.71EDE15818D4C2A1.title: "Blast Furnace"
	quest.7223101B97E1FDFC.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.7234FD5F79ABF6B0.quest_desc: [
		"When this treatise is near a workbench any major module made of stone will do extra damage and have better efficiency."
		""
		"Can be bought from mason villagers."
	]
	quest.723A9F5E5263517D.quest_desc: ["The second level of storage upgrade will increase the storage of a drawer block by 4 times."]
	quest.724FB950CC472BB4.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the age of automation!"
		""
		"Ore Processing is now at your fingertips."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a definitive tutorial on Ore Processing in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.724FB950CC472BB4.quest_subtitle: "I've been waiting for this!"
	quest.724FB950CC472BB4.title: "Setting up Ore Processing"
	quest.726011E852DAB862.quest_desc: ["A gearbox allows you to change the direction of rotation at a 90-degree angle. It can be toggled between horizontal and vertical positions."]
	quest.726011E852DAB862.title: "Gearbox"
	quest.727075AAF9F91FAE.quest_desc: [
		"To get your grubby hands on some Titanium, &aRutile&r must first be reduced to &aTitanium Tetrachloride&r in an &3HV Chemical Reactor&r, then reduced again in an &3EBF&r with &dMagnesium&r to finally arrive at Titanium."
		""
		"The &dCarbon&r, &dChlorine&r, &dOxygen&r, and &dMagnesium&r used in the process can be &6perfectly recovered&r from the byproduct &dCarbon Monoxide&r and &dMagnesium Chloride&r with no loss. If you set up a system to recover them, &athe only material&r that you'll need to provide for Titanium is &dRutile&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTitanium Tetrachloride&r also acts as a catalyst in the production of plastics. A touch of &aTiCl₄&r in the polymerisation process can increase the polymer yield to &6133%&r&r. Naturally, this is completely optional."
	]
	quest.727075AAF9F91FAE.quest_subtitle: "Nope, still not Titanium"
	quest.727075AAF9F91FAE.title: "Almost Titanium²"
	quest.72740001958E929A.quest_desc: [
		"This hatch allows you to store more &aData Storage Items&r than the basic one."
		""
		"Don't forget that this hatch requires a &9Data Orb&r for research."
	]
	quest.72740001958E929A.quest_subtitle: "Increased storage density!"
	quest.72740001958E929A.title: "Advanced Data Access Hatch"
	quest.7275F30F2B0F74CC.quest_desc: [
		"The Forged Workbench, while not necessary, looks really nice with the Forge Hammer. It can be picked up with silk touch. "
		""
		"Surrounding this quest are a number of parts that can be salvaged from Ancient Bases to get unique abilities."
	]
	quest.7275F30F2B0F74CC.title: "Forged Workbench"
	quest.727FB7F7A159DFDF.quest_desc: ["Из некрома можно сделать броню и мощное оружие."]
	quest.72B084925FDCDF1B.quest_desc: ["Обьедените первородную тьму с яблоком и получите &4яблоко тьмы&r."]
	quest.72B084925FDCDF1B.title: "Страшная еда"
	quest.72D5F73986EBD718.quest_desc: [
		"Enchanting in DawnCraft works very differently from vanilla minecraft. For starters, you will need enchanting knowledge lv2. This is obtained from the Guild Master's main quest line (specifically, the quest to defeat the Nine Tails boss). "
		""
		"There are 3 new values which effect the quality of your enchantments - Eterna, Quanta and Arcana. The number of enchantment clues can also be affected. See below for descriptions of each."
		""
		"&b&lEterna"
		"Represents how strong your enchantment is, increasing the level cost. Only blocks surrounding the enchanting table one-block away and two-blocks high will affect enchantment values. Enchantment levels can reach up to 100 (rather than the vanilla 30), allowing for rarer and higher-level enchantments than usual."
		""
		"&b&lQuanta"
		"Affects the potential power and variance of the enchantmenr. High quanta can lead to large boosts in enchantment quality, however you also risk getting lower level enchantments or even curses if you are unlucky. \"Rectification\" can be added via certain blocks to reduce the potential negative effects of quanta, making it a purely beneficial stat. An amount of quanta is always good to have, even without rectification."
		""
		"&b&lArcana"
		"Increases the number of enchantments and makes rare enchantments more common."
	]
	quest.72D5F73986EBD718.title: "Enchanting in DawnCraft"
	quest.72F0DFAF5CC6D0FE.quest_desc: ["&a4A&r of &bMV&r energy transmission may be appealing, but you probably don't need these at this point. Frankly, you might find it easier to just jump straight to the &6HV&r Superconductors. The option is always there if you need it. Boron can be obtained as a Salt processing byproduct."]
	quest.72F0DFAF5CC6D0FE.title: "MV Superconductors"
	quest.730043448A9ADBB6.quest_desc: [
		"Hello! You're probably looking to set up &abasic ore processing&r. This quest line will try to guide you through the necessary motions. As always, it's &6important&r to make the disclaimer that this isn't the only &o\"meta\"&r way to process your ores - a strong ore processing facility will treat each ore depending on the demands of your &bGregTech&r factory. We emphasise that you shouldn't take this guide as gospel."
		""
		"Ready to get &2into the weeds&r?"
	]
	quest.730043448A9ADBB6.quest_subtitle: "From one Ore, a great many dusts shall flow..."
	quest.730043448A9ADBB6.title: "Start here!"
	quest.7309B35D119998EE.quest_subtitle: "Portable energy storage that can be used to charge machinery when needed."
	quest.731C3214BB61FDAE.quest_subtitle: "Found underground city in the &aOverworld&r."
	quest.731C3214BB61FDAE.title: "Defeat a &6Warden"
	quest.7342F6461382E839.title: "Quantum"
	quest.735328E1D55DC57D.quest_desc: ["Откройте новую информацию о драконьей стали и кузне в бестиарии, а затем постройте кузню с помощью которой, вы будете ковать &bдраконью сталь&r."]
	quest.735328E1D55DC57D.quest_subtitle: "&bСоздание драконьей стали"
	quest.735328E1D55DC57D.title: "Драконья кузня"
	quest.736D489426858C6C.quest_subtitle: "Most basic processor."
	quest.737A99A32E3CC9CB.quest_desc: [
		"You can also make rotational power with diesel. Always ponder if you need help. "
		""
		"FYI: Since you can't rotate ponders around, if you're wondering why it may not be working, the pump from the Air Intake goes into the Diesel Engine, not the other way around."
	]
	quest.7385A70C3CA6DD47.quest_desc: [
		"The Forge Hammer can be found in Ancient Bases where it can be used to create higher tier gear. A standard workbench or a forged workbench can be used with it."
		""
		"To activate the hammer it must be powered with 2 filled Thermal Cells, which are inserted on the sides with a right click. Accesories can then be added to the other two sides."
	]
	quest.7385A70C3CA6DD47.quest_subtitle: "Use a Forge Hammer to craft a module requireing tier 5+ hammering"
	quest.7385A70C3CA6DD47.title: "Forge Hammer"
	quest.73D14FE0FE249386.quest_desc: ["Provides a high level of Rectification."]
	quest.73E8283634E5E33A.quest_desc: [
		"Don't worry, this is nothing compared to running an EBF."
		""
		"Hopefully for you, the &3LCR&r recipe in &2EMI&r for &aRadon&r should be self explanatory on how to set it up."
		""
		"Input some &aUranium&r, loop back the &dPlutonium&r using a &3Electric Furnace&r, and let the magic happen."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This cursed yet charming \"chain\" is inherited from GregTech 5. Plutonium 239 existing as an ore is a sort of a placeholder to avoid having to obtain it through complicated means."
	]
	quest.73E8283634E5E33A.quest_subtitle: "200 seconds?! WHAT?!"
	quest.73E8283634E5E33A.title: "Radon"
	quest.73F751C3DBC2E636.quest_desc: ["Несколько интересных блюд из лавомерки."]
	quest.73F751C3DBC2E636.title: "Блюда из лавомерки"
	quest.74180AC57AE9F0FE.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to your first (of many) forays into &bHydrocarbons&r! You may already know a few of them, like Petrol, Plastic, Alcohol... well, in GregTech, you'll mass-produce many of these things, and more! This topic can be confusing at times, so you'll want to read carefully in order to avoid getting lost in the details. Now..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Here in &bMV&r, there are two main goals of working with Hydrocarbons - Power and Plastics. The interesting part is how you'll accomplish this. There are two main paths you can take: &6Petrochemicals&r and &aBiochemicals&r. Both have their pros and cons - Petrochemicals typically provide &9higher yields&r and &benergy-efficiency&r, while Biochemicals are fully &drenewable&r. Your source of Power and Plastics is entirely &bup to you&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Ready to dive in? The &6Petrochemical&r route(s) are to the left of this quest - you've got three options here. For those with green thumbs, the &2Biochemical&r routes are diagonally right. Best of luck!"
	]
	quest.74180AC57AE9F0FE.quest_subtitle: "Getting industrial"
	quest.74223D24045FE969.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.7422BD3C0F060AC5.title: "Final Book"
	quest.7451BCBD5ECAF026.quest_desc: ["Её можно поставить."]
	quest.7451BCBD5ECAF026.title: "Хлебная корзина"
	quest.745A812FC4D17090.quest_desc: ["Shovels, they are great at digging up the soft stuff like dirt and sand and can also be used to make paths."]
	quest.747B62A955D0C629.title: "Visit &6Ancient factory"
	quest.748D2241F66FF644.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.748D2241F66FF644.quest_subtitle: "Coke is a useful fuel source that is much more powerful than any fuel source, and it is a small requirment for what is to come."
	quest.748E7791E3087456.quest_desc: [
		"* The Extractor has to be unused"
		""
		"* Unlike other artifacts found in the ruins this cannot be repaired with metal scrap"
	]
	quest.748E7791E3087456.quest_subtitle: "Replace the right head of a double headed tool with a Chtonic Extractor for a powerful harvesting tool"
	quest.7495FD1A88E6A10B.quest_desc: ["The Deployer mimics player actions. It can use tools, place blocks, or interact with mechanisms. This is critical for automating the creation of Precision Mechanisms."]
	quest.7495FD1A88E6A10B.title: "Deployer"
	quest.74A278B57EF76B3B.quest_subtitle: "Now we're cooking, perhaps there is more to this quarry than just this drill, maybe we can advance even further?"
	quest.74A278B57EF76B3B.title: "Bronze drill"
	quest.74B037D7031F4A78.quest_desc: [
		"&aEnriched Naquadah&r is an isotope of Naquadah, Nq-528. It is radioactive and will be used in (as of yet) unimplemented nuclear reactors."
		""
		"Currently, you just need it to make &9Trinium Coils&r."
	]
	quest.74B037D7031F4A78.quest_subtitle: "Naquadah, but radioactive!"
	quest.74B037D7031F4A78.title: "Enriched Naquadah"
	quest.74CE95FDE11033DB.quest_desc: ["Броня рыцарей Легиона Затмения. Когда-то в мире произошла большая война, в которой этот легион сражался за приход вечной ночи. Является довольно лёгким, тем самым не сковывая движений владельца."]
	quest.74CE95FDE11033DB.title: "Нагрудник солдата Затмения"
	quest.74DDCEE24E49AB88.title: "Any coal"
	quest.750B47CFDC4FAFEC.quest_desc: ["The modpack contains mods that may be removed after some time for various reasons."]
	quest.754DEFB6247B4FB5.quest_subtitle: "The ME Controller is the routing hub of a ME Network. Without it, only up to 8 devices can interact, any more and everything stops working.It is not possible to have 2 ME Controller in one ME Network.Unlike most ME Network devices, the ME Controller does not require channels, rather it emits them 8 or 32 per side, depending how many channels the device supports."
	quest.75608EDF99965533.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.75608EDF99965533.quest_subtitle: "Perfect! Now we can move our fluids properly now! Though it only works with one type of fluid at a time."
	quest.75608EDF99965533.title: "Fluid Transportation"
	quest.7567E885B7166603.quest_desc: [
		"Well... can you show us an &bMV&r Circuit as well?"
		""
		"&aAluminium&r is the main ingredient for &bMV&r machinery. Check &8aa&7aa&raall the way to the other side for the &2Sapphire Quest&r if you haven't acquired any &aAluminium Dust&r yet."
		""
		"Once you setup an &3MV Electrolyzer&r, you can get &aAluminium&r through many other ores. All of this quest's rewards bear &aAluminium&r, so keep an eye out for them when mining."
		""
		"The process of smelting Aluminium can be cut down by about a third with &9Nitrogen&r, which is obtained by centrifuging &9Air&r from a &3Gas Collector&r."
		""
		"&6You will still need MV Circuits in order to make MV machines!&r"
	]
	quest.7567E885B7166603.quest_subtitle: "We're basically in MV now, right?"
	quest.7573E48E9BEFFB00.quest_desc: ["Создайте комплект брони из &7чешуи дракона&r, чтобы все кто видели вас знали, что с вами лучше не связываться."]
	quest.7573E48E9BEFFB00.quest_subtitle: "&7Чёрный комплект"
	quest.75905E3672399A63.quest_desc: [
		"The &aZero Point Module&r (item) is a non-rechargable battery with TONS of energy stored. You may have found one of these before now, but you haven't been able to discharge it until reaching &cZPM&r."
		""
		"These can only be found as loot from &6Jungle Temples&r. They're exceptionally rare - don't worry about finding one. "
		""
		"This quest is &6optional&r and is just for fun. Feel free to hit the checkbox if you just want the completion points!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Zero Point Module, the full name of the ZPM tier, is also from Stargate. Its namesake is a device which generated crazy amounts of energy."
	]
	quest.75905E3672399A63.quest_subtitle: "Unlimited powah!"
	quest.75905E3672399A63.title: "Zero Point Module"
	quest.75A4BA8547564888.quest_subtitle: "Stores AE energy up to 1.6 million units. They do not accept power directly but are used to add additional power storage to an already existing ME Network."
	quest.75A4BA8547564888.title: "Storing Energy 2"
	quest.75F38905DEA60F15.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Assembler&r is a staple for every Tier; an important goal to unlock more recipes and progress further into the Age. Many in the community see crafting a voltage tier's Assembler as a sign of &oproperly&r reaching said voltage."
		""
		"That being said, welcome to &bMV&r!"
		""
		"The &bMV &3Assembler&r unlocks &eTransistors&r, &eCapacitors&r and &eInductors&r, used for the next tiers of Circuits."
	]
	quest.75F38905DEA60F15.quest_subtitle: "Assengers, Avemble"
	quest.75F38905DEA60F15.title: "Advanced Assembler"
	quest.761B9A10EA2161C1.quest_subtitle: "Photoelectric Panes are used to create Solar Panels."
	quest.762C48F0C2EA6B81.quest_desc: [
		"&aAmericium&r is a Fusion Mk2 material, used in large quantities in CEu progression!"
		""
		"It requires 2 Fusion steps to obtain - Lanthanum and Silicon will make &bLutetium&r, and combining this &bLutetium&r with Chrome will give you &aAmericium&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In Gregicality Legacy, Americium was replaced with Dubnium. Americium is a material only obtained from nuclear reactors, so GCYL changed it to the synthetic element Dubnium instead."
	]
	quest.762C48F0C2EA6B81.quest_subtitle: "It'd be nice if we could make this in a nuclear reactor..."
	quest.762C48F0C2EA6B81.title: "Americium"
	quest.7630C21661FED121.quest_subtitle: "Found in forests. Unlocks the &eLich Tower&r."
	quest.7630C21661FED121.title: "Defeat the &aNaga"
	quest.764091A111FB4DA6.quest_desc: [
		"&aCrystal CPUs&r are used to produce &9Crystal Circuits&r - who would have thought?"
		""
		"Producing these is quite a bit different from the previous circuit components. Instead of standard silicon wafers, these rely on &9Emerald&r or &9Olivine&r."
		""
		"Getting your first Crystal Chips will be difficult, so you may wish to invest in a high-tier Autoclave. If you use a &6HV&r Autoclave... well, we didn't take you for the gambling sort."
		""
		"After you get your first Chip, you can duplicate them with &9Europium&r. Don't worry about those other recipes yet, they're for later on in &cZPM&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eNote&r: An &9Advanced Item Detector&r cover will be useful for automating these. They work just like the Advanced Energy Detector."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT5u modpacks, making your first Crystal Chips required the autoclave to be in Low Gravity, which meant doing this process on a Galacticraft Space Station, or on the moon!"
	]
	quest.764091A111FB4DA6.quest_subtitle: "These don't even make any sense!"
	quest.764091A111FB4DA6.title: "Crystal CPU"
	quest.7649744CC59CA17A.quest_subtitle: "A component used in the creation of an illuminated panel."
	quest.768D429DF69F48DE.quest_subtitle: "4th Tier Capacitors used to upgrade to Niotic Machinery."
	quest.76B70EF552B35779.quest_desc: [
		"Obtaining paper is both more difficult and less efficient than in vanilla. Thanks, Greg."
		""
		"You'll need to grind &aSugar Canes&r into &aChad&r, and then smush the dust with a mallet and water."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 1:&r Don't worry, we're not cruel enough to have the recipe consume the bucket."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 2:&r Make a manual Sugar Cane farm. You could also automate one with Observers and Pistons. Shoutout to any &aNomifactory&r veterans."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 3:&r When you reach &7LV&r, you'll be able to make Paper from Wood."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 4:&r The Crafting Station makes this microcrafting absolutely &2trivial&r - use it!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 5:&r Paper will be used as a poor-quality wrapping material for the upcoming resistors."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 6:&r It is truly a pleasure to share this moment with you, our fellow Greg enjoyer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note 7:&r Yes, Paper Dust is really called that. Let's get the giggles out of the way now, shall we?"
	]
	quest.76B70EF552B35779.quest_subtitle: "#realism"
	quest.76B70EF552B35779.title: "Greg has struck again"
	quest.76F61E499780C30B.quest_desc: ["Invar has &650% more durability&r when used in GregTech tools compared to Iron (yes, that is the same as &aWrought Iron&r). Great for mining - you might want to consider using this in your tools if you &5haven't unlocked&r Steel."]
	quest.76F61E499780C30B.quest_subtitle: "An Iron-Nickel alloy"
	quest.76F61E499780C30B.title: "Invar"
	quest.77070668969E31BF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Styrene-Butadiene Rubber (SBR)&r is an enhanced type of Rubber."
		""
		"It can be used in place of Rubber in most recipes, and is &6four times more efficient&r at &ainsulating Cables&r. It is also strictly required for certain higher-tier recipes."
		""
		"This isn't exactly worth making until you get the &3Distillation Tower&r, but it eventually becomes easier with &dFuel Cracking&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Rubber will eventually be usurped by either &aSilicone Rubber&r or &aStyrene-Butadienne Rubber&r for &1IV&r Cables."
		""
		"Both these rubbers will be required once you make it to &dLuV&r."
	]
	quest.77070668969E31BF.quest_subtitle: "Steel Ball Run"
	quest.77070668969E31BF.title: "Styrene-Butadiene Rubber"
	quest.7707E5B061A7FFF7.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits along this line are &7LV&r, and are interchangeable in recipes."
		""
		"&cElectronic Circuits&r are the \"worst\" in terms of cost and effort required to produce, but you have to start somewhere."
		""
		"&eBasic Integrated Processors&r act as a middle layer between &cElectronic Circuits&r and &2Microchip Processors.&r"
		""
		"Finally, &2Microchip Processors&r will be the best option for the rest of the playthrough."
	]
	quest.7707E5B061A7FFF7.title: "&7LV&r Circuits"
	quest.77145113CD5B26FB.quest_desc: [
		"Source Berries produce more Source than other sources."
		""
		"This will also convert grass or dirt into Mycelium in a 3x3 area around it. It will also grow mushrooms around it if the space is empty."
	]
	quest.77145113CD5B26FB.quest_subtitle: "Generates Source from Nearby Food"
	quest.772F7CD63D31966A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Thermal Centrifuge&r is the most energy hungry out of the Ore Processing machines. It takes &aCrushed Ore&r or &aPurified Ore&r to give a different &6Byproduct&r from the &3Ore Washer&r, but at the same rate."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The GT5 Thermal Centrifuge required 48 EU/t to run. Yes, this may be above 32 EU/t, but GT5 had &dspecial mechanics&f where certain machines such as this one could accept more than 1 Amp."
		""
		"&oIn GTCE, the Thermal Centrifuge was changed to only work at &bMV&f with 60EU/t recipes. Let's be completely honest with you... what a &4complete waste of time&f! Never worth it. Thankfully, we've buffed the machine to be much more relevant."
	]
	quest.772F7CD63D31966A.quest_subtitle: "No, not THAT kind of Thermal"
	quest.772F7CD63D31966A.title: "Basic Thermal Centrifuge"
	quest.773377791C28B571.quest_desc: ["Убив василиска, вы получите &6кость иссушителя&r."]
	quest.7785E672EA6342AB.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &aсамку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &aбестиарии&r."]
	quest.7785E672EA6342AB.quest_subtitle: "&aЗелёное"
	quest.778B20E04E33C7C9.quest_desc: ["Этот кузнечный шаблон используется для улучшения возможностей шотгана."]
	quest.7796359B0F6A6606.quest_desc: ["A Backpack is your trusty companion in travels. It can be worn in the curios slot and opened with a hotkey (default 'B')."]
	quest.7796359B0F6A6606.title: "Backpack"
	quest.77B36844A2421C33.quest_desc: ["В саваннах можно встретить существ, от которых произошли курицы - &6Василисков&r. Их глаза обладают иссушающими свойствами, поэтому не советую смотреть им в глаза."]
	quest.77B7B1EDD19831E0.quest_desc: [
		"Making &dLuV&r Components will require more work. You'll need to make an &3Assembly Line&r in order to progress."
		""
		"This Multiblock has a &evariable size&r&r. Each &3ULV Input Bus&r along the bottom can only hold a &dsingle stack&r of items, so you'll need different lengths for different recipes."
		""
		"You'll want to build this with a size of &d10&r to get started, or of a size of &d14&r to accept all possible recipes in base GTCEu. &6Don't worry&r if you overbuild - it can run any recipe if it's too long, but you may find the casings quite &4expensive&r right now. &7Choices, &8choices!&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Recipes here will require &aFluids&r, so it's a good idea to keep the &3Input Hatches&r permanently filled with &dSoldering Alloy&r, &dLubricant&r and &dStyrene-Butadienne Rubber&r."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks two new tutorials on the Assembly Line and Research in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check them out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.77B7B1EDD19831E0.quest_subtitle: "AKA the \"Assline\""
	quest.77B7B1EDD19831E0.title: "Assembly Line"
	quest.77BBAB9CA586BB36.quest_desc: [
		"&5Ender Air&r is probably the most interesting of the three airs to distill. Requiring an &9IV Distillation Tower&r and distilling in batches of 200,000L, you'll need to outfit your DT with at least an &9IV&r Input Hatch (or an &5ME Hatch&r if you're inclined)."
		""
		"You're getting a ton of Nitrogen, Oxygen, Helium, and Deuterium - the latter of which is commonly used in &aFusion&r. Tritium is used to make &6Helium Plasma&r, which is commonly agreed to be the best plasma for &2power generation&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Krypton and Xenon are your run-of-the-mill &aEBF-boosting&r Noble gases. At this point, you should consider running most (if not all) of your EBF recipes on &bCircuit 2&r to benefit from the faster durations."
		""
		"Would you look at that - you get &dRadon&r as well! It's a slow process, especially when you consider that your old setup (did you set it up?) already loops on itself, but &dmore Radon&r is nice."
		""
		"Last but not least, you're getting a low chance of &3Ender Pearl Dust&r. The chances are low enough that you shouldn't give up on the Mixer recipe just yet... but once again, more &3Ender Pearls&r are nice!"
	]
	quest.77BBAB9CA586BB36.quest_subtitle: "Nitrogen, Oxygen, Helium, Krypton, Xenon, Radon, Ender Pearls..."
	quest.77BBAB9CA586BB36.title: "Liquid Ender Air"
	quest.77D82C14AF67BCEE.quest_desc: ["Это око находится под охраной магов из расы Кобольдов."]
	quest.77DBD93F55880929.quest_desc: ["Когда-то драконов в мире было намного больше, но рыцари-драконоборцы очень сильно сократили их популяцию. Теперь найти настоящего древнего дракона - большая редкость. Эта тяжёлая древняя броня,, принадлежавшая когда-то одному из сильнейших драконоборцев, впитала в себя силу поверженных драконов. Обеспечивает огромную защиту против драконов."]
	quest.77DBD93F55880929.title: "Ботинки драконоборца"
	quest.77EA56D16A9B3BFC.quest_desc: [
		"Rubber is an excellent insulation material, and that's exactly what it's used for in GTCEu."
		""
		"You'll want to use the &3Alloy Smelter&r to make &aRubber Bars&r. These ratios aren't particularly great, but we promise that making Rubber Bars will be much more efficient at &7LV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In base GregTech 5 &7(and in base GTCE)&f, you needed to get string and black wool carpets as your first insulation material. &8&mThat was obviously far, far more fun.&r"
	]
	quest.77EA56D16A9B3BFC.quest_subtitle: "Put that resin to use!"
	quest.77EA56D16A9B3BFC.title: "Rubbering up"
	quest.77EAEEF1DF1D8E22.quest_desc: ["Лунный кристалл является ценным ингридиентом для создания брони. По сути своей он является осколком души, поэтому может впитывать разные материалы и преобразовывать конечный результат в соответствие с ними."]
	quest.77EAEEF1DF1D8E22.title: "Лунный кристалл"
	quest.780A36F4890D3165.quest_desc: ["Full-size 1x1 storage drawers will store 32 stacks of an item."]
	quest.78123CEA9B11D861.quest_desc: ["Various tomes can be crafted, such as \"Tome of Miners\", \"Tome of Helmets\", and so-on. Search these in JEI to see all available tomes and recipes. These can be enchanted similarly to books, but will only recieve enchantments available to the appropriate tome (eg. a Tome of Helmets will only recieve viable helmet enchantments)."]
	quest.78123CEA9B11D861.title: "Tomes"
	quest.7813F183681E0342.quest_desc: [
		"In its simplest form, Ore Processing in GregTech boils down to &aconverting one Ore Block into two Ingots through two Dusts&r, like several other tech mods. "
		""
		"The added spice is the amount of steps, either optional or required."
		""
		"Ore Processing will be explained further once you get into &7LV&r."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on rudimentary Ore Processing in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.7813F183681E0342.quest_subtitle: "...and how do I get rid of it?"
	quest.7813F183681E0342.title: "What is this Mess?!"
	quest.7814B078C6256761.quest_desc: ["Used to extend the range of the ME wireless access point."]
	quest.7820DF52516344F4.quest_desc: [
		"Starting from here, you can now craft &dEV&r &3Energy&r and &3Dynamo Hatches&r! In &dEV&r, Energy Hatches now come with 4A, 16A, 32A or even 64A variants!"
		""
		"This is extremely useful for Multiblock generators, or boosting your GCYM machinery."
	]
	quest.7820DF52516344F4.quest_subtitle: "Perfectly regular progression"
	quest.7820DF52516344F4.title: "Upgrading your EBF III"
	quest.78277DBC07D3C45C.quest_desc: [
		"&aNaquadah&r is a late-game material with a variety of uses. It is required when building a Fusion Reactor and progressing to &cZPM&r, to name a few."
		""
		"For some reason, its fluid is a brilliant &agreen&r - don't ask us why."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Naquadah is a material originally from Stargate."
	]
	quest.78277DBC07D3C45C.quest_subtitle: "Don't you mean Stargatium?"
	quest.78277DBC07D3C45C.title: "Naquadah"
	quest.78464574AF8A27AC.quest_desc: [
		"Time to say goodbye to your &4Primitive Water Pumps&r. They've done you proud."
		""
		"Place this on the side of a machine to give it &616 buckets&o&r&r of Water every second!"
		""
		"Later on in &5EV&r, you can use these to craft Infinite Water Cells for your AE2 network."
	]
	quest.78464574AF8A27AC.quest_subtitle: "Truly revolutionary - water"
	quest.78464574AF8A27AC.title: "Infinite Water"
	quest.788795772632D09F.quest_desc: [
		"To progress further and get better hammers you will need to go exploring underground in cold biomes (Mountains, Taiga, etc.) for Ancient Bases. To help locate these bases a holosphere can be upgraded with an Eye of Ender to give it a proximity tracker of bases (they can sometimes be seen in the minimap while underground)."
		""
		"While exploring these dungeons it would be good to bring a hammer and claw tool to be able to salvage objects in the bases. When looking at blocks they will sometimes show a hammer or crowbar symbol along with a box where right clicking will do an action. A white icon means the action can happen, while red means it will not work, and yellow will have a chance to fail. Salvage will give you unique components and materials that you can use."
	]
	quest.788795772632D09F.title: "Exploration of Ancients Bases"
	quest.789E2DC829DD1828.quest_desc: [
		"Not to be confused with regular Granite, Red Granite has some useful utility when the dust is processed. "
		""
		"Electrolysing it yields Aluminium for slightly fewer steps than the renewable Clay electrolysis."
	]
	quest.789E2DC829DD1828.quest_subtitle: "Aluminium..."
	quest.79192BA29BE69170.quest_desc: [
		"If recipe sizes are starting to worry you, don't worry - &2AE2&r now allows you to place an unlimited amount of items into a processing pattern."
		""
		"Thanks to this innovation, you can automate all the &3Assembly Line&r recipes."
	]
	quest.79192BA29BE69170.title: "PackagedWho?"
	quest.7950278ADE16875A.quest_desc: ["The Apple Press is used to obtain juice and fruit mash. This is the first step towards creating fine beverages and wines."]
	quest.7950278ADE16875A.title: "Apple Press"
	quest.7953BCBBF9F386C4.quest_subtitle: "Ender Cores are a primary material used to create ender-based machinery."
	quest.796F33AE4A9CF30C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.796F33AE4A9CF30C.quest_subtitle: "The electric version of the Steam Blast Furnace, nothing more, nothing less. But it does add more recipes that can only be done with this furnace."
	quest.796F33AE4A9CF30C.title: "Induction Stove?"
	quest.797EB7DF0C07F327.quest_desc: [
		"From now? That's the basics of an &5ore processing setup&r. You can check your filters, make more machines, and generally improve efficiency, but if you've &6loosely&r followed everything on this page, you should be in &bgood stead&r!"
		""
		"&m&7Hopefully, some information here was of use.&r"
	]
	quest.797EB7DF0C07F327.quest_subtitle: "That wasn't so bad, now."
	quest.797EB7DF0C07F327.title: "We did it! Now what?"
	quest.79802A9D4A83E757.quest_desc: ["With a suitable Electrolyzer setup and a Singularity, large amounts of energy can be turned through Quantum Hawnking Radiation,  into Universally Useable Matter also known as UU Matter, the very fabric of the universe."]
	quest.79802A9D4A83E757.quest_subtitle: "This is a difficult bucket to use. With an electrolyzer and a singularity, large amounts of energy will be turned into Hawnking Radiation, into UU Matter, the very fabric of the universe!!"
	quest.79802A9D4A83E757.title: "UwU Matter"
	quest.799E9E9BA2416F0A.quest_desc: ["Этим шариком можно кидаться!"]
	quest.799E9E9BA2416F0A.title: "Огниво блуждающего огонька"
	quest.79A3560E017069DF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.79A3560E017069DF.title: "Ironwood armour"
	quest.79AF63E77AD70A93.title: "Bookshelf"
	quest.79B6E26E55934B4C.quest_desc: ["Concrete is a very durable building material also used in some heavy constructions."]
	quest.79B6E26E55934B4C.title: "Concrete"
	quest.79E4E53E9DF45549.quest_desc: [
		"The &aUV Mainframe&r is required to move into &3Fusion Mk2&r."
		""
		"It's also made in the Assembly Line."
		""
		"Passing over the ingredients we've already seen before, watch out for the &6HSS-E Frames&r."
	]
	quest.79E4E53E9DF45549.quest_subtitle: "...ah, here we go!"
	quest.79E4E53E9DF45549.title: "First UV Circuits!"
	quest.79F4B68189C05A25.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.79F4B68189C05A25.quest_subtitle: "The Assembler is a sophisticated machinery that will automate almost all of your machinery parts, but remember to make more of them to make it easier."
	quest.79F4B68189C05A25.title: "Machine Parts, ASSEMBLE!!"
	quest.7A121D5547606AC5.quest_desc: ["Находите различные реликвии и изучайте их, прокачивайте их способности и используйте их в своих приключениях и сражениях!"]
	quest.7A1E3C3A2D699C5B.quest_desc: [
		"&aHSS-G Coils&r bring up the Heat Capacity to &d5,400K&r."
		""
		"The ever-tempting &6Coil bonuses&r&r should be high incentive to make those early, as they become mandatory only during &dLuV&r."
		""
		"At this point, you may find yourself using only one &3Electric Blast Furnace&r for your entire base, powered with the highest available Voltage you can supply."
		""
		"&6Hot Metals&r will start taking longer to cool down, as unlike your EBFs, the &3Vacuum Freezer&r doesn't get perfect overclocks. For that, you probably want a dual &7(or quad)&r &3Vacuum Freezer&r."
	]
	quest.7A1E3C3A2D699C5B.quest_subtitle: "Approaching solar temperatures"
	quest.7A1E3C3A2D699C5B.title: "HSS-G Coils"
	quest.7A1E3E7E2DF17AD2.title: "Sawblade"
	quest.7A41038180C06B00.title: "Connector"
	quest.7A4358D94A9CE9CE.quest_desc: ["Убив плотоядного червя, вы получите &eхитин&r. Который можно использовать для создания брони."]
	quest.7A55CC71442CC854.quest_desc: ["You know the drill by now. It's an Assembler - what else do you need to know?"]
	quest.7A55CC71442CC854.quest_subtitle: "Pushing into EV"
	quest.7A55CC71442CC854.title: "EV Assembler"
	quest.7A64425597F58015.quest_desc: [
		"The Sifter sifts &dGem type&r &aPurified Ores&r to find &aExquisite&r and &aFlawless&r Gems, which can be cut into normal Gems. It also finds &aPurified Dusts&r of that gem. Overall, this gives a &6higher yield&r than other means."
		""
		"A small amount of &dFlawless Emeralds&r will be required in &bMV&r, and running ores in &3Sifting Machine&r is how you obtain these."
		""
		"&9Note:&r If you crushed Gem Ores (such as Diamond), it is critical you use this machine to recover the actual gems in non dust form. However, this is a rather slow process, so you may want to smelt this type of ore directly into the Gem."
	]
	quest.7A64425597F58015.quest_subtitle: "You're as Exquisite as the gems you sift!"
	quest.7A66998B5B887709.title: "Tools"
	quest.7A74F692F14F0FF8.quest_desc: [
		"&aEuropium&r is the first major Fusion Material. You'll be using this quite a lot going forwards."
		""
		"&eNote&r: The temperature of liquid Europium is very hot, but the fluid isn't a plasma. Plan your piping accordingly!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In Gregicality Legacy, Europium was replaced with Rutherfordium as the first fusion material, because Europium is actually found in Rare Earth and isn't fused in real life."
	]
	quest.7A74F692F14F0FF8.quest_subtitle: "Fusing Europium... whaaat?!"
	quest.7A74F692F14F0FF8.title: "Europium"
	quest.7AAA9CE6FA1E72F6.quest_subtitle: "Furnators use burning fuel sources such as coal and wood to generate power. The higher tier, the more power and efficiency created from fuel sources."
	quest.7AE6264633DF4EFE.quest_desc: ["Brass is the primary metal of this age. It's made by mixing copper and zinc in a melter."]
	quest.7AE6264633DF4EFE.title: "Brass Ingot"
	quest.7AE681E2AB31EA0D.quest_desc: [
		"&cZPM&r Circuits that aren't mainframes!"
		""
		"Don't lie - &bCrystal Supercomputers&r sound really cool, right?"
	]
	quest.7AE681E2AB31EA0D.quest_subtitle: "...wait, why'd things end here?"
	quest.7AE681E2AB31EA0D.title: "More ZPM Circuits"
	quest.7B09E0B3B3FB14FF.quest_desc: ["Когда-то драконов в мире было намного больше, но рыцари-драконоборцы очень сильно сократили их популяцию. Теперь найти настоящего древнего дракона - большая редкость. Эта тяжёлая древняя броня,, принадлежавшая когда-то одному из сильнейших драконоборцев, впитала в себя силу поверженных драконов. Обеспечивает огромную защиту против драконов."]
	quest.7B09E0B3B3FB14FF.title: "Нагрудник драконоборца"
	quest.7B0FC4A5072B0488.title: "8x cobblestone"
	quest.7B0FF43022F6C2EC.quest_desc: [
		"This questline serves as a quick guide to &9GregTech Amperage&r. As for &dVoltage&r mechanics, we'll go over those once you reach &bMV&r."
		""
		"&6&lTL;DR:&r For safety, match the Amperage limit of your Cables with the max amount of Amps provided by your Energy Producers."
		""
		"&6This quest unlocks a new tutorial on Amperage in the &lTips and Tricks&r&6 tab - check it out to learn more!&r"
	]
	quest.7B0FF43022F6C2EC.quest_subtitle: "Amps and You: a how-to"
	quest.7B0FF43022F6C2EC.title: "But what are Amps?"
	quest.7B3274DCE7597090.title: "Bastard Blade"
	quest.7B44018BC4C3DE5F.quest_desc: ["В подземельях этого мира, вы можете найти логова самых &6древних&r и &6могучих&r драконов. В их логовах таятся очень ценные сокровища, но их охраняют самые древник драконы. Осмелитесь ли вы бросить им вызов и &6одолеть их&r, чтобы заполучить &6яйцо дракона&r и &6вырастить&r своего великого и сильнейшего дракона?"]
	quest.7B6005A9F6F5C7FE.quest_subtitle: "Found in Glaciers."
	quest.7B6005A9F6F5C7FE.title: "Defeat the &f&lSnow Queen"
	quest.7BC94372A9C4E217.quest_desc: ["The good old fashioned slice and dicer."]
	quest.7BC94372A9C4E217.quest_subtitle: "Place a vanilla sword in a workbench and upgrade it"
	quest.7BE7DE4C0109D788.quest_desc: [
		"Don't let EMI fool you... there's only one possible recipe right now for this Primitive Diode."
		""
		"Diodes have a infamously &4nasty recipe&r, but they will become cheaper and more convenient once you can obtain &ePolyethylene&r."
		""
		"This is required for &dMV Circuits&r."
	]
	quest.7BE7DE4C0109D788.quest_subtitle: "Don't be swayed by EMI!"
	quest.7C104C2D2F1FD1A2.quest_desc: ["Откройте новую информацию о драконьей стали и кузне в бестиарии, а затем постройте кузню с помощью которой, вы будете ковать &dдраконью сталь&r."]
	quest.7C104C2D2F1FD1A2.quest_subtitle: "&dСоздание драконьей стали"
	quest.7C104C2D2F1FD1A2.title: "Драконья кузня"
	quest.7C1B5559A03F6E02.quest_desc: [
		"This vein starts to become notable for its Magnesium output starting in the midgame."
		""
		"Olivine also has various uses, as it can substitute &aEmerald&r in a couple of recipes."
	]
	quest.7C1B5559A03F6E02.quest_subtitle: "Source of Magnesium"
	quest.7C1B5559A03F6E02.title: "Olivine"
	quest.7C35B6B0B4CFFEB2.quest_desc: [
		"A good source of &6Heavy Oil&r, which is useful for &6Diesel&r setups early on."
		""
		"If you don't want to spend time processing Oilsands through your setup, you can always just &bCentrifuge&r it directly to get the Heavy Oil."
	]
	quest.7C35B6B0B4CFFEB2.quest_subtitle: "Source of the American Dream"
	quest.7C35B6B0B4CFFEB2.title: "Oilsands"
	quest.7C46763C2EC5FD81.quest_desc: ["Одолейте древнюю &cсамку&r дракона и заполучите одно из двенадцати яиц! И начните растить своего собственного дракона. Про то как это делать можно прочитать в &cбестиарии&r."]
	quest.7C46763C2EC5FD81.quest_subtitle: "&cКрасное"
	quest.7C4EEE4A53E2A5C7.quest_desc: ["Создайте броню &2мирмекса&r."]
	quest.7C5C1CA5A7954896.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.7C5C1CA5A7954896.quest_subtitle: "Steel is the next upgrade to such advanced machinery as it was not only complicated to reach this point, but also shows your ability to think ahead."
	quest.7C5C1CA5A7954896.title: "&8A Kilogram of Feathers or A Kilogram of Steel?"
	quest.7C73324F8156602C.quest_desc: ["Use the ingots of &6ignitium&r to create a powerful piece of equipment. It will definitely not let you down in battle...."]
	quest.7C756F5DCE15A93C.quest_desc: [
		"The modpack implements a fast travel system via the &cVia Romana&r mod."
		""
		"To use your new fast travel system, &csimply left-click&r the sign."
		""
		"To fast travel across a charted path, you just need to place some signs."
		"Placing a sign or editing an existing one will give you the option to link it to the nearest path"
		""
		"The blocks that can be used for paths are non-naturally occurring wood, stone, and bricks (plus path blocks)."
		""
		"This should work with most modded signs as well! Supplementaries signs are an especially good fit for this mod"
	]
	quest.7C756F5DCE15A93C.title: "Fast Travel"
	quest.7CA4A0722A359C4E.quest_desc: ["Очередной вид мяса, выпадающий с хоглина."]
	quest.7CA4A0722A359C4E.title: "Ветчина из хоглина"
	quest.7CAD6FF241A827F7.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have Steel, you can make a &3Flint and Steel&r. You now have access to the &4Nether&r."
		""
		"&o&8You could also light the Nether portal using... natural means. Dirty cheater.&r"
		""
		"The &4Nether&r has more veins to mine, and with those veins, new ores to discover. Check the Ore Tab to learn more about the Nether Veins."
		""
		"Additionally, &6Nether Ores are worth two Overworld Ores&r if mined with &3Silk Touch&r. It'd be great if you could craft the book directly, huh? ;)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&4Nether&r veins will take more effort to find - and are more dangerous to mine - than &2Overworld&r veins. Keep on top of your mining by using Waypoints - and remember that veins can be above you as well!"
		""
		"If you're yet to transition to &dPeaceful&r, it isn't too late to make the switch! There's no need to bother fighting Ghasts or Blazes in GTCEu."
		""
		"This is because the Blaze/Magma Cube and Enderman loot tables have been changed in this pack to &5Sulfur Dust&r and &5Ender Pearl Dust&r respectively, so you can't just rush the End."
	]
	quest.7CAD6FF241A827F7.quest_subtitle: "Why WOULDN'T it be made of Steel?"
	quest.7CAD6FF241A827F7.title: "Journey to the Nether"
	quest.7CC40BDAA803D044.quest_desc: [
		"The &3IV Cutting Machine&r is required to unlock &3IV Energy and Dynamo Hatches&r."
		""
		"Upgrading this to its &2GCYM&r variant isn't a bad idea."
	]
	quest.7CC40BDAA803D044.title: "IV Cutting Machine"
	quest.7CC79617A4965F25.quest_desc: [
		"&aPolytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)&r is a &7Carbon&r-&bFluorine&r polymer. Similarly to PVC, PTFE can be used to increase the yield of Plastic Circuit Boards and other crafts. Presently, it is used to make the walls of &3Large Chemical Reactors&r."
		""
		"&3Chlorine&r is required in the process, which is fully recycled if you electrolyze the &aHydrochloric Acid&r waste."
		""
		"&bFluorine&r will also be used in the &aUranium&r and &7Naquadah&r refinement processes."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r From this point onwards, you should be solidifying Polymers as &dBar&r (Ingot) form, as they can easily be shaped to whichever form you will need using the &3Extruder&r."
	]
	quest.7CC79617A4965F25.quest_subtitle: "A.K.A - Teflon"
	quest.7CC79617A4965F25.title: "Polytetrafluoroethylene"
	quest.7CCC1BDDE0C67F16.quest_desc: [
		"Crates are flat upgrades to Chests. A single block space that stores more items - what more could you ask for?"
		""
		"Where they shine is the fact that they &6accept Covers&r, making them perfect candidates for buffers in automation."
	]
	quest.7CCC1BDDE0C67F16.quest_subtitle: "Earlygame buffering"
	quest.7CCC1BDDE0C67F16.title: "GregTech Storage"
	quest.7CE179A962FC3C2D.quest_desc: ["В пустынях под песком обитают &eплотоядные черви&r, которые охотятся на всё, что движется над песком..."]
	quest.7CE18D246F01445D.quest_subtitle: "A Digital World! Finally, we're at this stage, where things get even more ridiculously complex. Remember to read carefully."
	quest.7CE18D246F01445D.title: "&9I want a console now!"
	quest.7CFC112B8F460549.quest_desc: [
		"You should have all the tools available to produce &aPolybenzimidazole&r on your own! Good luck - it's a 14-step process, and it's no slouch at that."
		""
		"&aPBI&r only becomes mandatory to progress from &dLuV&r to &cZPM&r, but tackling it earlier will unlock the &6Advanced SMDs&r."
	]
	quest.7CFC112B8F460549.quest_subtitle: "GTCEu's toughest polymer!"
	quest.7CFC112B8F460549.title: "Polybenzimidazole"
	quest.7D15EEE81B1A3100.quest_desc: [
		"Note that in theory, the &3EV Chemical Reactor&r is skippable by using the &3Large Chemical Reactor&r instead, but we're evil enough to force you to make this."
		""
		"&7It's still useful due to its compact size!"
		""
		"&8Honestly, if making one of these is a huge problem material-wise, take a look at your infrastructure."
	]
	quest.7D15EEE81B1A3100.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry gets even harder"
	quest.7D15EEE81B1A3100.title: "Extreme Chemical Reactions"
	quest.7D1620BEF949D9C6.quest_subtitle: "Found inside the Monastery, a structure that spawns in the &bFrozen Peaks&r biome"
	quest.7D3D156BE9C9E150.quest_subtitle: "This is not an easy metal to work with, remember that you need machinery to even bend this, but it shows its durability."
	quest.7D3D156BE9C9E150.title: "Titanium"
	quest.7D4B8F84394B1B35.quest_subtitle: "I wonder if this steam turbine can blow us away? Nah."
	quest.7D57A14810BC0CBE.title: "Kill &6Ignis"
	quest.7D66E73514323E51.quest_desc: ["An unusual shelf, decreases Eterna but adds maximum chaos."]
	quest.7D7A4CC66A3C193F.quest_desc: ["&bNitrogen&r is commonly obtained from centrifuging air. It's very useful, speeding up recipes in many multiblocks like the &bElectric Blast Furnace&r and the &6Pyrolyse Oven&r. We would &chighly&r recommend setting up a dedicated passive line to generate Nitrogen!"]
	quest.7D7A4CC66A3C193F.quest_subtitle: "Free nitro?"
	quest.7D7A4CC66A3C193F.title: "Nitrogen"
	quest.7DC321C2DE684FC1.title: "Ae2 Guide"
	quest.7DDCB711526F37A0.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Portable Cell&r serves as an early-game digital backpack alternative! It holds up to &a54&r types of items."
		""
		"What's more, it acts just like a regular AE2 Storage Cell. Once you get an ME System running, you can simply drop it into an &aME Drive&r or &b&aME IO Port&r for convenience."
		""
		"The Portable Cell's energy only drains when it's open. With &6167 minutes&r of juice stored in it thanks to changed config, you shouldn't worry about it running out of energy."
		""
		"Regardless, you will be able to &dcharge&r it in &7LV&r in &3machine Charger slots&r, &3Turbo Chargers&r or &3Battery Buffers&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cWarning&r: Attempting to store items with very large NBT Tags may result in them getting &cstuck&r. So far it seems that the Building Gadgets, Terminal and Clipboards are &lsafe&r, but you never know what could happen."
		""
		"If something gets stuck, build a simple AE2 Network with just an Energy Acceptor, an IO Port and a Storage Bus on a chest, then place your Portable Cell inside the IO Port. This will spit out any stored items into the chest."
	]
	quest.7DDCB711526F37A0.quest_subtitle: "A higher-tech Backpack! "
	quest.7DDCB711526F37A0.title: "Portable Cell"
	quest.7DEB73FD649BDFB6.quest_desc: [
		"Alright - your first &oproper&r &aGregTech&r tool. The first of &dmany&r."
		""
		"GT tools can be made out of many different materials. When used in crafting recipes, they &baren't consumed&r, instead losing durability. You'll want to start with an Iron tool - but you could opt for Wrought Iron if you already tackled that quest."
		""
		"&9&lHammer&f:&r A crafting tool that shows up in a lot of earlygame recipes. Its secondary function is muting machines by &msmacking&r right-clicking them."
		""
		"As a sidenote on all &aGregTech&r tools, you can repair them in an Anvil using the material of the tool itself, just like any vanilla tool. If you are finding yourself short on experience, &eBottles o' Enchanting&r are now craftable."
	]
	quest.7DEB73FD649BDFB6.quest_subtitle: "Your first GT Tool!"
	quest.7DEB73FD649BDFB6.title: "STOP! Hammer time!"
	quest.7DF12C07C3A70257.quest_desc: ["Доспех Героя, сразившего Тёмного Лорда в жестокой битве. После этого силы тьмы отступили обратно в Бездну и больше не предпринимали попыток нападения. Этот доспех впитал в себя сущность того героя и наделяет владельца силой и регенерацией."]
	quest.7E2076D45F83D9C3.quest_desc: ["The &aWireless Connector&r will help with logistics, giving &9Wireless Transfer&r for your ME Network with unlimited range. The energy cost scales exponentially with transfer distance."]
	quest.7E2076D45F83D9C3.quest_subtitle: "To infinity, and beyond!"
	quest.7E2076D45F83D9C3.title: "The Power of Wireless"
	quest.7E5E23283941E6BF.quest_desc: ["Находится на заброшенной фабрике глубоко под землёй под защитой &4механического чудовища."]
	quest.7E67F5E432F705E5.quest_desc: ["Победите мини-босса живущего в забвенных пустотах и получите &4первородную тьму&r."]
	quest.7EB2ED772BB8BBE8.quest_desc: ["После победы над огненым драконом, вы можете ощутить себя настоящим &aдраконоборцем&r! Заберите чешую дракона, чтобы создать комплект могучей брони из его чешуи."]
	quest.7EB2ED772BB8BBE8.quest_subtitle: "&aЗелёная"
	quest.7EB363A3DBFB851F.quest_desc: ["The Inscriber is used to create processors and prints. It's the heart of your AE2 automation."]
	quest.7EB363A3DBFB851F.title: "Inscriber"
	quest.7ECBE787B68EAF9A.quest_desc: ["&6Драконья&r еда поможет вашему дракону расти быстрее."]
	quest.7ECD974215E77432.quest_desc: [
		"Just so you're aware - vanilla farms such as &7Iron Golems&r or &ePiglins&r have been &4disabled&r in this pack. There are obviously ways to cheese the pack (such as some good old Minecraft &acapitalism&r, &mif you catch our drift&r), but we encourage you to try to play without taking advantage of some notorious vanilla \"&ocheese&r\"."
		""
		"It's possible that in the future, we'll just make a core-mod for the pack, so players can re-enable the disabled mob drops. For now, the drops are disabled via &5KubeJS script&r, so if you're script-savvy, the file can be removed at &o&7server_scripts/vanilla/loot_drops.js&r."
	]
	quest.7ECD974215E77432.quest_subtitle: "Is it safe? Is it alright?"
	quest.7ECD974215E77432.title: "What about my mob farm?"
	quest.7EF060B2F3F60197.quest_desc: ["Создайте &eпервобытную&r броню."]
	quest.7F098E39492F5712.quest_subtitle: "To craft the processors required for more advanced machines, you'll need the Inscriber. Each type of processor has an associated press, which you will find in meteorites. Each operation requires 1k AE charged up."
	quest.7F2042C72171EFEA.quest_desc: ["Убивая местных жителей, вы будете получать разные ресурсы, из которых можно создать &eвкусную&r еду..."]
	quest.7F2042C72171EFEA.title: "Пещерная еда"
	quest.7F272A099E65F848.quest_desc: [
		"&aPlatinum&r (needed for SMD Diodes) has its own dedicated Quest in the &5EV&r tab."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The SMD Inductors make an appearance in GTCEu for the first time. It's more consistent and convenient to have all Circuit components receive an SMD counterpart."
	]
	quest.7F272A099E65F848.title: "More SMD Components"
	quest.7F2FE3AF6F0C1190.quest_desc: [
		"The &aAdvanced Energy Detector&r is an RS-latch for Energy Control."
		""
		"Slap it on a &3Battery Buffer&r, set a Minimum EU near 0, and a Maximum EU near the max capacity."
		""
		"The Cover will output a &4Redstone&r signal until the high threshold is reached, and then it will wait until the low threshold is reached to output redstone again."
		""
		"This is a must to automate inertia-based power generators such as Boilers, or more importantly &3Large Turbines&r."
	]
	quest.7F2FE3AF6F0C1190.quest_subtitle: "Save on Redstone contraptions"
	quest.7F2FE3AF6F0C1190.title: "Advanced Energy Detector"
	quest.7F41EEF87B3A8B84.quest_desc: ["Remember that pressurizing water into HP water costs a lot of energy, but the turbine will not give it back!"]
	quest.7F41EEF87B3A8B84.quest_subtitle: "You can use a Heat Exchanger to recover the HP water for another cycle."
	quest.7F96B49412F52611.quest_desc: [
		"The Compressor will turn ingots into plates at 1:1 ratio."
		""
		"It can also turn each double ingot into 2 plates."
	]
	quest.7F96B49412F52611.quest_subtitle: "This is probably the first machine you will want to build as it saves your hammer from hammering away their durability."
	quest.7F96B49412F52611.title: "Mechanical Press, but more Modern!"
	quest.7FA0ACB7F161F378.quest_desc: [
		"&aTitanium&r has the highest corrosion resistance and strength-to-density ratio of any metallic element, so it's only natural that we'll be using it as the main material in our &5EV&r machinery."
		""
		"Confirm that your closed loop for &aRutile&r is up to standard, and prepare to run a dedicated &3EBF&r for hours."
		""
		"A quick aside - now we're at &5EV&r, single block generators are about to fall out of style! You'll need to run several &3HV Generators&r to keep up - later, upgrades to Multiblock Generators will be required."
		""
		"Whilst Multiblock generators are much more expensive, you'll find them to be much more energy efficient!"
	]
	quest.7FA0ACB7F161F378.quest_subtitle: "Titanite Slab"
	quest.7FA0ACB7F161F378.title: "Titanium"
	quest.7FB2D6C9A3763A47.quest_desc: [
		"You might already be familiar with EU as the Energy Unit for Electric machines - but what about Steam?"
		""
		"Steam machines will run using a proportional amount of steam at a 1:1 ratio of EU to Steam as listed in your recipe viewer of choice."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"After each recipe, the Steam machines will vent cooler steam (with snazzy particles) from the side with the square. This is the exhaust port."
		""
		"Important: Keep the exhaust port unblocked - this is neither an input nor an output slot! If the machine fails to vent steam, it will stop working."
		""
		"Reminder: Use your Wrench to change which side the exhaust port is facing (right-click)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Regular Steam Machines are twice as slow to complete recipes as is listed in EMI. To bring your machines up to speed, you may want to pursue High Pressure Steam machinery."
		""
		"High Pressure Steam Machines are the same speed as indicated by EMI, but with adjusted steam consumption. You will unlock them once you obtain Steel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Psst! If you're not in a Hardcore world, we invite you to stand on top of pipes transporting steam, or stand right in front of the vent as the machines are running recipes."
	]
	quest.7FB2D6C9A3763A47.quest_subtitle: "https://store.steampowered.com/"
	quest.7FB2D6C9A3763A47.title: "Steam Power"
	quest.7FCFE4C40837CF5E.quest_desc: [
		"A shopping list for anyone looking to automate &6Ore Processing&r on a large scale:"
		""
		"&9-&r One or more &3IV Macerators&r."
		"&9-&r The &3Large Centrifuge&r. Set it to work as a Thermal Centrifuge, and you're off to the races."
		"&9-&r One or more &3MV Electrolyzers&r - you could possibly make the large version if there's enough demand."
		"&9-&r A &3Multi Smelter&r."
		"&9-&r A &3Packager&r of any tier for those pesky Small/Tiny Dusts (think Rare Earth!)"
		"&9-&r Inventories acting as a large buffer, such as &3Tungstensteel Crates&r."
		"&9-&r &3ME Storage Buses&r, or a lot of &3Item Pipes&r + &aFilter covers&r, or &aItem Tag Filters&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"What you may &ealso want to&r add:"
		""
		"&9-&r A few &3LV Ore Washers&r for quick washing purposes."
		"&9-&r Alternately, a &3Large Ore Washer&r, accompanied with a set of &3Distilleries&r for &dDistilled Water&r."
		"&9-&r A second &3Large Centrifuge&r... this time set to Centrifuge mode for impure/purified dusts."
		"&9-&r &3Chemical Baths&r for the special Byproducts that require &dMercury&r or &dSodium Persulfate&r to obtain."
		"&9-&r &3Sifters&r of any tier for gem ores."
		"&9-&r &3Electromagnetic Separators&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If the Large Machines aren't your thing, you could always try using tons of &7LV&r machinery, and route with some clever piping."
		""
		"Overclocking is &cnot&r energy efficient, which is why it is generally better to go for &6low-tier machines&r in &3passive setups&r. One could also argue they are cheaper."
		""
		"In previous versions of GregTech, you could just use &3Processing Arrays&r, as they could condense many low-tier machines down into a &asingle speedy multiblock&r. Players desiring &esimilar processing speeds&r nowadays should really look to the &bGCYM machinery&r - it's quick, easy to upgrade when you tier up (&dEnergy Hatches&r are usually cheaper than 16 low-tier machines!), and c'mon now... they just look really cool."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&o&7\"Should I go for the optional byproducts?\""
		""
		"Yes."
		""
		"However, the \"routes\" you take your ores through processing is up to you. Want to macerate twice because you prefer the other byproducts? Go ahead!"
		""
		"Note that &3Thermal Centrifuging&r is usually a good idea, as doing so unlocks a &6unique Byproduct&r from the maceration step."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Chalcopyrite, Chalcocite, Bornite, Tetrahedrite, Pentlandite and Sheldonite ores should all be turned into their &dPurified Crushed&r variants and sent to your &6Platinum Group Metal&r chain."
		""
		"Purified Crushed Galena/Sphalerite should be reserved for Indium until you set up the Naquadah line. At that point, you'll have more Indium than you'll ever need."
		""
		"&aGallium&r, &aChrome&r, &aNiobium&r, &aRare Earths&r, and &aGlowstone&r are all &6Byproducts&r you might want to prioritise. "
		""
		"If you think we're missing any pertinent products, hit us up on Discord, and we'll be sure to add your favourites to this list."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"As you've probably realised, Applied Energistics 2 will be very, very helpful when automating all of this."
		""
		"&3ME Storage Buses&r are very powerful for routing items when they enter your ME network. They also have a huge whitelist or blacklist configuration. Attach them to some &3Tungstensteel Crates&r to buffer intermediate items, or use a dedicated AE2 subnet."
		""
		"To combine &aSmall Dusts&r into full &aDusts&r, you'll want a &3Storage Bus&r on high priority paired with an &dItem Tag&r filter set to &e&ldusts/small&r. Note that Small Dusts may be used for Boules, and a few Tiny Dusts are needed for the PBI chain, so you can blacklist them from the filter if you desire."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For ores that you want to process quickly but don't care for the Byproducts as the full \"route\" would take too long in the machines, prioritize filtering them for quick washing."
		""
		"The typically \"best\" path is: Macerator -> Ore Washing -> Thermal Centrifuge -> Macerator. If you deviate from it for various reasons, you're gonna have to set filters &emanually&r. Gasp!"
	]
	quest.7FCFE4C40837CF5E.quest_subtitle: "Extracting an ore's full potential... at last!"
	quest.7FDA72264E869611.quest_desc: ["Can consume an item to transfer some enchantments to itself. Used in an anvil. Can be a good way of moving enchantments from one item to another, but you never know exactly what you will get..."]
	quest.7FDF913E073F05AE.quest_desc: ["&d&k0&r В пещерах этого обычного мира, вы можете встретить мимиков, которые представляют из себя нежить в виде сундука, убив его, вы получите артефакт, который можно использовать. Также их можно найти в сундуках разных структур."]
	quest.7FF95F1216D104B2.quest_desc: [
		"&o...or perhaps it was the opposite?&r"
		""
		"The &3Steam Grinder&r can pulverize &6large batches of items quickly&r and effortlessly&r, sort of like a parallel Macerator."
		""
		"This thing is incredibly good for its tier. It's actually as strong as 5.3 &6HV&r Macerators, and only requires a trickle of Steam to power."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This Multiblock originally comes from GT++. It required Tumbaga to craft, an alloy with a mix of Gold and Bronze."
	]
	quest.7FF95F1216D104B2.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Oven's elder brother"
